KA_WEB_CHUNK(10,[{"n":"Lemon Curd","c":"saucen","k":"","p":12,"t":20,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["120 ml Zitronensaft","2 EL frisch abgeriebene Zitronenschale","80 g Zucker","3 Eier","60 ml ungesalzene Butter","1 Prise Salz (optional, betont Süße und Geschmack)"],"s":["Cut the butter into small chunks.","Put eggs, zest, sugar, and salt into saucepan.","Whisk ingredients in pan until frothy and light in color (1–2 minutes).","Add lemon juice and whisk for 30 seconds.","Add butter chunks.","Set pan on stove burner, turn on heat to medium-to-low, and start whisking contents so they don't coagulate or stick to bottom of pan.","Whisk constantly until butter melts and mixture thickens, then whisk another two minutes. Do not let mixture boil. It should be quite steamy (about 185°F / 85°C).","If desired, pour the mixture through the strainer to remove the zest and any other solids. Work the mixture through the strainer with the spatula; rake mixture off bottom of strainer into bowl.","Pour mixture from bowl into jar to within ¼ inch (0.75 cm) from top, taking care not to get mixture on rim, then seal jar with lid.","Refrigerate to thicken the product further. Store in the refrigerator."],"x":["Grate only the yellow lemon zest, avoiding the bitter inner white pith.","The curd can also be stored in any other suitable container.","fr:Livre de cuisine/Crème de citron"],"desc":"Lemon curd is a custard-like dessert sauce made with eggs, lemon juice and zest, sugar, and butter. It keeps for up to a week in the refrigerator, and it is excellent on shortbread, biscuits, scones, and English muffins. It can also be used in a variety of other dessert preparations.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Curd","i":"wb-en-2500","im":["5/50/Lemoncurd.jpg/960px-Lemoncurd.jpg","unbekannt","CC BY-SA 3.0","Lemoncurd.jpg","w"],"og":["½ cup (120 ml) lemon juice","2 tablespoons freshly-grated lemon zest","⅓ cup (80 g) white granulated sugar","3 eggs","¼ cup (60 ml) unsalted butter","1 pinch salt (optional, to bring out sweetness and flavor of finished product)"]},{"n":"Zitronencreme-Törtchen (Pastel de Nata)","c":"brot","k":"","p":12,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["400 g TK-Blätterteig, aufgetaut","2 Tassen Sahne","¼ Tasse Weizenmehl","6 Eigelb","1 Tasse Zucker","2 TL abgeriebene Zitronenschale","1 EL Puderzucker"],"s":["Preheat oven to 425°F (220°C).","Roll half the dough out to 14×10-inch rectangle. Use a 4 ½-inch round cookie cutter to out circles.","Press the dough circles into 12 muffin cups. Line each with foil, then fill with pie weights. Freeze about 15 minutes.","Bake pastry shells in bottom third of oven for 10 minutes. Remove foil and weights; let cool for 10 minutes.","Meanwhile, in microwaveable bowl, whisk together cream, flour, egg yolks, sugar, and lemon zest. Microwave at medium for about 8 minutes, or until it reaches the consistency of pudding, whisking every minute or so.","Strain pudding into bowl; let cool for 5 minutes.","Pour pudding into shells. Broil 6 inches from the heat source for 3 minutes. Let cool on rack for 15 minutes","Remove pastries from pan, and refrigerate for about 4 hours.","Sprinkle with icing sugar and serve."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Custard_Pastry_Cups_(Pastel_de_Nada)","i":"wb-en-2501","on":"Lemon Custard Pastry Cups (Pastel de Nada)","og":["400 grams frozen puff pastry, thawed","2 cups cream","¼ cup all-purpose flour","6 egg yolks","1 cup white granulated sugar","2 tsp lemon zest","1 tbsp icing sugar"]},{"n":"Zitronenkuchen mit Zuckerguss (Lemon Drizzle)","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":16,"t":40,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Kuchen","280 g ungesalzene Butter, plus etwas zum Einfetten","280 g feiner Zucker","5 Eier (Größe M)","Schale und Saft von 1 Zitrone","300 g selbsttreibendes Mehl (Mehl mit Backpulver)","1 ½ TL Backpulver","#Zuckerguss","150 g Puderzucker","Saft von ½ Zitrone"],"s":["Preheat the oven to . Grease and line a square cake tin.","Beat the butter and sugar in a mixing bowl, until soft and fluffy.","Beat in the eggs, one at a time, then lemon juice and zest.","Fold the flour and baking powder into the mixture.","Spoon the mixture into the cake tin.","Bake for 25 minutes until a skewer inserted into the center comes out clean.","Transfer the cake to a wire rack and leave it to cool.","Mix the icing sugar and lemon juice in a bowl until it is thick enough to coat the back of spoon.","Drizzle the icing over the cake.","Enjoy!"],"x":[],"desc":"Lemon drizzle cake is a simple butter cake flavored with lemon zest and juice, and topped with a lemony icing.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Drizzle_Cake","i":"wb-en-2502","im":["6/65/Blueberry_and_lemon_drizzle_cake_-_Central_Cafe%2C_Natural_History_Museum_2026-09-03.jpg/960px-Blueberry_and_lemon_drizzle_cake_-_Central_Cafe%2C_Natural_History_Museum_2026-09-03.jpg","Andy Li","CC0","Blueberry and lemon drizzle cake - Central Cafe, Natural History Museum 2026-09-03.jpg","c"],"on":"Lemon Drizzle Cake","og":["#Cake","280 g (9.9 oz/2¼ sticks) unsalted butter, plus extra for greasing","280 g (9.9 oz/1¼ cups) superfine sugar","5 standard eggs","Zest and juice of 1 lemon","300 g (11 oz/2¼ cups) self-raising flour","1½ teaspoons baking powder","#Icing","150 g (5.3 oz/1¼ cups) powdered sugar","Juice of ½ lemon"]},{"n":"Zitronenguss","c":"veggie","k":"USA","p":6,"t":0,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["1 Eigelb","2 EL Zitronensaft","1 Prise Salz","1 ½ Tassen Puderzucker"],"s":["Break the egg yolk into a small bowl.","Add the lemon juice and salt; beat lightly.","Gradually beat in confectioner's sugar."],"x":["If you want extra-stiff icing, add a little more powdered sugar."],"desc":"__NOTOC__ | American cuisine | Vegetarian Cuisine | Dessert","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Icing","i":"wb-en-2503","on":"Lemon Icing","og":["1 egg yolk","2 tablespoons lemon juice","1 pinch of salt","1½ cups confectioner's sugar"]},{"n":"Zitronen-„Impossible“-Pie","c":"brot","k":"","p":4,"t":135,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 Eier","½ Tasse Zitronensaft","1 ⅔ Tassen Milch","1 Tasse Weizenmehl (Type 405)","½ Tasse Zucker","1 Tasse Kokosraspel (optional)"],"s":["Preheat oven to 190°C (375°F).","Whisk all ingredients until thoroughly mixed. The optimal method is to whisk the wet ingredients first and slowly add the dry ingredients while whisking slowly.","Pour into greased baking dish.","Bake until an inserted skewer comes out clean. It should take at least 45 minutes.","Serve hot or cold with ice cream."],"x":["Use orange juice instead of lemon."],"desc":"The impossible pie is so-called because it has no crust but separates into layers while baking. It has a unique taste that is very nice.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Impossible_Pie","i":"wb-en-2504","on":"Lemon Impossible Pie","og":["4 eggs","½ cup lemon juice","1⅔ cup milk","1 cup plain flour","½ cup white granulated sugar","1 cup shredded coconut (optional)"]},{"n":"Italienisches Zitronen-Eis (Granita)","c":"dessert","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Tassen Wasser","1 Tasse heller Maissirup","½ Tasse weißer Zucker","⅔ Tasse Zitronensaft"],"s":["In heavy, medium-sized saucepan, stir together water, corn syrup, and sugar.","Heat to boiling over medium-high heat. Reduce heat to low and simmer, uncovered, 5 minutes.","Remove from heat; cool for 30 minutes. Stir in lemon juice.","Pour mixture into a 9 inch square baking pan. Cover surface with plastic wrap.","Freeze 3–4 hours, or until frozen but still soft in center.","Spoon into blender container; cover. Blend on high speed until mixture becomes white and creamy.","Turn back into the pan. Cover with plastic wrap. Freeze mixture about 3 hours or until firm."],"x":[],"desc":"Italian ice, also known as water ice, is a frozen dessert made from either concentrated syrup flavoring or fruit purees.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Italian_Ice","i":"wb-en-2505","im":["8/8a/Lime_Italian_Ice_%28Brooklyn%2C_NY%29.jpg/960px-Lime_Italian_Ice_%28Brooklyn%2C_NY%29.jpg","vige","CC BY 2.0","Lime Italian Ice (Brooklyn, NY).jpg","w"],"on":"Lemon Italian Ice","og":["2 cups water","1 cups light corn syrup","½ cup white sugar","⅔ cup lemon juice"]},{"n":"Zitronenmayonnaise","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["8 Eigelb","½ Tasse natives Olivenöl extra, aufgeteilt","2 EL frisch gepresster Zitronensaft","1 TL Cayennepfeffer","¾ TL Salz","¾ TL weißer Pfeffer","2 TL fein abgeriebene Zitronenschale"],"s":["Whisk together all ingredients except for oil in a large bowl.","One tablespoon at a time, slowly drizzle in oil while continually and vigorously whisking. Do not stop whisking, or the mayonnaise may separate.","Keep refrigerated for up to 3 weeks in a nonreactive container."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Mayonnaise","i":"wb-en-2506","im":["6/60/Mayonnaise_%281%29.jpg/960px-Mayonnaise_%281%29.jpg","jules","CC BY 2.0","Mayonnaise (1).jpg","w"],"on":"Lemon Mayonnaise","og":["8 egg yolks","½ cup extra-virgin olive oil, divided","2 tbsp freshly-squeezed lemon juice","1 tsp cayenne pepper","¾ tsp salt","¾ tsp white pepper","2 tsp finely-grated lemon zest"]},{"n":"Zitronen-Baiser-Pie (amerikanisch)","c":"kuchen","k":"USA","p":6,"t":45,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Kuchenfüllung","360 ml kaltes Wasser","240 g Zucker","2 EL Weizenmehl","3 EL Speisestärke","¼ TL Salz","120 ml Zitronensaft (von etwa 2 Zitronen oder Zitronensaft aus der Flasche)","1 EL abgeriebene Zitronenschale (von etwa 2 Zitronen)","2 EL Butter","4 Eigelb, verquirlt","⅛ TL gemahlene Kurkuma","#Baiser","4 Eiweiß","¼ TL Weinstein","6 EL Zucker"],"s":["Prepare and bake Grandma's Pie Crust or a ready-made refrigerated or frozen pie crust.","Let cool.","In a saucepan whisk together water, sugar, flour, cornstarch, salt, turmeric, lemon juice and lemon zest. Make sure any flour or cornstarch lumps are stirred until they dissolve.","Cook over medium heat until mixture starts to simmer. Stir constantly.","Add butter, then stir until melted.","Beat egg yolks in a small bowl. Add about ½ cup (120 g) of hot lemon mixture into eggs and stir well. This tempers the egg yolks so they won't scramble when added to the simmering lemon mixture.","Pour tempered egg mixture into pan of simmering lemon mixture. Stir until well mixed.","Continue simmering lemon filling about 2 minutes until it thickens, stirring constantly.","Pour into cooled pie shell and allow to cool while preparing meringue.","Place 4 egg whites in mixer and whip at high speed until they start to foam.","Add cream of tartar to egg whites then, while continuing to beat, add sugar, 1 tablespoon at a time. Beat about 30 seconds between tablespoonfuls of sugar.","Continue to beat meringue until stiff peaks form when beaters are raised from bowl.","Spread meringue over pie, starting on lemon pie filling, using rubber spatula. Spread over edges of crust, completely sealing in the lemon pie filling.","To form peaks in meringue, use the flat side of a rubber spatula to touch the meringue and pull away. Repeat over entire surface of meringue.","Place pie in 350°F (180°C) oven for 15 minutes until high points of meringue are lightly browned.","Serve at room temperature or chilled."],"x":["The pie filling is quite hot when pouring it into pie shell.","Keep this pie refrigerated.","In humid weather meringue may \"weep\" (small dots of liquid form on the surface). To lessen this possibility, apply meringue to lemon filling while it is still hot, cool pie to room temperature before refrigerating, and/or use powdered sugar instead of granulated sugar when making the meringue."],"desc":"This is the American old-fashioned lemon meringue pie with a gel-like filling. If you want a sticky filling, use the British Lemon Meringue Pie recipe instead.","img":"Lemon Meringue Pie 1.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Meringue_Pie_(American)","i":"wb-en-2507","im":["1/14/Lemon_Meringue_Pie_1.jpg/330px-Lemon_Meringue_Pie_1.jpg","H Padleckas","CC BY-SA 3.0","Lemon Meringue Pie 1.jpg","r"],"on":"Lemon Meringue Pie (American)","og":["#Pie filling","1½ cups (360 ml) cold water","1 cup (240 g) white granulated sugar","2 tablespoons all-purpose flour","3 tablespoons cornstarch","¼ teaspoon salt","½ cup (120 ml) lemon juice (from about 2 lemons or bottled lemon juice)","1 tablespoon lemon zest (from about 2 lemons)","2 tablespoons butter","4 egg yolks, beaten","⅛ teaspoon ground turmeric","#Meringue","4 egg whites","¼ teaspoon cream of tartar","6 tablespoons white granulated sugar"]},{"n":"Zitronen-Baiser-Pie (britisch)","c":"kuchen","k":"Großbritannien","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["8 Vollkornkekse (Digestive) (einfache Teekekse)","2 britische EL Butter (36 ml)","1 Dose gezuckerte Kondensmilch (300 ml)","1–2 Zitronen, Schale abgerieben und Saft ausgepresst","1 Eigelb","3 Eiweiß","6 britische EL feiner Zucker (108 ml)"],"s":["Pound the digestive biscuits into crumbs with the end of a rolling pin.","Add sufficient melted butter to the crumbs to make the mixture cohesive. Mix well, then press it into the bottom of a 10 inch (25 cm) diameter, 1 inch deep pie dish. Press down firmly with the tip of a spoon to make the base.","Combine the sweetened condensed milk and egg yolk. Stir gently, then mix in the lemon zest and juice to taste—more will be better, but be careful not to add too much or it will spoil the texture. Do not stir too much.","Pour the filling into the pie dish, covering the biscuit layer.","Whip the egg whites until foamy. Gradually beat in the sugar until you get stiff peaks.","Spoon the meringue into the pie dish, sealing around the edges.","Bake in a moderately cool oven (325 °F / 162 °C) for about 45 minutes until the meringue is a light golden brown. The aim is to cook the meringue and partly cook the centre (unlike, say, Baked Alaska, where only the top of the meringue is flash-cooked).","Remove from the oven, allow to cool, and place in the refrigerator for 2 hours to set.","Enjoy."],"x":["There are 2 types of lemon meringue pie. The more common version has a lemon \"gel\" in the centre (which is often a luminous yellow colour), and a hard pastry base. The version above is much stickier.","In an earlier version, the filling used 3 egg yolks. It isn't necessary.","When making the middle, it's essential to mix in the egg before the lemon. The acidity of the lemon acts on the yolk protein to thicken it; putting in the lemon first (which is tempting if you want to \"add lemon to taste\" without eating raw egg yolk) will cause the yolk to go \"stringy\" on contact."],"desc":"These instructions will make a sticky and indulgent lemon meringue pie. If you want the American gel-like centre, use the other recipe instead.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Meringue_Pie_(British)","i":"wb-en-2508","im":["6/68/LemonMerangePie.jpg/960px-LemonMerangePie.jpg","Travellers & Tinkers","CC BY-SA 4.0","LemonMerangePie.jpg","w"],"on":"Lemon Meringue Pie (British)","og":["8 digestive biscuits (plain/tea biscuits)","2 imperial tbsp (36 ml / 2.4 US tbsp) butter","1 tin (300 ml) sweetened condensed milk","1–2 lemons, zested and juiced","1 egg yolk","3 egg whites","6 imperial tbsp (108 ml / 7.2 US tbsp) caster sugar"]},{"n":"Zitronen-Baiser-Pie (vegan)","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":2,"l":"en","g":["1 gebackener veganer Mürbeteigboden","#Füllung","1 ¼ Tassen Zucker","½ Tasse Speisestärke","¼ TL Agar-Agar","¼ TL Salz","1 ¼ Tassen Pflanzenmilch","1 Tasse kaltes Wasser","¾ Tasse frischer Zitronensaft","1 ½ EL abgeriebene Zitronenschale","⅛ TL Kurkuma","#Baiser","9 TL Tapiokastärke","9 TL Kartoffelstärke","1 ½ TL Backpulver","¾ TL Guarkernmehl","½ Tasse + 2 EL kaltes Wasser","½ Tasse Zucker","¾ TL Zitronensaft"],"s":["Add all the filling ingredients to a saucepan, bring to boil, and whisk for a few minutes. When you can’t stir anymore it’s ready.","Keep the filling warm and covered while preparing the meringue.","Combine the starches, baking powder, guar gum, lemon juice, and about half the water. Whip by hand until stiff peaks start to form.","Add the rest of the water and the sugar slowly, and mix. It should be thick enough that it will have stiff peaks that don’t fall. If it is not thick enough, mix in a little more tapioca starch.","As soon as the meringue is done, pour the filling into the pie crust. While the filling is hot, spread meringue over filling, carefully sealing to edge of crust. Using a rubber spatula, touch flat side of spatula on meringue and pull away.","Repeat over entire surface of meringue.","Bake in a 350 °F (180 °C) oven for 10–15 minutes. Cool on rack for 1 hour.","Serve at room temperature or chilled."],"x":["The pie filling is quite hot when pouring it into pie shell."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Meringue_Pie_(Vegan)","i":"wb-en-2509","im":["6/68/LemonMerangePie.jpg/960px-LemonMerangePie.jpg","Travellers & Tinkers","CC BY-SA 4.0","LemonMerangePie.jpg","w"],"on":"Lemon Meringue Pie (Vegan)","og":["1 baked vegan pie crust","#Filling","1¼ cup white granulated sugar","½ cup cornstarch","¼ teaspoon agar","¼ teaspoon salt","1 ¼ cup non-dairy milk","1 cup cold water","¾ cup fresh lemon juice","1 ½ tablespoons lemon zest","⅛ teaspoons turmeric","#Meringue","9 teaspoons tapioca starch","9 teaspoons potato starch","1 ½ teaspoon baking powder","¾ teaspoons guar gum","½ cup + 2 tablespoons cold water","½ cup white granulated sugar","¾ teaspoons lemon juice"]},{"n":"Zitronen-Mille-feuille","c":"kuchen","k":"Frankreich","p":10,"t":20,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Teig","375 g fertiger Blätterteig","1 Ei, verquirlt","2 gestrichene EL Puderzucker","#Zitronenfüllung","3 Eigelb","1 ganzes Ei","75 g feiner Zucker","275 ml Milch","40 g Weizenmehl (Type 405) (Weizenmehl)","3 große Zitronen, Schale abgerieben und Saft ausgepresst"],"s":["Preheat the oven to 400 °F (200 °C).","Unroll the pastry on a lightly floured surface.","Trim the pastry so that you are left with a rectangle approximately 23 x 25.5 cm.","Roll out the larger piece of pastry to a 30 cm square, making sure you use a very even, gentle pressure on the rolling pin so that you end up with nice even edges.","Grease a baking sheet and use the rolling pin to transfer the pastry to the baking sheet.","Prick the surface of the pastry with a fork. Brush the pastry all over with the beaten egg.","Place the baking sheet on a high shelf in the oven and bake for 12–15 minutes until crisp and golden.","To get it extra crisp, heat the oven to its highest setting, sift 1 teaspoon of the icing sugar all over the pastry, and flash it under the grill.","Remove from the grill and, using a sharp knife, cut the square into three equal strips.","Turn the strips over, sift the rest of the icing sugar over them, and then flash them under the grill again.","Cool on a wire rack, then store in a polythene box, each layer separated with greaseproof paper.","Place the egg yolks and whole egg into a roomy bowl.","Use an electric mixer to whip the eggs together with the castor sugar until the mixture is pale, thick and creamy (4–5 minutes). Add the milk as you mix.","Sift the flour onto the mixture and whisk again until smooth.","Add the lemon zest and juice.","Place a pastry strip on the plate, and cover with half the lemon filling.","Put the second pastry strip on the creme, and cover with the remaining lemon filling.","Finally, top with the final pastry strip."],"x":[],"desc":"Mille-feuille (literally \"a thousand leaves/sheets\") is a French pastry made of many puff pastry layers.","img":"Mille-feuille 01.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Mille-feuille","i":"wb-en-2510","im":["7/7e/Mille-feuille_01.jpg/960px-Mille-feuille_01.jpg","Miya","CC BY-SA 3.0","Mille-feuille 01.jpg","r"],"on":"Lemon Mille-feuille","og":["#Pastry","375 g (12 oz) ready-made puff pastry","1 egg , beaten","2 level tablespoons icing sugar","#Lemon filling","3 egg yolks","1 whole egg","75 g (4 Tbsp) castor sugar","275 ml (1¼ cups) milk","40 g (4 Tbsp) plain (all-purpose) flour","3 large lemons, zested and juiced"]},{"n":"Eingelegte Zitronen I","c":"veggie","k":"Indien","p":1,"t":20,"d":2,"v":2,"l":"en","g":["12 kleine oder 6 große Zitronen (am besten dünnschalig)","1 große oder 2 kleine Zitronen, ausgepresst","½ Tasse Salz","¼ Tasse rotes Chilipulver","½ Tasse Zucker","3 TL gemahlene Kurkuma","1 TL Bockshornkleesamen","1 TL schwarze Senfsamen","¼ TL Asafoetida-Pulver (für die glutenfreie Variante weglassen)"],"s":["Wash the lemons and dry them well, leaving no water on the lemons. Trim off the stalk and any odd bits.","Cut the lemons in to small pieces about 2 cm (¾ inch) on each side, and place in a bowl.","Dry-roast the fenugreek, black mustard, and asafoetida together in a pan on a medium heat for about 5 minutes. Don't burn them!","Grind the roasted spices in a grinder or a mortar and pestle.","Add the ground spices, turmeric powder, salt, sugar and chili powder to the bowl and mix together well.","Pack the mixture into a 2 litre (2 quart) jar, or use a couple of smaller jars. Don't fill quite to the top—allow at least 1 cm space.","Sit the jar where it will get the heat of the sun. Bring the jar inside in the evening, and put it back out in the morning. Do this for at least a month in summer, two months in winter. The warmth of the sun will help the pickle to ferment."],"x":["Don't worry about the amount of sugar in the recipe, because it will be fermented away over time.","Asafoetida powder generally has wheat flour added to it to help it flow well. You can omit this ingredient if you want to make it gluten-free."],"desc":"Lemon pickle is a traditional condiment used with Indian food. Many pickle recipes from India have oil to help preserve the pickle, but this recipe uses no oil.","img":"Lemon Pickle.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Pickle_I","i":"wb-en-2511","im":["2/29/Lemon_Pickle.jpg/500px-Lemon_Pickle.jpg","Webaware","Public domain","Lemon Pickle.jpg","r"],"on":"Lemon Pickle I","og":["12 small or 6 large lemons (thin skins preferred)","1 large or 2 small lemons, juiced","½ cup salt","¼ cup red chile powder","½ cup sugar","3 tsp turmeric powder","1 tsp fenugreek seed","1 tsp black mustard seed","¼ tsp asafoetida powder (omit for gluten-free version)"]},{"n":"Eingelegte Zitronen II","c":"veggie","k":"Indien","p":1,"t":20,"d":2,"v":2,"l":"en","g":["8 kleine oder 4 große Zitronen","½ Tasse Salz","¼–½ Tassen Zucker","4 kleine grüne Chilis, fein gehackt","1 EL gelbe Senfsamen","1 EL gemahlener Ingwer","1 TL Bockshornkleesamen","¼ TL gemahlene Kurkuma","1–2 Sternanis"],"s":["Cut lemons into small pieces, and place in a bowl.","Cover with salt and set aside for at least 4 hours (24 is better).","Dry-roast the yellow mustard seeds, fenugreek seeds, star anise, and chopped chilis in a pan over high heat, shaking constantly—don't burn them!","Strain the juice from the lemons into a small saucepan, add the turmeric, ginger and sugar, and simmer for 2–3 minutes until the sugar has dissolved. If there isn't enough juice, add 1–2 tablespoons water.","Add the spices and sugar mixture to the bowl of lemons, and mix together well.","Pack into a pint jar, pressing the pieces in if needed, to ensure that the liquid covers all the lemon pieces.","Set aside to mature for 1 month."],"x":["If you don't have fresh chilis, add some dried chilis or chili powder. The pickle in the photo has three whole dried chilis in it."],"desc":"Lemon pickle is a traditional condiment used with Indian food. Many pickle recipes from India have oil to help preserve the pickle, but this recipe uses no oil.","img":"Lemon pickle star anise.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Pickle_II","i":"wb-en-2512","im":["d/da/Lemon_pickle_star_anise.jpg/330px-Lemon_pickle_star_anise.jpg","Webaware","Public domain","Lemon pickle star anise.jpg","r"],"on":"Lemon Pickle II","og":["8 small or 4 large lemons","½ cup salt","¼–½ cup sugar","4 small green chiles, finely chopped","1 tablespoon yellow mustard seed","1 tablespoon ground ginger","1 teaspoon fenugreek seed","¼ teaspoon turmeric powder","1–2 star anise pods"]},{"n":"Zitronen-Mohn-Muffins (glasiert)","c":"brot","k":"","p":12,"t":24,"d":2,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["80 ml Milch","60 ml Pflanzenöl","160 ml fettfreier Zitronenjoghurt","1 Ei","300 g Weizenmehl","60 g Zucker","2 EL Mohn","1 EL abgeriebene Zitronenschale","¼ TL Zitronenextrakt","2 ½ TL Backpulver","½ TL Natron","½ TL Salz","120 g Puderzucker","2 ½ TL Zitronensaft"],"s":["Preheat the oven to 400°F (200°C).","Grease a 12-cup muffin tin with cold butter.","Sift the flour, sugar, poppy seeds, lemon zest, lemon extract, baking powder, and salt into a medium bowl.","In a separate bowl, mix the milk, oil, lemon yogurt, and egg together.","Fold the dry ingredients into the wet mixture in three steps. Take care not to over-mix the batter.","Divide the batter between the muffin cups.","Bake for 16 minutes, or until golden brown. Muffins should be springy to the touch and a toothpick stuck in will come out clean.","While muffins are baking, prepare the glaze: Stir confectioners' sugar with the lemon juice until smooth.","Drizzle muffins with glaze.","Let cool on rack for 10 minutes and remove from muffin tin."],"x":["⅛ cup (30 g) sliced almonds can be sprinkled on after glazing for artistic flair.","Fresh Fruit and Yogurt Parfait: Slice your muffins in half and layer them with fresh berries, yogurt, and a drizzle of honey for a refreshing breakfast."],"desc":"This delicious muffin recipe is a treat for a special morning.","img":"Lemon Poppy Seed Muffins Glazed In Box.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Poppy_Seed_Muffins_(Glazed)","i":"wb-en-2513","im":["a/aa/Lemon_Poppy_Seed_Muffins_Glazed_In_Box.jpg/960px-Lemon_Poppy_Seed_Muffins_Glazed_In_Box.jpg","No machine-readable author provided. Ozten~commonswiki assum","CC BY 2.5","Lemon Poppy Seed Muffins Glazed In Box.jpg","r"],"on":"Lemon Poppy Seed Muffins (Glazed)","og":["⅓ cup (80 ml) milk","¼ cup (60 ml) vegetable oil","⅔ cup (160 ml) nonfat lemon yogurt","1 egg","1 ¾ cups (300 g) all-purpose flour","¼ cup (60 g) white granulated sugar","2 tbsp poppy seeds","1 tbsp lemon zest","¼ tsp lemon extract","2½ tsp baking powder","½ tsp baking soda","½ tsp salt","½ cup (120 g) confectioners' sugar","2 ½ tsp lemon juice"]},{"n":"Zitronen-Mohn-Pfannkuchen","c":"kuchen","k":"USA","p":8,"t":10,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse gebleichtes Weizenmehl","2 TL Zucker","½ TL Salz","½ TL Backpulver","¼ TL Natron","1 TL fein abgeriebene Zitronenschale","1 TL Mohn","¾ Tasse Buttermilch","¼ Tasse Milch","1 großes Ei","2 EL ungesalzene Butter, geschmolzen","1 TL Vanilleextrakt","Pflanzenöl zum Einpinseln der Platte"],"s":["Heat a large non-stick skillet or griddle over low heat while preparing ingredients.","Mix flour, sugar, salt, baking powder, and baking soda in medium bowl.","Whisk lemon zest and poppy seeds into dry ingredients.","Microwave buttermilk and milk in a 2-cup Pyrex measuring cup to room temperature, 20 to 30 seconds.","Whisk in egg, butter, and vanilla.","Add wet ingredients to dry ingredients and whisk until just mixed.","Return batter to measuring cup, stirring in a teaspoon or two of water, if necessary, to make a thick, but pourable batter.","Increase heat to medium and generously brush skillet or griddle with oil.","When oil starts to spider, but before it starts to smoke, pour batter, about ¼ cup at a time. Work in batches, if necessary, to avoid overcrowding.","When pancake bottoms are golden brown and tops start to bubble, 2 to 3 minutes, flip pancakes.","Cook until pancakes are golden brown on remaining side.","Repeat, brushing skillet or griddle with oil.","Serve hot."],"x":["Use all-purpose flour (which is softer than unbleached), not unbleached flour to make a tender pancake.","If using salted butter, reduce salt to ¼ teaspoon.","I usually substitute a tablespoon of lemon juice (or vinegar) in milk for the buttermilk.","Pancake batter should pour, not glug! On the other hand, runny batter makes thin, oddly shaped pancakes that frequently collide on the griddle. Stir in a touch more flour into thin batter. For batter that's too thick, whisk in water, a teaspoon at a time.","This recipe easily doubles for a crowd."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Poppy_Seed_Pancakes","i":"wb-en-2514","on":"Lemon Poppy Seed Pancakes","og":["1 cup all-purpose bleached flour","2 teaspoons sugar","½ teaspoon salt","½ teaspoon baking powder","¼ teaspoon baking soda","1 teaspoon finely-grated lemon zest","1 teaspoon poppy seeds","¾ cup buttermilk","¼ cup milk","1 large egg","2 tablespoons unsalted butter, melted","1 teaspoon vanilla extract","Vegetable oil for brushing griddle"]},{"n":"Zitroneneis am Stiel","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["250 ml frischer Zitronensaft","160–225 g weißer Zucker oder Turbinado-Zucker","1.2–1.5 l Wasser"],"s":["Combine the lemon juice and sugar in a pitcher or jug. Stir until the sugar is dissolved.","Stir in the water.","Divide the mixture between popsicle molds.","Insert a pop stick into each hole of the molds.","Put the popsicle molds into the freezer, and let it freeze for at least 5 hours, or until solid."],"x":["Using turbinado sugar will result in a golden-brown color and mild caramel flavor.","Because sugar dissolves more easily in warm liquid, you may want to heat some of the water and dissolve the sugar in it before combining with the remaining ingredients.","Hard lemonade incorporates an alcoholic spirit, such as tequila, gin, or vodka with the lemonade.","Various fruits, such as strawberries and raspberries can be added for color and flavor. A small amount of beet juice results in pink lemonade with little change in flavor.","Herbs such as mint, borage, lavender, and lemon verbena can change the aroma of the drink.","Including the lemon peels, bruised and sliced, gives more bite and a stronger aroma."],"desc":"Lemon popsicles are a refreshing frozen treat, also called lemon pop or frozen lemon stick. Regardless of what you call it, it is bound to be delicious! It is popular in the United States during the spring and summer, especially at beaches, picnics, and backyard parties.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Popsicle","i":"wb-en-2515","im":["8/80/Creative_lemon_popsicles_with_blue_molds_and_fresh_lemon_slices_on_a_colorful_surface.jpg/960px-Creative_lemon_popsicles_with_blue_molds_and_fresh_lemon_slices_on_a_colorful_surface.jpg","Shixart1985","CC BY 2.0","Creative lemon popsicles with blue molds and fresh lemon slices on a colorful surface.jpg","c"],"on":"Lemon Popsicle","og":["1 cup (250 ml/8.5 oz) fresh lemon juice","¾–1 cup (160–225 g/5.6–7.9 oz) white or turbinado sugar","5–6 cups (1.2–1.5 L) water"]},{"n":"Zitronen-Rührkuchen","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Kuchen","1 EL Butter, weich, zum Einfetten der Form","1 EL Mehl zum Bestäuben der Form","1 ½ Tassen Kuchenmehl (Type 405)","1 TL Backpulver","½ TL Salz","16 EL ungesalzene Butter, weich","1 ¼ Tassen weißer Zucker","2 EL abgeriebene Schale von 2 mittelgroßen Zitronen","2 TL Saft derselben 2 Zitronen","4 große Eier","1 ½ TL Vanilleextrakt","#Zitronenglasur (optional)","½ Tasse Zucker","¼ Tasse Saft von 1 bis 2 mittelgroßen Zitronen"],"s":["Adjust oven rack to middle position and heat oven to 350 °F.","Grease a 9x5-inch Pyrex loaf pan with 1 tablespoon softened butter; dust with 1 tablespoon cake flour, tapping out excess.","In a medium bowl, whisk together flour, baking powder, and salt; set aside.","In glass measuring cup or microwave-safe bowl, microwave butter, covered with plastic wrap, in 30-second bursts until melted. Whisk melted butter thoroughly.","In food processor, pulse sugar and lemon zest until combined. Add lemon juice, eggs, and vanilla; process until combined. With processor running, drizzle melted butter through feed tube. Transfer mixture to large bowl.","Sift flour mixture over batter in three steps, gently whisking after each addition.","Pour batter into prepared pan and bake 15 minutes.","Reduce oven temperature to 325 °F and continue to bake until deep golden brown and a skewer inserted in center comes out clean (about 35 minutes), rotating pan halfway through baking time.","Cool in pan for 10 minutes, then turn cake onto wire rack, poke on top and sides with a toothpick or skewer, and brush on lemon glaze (see below). Cool to room temperature (at least 1 hour).","While cake is cooling, bring sugar and lemon juice to boil in small nonreactive saucepan, stirring occasionally to dissolve sugar.","Reduce heat to low and simmer until thickened slightly, about 2 minutes.","Brush glaze onto cake."],"x":["Once cooled, cake can be wrapped tightly in plastic wrap and stored at room temperature for up to 5 days.","Lemon-Poppy seed Pound Cake: Follow the above recipe through step 2. Toss 1 tablespoon flour mixture with ⅔ cup poppy seeds in small bowl; set aside. Continue with recipe from step 3, folding poppy seed mixture into batter after flour is incorporated."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Pound_Cake","i":"wb-en-2516","im":["9/9a/Pound_cake_2.jpg/960px-Pound_cake_2.jpg","Douglas Paul Perkins","CC BY 3.0","Pound cake 2.jpg","w"],"on":"Lemon Pound Cake","og":["#Cake","1 tablespoon butter, softened, for greasing pan","1 tablespoon flour for dusting pan","1½ cups cake flour","1 teaspoon baking powder","½ teaspoon salt","16 tablespoons unsalted butter, softened","1¼ cups white sugar","2 tablespoons grated zest from 2 medium lemons","2 teaspoons juice from same 2 lemons","4 large eggs","1½ teaspoons vanilla extract","#Lemon glaze (optional)","½ cup sugar","¼ cup juice from 1–2 medium lemons"]},{"n":"Zitronenpuddings (gebacken)","c":"dessert","k":"","p":6,"t":60,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["Schale und Saft von 1 großen Zitrone","3 Eier, verquirlt","110 g feiner Zucker, plus etwas zum Bestäuben","115 g ungesalzene Butter, weich, plus etwas zum Einfetten","60 ml Weißwein","¼ Tasse Weinbrand","1 TL Rosenwasser","1 Rolle fertig ausgerollter Blätterteig","Weizenmehl zum Bestäuben"],"s":["Preheat the oven to .","Cream the butter and sugar in a mixing bowl until light and fluffy.","Beat in the eggs, then the wine and brandy.","Stir in lemon zest and juice.","Grease a ovenproof bowl. Unroll the pastry on a floured surface.","Cut out a circle just large enough to cover the surface of the bowl, and line the bowl with pastry.","Pour in the mixture.","Bake for 30 minutes until the top is a light brown in color.","Take the pudding out of the oven and leave it to cool.","Dust the pudding with a little extra sugar."],"x":[],"desc":"This recipe is adapted from the public domain cookbook Seventy-Five Receipts for Pastry, Cakes, and Sweetmeats.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Puddings_(Baked)","i":"wb-en-2517","im":["b/bd/Lemon_delicious_pudding_-_4928369507.jpg/960px-Lemon_delicious_pudding_-_4928369507.jpg","jules","CC BY 2.0","Lemon delicious pudding - 4928369507.jpg","c"],"on":"Lemon Puddings (Baked)","og":["Zest and juice of 1 large lemon","3 eggs, beaten","½ cup (110 g/3.9 oz) caster sugar, plus extra for dusting","1 stick () unsalted butter, softened, plus extra for greasing","½ cup (60 ml/2 fl oz) white wine","¼ cup () brandy","1 teaspoon rose water","1 sheet () ready-rolled puff pastry","All-purpose flour for dusting"]},{"n":"Zitronenreis","c":"beilagen","k":"Indien","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 Tassen gekochter weißer Reis","1 TL Senfsamen","3 EL Sesamöl (auch Til- oder Gingelly-Öl bzw. Nallennai genannt)","2 EL Schälerbsen","2 EL Erdnüsse (Erdnüsse)","½ TL Asafoetida (Asant) (Heengh bzw. Perungayum, Asant)","3–4 getrocknete rote Chilis, in Stücke gebrochen","4–5 Curryblätter","2 Zitronen, ausgepresst, oder 4 EL Zitronenkonzentrat","1 TL gemahlene Kurkuma","¾ EL Salz"],"s":["Heat the oil in a pan.","Add groundnuts and split-peas, and fry until golden brown.","Add mustard seeds, asafoetida, curry leaves, and red chillies. Wait until the mustard seeds sputter.","Mix in a little salt, turmeric powder and lemon concentrate.","Let it boil and reduce.","Remove pan from stove, add to the rice, and mix well."],"x":["Add a little oil to the raw rice before cooking it. This gives it a better texture.","Serve with potato chips or pickles.","1 tsp sesame seeds can be roasted and added for more taste."],"desc":"Lemon rice is a specialty of the South Indian coastal state of Tamil Nadu.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Rice","i":"wb-en-2518","im":["f/f4/Chitranna_and_Payasa.jpg/960px-Chitranna_and_Payasa.jpg","Radhikapavan","CC BY-SA 4.0","Chitranna and Payasa.jpg","w"],"on":"Lemon Rice","og":["4 cups cooked white rice","1 tsp mustard seeds","3 tbsp sesame oil (also called til/gingely oil or NaLEnnai)","2 tbsp split peas","2 tbsp groundnuts (peanuts)","½ tsp asafoetida (heengh/perungayum)","3–4 dry red chillies, broken into pieces","4–5 curry leaves","2 lemons, juiced, or 4 tbsp lemon concentrate","1 tsp turmeric powder","¾ tbsp salt"]},{"n":"Schweinefilet mit Zitrone und Rosmarin","c":"fleisch","k":"USA","p":8,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 mittelgroße Zwiebel, fein gehackt","2 EL Oliven- oder Rapsöl","1 EL Zitronensaft","1 TL fein gehackter frischer Rosmarin","1 TL fein gehackter frischer Thymian","1 TL abgeriebene Zitronenschale","1 Knoblauchzehe, fein gehackt","½ TL Salz","½ TL Pfeffer","2 Schweinefilets (900 g)"],"s":["Combine the chopped onion, oil, lemon juice, rosemary, thyme, lemon peel, minced garlic, salt, and pepper. Rub this mixture over tenderloins.","Let the tenderloins marinate, refrigerated, for as long as you want, or just immediately proceed with cooking.","Place the meat on a rack in a shallow roasting pan.","Bake uncovered at 400°F (205°C) or until a meat thermometer reads 160°F (70°C).","Cover with foil and let stand 10 minutes before slicing."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Rosemary_Pork_Tenderloin","i":"wb-en-2519","on":"Lemon Rosemary Pork Tenderloin","og":["1 medium onion, finely chopped","2 tablespoon olive or canola oil","1 tablespoon lemon juice","1 teaspoon minced fresh rosemary","1 teaspoon minced fresh thyme","1 teaspoon grated lemon peel","1 garlic clove, minced","½ teaspoon salt","½ teaspoon pepper","2 ea. (2 lb / 900 g) pork tenderloins"]},{"n":"Zitronen-Sharbat","c":"getraenke","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse Wasser","3 EL frischer Zitronensaft","1 TL Zucker","1 Prise Salz","schwarzer Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","Schwarzsalz (Kala Namak), nach Geschmack"],"s":["Mix lemon juice and water.","Add sugar and salt.","Add black pepper and black salt to taste.","Stir well and serve over ice."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Sharbat","i":"wb-en-2520","on":"Lemon Sharbat","og":["1 cup water","3 tablespoons fresh lemon juice","1 teaspoon sugar","1 pinch salt","Black pepper to taste","Black salt to taste"]},{"n":"Zitronenbiskuit","c":"kuchen","k":"USA","p":4,"t":60,"d":2,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["225 g Zucker","3 EL Mehl","1 Zitrone, Schale abgerieben und Saft ausgepresst","2 Eier, getrennt","1 EL Butter","1 Prise Salz","250 ml Milch"],"s":["Lightly beat egg yolks.","Mix the sugar and flour together, then add the lemon juice and zest, yolks, butter and salt.","Stir in the milk and mix well.","Whip the egg whites until stiff and fold into the first mixture.","Pour batter into custard cups or ramekins.","Set the cups in a pan of hot water and bake at for about 40 minutes."],"x":["The sponge may also be baked in a pie shell."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Sponge","i":"wb-en-2521","on":"Lemon Sponge","og":["1 cup (225 g/7.9 oz) granulated sugar","3 tablespoons flour","1 lemon, zested and juiced","2 eggs, separated","1 tablespoon butter","1 pinch of salt","1 cup (250 ml/8.5 oz) milk"]},{"n":"Zitronenschnitten","c":"brot","k":"","p":4,"t":60,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Boden","480 ml Weizenmehl","180 ml Puderzucker","240 ml Margarine (weich)","#Belag","4 Eier","80 ml Zitronensaft","360 ml weißer Zucker","60 ml Weizenmehl","1 TL Natron (5 ml)","1 EL abgeriebene Zitronenschale (15 ml) (Schale)","Puderzucker, nach Bedarf"],"s":["Combine flour and sugar in a medium mixing bowl.","Cut in margarine until mixture resembles fine crumbs.","Press firmly into a greased square (8 x 8 or 9 x 9-inch) pan.","Bake at 350°F (180°C) for about 20–30 minutes, until lightly browned. Prepare the topping in the meantime.","Beat eggs in large mixing bowl until frothy. Stir in the lemon juice and rind.","In another bowl, stir together the sugar, flour, and baking powder.","Add dry mixture to wet mixture. Stir until just moistened.","Spread evenly over the hot base, and return to oven to bake for 20–25 minutes, or until set.","Let squares cool before removing from pan and cutting. Dust with powdered sugar."],"x":[],"desc":"A wonderful square recipe with the flavor of lemon.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon_Squares","i":"wb-en-2522","im":["4/45/Lemon_Bar.jpg/960px-Lemon_Bar.jpg","Kjp001","CC BY-SA 4.0","Lemon Bar.jpg","w"],"on":"Lemon Squares","og":["#Base","2 cups (480 ml) all-purpose flour","¾ cup (180 ml) powdered sugar","1 cup (240 ml/g) margarine (softened)","#Topping","4 eggs","⅓ cup (80 ml) lemon juice","1 ½ cup (360 ml) white sugar","¼ cup (60 ml) all-purpose flour","1 teaspoon (5 ml) baking soda","1 tablespoon (15 ml) grated lemon peel (zest)","Powdered sugar, as needed"]},{"n":"Zitronen-Limetten-Limonade I","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":1500,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 ganze Zitronen, gewaschen","4 ganze Limetten, gewaschen","120 ml weißer Zucker","4 TL Limettensaft (20 ml)","Sprudelwasser, nach Bedarf"],"s":["Remove the zest from the lemons and limes in strips, leaving behind the bitter white pith.","Combine the sugar and zest in a container, and let this sit in the fridge for 24 hours. The sugar will extract the liquid from the citrus peels and produce a syrupy liquid.","Strain the solids out of the peel and sugar mixture.","Mix the peel and sugar mixture with lime juice. This should produce slightly under ½ cup (120 ml) of syrup.","To make the finished soda, mix 1 volume of syrup with 5 volumes of carbonated water."],"x":["You can make a Shirley Temple by mixing five crushed frozen cherries with the zest and sugar or by adding a volume of grenadine syrup for every volume of lemon-lime syrup when making the finished soda."],"desc":"Lemon-lime soda is a carbonated beverage flavored similarly to lemon- and limeade. This recipe originates from Flavorlab.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon-Lime_Soda_I","i":"wb-en-2523","im":["2/2b/Limeade.jpg/500px-Limeade.jpg","Michael Fludkov","CC BY 2.0","Limeade.jpg","w"],"on":"Lemon-Lime Soda I","og":["2 whole lemons, washed","4 whole limes, washed","½ cup (120 ml) white sugar","4 tsp (20 ml) lime juice","Carbonated water, as needed"]},{"n":"Zitronen-Limetten-Limonade II","c":"welt","k":"","p":5,"t":30,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["3 Tropfen Zitronenöl","3 Tropfen Limettenöl","1 TL geschmacksneutraler Alkohol mit 75 % Vol. oder eine Mischung aus ½ TL Gummi arabicum und ½ TL Wasser (5 ml) (2,5 ml) (2,5 ml)","1 TL Zitronensäure (5 ml)","4 TL Wasser (20 ml)","200 ml Wasser","360 ml weißer Zucker"],"s":["Combine the spirit or gum arabic water and oils together in a small cup, mixing well. Set aside.","Transfer this mixture into a larger container.","Put the citric acid, water, and white sugar into the container. Stir well.","To make the finished soda, combine 1 volume of syrup with 5 volumes of carbonated water."],"x":["Use a clean eye dropper to measure drops. Do not use a pipette, an eye dropper previously used for dispensing medication, or a spoon to measure drops.","You can make a Shirley Temple by mixing five crushed frozen cherries with the zest and sugar or by adding a volume of grenadine syrup for every volume of lemon-lime syrup when making the finished soda."],"desc":"Lemon-lime soda is a carbonated beverage flavored similarly to lemon- and limeade. This recipe is from Vintage American Cocktails & Sodas.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemon-Lime_Soda_II","i":"wb-en-2524","on":"Lemon-Lime Soda II","og":["3 drops lemon oil","3 drops lime oil","1 tsp (5 mL) 150+ proof unflavored spirit OR a mixture of ½ tsp (2.5 mL) gum arabic with ½ tsp (2.5 mL) water","1 tsp (5 mL) citric acid","4 tsp (20 mL) water","6⅔ oz (200 mL) water","1½ cups (360 mL) white sugar"]},{"n":"Limonade","c":"welt","k":"USA","p":4,"t":10,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["250 ml frischer Zitronensaft","160–225 g weißer Zucker oder Turbinado-Zucker","1.2–1.5 l Wasser"],"s":["Combine the lemon juice and sugar in a pitcher or jug. Stir until the sugar is dissolved.","Stir in the water.","Chill and/or serve over ice."],"x":["Using turbinado sugar will result in a golden-brown color and mild caramel flavor.","Because sugar dissolves easier in warm liquid, you may want to heat some of the water and dissolve the sugar in it before combining with the remaining ingredients.","Hard lemonade incorporates an alcoholic spirit, such as tequila, gin, or vodka to the lemonade.","Various fruits, such as strawberries and raspberries can be added for color and flavor. A small amount of beet juice results in pink lemonade with little change in flavor.","Herbs such as mint, borage, lavender, and lemon verbena can change the aroma of the drink.","Including the lemon peels, bruised and sliced, gives more bite and a stronger aroma."],"desc":"__NOTOC__ | Cuisine of the United States | Beverages","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemonade","i":"wb-en-2525","im":["1/10/Lemonade_-_27682817724.jpg/960px-Lemonade_-_27682817724.jpg","HarshLight","CC BY 2.0","Lemonade - 27682817724.jpg","w"],"on":"Lemonade","og":["1 cup (250 ml/8.5 oz) fresh lemon juice","¾–1 cup (160–225 g/5.6–7.9 oz) white or turbinado sugar","5–6 cups (1.2–1.5 L) water"]},{"n":"Limonade (extrasauer)","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":15,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["etwa 6 mittelgroße Zitronen, ausgepresst, ergibt 1 Tasse (250 ml) Saft","850 ml Wasser","160 g feiner Zucker"],"s":["Juice the lemons on a citrus reamer. Rolling the lemons on the counter with moderate pressure prior to juicing will result in more juice from each lemon. Try to keep out the seeds. If you prefer lemonade with no pulp, strain the juice to remove it.","Dissolve the sugar in the water. Heat may be helpful if using a large amount of sugar.","Combine the juice and sugar water in a pitcher. Stir well.","Chill or serve over ice cubes."],"x":["The sugar can be adjusted by ± ¼ cup (55 g/1.9 oz)."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lemonade_(Extra-sour)","i":"wb-en-2526","im":["1/10/Lemonade_-_27682817724.jpg/960px-Lemonade_-_27682817724.jpg","HarshLight","CC BY 2.0","Lemonade - 27682817724.jpg","w"],"on":"Lemonade (Extra-sour)","og":["about 6 medium lemons, juiced to yield 1 cup (250 ml/8.5 oz) juice","3¼ cups (850 ml/29 oz) water","¾ cup superfine sugar (160 g/5.6 oz)"]},{"n":"Linsenburger","c":"veggie","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["1 ½ Tassen getrocknete Linsen, verlesen","3–4 Tassen Wasser oder Gemüsebrühe","1 EL Knoblauchsalz","1 EL Butter","1 TL Olivenöl","1 mittelgroße bis große Möhre, fein gewürfelt","1 Stange Staudensellerie, fein gewürfelt","2 EL fein gehackte Zwiebel","4 EL getrocknete Petersilie","1–2 EL Worcestersoße","2 ganze Eier","¼–1 Tassen normale oder italienische Semmelbrösel","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pfeffer, nach Geschmack"],"s":["Place the lentils in a large saucepan, and add water or stock so that it covers the lentils by at least 2 inches (check the cooking instructions for the type of lentil you are using, as some may require soaking before cooking).","Cook for the approximate time as suggested by the lentil package (usually 30–45 minutes at a boil).","Place the cooked lentils into a fine sieve and allow to drain and cool.","Sauté the carrot and celery in the butter and oil over medium heat until softened (about 10 minutes).","Just before the carrot and celery are done, add the dried onion and parsley.","Place the drained and cooled lentils in a large bowl, add the carrot mixture, and mash everything with a potato masher. Don't over-mash; it is fine to leave some of the lentils whole.","Taste and adjust seasoning if necessary.","Add the eggs and about ¼ cup bread crumbs, and stir to combine all the ingredients. Continue to add bread crumbs until you have a slightly moist but not wet mixture.","Form mixture into patties. Place the formed patties onto a plate and layer with waxed paper in between. Cover and refrigerate for at least 1 hour.","To cook, it is best to use either a large sauté pan or a griddle on the grill—these burgers don't do well on grill grates. Cook over medium to medium-high heat until warmed through and a nice crust has formed on the outside.","Depending on the thickness of the burgers, this will take anywhere from 3–7 minutes per side.","To serve, you can place on a bun with the usual accoutrements or go crazy with whatever you think will go (garlic aioli, roasted peppers, etc). You could also serve without the bun with grilled pineapple, barbecue sauce, etc—the choices are endless."],"x":[],"desc":"Originally posted to Foodista by user dad1337. Foodista recipes are released under a CC-BY license.","img":"Lentil burger.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lentil_Burgers","i":"wb-en-2527","im":["b/b0/Lentil_burger.jpg/960px-Lentil_burger.jpg","dad1337/Foodista","CC BY 3.0","Lentil burger.jpg","r"],"on":"Lentil Burgers","og":["1½ cups dried lentils, picked through","3–4 cups water or vegetable stock","1 tbsp garlic salt","1 tbsp butter","1 tsp olive oil","1 medium to large carrot, finely diced","1 stalk celery, finely diced","2 tbsp minced onion","4 tbsp dried parsley","1–2 tbsp Worcestershire sauce","2 whole eggs","¼–1 cup plain or Italian bread crumbs","Salt to taste","Pepper to taste"]},{"n":"Linsen-Reis-Braten","c":"veggie","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["½ Tasse Linsen","2 ½ Tassen Gemüsebrühe","1 Lorbeerblatt","½ Tasse Naturreis (wird nicht ganz gebraucht)","1 Ei, verquirlt","etwa 2 EL gewürzte Semmelbrösel","½ fein gehackte Zwiebel","1 EL Olivenöl"],"s":["Combine the lentils and the bay leaf with 1½ cups of the stock. Cover and simmer for approximately 45 minutes, or until lentils are tender but not falling apart (they should offer slight resistance to the bite).","You may need to add additional stock during cooking; the lentils should remain covered.","Meanwhile, cook the brown rice in 1 cup of the stock: bring the stock to a boil, add rice, reduce heat to low, cover, and cook at the lowest heat for 50 minutes.","Empty about three-quarters of the rice into a bowl, along with lentils. A little liquid from the lentils should be added—maybe 2–3 tablespoons worth, but not too much.","Add the egg, onion, olive oil, and bread crumbs to the lentil-rice mixture. Adjust ratio of rice to lentils by adding more rice if desired. Mix in bread crumbs until mixture holds together.","Place mixture in a small greased baking dish, and bake at 350°F for 35 minutes, or until a crust is formed around the edge.","Allow to cool for at least 10 minutes before cutting and serving."],"x":[],"desc":"Lentil rice loaf isn't exactly a meatloaf imitation, but it is a hearty version of a vegetarian classic.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lentil_Rice_Loaf","i":"wb-en-2528","im":["6/61/Adas_polo.JPG/960px-Adas_polo.JPG","MRG90","CC BY-SA 4.0","Adas polo.JPG","w"],"on":"Lentil Rice Loaf","og":["½ cup lentils","2½ cups vegetable stock","1 bay leaf","½ cup brown rice (not all will be used)","1 egg, beaten","About 2 tablespoons seasoned bread crumbs","½ finely-chopped onion","1 tablespoon olive oil"]},{"n":"Linsen-Wurst-Eintopf","c":"suppen","k":"Deutschland","p":2,"t":60,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["250 g getrocknete braune Linsen","1 l Wasser für die Linsen (für die Soße nötig, nicht mehr nehmen)","1 Möhre, gewürfelt","1 Zwiebel, gehackt","2–3 Kartoffeln, geschält","2 Zehen Knoblauch","2 Paar Brühwürste, ganz oder in Stücken","1 großes Stück geräucherter Schweinebauch","mehr als 1 Lorbeerblatt","40 g Butter","40 g Mehl","½ l Wasser","1 EL Tomatenmark","2 EL Rotweinessig","1 TL Honig","etwa 1 TL Salz","Pfeffer"],"s":["Wash the lentils in sieve and cook them over low heat in the 1 litre of water for 40–50 minutes.","About 20 minutes before the end of the cooking, add the carrot, onion, potatoes, garlic, sausages, bay leaf, and pork belly.","After cooking, put the pot on the side and keep it warm.","Melt the butter in the little pot, add the flour, and cook carefully until brown, stirring the whole time.","Slowly and gradually add the ⅓ litre water, and bring to a boil.","Add the tomato paste, vinegar, and honey. Season with salt and pepper to your liking.","Stir the sauce into the lentils, mix well, and keep warm."],"x":["Perhaps at first you will think, \"how can vinegar go in this stew?\"; you will be surprised how well it fits, so don't be shy with it. You can also serve additional vinegar along with the meal.","Before eating, pick out the bay leaves.","Like many stews, lentil stew should be re-heated and tastes better the next day."],"desc":"This lentil and sausage stew is intended for eating with spätzle. It is a slightly modified recipe; the traditional one has no tomato and honey. But, as with many \"national meals,\" there are different opinions. Try different variations until you get your own taste for it; the most important things f","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lentil_and_Sausage_Stew","i":"wb-en-2529","on":"Lentil and Sausage Stew","og":["250 grams dry brown lentils","1 litre water for the lentils (needed for the sauce; don't use more)","1 carrot, diced","1 onion, chopped","2–3 potatoes, peeled","2 cloves of garlic","2 pairs of scalded sausage, whole or in pieces","1 large piece of smoked pork belly",">1 bay leaf","40 grams butter","40 grams flour","½ litre water","1 tablespoon tomato paste","2 tablespoons red wine vinegar","1 teaspoon honey","about 1 teaspoon salt","Pepper"]},{"n":"Suppe mit Linsen, Graupen und Tomaten","c":"suppen","k":"Großbritannien","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["240 ml Linsen","2 gehäufte EL Gerste (30 ml)","1 EL Butter (15 ml)","1 Zwiebel, gewürfelt","720 ml Wasser","2 Tomaten, geschält, entkernt, und gewürfelt","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pfeffer, nach Geschmack"],"s":["Soak the lentils and barley together overnight, then drain. This step is optional.","Fry the onion in the butter until soft.","Add the lentils, barley, and water.","Cook until the lentils are tender—this will take longer if grains are not soaked.","Add the tomatoes when the soup is almost ready.","Purée with a food mill, blender, or food processor.","Reheat and adjust the seasoning."],"x":[],"desc":"Alexandra soup is a puréed vegetable soup, containing lentils, barley, and tomato. It makes for a warming meal.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lentil,_Barley,_and_Tomato_Soup","i":"wb-en-2530","im":["8/8c/Tomato_soup%2C_plant-based_%2844040252791%29.jpg/960px-Tomato_soup%2C_plant-based_%2844040252791%29.jpg","Ella Olsson from Stockholm, Sweden","CC BY 2.0","Tomato soup, plant-based (44040252791).jpg","w"],"on":"Lentil, Barley, and Tomato Soup","og":["1 cup (240 ml) lentils","2 heaped tablespoons (30 ml) barley","1 tablespoon (15 ml) butter","1 onion, diced","3 cups (720 ml) water","2 tomatoes, peeled, seeded, and diced","Salt to taste","Pepper, to taste"]},{"n":"Curry mit Linsen, Kartoffeln und Tomaten","c":"suppen","k":"Indien","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse rote Linsen","4 Tassen Wasser","1 TL Salz","1 Lorbeerblatt","1 EL Margarine oder Butter","1 EL Olivenöl","2 große Kartoffeln, in 1-cm-Würfel geschnitten","1 TL Kurkuma","½ TL Cayennepfeffer","790 g gewürfelte Tomaten aus der Dose","2 TL Garam Masala","1 TL Honig oder Zucker"],"s":["In a large pot, combine and cook water, lentils, salt and bay leaf.","In a large frying pan, combine potatoes, turmeric, cayenne pepper, olive oil and margarine. Fry for 5–10 minutes.","Add potato mixture to the pot with the lentils along with all remaining ingredients. Cook until the potatoes are soft and tender.","Remove bay leaf before serving."],"x":[],"desc":"This creates a healthy, inexpensive and easy stew with depths of flavor. This recipe is fairly low on the heat scale, but feel free to add more cayenne pepper to up its spiciness. It is excellent served with chapatis or rice.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lentil,_Potato,_and_Tomato_Curry","i":"wb-en-2531","on":"Lentil, Potato, and Tomato Curry","og":["1 cup red split lentils","4 cups water","1 teaspoon salt","1 bay leaf","1 tablespoon margarine or butter","1 tablespoon olive oil","2 large potatoes, cut into ½ inch cubes","1 teaspoon turmeric","½ teaspoon cayenne pepper","28 ounces canned diced tomatoes","2 teaspoons garam masala","1 teaspoon honey or sugar"]},{"n":"Linsen mit Reis (Mujaddara)","c":"veggie","k":"Libanon","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":2,"l":"en","g":["½ Tasse braune Linsen, eine Stunde oder länger eingeweicht","½ Tasse Zwiebel, in Scheiben geschnitten","etwas gehackte Möhre, Staudensellerie, usw. (optional)","2 EL Olivenöl","½ Tasse brauner Langkornreis, abgespült","3 Tassen Wasser","½ TL ganzer oder gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","fein gehackter Knoblauch (optional)","getrocknete Chilischote (optional)","½ Zimtstange (optional)","ein paar Kardamomkapseln (optional)","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pfeffer, nach Geschmack"],"s":["Pick over the lentils to remove any stones.","Sauté the onion and any other vegetables in the olive oil for a minute or two.","If desired, sauté the rice for a short time, but do not let it burn.","Add the rice, water, cumin, garlic, chili pepper, cinnamon, and cardamom to the pot of onions. Bring to a boil, cover, and simmer for 40 minutes to 1 hour.","You will have to check it occasionally and add water—the final product should have some liquid but should not be very soupy. It is finished when the rice and lentils are both no longer crunchy.","Season with salt and pepper."],"x":["A little Parmesan cheese is tasty sprinkled on as a garnish.","Sauté some chopped onion and garlic quickly in oil until it browns (a slight burning is good), then stir it into some natural yogurt and use as a garnish."],"desc":"Mjeddrah is a stout lentil and rice stew, a Lebanese staple.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lentils_and_Rice_(Mjeddrah)","i":"wb-en-2532","im":["7/70/Lentils_And_Rice_%28140491283%29.jpeg/960px-Lentils_And_Rice_%28140491283%29.jpeg","J Doll","CC BY 3.0","Lentils And Rice (140491283).jpeg","c"],"on":"Lentils and Rice (Mjeddrah)","og":["½ cup brown lentils, soaked an hour or more","½ cup onion, sliced","A little chopped carrot, celery, etc. (optional)","2 tablespoons olive oil","½ cup long grain brown rice, rinsed","3 cups water","½ teaspoon whole or ground cumin","Minced garlic (optional)","Dried chile pepper (optional)","½ cinnamon stick (optional)","A few cardamom pods (optional)","Salt to taste","Pepper to taste"]},{"n":"Leongs Cashew-Hähnchen","c":"saucen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Hähnchen","2 mittelgroße Hähnchenbrüste","3 Eier","1 Tasse Milch","1 Tasse Weizenmehl","Salz (nach Geschmack)","Cashewkerne, nach Belieben gehackt","Frühlingszwiebeln, gehackt","#Soße","1 Dose Hühnerbrühe","1 EL Speisestärke","2 EL kaltes Wasser","2 EL Sojasoße","2 EL Austernsoße"],"s":["Debone and cut chicken breasts into bite-sized pieces.","Beat eggs and mix with milk.","Combine flour and salt.","Dip breasts into egg/milk combination, then into flour.","Deep fry the chicken until golden and cooked through.","For the sauce, heat broth in a saucepan on low to medium heat.","Make a cornstarch slurry with the cornstarch and cold water. Set aside.","Add oyster sauce and soy sauce to the broth. Continue heating the sauce.","Add the cornstarch slurry as needed to thicken the sauce until it reaches the desired consistency.","Serve chicken on fried rice, cover liberally with sauce, and garnish with cashews and green onions."],"x":[],"desc":"Cashew chicken was invented at Leong's Tea House in Springfield, Missouri. Leong had difficulty popularizing Chinese cuisine in the area and based the dish on the popular fried foods common in the Ozarks. The dish is not truly Chinese, but rather an American dish with a \"Chinese\" theme.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Leong's_Cashew_Chicken","i":"wb-en-2533","im":["3/36/Cashewchickenphoto.jpg/960px-Cashewchickenphoto.jpg","Simon Law from Montréal, QC, Canada","CC BY-SA 2.0","Cashewchickenphoto.jpg","w"],"on":"Leong's Cashew Chicken","og":["#Chicken","2 medium chicken breasts","3 eggs","1 cup milk","1 cup all-purpose flour","Salt (to taste)","Cashews, optionally chopped","Green onions, chopped","#Sauce","1 can chicken broth","1 Tbsp cornstarch","2 Tbsp cold water","2 Tbsp soy sauce","2 Tbsp oyster sauce"]},{"n":"Salatsuppe","c":"suppen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["Brühe","2 Bund Sauerampfer, gewaschen und zerteilt","1 Bund Endivie, gewaschen und zerteilt","1 Kopf Blattsalat, gewaschen und zerteilt","1 kleines Bund Kerbel, gewaschen und zerteilt","115 g Staudensellerie, gewaschen und zerteilt","1 Möhre, gewaschen und zerteilt","1 Zwiebel, geschält und zerteilt","Baguettescheiben, geröstet","Parmesan, gerieben"],"s":["Boil everything except for the bread and cheese in the stock for an hour.","Put some slices of toasted French roll into a bowl, and pour the soup over them.","Serve with grated Parmesan."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lettuce_Soup","i":"wb-en-2534","im":["c/cb/Butter_lettuce_soup.jpg/960px-Butter_lettuce_soup.jpg","stu_spivack","CC BY-SA 2.0","Butter lettuce soup.jpg","w"],"on":"Lettuce Soup","og":["Stock","2 bunches of sorrel, washed and cut up","1 bunch of endive, washed and cut up","1 head of lettuce, washed and cut up","1 small bunch of chervil, washed and cut up","1 stick of celery,washed and cut up","1 carrot, washed and cut up","1 onion, peeled and cut up","Sliced French bread, toasted","Parmesan cheese, grated"]},{"n":"Liberianischer Butterreis","c":"beilagen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Tassen Langkornreis","4 Tassen Hühnerbrühe (oder Gemüsebrühe)","1 Zwiebel, fein gehackt","2 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","2 EL Butter","1 Lorbeerblatt","Salz, nach Geschmack","schwarzer Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","frische Petersilie oder Koriander, gehackt (zum Garnieren)"],"s":["Rinse the rice thoroughly under cold water until the water runs clear. Drain the rice and set it aside.","In a large pot, melt the butter over medium heat.","Add the chopped onion and minced garlic to the pot. Sauté until the onion becomes translucent and the garlic becomes fragrant.","Stir in the drained rice and coat it well with the buttery mixture.","Pour in the broth and add the bay leaf to the pot. Season with salt and black pepper to taste. Stir well.","Bring the mixture to a boil, then reduce the heat to low. Cover the pot with the lid and let the rice simmer for about 15–20 minutes, or until all the liquid is absorbed and the rice is cooked and fluffy.","Remove the pot from the heat and let the rice rest for a few minutes before fluffing it with a fork.","Garnish with chopped fresh parsley or cilantro before serving."],"x":["For a richer taste, you can use chicken broth instead of vegetable broth.","You can add some diced vegetables like carrots or peas to the rice for extra flavor and color.","Leftover rice can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days. Reheat before serving.","Liberian butter rice complements various proteins and vegetables, making it a versatile and tasty addition to your meals."],"desc":"Liberian butter rice is a flavorful and comforting dish that is a popular staple in Liberian cuisine. Made with aromatic ingredients and cooked in butter, this rice dish has a rich and delicious taste that pairs well with a variety of proteins and vegetables. It's a versatile side dish that can be s","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Butter_Rice","i":"wb-en-2535","on":"Liberian Butter Rice","og":["2 cups long-grain rice","4 cups chicken broth (or vegetable broth)","1 onion, finely chopped","2 cloves of garlic, minced","2 tablespoons butter","1 bay leaf","Salt, to taste","Black pepper, to taste","Fresh parsley or cilantro, chopped (for garnish)"]},{"n":"Liberianische Maniokblattsuppe","c":"suppen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["910 g Maniokblätter, frisch oder tiefgekühlt","450 g Fleisch (Rind, Hähnchen oder Fisch), in mundgerechte Stücke geschnitten","1 Zwiebel, fein gehackt","2–3 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","1 Stück Ingwer, gerieben","2–3 Scotch-Bonnet-Chilis, fein gehackt","2 EL Palmöl","4–5 Tassen Hühnerbrühe oder Wasser","1 Süßkartoffel, geschält und gewürfelt","1 Kochbanane, geschält und in Scheiben geschnitten","Salz, nach Geschmack","gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer, nach Geschmack"],"s":["If using fresh cassava leaves, wash them thoroughly and remove any tough stems. If using frozen cassava leaves, thaw them according to the package instructions.","In a large pot, heat the palm oil over medium heat.","Add the chopped onion, minced garlic, and grated ginger to the pot. Sauté until the onion becomes translucent and fragrant.","Stir in the chopped Scotch bonnet peppers and cook for a few minutes to release the flavors.","Add the meat to the pot and cook until it is browned on all sides.","Pour in the chicken broth or water and bring the mixture to a simmer. Cover the pot and let the meat cook for about 20–25 minutes, or until it is tender.","Add the diced sweet potato and sliced plantain to the pot. Let the soup simmer for another 10–15 minutes, or until the vegetables are cooked through.","Stir in the cassava leaves and let the soup simmer for an additional 45 minutes to 1 hour, stirring occasionally to prevent sticking.","Season the soup with salt and ground black pepper to taste. Adjust the seasoning according to your preference.","Remove the pot from the heat and let the soup rest for a few minutes before serving."],"x":["Cassava leaves can be found in African or international grocery stores. If unavailable, you can substitute with spinach or other leafy greens, but the taste will be different.","The longer the cassava leaf soup cooks, the more flavorful it becomes. It is traditionally simmered for several hours to develop its rich taste.","This soup is often served with rice or fufu, a starchy side dish made from cassava, plantains, or other ingredients.","Cassava leaves are a good source of vitamins A and C, as well as calcium and iron.","The meat and vegetables in the soup provide protein, vitamins, and minerals."],"desc":"Liberian cassava leaf soup is a delicious and hearty dish that is widely enjoyed in Liberia. Made with cassava leaves, meat, and an assortment of vegetables, this soup is a flavorful and nutritious meal that is perfect for gatherings and special occasions.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Cassava_Leaf_Soup","i":"wb-en-2536","on":"Liberian Cassava Leaf Soup","og":["2 pounds cassava leaves, fresh or frozen","1 pound meat (beef, chicken, or fish), cut into bite-sized pieces","1 onion, finely chopped","2–3 cloves of garlic, minced","1 piece of ginger, grated","2–3 Scotch bonnet chile peppers, finely chopped","2 tablespoons palm oil","4–5 cups chicken broth or water","1 sweet potato, peeled and diced","1 plantain, peeled and sliced","Salt, to taste","Ground black pepper, to taste"]},{"n":"Liberianische Hähnchensoße","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1,35 kg Hähnchen, in mittelgroße Stücke geschnitten","Salz, nach Geschmack","gemahlener roter oder schwarzer Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","2 EL Hühnerbrühwürfel","2 mittelgroße Zwiebeln, sauber gehackt","4 frische Tomaten","4 mittelgroße rote Paprika","5 Zehen Knoblauch","½ Tasse Basilikum und Petersilie","½ Tasse Pflanzenöl","2 EL Tomatenmark","910 g beliebiges getrocknetes Fischsteak, geputzt","geräuchertes Paprikapulver (optional)","1 TL gemahlener Ingwer","1 TL Cayennepfeffer","2 mittelgroße Habanero-Chili, sauber gehackt","450 g große Garnelen, geputzt"],"s":["In a medium-size saucepan, boil the chicken with salt, pepper, some chopped onions, and 1 tablespoon of the chicken bouillon. Let them cook until tender—the cooking time varies according to the chicken.","Remove the chicken to a bowl, reserving the stock.","In a blender, purée the tomatoes, red bell pepper, onions, garlic, basil, and parsley.","Add ½ cup oil to a pot, then add the blended mixture followed by the tomato paste. Allow it to cook for about 15 minutes, stirring the pot frequently as the sauce simmers.f","Add the reserved chicken broth, then the chicken, dried fish, smoked paprika, ginger powder, cayenne pepper, and habanero pepper. Let simmer for about 10 minutes.","Add the shrimp and cook for about 5 minutes.","Adjust the stew with water, broth, and/or bouillon cubes if needed.","Enjoy with any complimentary dish of your choice."],"x":["It is not compulsory to use fish when preparing this stew.","You can use any variety of tomatoes such as canned tomatoes, fresh tomatoes, or Roma tomatoes.","Use any range of vegetables such as carrot, green beans.","You can also make use of extra spices such as curry powder, thyme, and bay leaves as desired."],"desc":"Liberian chicken gravy is a delicious African stew. A lot of oil is required to cook most African stews, but when it comes to this dish, you don't need so much.","img":"Chicken Gravy 02.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Chicken_Gravy","i":"wb-en-2537","im":["d/d2/Chicken_Gravy_02.jpg/960px-Chicken_Gravy_02.jpg","Nandhinikandhasamy","CC BY-SA 4.0","Chicken Gravy 02.jpg","r"],"on":"Liberian Chicken Gravy","og":["3 lb chicken, cut into medium pieces","Salt to taste","Ground red or black pepper to taste","2 tablespoons chicken bouillon cube","2 medium-size onions, neatly chopped","4 fresh tomatoes","4 medium-size red bell pepper","5 cloves of garlic","½ cup basil and parsley","½ cup vegetable oil","2 tablespoons tomato paste","2 lb any type of dried fish steak of your choice, cleaned","Smoked paprika (optional)","1 teaspoon ginger powder","1 teaspoon cayenne pepper","2 medium-size habanero pepper, neatly chopped","1 pound large shrimp, cleaned"]},{"n":"Liberianischer Blattkohleintopf","c":"suppen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 EL Pflanzenöl","1 Zwiebel, fein gehackt","2 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","1 Tomate, gewürfelt","1 rote Paprika, gewürfelt","1 grüne Paprika, gewürfelt","1 TL Paprikapulver","½ TL gemahlener Cayennepfeffer (optional, für Schärfe)","1 Bund frischer Blattkohl, gewaschen und gehackt","Salz, nach Geschmack","2 Tassen Gemüsebrühe (oder Wasser)"],"s":["In a large pot, heat the vegetable oil over medium heat.","Add the chopped onion and minced garlic to the pot. Sauté until the onion becomes translucent and the garlic becomes fragrant.","Stir in the diced tomato, red bell pepper, and green bell pepper. Cook for a few minutes until the vegetables are softened.","Add the chopped collard greens to the pot and mix well with the sautéed vegetables.","Season the stew with ground paprika, ground cayenne pepper (if using), and salt to taste. Stir to coat the collard greens and vegetables with the spices.","Pour in the vegetable broth (or water) to the pot, ensuring that the collard greens are well covered.","Cover the pot and let the stew simmer on low heat for about 30–40 minutes, or until the collard greens are tender and flavorful.","Taste and adjust the seasoning if needed, adding more salt or spices according to your preference.","Serve as a main dish with rice or bread, and enjoy."],"x":["You can add other vegetables like carrots or sweet potatoes to the stew for extra flavor and nutrition.","For a richer taste, you can add some coconut milk to the stew during cooking.","Leftover stew can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days. Reheat before serving."],"desc":"Liberian collard green stew is a hearty and flavorful dish that is a staple in Liberian cuisine. Made with tender collard greens and a rich tomato-based sauce, this stew is both nutritious and delicious. It can be served as a main course with rice or bread, and it's perfect for sharing with family a","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Collard_Greens_Stew","i":"wb-en-2538","on":"Liberian Collard Greens Stew","og":["2 tablespoons vegetable oil","1 onion, finely chopped","2 cloves of garlic, minced","1 tomato, diced","1 red bell pepper, diced","1 green bell pepper, diced","1 teaspoon ground paprika","½ teaspoon ground cayenne pepper (optional, for heat)","1 bunch of fresh collard greens, washed and chopped","Salt, to taste","2 cups vegetable broth (or water)"]},{"n":"Liberianische Bohnen Torborgee","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1,35 kg getrocknete Bohnen","4 Tassen Gemüsebrühe","2 mittelgroße Zwiebeln, sauber gehackt","1 Tasse Wasser","620 g Seitan","2 Habanero-Chili, sauber gehackt","1 Tasse Palmöl","½ TL Natron (2 Prisen), in warmem Wasser aufgelöst","1 TL Salz, oder nach Geschmack"],"s":["Pick over the beans and remove any unwanted ones. You may soak them overnight to reduce the cooking period. Place beans in a pot and cover with water. Boil until tender, adding water if needed.","Drain and mash the beans to your preferred consistency.","Bring the vegetable broth to a boil in a separate pot. Stir in the mashed beans along with the onions, 1 cup water, seitan, and habanero pepper. Boil for about 20–25 minutes.","Stir in the palm oil. Reduce to low heat and simmer for about 5 minutes, stirring to prevent burning.","Stir in the potash and salt to taste.","Remove from the heat and let rest for about 5 minutes.","Enjoy with any complimentary dish of your choice such as bread, rice, or garri."],"x":["If you are using baking soda, the stew will foam.","You can prepare the torborgee with any type of beans, including kidney beans, pinto beans and cranberry beans."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Country_Beans_Torborgee","i":"wb-en-2539","on":"Liberian Country Beans Torborgee","og":["48 oz dried beans","4 cups vegetable broth","2 medium size onions, neatly chopped","1 cup water","22 oz seitan","2 habanero pepper, neatly chopped","1 cup palm oil","½ teaspoon country soda or 2 pinches of baking soda, dissolved in warm water","1 teaspoon of salt or to taste"]},{"n":"Liberianischer Auberginen-Eintopf","c":"suppen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 EL Palmöl","1 Zwiebel, fein gehackt","2 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","450 g Fleisch (Rind, Hähnchen oder Ziege), in Stücke geschnitten, oder Fisch (Tilapia oder Wels), geputzt und ausgenommen","2 Tassen Hühnerbrühe oder Wasser","1 Tomate, gewürfelt","1 Paprikaschote, gewürfelt","1 scharfe Chili, gehackt (optional, für Schärfe)","1 TL gemahlener Pfeffer","2 große Auberginen, geschält und gewürfelt","Salz, nach Geschmack"],"s":["In a large pot, heat the palm oil over medium heat.","Add the chopped onions and minced garlic to the pot. Sauté until the onions are soft and translucent.","If using meat, add the meat pieces to the pot and cook until they are browned on all sides.","Pour in the chicken broth or water and bring the mixture to a simmer.","Add the diced tomato, bell pepper, and chopped hot pepper (if using) to the pot. Stir well to combine with the other ingredients.","Gently add the diced eggplant to the pot and stir to incorporate with the other ingredients.","Season the stew with ground pepper and salt to taste. Adjust the seasoning according to your preference.","Let the stew simmer for about 20–25 minutes or until the eggplant is tender and cooked through.","Stir occasionally during cooking to prevent sticking and to ensure even cooking.","Remove the pot from the heat and let the stew rest for a few minutes before serving."],"x":["You can add other vegetables like carrots, okra, or spinach to the stew for added nutrition and flavor.","If using fish, be sure to remove any bones before adding it to the stew.","This stew can be made with any type of meat or fish according to your preference.","Liberian eggplant stew can be enjoyed as a standalone dish or served with rice, fufu, or bread.","Eggplant is a low-calorie vegetable and is a good source of fiber, vitamins, and minerals."],"desc":"Liberian eggplant stew is a delectable dish that highlights the unique flavors of eggplant in Liberian cuisine. This hearty stew is made with tender eggplant, savory meat or fish, and a medley of aromatic spices. It is a popular and comforting meal in Liberia, often served with rice or fufu.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Eggplant_Stew","i":"wb-en-2540","on":"Liberian Eggplant Stew","og":["2 tablespoons palm oil","1 onion, finely chopped","2 cloves of garlic, minced","1 pound meat (beef, chicken, or goat), cut into pieces, or fish (tilapia or catfish), cleaned and gutted","2 cups chicken broth or water","1 tomato, diced","1 bell pepper, diced","1 hot pepper, chopped (optional, for heat)","1 teaspoon ground pepper","2 large eggplants, peeled and diced","Salt, to taste"]},{"n":"Liberianischer gebratener Fisch","c":"fisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["910 g frischer Fisch (Tilapia, Snapper oder ein anderer festfleischiger weißer Fisch)","1 Tasse Weizenmehl","1 TL Salz","½ TL gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","½ TL Paprikapulver","½ TL Knoblauchpulver","½ TL Zwiebelpulver","½ TL Cayennepfeffer (optional)","½ Tasse Buttermilch","Pflanzenöl, zum Braten"],"s":["Clean and gut the fish, removing any scales and innards. Rinse the fish thoroughly under cold running water and pat them dry with paper towels.","In a large bowl, mix the all-purpose flour, salt, ground black pepper, paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, and cayenne pepper (if using).","Pour the buttermilk into another bowl.","Dip each fish into the buttermilk, allowing any excess to drip off, and then coat the fish with the seasoned flour mixture, pressing the flour onto the fish to adhere.","Heat about 1 inch of vegetable oil in a deep frying pan or pot over medium-high heat. To test if the oil is hot enough, drop a small piece of bread into the oil; it should sizzle and turn golden brown.","Carefully place the coated fish in the hot oil, working in batches if necessary to avoid overcrowding the pan.","Fry the fish for about 3–4 minutes per side, or until they are golden brown and cooked through. Use tongs or a slotted spoon to flip the fish during frying.","Remove the fried fish from the oil and place them on a plate lined with paper towels to drain any excess oil.","Serve the fish hot, with your favorite side dishes like plantains, rice, or salad."],"x":["You can adjust the level of spiciness by increasing or decreasing the amount of cayenne pepper in the seasoning mixture.","For a gluten-free version, you can use cornmeal or rice flour instead of all-purpose flour.","Make sure the oil is hot enough before frying to ensure that the fish comes out crispy and not greasy.","Leftover fried fish can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 2 days. To reheat, place the fish in the oven at 350°F (175°C) for a few minutes until warmed through.","Fish is a rich source of protein and essential omega-3 fatty acids."],"desc":"Liberian fried fish is a popular and delicious dish in Liberia. Made with fresh fish and a flavorful spice blend, this dish is crispy on the outside and tender on the inside, making it a delightful meal for seafood lovers.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Fried_Fish","i":"wb-en-2541","on":"Liberian Fried Fish","og":["2 pounds fresh fish (tilapia, snapper, or any firm white fish)","1 cup all-purpose flour","1 teaspoon salt","½ teaspoon ground black pepper","½ teaspoon paprika","½ teaspoon garlic powder","½ teaspoon onion powder","½ teaspoon cayenne pepper (optional)","½ cup buttermilk","Vegetable oil, for frying"]},{"n":"Liberianische gebratene Kochbananen mit Bohnen","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["3 reife Kochbananen","Pflanzenöl, zum Braten","1 Zwiebel, fein gehackt","2 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","1 Tasse gekochte Bohnen (Augenbohnen oder Kidneybohnen)","1 TL Paprikapulver","½ TL gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","Salz, nach Geschmack"],"s":["Peel the ripe plantains and cut them into diagonal slices, about ½ inch thick.","In a large frying pan, heat vegetable oil over medium-high heat.","Fry the plantain slices in batches until they are golden brown and crispy on both sides. Use a slotted spoon to transfer the fried plantains to a plate lined with paper towels to drain any excess oil.","In the same frying pan, sauté the chopped onion and minced garlic until they become translucent and fragrant.","Add the cooked beans to the pan and mix well with the onions and garlic.","Season the beans with ground paprika, ground black pepper, and salt to taste. Stir to coat the beans evenly with the spices.","Cook the bean mixture for a few minutes until it is heated through.","Serve the fried plantains alongside the seasoned beans and enjoy this delightful and flavorful Liberian dish."],"x":["Adjust the seasoning according to your taste preferences. You can add other spices like cayenne pepper or thyme for extra flavor.","If you prefer a sweeter taste, you can sprinkle a little brown sugar on the fried plantains before serving.","This dish can be served as a main course with rice or as a side dish with grilled or fried fish or meat.","Leftover fried plantains and beans can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 2 days. Reheat before serving.","Beans are rich in protein, dietary fiber, and various nutrients such as iron and folate."],"desc":"Liberian fried plantains with beans is a popular and delicious dish in Liberia. It combines the sweet and savory flavors of ripe plantains with the heartiness of cooked beans. This dish can be served as a main course or as a side dish, and it's perfect for any occasion.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Fried_Plantains_with_Beans","i":"wb-en-2542","on":"Liberian Fried Plantains with Beans","og":["3 ripe plantains","Vegetable oil, for frying","1 onion, finely chopped","2 cloves of garlic, minced","1 cup cooked beans (black-eyed peas or kidney beans)","1 teaspoon ground paprika","½ teaspoon ground black pepper","Salt, to taste"]},{"n":"Liberianische frittierte Süßkartoffelbällchen","c":"snacks","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 große Süßkartoffeln, gekocht und zerdrückt","1 Ei, leicht verquirlt","¼ Tasse Weizenmehl","1 TL Backpulver","½ TL Salz","¼ TL schwarzer Pfeffer","¼ TL gemahlener Zimt","¼ TL gemahlene Muskatnuss","¼ TL Gewürznelken","Pflanzenöl, zum Braten"],"s":["In a large mixing bowl, combine the mashed sweet potatoes with the beaten egg.","In a separate bowl, whisk together the all-purpose flour, baking powder, salt, black pepper, ground cinnamon, ground nutmeg, and cloves.","Gradually add the dry ingredients to the sweet potato mixture, stirring until well combined.","Heat vegetable oil in a large pot or deep-fryer to 350°F (175°C).","Using a spoon or cookie scoop, carefully drop spoonfuls of the sweet potato mixture into the hot oil.","Fry the sweet potato puffs in batches for about 3–4 minutes or until they are golden brown and crispy.","Remove the fried puffs from the oil using a slotted spoon, and place them on a plate lined with paper towels to drain any excess oil.","Serve warm as a snack or appetizer."],"x":["You can adjust the seasoning according to your taste preferences. Add more spices or herbs for a bolder flavor.","These sweet potato puffs can be served with your favorite dipping sauce, such as ketchup or aioli.","Leftover sweet potato puffs can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days. Reheat them in the oven or microwave before serving.","Sweet potatoes are a good source of vitamins, minerals, and fiber."],"desc":"Liberian fried sweet potato puffs are delightful and flavorful snacks that make a perfect treat for any occasion. Made with mashed sweet potatoes, these puffs are seasoned with a blend of spices and herbs, giving them a unique taste that will keep you coming back for more. They are fried to golden p","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Fried_Sweet_Potato_Puffs","i":"wb-en-2543","on":"Liberian Fried Sweet Potato Puffs","og":["2 large sweet potatoes, boiled and mashed","1 egg, lightly beaten","¼ cup all-purpose flour","1 teaspoon baking powder","½ teaspoon salt","¼ teaspoon black pepper","¼ teaspoon ground cinnamon","¼ teaspoon ground nutmeg","¼ teaspoon cloves","Vegetable oil, for frying"]},{"n":"Liberianischer Fufu","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["910 g Maniok, Yamswurzeln, oder Kochbananen","Wasser"],"s":["Peel and cut the cassava, yams, or plantains into chunks, and place them in a large pot.","Add enough water to cover the vegetables, and bring the pot to a boil over high heat.","Reduce the heat to medium and let the vegetables simmer until they are tender and easily pierced with a fork.","Drain the water from the cooked vegetables, and transfer them to a large bowl.","Use a potato masher, or mortar and pestle to pound the vegetables into a smooth, thick paste. You can also use a stand mixer or food processor for this step.","Continue pounding and kneading the mixture until it forms a smooth and stretchy dough-like consistency. This process may take some time and effort, but it is essential for achieving the right texture.","Once the fufu has reached the desired consistency, shape it into small balls or serve it as a large mound on a serving platter.","Serve with various soups and stews. It can be used as a utensil to scoop up the soup or stew."],"x":["To enhance the flavor, you can add a pinch of salt or other seasonings to the cooked vegetables before pounding.","Some people prefer their fufu to be softer, while others prefer it to be firmer. Adjust the amount of pounding and kneading to achieve your desired texture.","Leftover fufu can be stored in the refrigerator for up to 2 days. To reheat, steam it or place it in a microwave for a few minutes until warmed through.","Fufu is naturally gluten-free and can be enjoyed by those with gluten sensitivities."],"desc":"Liberian fufu is a staple food in Liberia and many other West African countries. It is made from starchy vegetables like cassava, yams, or plantains, which are boiled, pounded, and formed into a smooth, dough-like consistency. Fufu is typically served with various soups and stews, making it a versat","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Fufu","i":"wb-en-2544","im":["1/1f/Wrapped_fufu.jpg/330px-Wrapped_fufu.jpg","daSupremo","CC BY-SA 4.0","Wrapped fufu.jpg","w"],"on":"Liberian Fufu","og":["2 pounds cassava, yams, or plantains","Water"]},{"n":"Liberianischer Jollof-Reis","c":"beilagen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 große Hähnchenbrüste, gewürfelt","Salz, nach Geschmack","Chilipulver, nach Geschmack","1 Tasse Pflanzenöl","1 große milde Zwiebeln, sauber gehackt","910 g gekochtes Schweine- oder Rindfleisch, gewürfelt","2 Beutel TK-Mischgemüse (z. B. Zuckermais, grüne Bohnen usw.), aufgetaut und abgetropft","2 mittelgroße Dosen Tomatenmark","4 Hühnerbrühwürfel, zerdrückt","1,35 kg gedämpfte Garnelen (optional)","2 Tassen gewürfelte Paprika","5 Tassen Reis, abgespült"],"s":["Season the chicken with salt and red pepper. Leave it to stand for about 5 minutes.","In a frying pan, brown the chicken in hot vegetable oil. Then transfer the chicken to a large pot.","In the same frying pan, add the onions and beef or pork. Fry lightly and add to the pot with the chicken.","Combine the mixed vegetables, tomato paste, bouillon cubes, salt to taste, shrimp, and bell pepper. Leave to simmer for about 10 minutes.","Add the rice, stir well, and cook over low heat for about 40–45 minutes.","Serve hot."],"x":["Ingredients for this recipe vary between people. Some people might use shrimp, curry powder, or even thyme to prepare it—it just depends on what you like and what you want to see in your food.","For the vegetables you can make use of any okay by you (e.g. spring onions, red beans, etc)"],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Jollof_Rice","i":"wb-en-2545","im":["0/0a/Jollof_Rice_with_Stew.jpg/960px-Jollof_Rice_with_Stew.jpg","Noahalorwu","CC BY-SA 4.0","Jollof Rice with Stew.jpg","w"],"on":"Liberian Jollof Rice","og":["2 large chicken breasts, cut into cubes","Salt to taste","Chile powder to taste","1 cup vegetable oil","1 large sweet onions, neatly chopped","2 pounds boiled pork or beef, cut into cubes","2 bags of frozen mixed vegetables (such as sweet corn, string beans, etc), thawed and drained","2 medium-size cans of tomato paste","4 chicken bouillon cubes, crushed","3 pounds steamed shrimp (optional)","2 cups diced bell pepper","5 cups rice, rinsed"]},{"n":"Liberianischer Palmöleintopf","c":"suppen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse Palmöl","1 Zwiebel, fein gehackt","2 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","1 grüne Paprika, gewürfelt","1 rote Paprika, gewürfelt","1 Scotch-Bonnet-Chilischote, fein gehackt (optional, für Schärfe)","450 g Hähnchen, in Stücke geschnitten","2 Tassen Hühnerbrühe","450 g Fisch, in Steaks oder Filets geschnitten","230 g Okra, in Scheiben geschnitten","1 Aubergine, gewürfelt","Salz, nach Geschmack","gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer, nach Geschmack"],"s":["In a large pot, heat the palm oil over medium heat.","Add the chopped onion and minced garlic to the pot. Sauté until the onion becomes translucent and fragrant.","Stir in the diced green and red bell peppers and chopped Scotch bonnet pepper (if using). Cook for a few minutes until the peppers start to soften.","Add the chicken pieces to the pot and cook until they are lightly browned on all sides.","Pour in the chicken broth and bring the mixture to a simmer. Cover the pot and let the chicken cook for about 20–25 minutes, or until it is fully cooked and tender.","Once the chicken is cooked, add the fish steaks or fillets to the pot and let them simmer in the stew for an additional 5–10 minutes, or until they are cooked through.","Stir in the sliced okra and diced eggplant. Let the stew simmer for another 5–7 minutes, or until the vegetables are tender.","Season the stew with salt and ground black pepper to taste. Adjust the seasoning according to your preference.","Remove the pot from the heat and let the stew rest for a few minutes before serving."],"x":["Palm oil gives the stew its distinctive flavor and vibrant red color. It is a traditional ingredient in Liberian cuisine and can be found in specialty African grocery stores.","For a spicier version, you can add more Scotch bonnet pepper or a pinch of cayenne pepper to the stew.","This stew is traditionally served with rice or fufu, a starchy side dish made from cassava or other root vegetables."],"desc":"Liberian palm oil stew is a delicious and hearty dish from Liberia. Made with a rich combination of palm oil, vegetables, and protein, this stew is a staple in Liberian cuisine and is often served with rice or fufu.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Palm_Oil_Stew","i":"wb-en-2546","on":"Liberian Palm Oil Stew","og":["1 cup palm oil","1 onion, finely chopped","2 cloves of garlic, minced","1 green bell pepper, diced","1 red bell pepper, diced","1 Scotch bonnet chile pepper, finely chopped (optional, for spiciness)","1 pound chicken, cut into pieces","2 cups chicken broth","1 pound fish, cut into steaks or fillets","½ pound okra, sliced","1 eggplant, diced","Salt, to taste","Ground black pepper, to taste"]},{"n":"Liberianische Pepper Soup","c":"suppen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 EL Palmöl","1 Zwiebel, fein gehackt","2 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","1 Ingwer, gerieben","2 Scotch-Bonnet-Chilis, fein gehackt","1 Lorbeerblatt","450 g Hähnchen, in Stücke geschnitten","4–5 Tassen Hühnerbrühe","450 g Fisch, in Steaks oder Filets geschnitten","1 Kochbanane, geschält und in Scheiben geschnitten","1 Möhre, in Scheiben geschnitten","Salz, nach Geschmack","gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer, nach Geschmack"],"s":["In a large pot, heat the palm oil over medium heat.","Add the chopped onion, minced garlic, and grated ginger to the pot. Sauté until the onion becomes translucent and fragrant.","Stir in the chopped Scotch bonnet peppers and bay leaf. Cook for a few minutes to release the flavors.","Add the chicken pieces to the pot and cook until they are lightly browned on all sides.","Pour in the chicken broth and bring the mixture to a simmer. Cover the pot and let the chicken cook for about 20–25 minutes, or until it is fully cooked and tender.","Once the chicken is cooked, add the fish steaks or fillets to the pot and let them simmer in the soup for an additional 5–10 minutes, or until they are cooked through.","Stir in the sliced plantain and carrot. Let the soup simmer for another 5–7 minutes, or until the vegetables are tender.","Season the soup with salt and ground black pepper to taste. Adjust the seasoning according to your preference and desired level of spiciness.","Remove the pot from the heat and let the soup rest for a few minutes before serving."],"x":["Liberian pepper soup is traditionally served with rice, fufu, or other starchy side dishes.","For a milder version, you can reduce the amount of Scotch bonnet peppers used or remove the seeds before chopping them.","You can also add other vegetables such as bell peppers, spinach, or cabbage to the soup for added flavor and nutrition."],"desc":"Liberian pepper soup is a flavorful and spicy soup from Liberia. It is a popular dish that is often enjoyed as a warming and comforting meal, especially during cold weather or when feeling under the weather.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Pepper_Soup","i":"wb-en-2547","im":["0/00/Assorted_meat_pepper_soup_at_Lagos_Island.jpg/960px-Assorted_meat_pepper_soup_at_Lagos_Island.jpg","bob walker","CC BY-SA 2.0","Assorted meat pepper soup at Lagos Island.jpg","w"],"on":"Liberian Pepper Soup","og":["2 tablespoons palm oil","1 onion, finely chopped","2 cloves of garlic, minced","1 ginger, grated","2 Scotch bonnet chile peppers, finely chopped","1 bay leaf","1 pound chicken, cut into pieces","4–5 cups chicken broth","1 pound fish, cut into steaks or fillets","1 plantain, peeled and sliced","1 carrot, sliced","Salt to taste","Ground black pepper, to taste"]},{"n":"Liberianische Kartoffelblätter","c":"beilagen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["3 große Bund Süßkartoffelblätter (siehe Hinweise)","Pflanzenöl","2 große Zwiebeln, sauber gehackt","910 g Fleisch, in mittelgroße Würfel geschnitten","Würzsalz, nach Geschmack","Zwiebelpulver, nach Geschmack","Hühnerbrühwürfel, zerdrückt","gemahlener roter oder schwarzer Pfeffer, nach Geschmack"],"s":["Wash the potato greens very well, and remove the leaves from the stems. Chop the leaves into small pieces and set aside.","Heat a few tablespoons of oil in a large pot. Add the onions and meat, and cook until almost done. Remove from the pot and set aside.","Add the potato greens, and fry for about 15 minutes or until tender. Stir frequently to prevent burning.","Add enough water to cover the greens, and season to taste with salt, onion powder, bouillon cubes, and ground pepper.","Cook over medium heat until all the water is gone, stirring frequently.","Remove from the heat and serve."],"x":["Do not eat white potato greens—they are toxic. Sweet potato greens, however, are safe. You can get potato greens from the market or from local farmers.","If desired, add a pinch of baking soda to the greens when cooking to keep their green color."],"desc":"This is an easy and delicious dish popularly cooked in West Africa.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liberian_Potato_Greens","i":"wb-en-2548","on":"Liberian Potato Greens","og":["3 large bunches of sweet potato greens (see notes)","Vegetable oil","2 big onions, neatly chopped","2 lbs meat, cut into medium cubes","Seasoned salt to taste","Onion powder to taste","Chicken bouillon cubes, crushed","Ground red or black pepper to taste"]},{"n":"Leichte, lockere Pfannkuchen","c":"kuchen","k":"USA","p":8,"t":10,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse gebleichtes Weizenmehl","2 TL Zucker","½ TL Salz","½ TL Backpulver","¼ TL Natron","¾ Tasse Buttermilch","¼ Tasse Milch","1 großes Ei","2 EL ungesalzene Butter, geschmolzen","1 TL Vanilleextrakt","Pflanzenöl zum Einpinseln der Platte"],"s":["Heat a large non-stick skillet or griddle over low heat while preparing ingredients.","Mix flour, sugar, salt, baking powder, and baking soda in medium bowl.","Microwave buttermilk and milk in a 2-cup Pyrex measuring cup until room temperature (20–30 seconds).","Whisk in egg, butter, and vanilla.","Add wet ingredients to dry ingredients and whisk until just mixed.","Return batter to measuring cup, stirring in 1–2 teaspoons water if necessary to make a thick but pourable batter.","Increase heat to medium and generously brush skillet or griddle with oil.","When oil starts to spider, but before it starts to smoke, ladle in batter about ¼ cup at a time to make pancakes. Work in batches, if necessary, to avoid overcrowding.","When pancake bottoms are golden brown and tops start to bubble (2–3 minutes), flip pancakes.","Cook until pancakes are golden brown on remaining side.","Repeat, brushing skillet or griddle with oil between batches of pancakes.","Serve hot."],"x":["Use bleached flour to make a tender pancake.","If using salted butter, reduce salt to ¼ teaspoon.","Pancake batter should pour, not glug! On the other hand, runny batter makes thin, oddly-shaped pancakes that frequently collide on the griddle. Stir in a touch more flour into thin batter. For batter that's too thick, whisk in water a teaspoon at a time.","This recipe easily doubles for a crowd."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Light_Fluffy_Pancakes","i":"wb-en-2549","on":"Light Fluffy Pancakes","og":["1 cup all-purpose bleached flour","2 teaspoons sugar","½ teaspoon salt","½ teaspoon baking powder","¼ teaspoon baking soda","¾ cup buttermilk","¼ cup milk","1 large egg","2 tablespoon unsalted butter, melted","1 teaspoon vanilla extract","Vegetable oil for brushing griddle"]},{"n":"Limetten-Mascarpone-Käsekuchen","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":8,"t":60,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["500 g Mascarpone oder Frischkäse","4 Limetten (am besten unbehandelt)","200 g Ingwerkekse, zerdrückt oder in der Küchenmaschine gemahlen","50 g Butter","Puderzucker, nach Geschmack"],"s":["Melt the butter in a saucepan and add the biscuit crumbs. Press firmly into a 20 cm diameter loose-bottomed pan and put aside.","Put the mascarpone in a bowl and beat until firm.","Add the juice of 3 of the limes and the grated or zested rind of all 4 into the cheese. Stir, adding icing sugar to taste.","Spread the cheese mixture over the biscuit base and chill for an hour or so before serving."],"x":["Feel free to serve with grated chocolate."],"desc":"Lime and mascarpone cheesecake is a very creamy and delightfully simple dessert. It can be prepared ahead of time and stored in the fridge. No cooking is required.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lime_and_Mascarpone_Cheesecake","i":"wb-en-2550","im":["e/ea/Baked_cheesecake_with_raspberries_and_blueberries.jpg/960px-Baked_cheesecake_with_raspberries_and_blueberries.jpg","zingyyellow","CC BY 2.0","Baked cheesecake with raspberries and blueberries.jpg","w"],"on":"Lime and Mascarpone Cheesecake","og":["500 g mascarpone cheese or plain cream cheese","4 limes (preferably unwaxed)","200 g ginger nut biscuits, crushed or ground in a food processor","50 g butter","Icing sugar to taste"]},{"n":"Limoncello","c":"getraenke","k":"Italien","p":45,"t":20,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["15 Zitronen","4 Tassen feiner Zucker","2 Flaschen Wodka (50 % Vol., je 0,75 l) (insgesamt 1,5 l)","5 Tassen Wasser"],"s":["Wash the lemons with a vegetable brush and hot water to remove any residue of pesticides or wax. Carefully zest the lemons with a zester or vegetable peeler so there is no white pith on the peel.","In a 1-gallon glass jar, combine half the vodka and the lemon zest. Cover the jar and let sit at room temperature for at least 10 days, and up to 40 days in a cool dark place.","In a large saucepan, combine the sugar and water and cook until thickened (about 5–7 minutes). Let the syrup cool before adding it to the limoncello mixture. Add the additional fifth of vodka. Allow to rest for another 10–40 days.","After the rest period, strain and bottle, discarding the lemon zest. Keep in the freezer until ready to serve."],"x":["Wondering what to do with the lemons after you've zested them? Try making lemonade, ginger beer, or sima."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Limoncello","i":"wb-en-2551","im":["f/fb/Homemade_limoncello.jpg/500px-Homemade_limoncello.jpg","Alessio Damato","CC BY-SA 3.0","Homemade limoncello.jpg","c"],"og":["15 lemons","4 cups superfine sugar","2 fifths (1.5 litres total) 100 proof vodka","5 cups water"]},{"n":"Limoncello II","c":"getraenke","k":"","p":22,"t":20,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["5–7 unbehandelte Zitronen","300 ml Weingeist mit 95 % Vol.","700 ml Wasser","500 ml Zucker"],"s":["Peel lemons, avoiding or removing the bitter white pith.","Combine lemon peel and alcohol in the mason jar.","Cover the jar and let infuse for 20 days.","After infusion is complete, create a simple syrup by boiling the water stirring in the sugar until dissolved.","Allow syrup to cool completely, then strain the infused alcohol into it. Stir well to combine.","Bottle the limoncello or return to the jar for storage."],"x":["Feel free to scale the recipe up or down, and adjust the sugar to the sweetness you like, but the ABV should remain somewhere around 28–30%."],"desc":"This is an alternative limoncello recipe.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Limoncello_II","i":"wb-en-2552","og":["5–7 unwaxed lemons","300 ml 95% ABV grain alcohol","700 ml water","500 ml sugar"]},{"n":"Linguine Primavera nach mediterraner Art","c":"veggie","k":"Italien","p":2,"t":30,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["1 EL Olivenöl","2 EL frisch gehackter Knoblauch","¼ Tasse geröstete rote Paprika, in feine Streifen geschnitten","¼ Tasse getrocknete Tomaten, in feine Streifen geschnitten","¼ Tasse entsteinte Kalamata-Oliven","1 Artischockenherz (aus der Dose geht auch), in 8 Stücke geschnitten","½ Tasse trockener Weißwein","½ Tasse Hühnerbrühe","½ TL getrockneter Oregano","½ TL getrocknetes Basilikum","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","Knoblauchgranulat, nach Geschmack","½ Tasse frische Brokkoliröschen","230 g Linguine, al dente gekocht und abgetropft","etwa ¼ Tasse zerbröckelter Feta zum Garnieren","1–2 EL gehackte Petersilie zum Garnieren"],"s":["Heat oil in a sauté pan over high heat.","Add garlic, and sauté until it just begins to brown (about 1 minute). Be careful not to burn it.","Stir in red peppers, sun-dried tomatoes, olives, and artichoke heart.","Add white wine, chicken broth, oregano and basil, and bring to a boil.","Season to taste with salt, pepper and granulated garlic.","Add broccoli and cook just until bright green and tender (1–2 minutes).","Add pasta and toss to combine.","Garnish with crumbled feta cheese and chopped parsley, and serve hot."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Linguine_Primavera_Mediterranean","i":"wb-en-2553","on":"Linguine Primavera Mediterranean","og":["1 tablespoon olive oil","2 tablespoons freshly-minced garlic","¼ cup roasted red peppers, julienned","¼ cup sun-dried tomatoes, julienned","¼ cup pitted Kalamata olives","1 artichoke heart (canned is fine), cut into 8 pieces","½ cup dry white wine","½ cup chicken broth","½ teaspoon dried oregano","½ teaspoon dried basil","Salt to taste","Pepper to taste","Granulated garlic, to taste","½ cup fresh broccoli florets","½ pound linguine, cooked al dente and drained","About ¼ cup crumbled feta cheese for garnish","1–2 tablespoons chopped parsley for garnish"]},{"n":"Leberspieße","c":"welt","k":"Marokko","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["½ kg Leber","1 TL Paprikapulver","Salz","Pfeffer","1 Handvoll frischer Koriander, fein gehackt","2–3 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt (optional)","1 EL Sonnenblumen- oder Olivenöl"],"s":["Cut the liver into small cubes about 1 cm square, and put them in a container.","Add paprika, some salt and pepper, chopped coriander, minced garlic, and oil to the liver.","Mix this all together and leave to marinate for 30 minutes or more.","Slide the meat onto skewers, and grill to preferred level of char."],"x":[],"desc":"Liver kebabs taste very good and are ideal for feeding young children liver as long as you don't tell them beforehand what it is. Served with fresh bread and Moroccan Salad, the kebabs make a nice meal.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liver_Kebabs","i":"wb-en-2554","im":["5/5b/Lula_kebab_2.jpg/960px-Lula_kebab_2.jpg","Lesya Dolyk","CC BY-SA 2.0","Lula kebab 2.jpg","w"],"on":"Liver Kebabs","og":["½ kg liver","1 tsp paprika","Salt","Pepper","1 handful fresh coriander, finely chopped","2–3 cloves garlic, minced (optional)","1 tbsp sunflower or olive oil"]},{"n":"Leber mit Zwiebeln","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 kg Kartoffeln","2 große Zwiebeln, in dünne Scheiben geschnitten","Öl oder Butter zum Braten","frisches oder tiefgekühltes grünes Gemüse, z. B. Erbsen, Grünkohl, Kohl, Brokkoli, usw.","Mehl","Salz","Pfeffer","ein großes Stück Butter","ein Schuss Milch, Sahne, Crème fraîche, oder Ähnliches","etwa 500 g Lamm- oder Rinderleber, in Scheiben geschnitten","Henderson's Relish (Würzsoße), Worcestersoße, oder Ähnliches (optional)"],"s":["Wash (and optionally peel) the potatoes and put in a pan of boiling water.","Fry onions gently in a large frying pan with some of the oil.","While the onions are frying, prepare the green vegetables.","Prepare a plate or wide bowl, covering it in flour mixed with a bit of salt and pepper. This is for dusting the liver prior to frying.","Once the potatoes are cooked, drain and then mash them, adding butter and cream or milk until you have the desired consistency. Put a lid on the pan to keep warm.","Once the onions are soft, remove them from the pan with a slotted spoon, squeezing the oil or butter back into the frying pan as you remove them. Put them in a bowl on one side.","Turn the heat of your frying pan up as high as possible and add a bit more oil or butter if necessary.","Arrange the liver, flour and frying pan in a straight line.","Start the process of dusting the slices of liver with flour on both sides and adding them to the hot pan. This needs to be done as quickly as possible and can be quite messy.","Do not over-crowd the pan—if you find the liver takes up more surface-space than is available then leave the remains on one side and fry in a second batch.","Cook the liver quickly, for only about a minute on each side so the slices are still pink within. Turn them over a couple of times. Quite a bit of the flour and blood will stick to the bottom of the pan.","This is ok—don't scrape it off as it will be used for the gravy in a moment.","Once the liver is done to your satisfaction remove it from the pan and put directly onto warmed plates. Have someone else serve out the mash and vegetables while you finish the gravy.","The trick is to try and not let everything else get cold while you are doing this.","Leaving the pan on a high heat, put the onions back in, add a good splash of Hendersons, and stir vigorously while adding boiling water, dissolving the juices stuck to the bottom of the pan.","The gravy should thicken from the flour already stuck to the bottom of the pan. If it doesn't get thick enough you can add a bit more flour or cornflour (mixed with a little cold water in a small cup to avoid lumps).","Once the gravy is hot and thickened, spoon generously over the plates."],"x":["When making the gravy, you can re-use the hot water from the vegetables. This can be a smooth maneuver, draining it into the gravy as you pass the pan over to be served onto plates."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liver_and_Onions","i":"wb-en-2555","im":["4/47/Tortillas_con_biste_de_higado.jpg/250px-Tortillas_con_biste_de_higado.jpg","Jdvillalobos","CC BY 3.0","Tortillas con biste de higado.jpg","w"],"on":"Liver and Onions","og":["1 kg potatoes","2 large onions, sliced thin","Oil or butter for frying","Fresh or frozen green vegetables, such as peas, kale, cabbage, broccoli, etc.","Flour","Salt","Pepper","Large knob of butter","A splash of milk, cream, crème fraîche, or similar","about 500 g lamb or ox liver, sliced","Henderson's relish, Worcestershire sauce, or similar (optional)"]},{"n":"Liverpooler Lamm-Gemüse-Eintopf (Scouse)","c":"suppen","k":"Großbritannien","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["ein günstiges Stück Lamm oder Hammel (z. B. Brust oder Vorderviertel)","etwas Öl","Zwiebeln, gehackt","Möhren, gehackt","Wasser oder Fleischbrühe","Kartoffeln, gewürfelt"],"s":["Remove the meat from the bone (if needed), and dice it.","Heat a little oil in a large saucepan. Add the meat, and brown it.","Add the chopped onions, carrots, and water or meat stock, and as many potatoes as possible.","Simmer until everything is cooked."],"x":[],"desc":"This is a traditional recipe for Liverpool scouse, also known as \"lobscouse\". The sauce is not thickened, and it is usual to serve with preserved beetroot or red cabbage and white bread with butter. An even more impoverished variety of this dish is 'blind Scouse', which features no meat.","img":"Posh Scouse at Liverpool Maritime Museum - Flickr - Radarsmum67.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Liverpool_Lamb_and_Vegetable_Soup_(Scouse)","i":"wb-en-2556","im":["7/7b/Posh_Scouse_at_Liverpool_Maritime_Museum_-_Flickr_-_Radarsmum67.jpg/960px-Posh_Scouse_at_Liverpool_Maritime_Museum_-_Flickr_-_Radarsmum67.jpg","Radarsmum67 from Liverpool, UK.","CC BY 2.0","Posh Scouse at Liverpool Maritime Museum - Flickr - Radarsmum67.jpg","r"],"on":"Liverpool Lamb and Vegetable Soup (Scouse)","og":["A cheap cut of lamb or mutton (such as breast or forequarter)","A little oil","Onions, chopped","Carrots, chopped","Water or meat stock","Potatoes, diced"]},{"n":"Lo Mein","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":25,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Teil Fleisch für die Pfanne (z. B. Schwein, Rind, Garnelen)","1 Teil Gemüse für die Pfanne (z. B. Wasserkastanien, Spargel, Brokkoli, Kürbis, Bambussprossen)","1 Teil gekochte Lo-Mein-Nudeln","so viel Sojasoße, dass alle Zutaten gut überzogen sind","so viel Olivenöl, dass der Pfannenboden bedeckt ist","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","zerdrückter oder gehackter Knoblauch (optional)","Sojasprossen (optional)"],"s":["Cook noodles in a pot according to the package directions.","Coat a skillet with olive oil and place on stove with medium to low heat. Add garlic if desired, but don't let it burn.","Add meat and vegetables to skillet, season with salt and pepper, lightly coat with soy sauce, and cook everything until it's done (about 8–10 minutes).","If using, add bean sprouts right before everything is finished cooking, and cook them until they turn mildly translucent.","Strain noodles and add them to the stir fry.","Coat with soy sauce and cook for roughly 1 minute in order to sear in the flavor."],"x":["Spaghetti noodles work well too. For a healthier option, try whole-grain spaghetti noodles.","When adding the soy sauce, start out light. Taste and then add more. It's much easier to add ingredients than remove them."],"desc":"This lo mein recipe is very flexible. Add what ever ingredients you think will fit. A popular combination is pork with water chestnuts and asparagus. \"Stir fry-style meats and vegetables\" simply refers to ingredients cut in pieces that are slightly smaller than bite-size and perfect for pan frying.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lo_Mein","i":"wb-en-2557","im":["https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8b/Real_lo_mein.jpg","Slakjaw ( talk )","CC-BY-3.0","Real lo mein.jpg","w"],"og":["1 part stir fry meat (e.g. pork, beef, shrimp)","1 part stir fry vegetables (e.g. water chestnuts, asparagus, broccoli, squash, bamboo shoots)","1 part cooked lo mein noodles","Enough soy sauce to heavily coat all the ingredients","Enough olive oil to coat a skillet","Salt to taste","Pepper to taste","Crushed/minced garlic (optional)","Bean sprouts (optional)"]},{"n":"Hummerbisque","c":"suppen","k":"Frankreich","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 ½ Tassen gegartes Hummerschwanzfleisch","2 Tassen Hühnerbrühe","2 Tassen Schlagsahne","12 Zweige frischer Dill","¼ Tasse frisch gepresster Zitronensaft","1 EL Olivenöl","¼ Tasse fein gewürfelter Staudensellerie","1 große Zwiebel, fein gewürfelt","1 EL fein gehackter Knoblauch","Salz","frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","3 Lorbeerblätter"],"s":["Heat oil in a large pot over medium high heat. Add celery, onion, and garlic and sauté until garlic is golden and onions are translucent.","Add remaining ingredients, 1 tsp salt, and freshly ground black pepper. Remove bay leaves and reserve.","Purée soup until smooth using an immersion blender.","Add bay leaves and bring to a boil. Reduce heat to medium low and cook 10 minutes.","Remove bay leaves and ladle into individual bowls. Grind on some black pepper and sprinkle with some dill, if desired, before serving."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lobster_Bisque","i":"wb-en-2558","im":["8/89/Lobster_bisque.jpg/960px-Lobster_bisque.jpg","unbekannt","CC BY-SA 2.0","Lobster bisque.jpg","w"],"on":"Lobster Bisque","og":["1 ½ cups cooked lobster tail meat","2 cups chicken broth","2 cups heavy cream","12 sprigs fresh dill","¼ cup freshly-squeezed lemon juice","1 tbsp olive oil","¼ cup finely-diced celery","1 large onion, finely diced","1 tbsp minced garlic","Salt","Freshly-ground black pepper","3 bay leaves"]},{"n":"Hummer Thermidor","c":"fisch","k":"Frankreich","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["225 g gegartes Hummerfleisch, am besten vom Schwanzende, siehe Hinweise","1 gesäuberte Hummerschwanzschale","3 EL Butter oder Margarine","240 ml Schlagsahne","2 Eigelb","120 ml Sherry oder Weinbrand","120 g geriebener Gruyère oder Mozzarella","Salz","frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer"],"s":["In a serving bowl, mix together egg yolks and cream, then set aside for later use.","In a saucepan large enough to accommodate everything, warm the butter over low heat until it melts.","Add the cooked lobster meat and wine to the butter, then sauté over medium-high heat for about 2–3 minutes, or until the meat is warmed through and the wine has been mostly absorbed.","Slowly add the cream and egg mixture, stirring all the time to ensure that the sauce is evenly mixed.","When the sauce has thickened remove from heat.","Set oven to broil or prepare an open flame.","Carefully stuff the empty lobster tail with the filling.","Top the filling with the grated cheese, salt, and pepper.","Place the filled shell underneath the open flame and broil for 3–8 minutes, or until the cheese melts and turns a golden brown.","Remove from the oven, and serve on a warmed plate with garnish and appropriate accompaniments."],"x":["Cooking and shelling a fresh lobster can be a time consuming process, so frozen or pre-shelled tail meat is often used as a substitute. If you would like to prepare your own lobster meat, refer to the recipe for boiled lobster.","While the base preparation of Lobster Thermidor often remains the same, the type of wine or cheese used, or the way that the lobster is cooked differs.","Some preparations include utilizing the broth generated from cooking the lobster with carrots, celery, tarragon, and wine as an additional ingredient to thicken the sauce of cream and sherry."],"desc":"Lobster thermidor is a dish created by stuffing an empty lobster tail with sautéed lobster meat that is cooked with butter, a light wine (often sherry), and cream. The resulting sauce is stuffed into a lobster shell then topped with either a cheese, mushrooms or combination of vegetables before bein","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lobster_Thermidor","i":"wb-en-2559","im":["4/48/Lobster_Thermidor_entree.jpg/960px-Lobster_Thermidor_entree.jpg","thefoodplace.co.uk","CC BY 2.0","Lobster Thermidor entree.jpg","w"],"on":"Lobster Thermidor","og":["½ lb (225 g) cooked lobster meat, preferably from the tail; see notes","1 cleaned lobster tail shell","3 tablespoons butter or margarine","1 cup (240 ml) heavy cream","2 egg yolks","½ cup (120 ml) sherry or brandy","½ cup (120 g) grated gruyere or mozzarella cheese","Salt","Freshly-ground black pepper"]},{"n":"Loco Moco (Reis mit Ei und Hamburger)","c":"beilagen","k":"Hawaii","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Eier","1 Hamburger-Patty","½–1 Tassen ungekochter Reis (nach Vorliebe)","Bratensoße"],"s":["Cook the eggs sunny side up.","Cook the hamburger to your preference.","Steam the rice, and heat up the gravy.","Assemble the components in the following order","Rice on bottom","Hamburger on top of rice","Eggs","Gravy."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Loco_Moco_(Rice_with_Egg_and_Hamburger)","i":"wb-en-2560","im":["b/b3/Loco_moco_%2832605169782%29.jpg/960px-Loco_moco_%2832605169782%29.jpg","California Cow from Seattle, USA","CC BY 2.0","Loco moco (32605169782).jpg","w"],"on":"Loco Moco (Rice with Egg and Hamburger)","og":["2 eggs","1 hamburger patty","½–1 cup uncooked rice (per preference)","Gravy"]},{"n":"Locrio (dominikanisches Hähnchen mit Reis)","c":"fleisch","k":"Dominikanische Republik","p":4,"t":0,"d":3,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["¼ Tasse Öl zum Braten","1 EL Zucker","1.8 kg Hähnchen, in Stücke geschnitten","½ Tasse Oliven oder Kapern (entsteint)","2 EL Öl, für den Zeitpunkt, wenn der Reis fast fertig ist","½ Tasse fein gewürfelter Staudensellerie","½ Tasse fein gewürfelte Zwiebel","2 Zehen Knoblauch, gehackt","4 Tassen Reis","5 ¼ Tassen Hühnerfond oder Wasser","¼ Tasse Tomatenmark","1 TL Salz, oder nach Geschmack","1 TL Thymian","½ TL Oregano (optional)","1 TL gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer"],"s":["Heat the ¼ cup oil in a pot over high heat.","Add the sugar to the pot. Let it melt and caramelize, turning light brown. Pay close attention and don't let the sugar burn. Do not use plastic utensils to stir the sugar, since it will be at around 350°F (175°C).","Add the meat to the caramel and let it brown on all sides. Remove and reserve the meat.","Add the garlic, onions, and celery to the pot. Fry.","Add rice and cooked meat to pot with the vegetables. Whisk together chicken stock and tomato paste until smooth, then stir it into the rice mixture. Stir in the salt, pepper, thyme, and olives.","Check the seasoning. If the salt level is good, add an extra ½ tsp of salt. This is because the rice will absorb some of the salt, and it will come out a bit flat in the end unless you add extra salt.","Bring to a boil over high heat. Let it boil, stirring occasionally, until the water is absorbed. The high heat is needed to bring the rice temperature up so that it cooks. If you lower the flame at this point, the rice might not cook all the way.","Cover, lower the heat, and let it cook for 15 minutes.","Uncover, sprinkle 2 Tbsp oil on top, and stir so that the uncooked rice on top goes to the bottom. Cook for another 5 minutes.","If rice still not cooked, give it another stir and cook for another 5 minutes. Sometimes you may need more time; see notes below.","Turn heat on high for a couple of minutes to brown and toast the rice on bottom. Sometimes it does this by itself during the main cooking so you don't have to do this. Experience will tell.","Serve.","Preheat oven to 350°F (125°C).","Proceed with the recipe as above, using an oven-proof pot, until the rice absorbs all the liquid. Once this happens, cover the pot, put it in the oven, and bake for 30 minutes.","Add 2 tbsp oil, and stir so the uncooked rice is on the bottom and the bottom rice is on the top. Bake for another 20 minutes.","Stir. If it is still not fully cooked, bake another 20 minutes.","Serve."],"x":["If the rice doesn't cook but all the water was absorbed, you can separate the rice from the meat, put it in a bowl, and give it 5 minutes on high in the microwave. Often there wasn't enough heat to cook the rice. On some stoves, once covered (as mentioned above), you may have to cook 20 minutes, add oil, stir, and cook another 20–40 minutes, stirring every 10 minutes.","It is also helpful to put a sheet or two of aluminium foil over the pot before putting the lid on. That helps seal the lid and keep the heat/steam from escaping, and the rice often comes out better.","Some people deep fry the meat separately, remove the excess oil, and then caramelize the sugar.","The ingredients of the sofrito vary, and can be made in advance. Some add cilantro, bell peppers, culantro, and other aromatics to it.","Other vegetables such as 1 cup of cubed auyama squash are sometimes added with the rice.","Some people use Sazón Completo for the seasoning. Although it is not authentic, you can also add 1 tsp ajinomoto (味の素), which is similar."],"desc":"A locrio is a common Dominican dish similar to paella. Like paella, there are many variations. The main point is to have a little tomato sauce/paste for coloring, and some caramelized sugar. In that way it is similar to the Trinidadian pilau. Like paella, the rice at the bottom should be toasted or ","img":"Locrio de Pollo (Dominicano).jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Locrio_(Dominican_Chicken_and_Rice)","i":"wb-en-2561","im":["6/60/Locrio_de_Pollo_%28Dominicano%29.jpg/960px-Locrio_de_Pollo_%28Dominicano%29.jpg","Ll1324","CC0","Locrio de Pollo (Dominicano).jpg","r"],"on":"Locrio (Dominican Chicken and Rice)","og":["¼ cup oil for frying","1 tbsp sugar","4 lbs (1.8 kg) chicken, cut in pieces","½ cup olives (pitted) or capers","2 tbsp oil, for when rice is almost done","½ cup finely diced celery","½ cup finely diced onion","2 cloves of garlic, chopped","4 cups rice","5¼ cups chicken stock or water","¼ cup tomato paste","1 tsp salt or to taste","1 tsp thyme","½ tsp oregano (optional)","1 tsp ground black pepper"]},{"n":"Lolly Cake (Kekskuchen mit Fruchtbonbons)","c":"kuchen","k":"Neuseeland","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["250 g Malzkekse (1 Päckchen)","1 Prise Zimt (optional)","120 g Butter","200 g gezuckerte Kondensmilch (½ Dose bzw. 200 g)","180 g Fruchtsnacks (Puffs) (1 Päckchen)","Kokosraspel"],"s":["Crush the biscuits. They don't need to be a fine dust—some pieces can be left partially-crushed to give the cake a nicer texture.","Mix in cinnamon, if you want it.","Warm the butter and condensed milk in the microwave for 30 seconds until the butter is very soft. It's okay if the butter melts a bit.","Cut the fruit puffs in half if you want or leave them whole.","Mix the fruit puffs with the crushed biscuits, then add the butter and condensed milk. Mix well.","Roll the mixture into a log shape, or roll small amounts into little balls.","Roll the log or balls in the shredded coconut until completely covered.","Place on a tray and cover with plastic wrap to keep moist. Chill for several hours in the fridge until hardened.","Cut cake while still cold before it warms up again"],"x":[],"desc":"Lolly cake is a New Zealand cake which features lollies in the ingredients and thus can be thought of as \"candy cake\". The traditional candy used is Fruit Puffs which are like firm, slightly chewy marshmallows and are obviously fruity. Malt biscuits and coconut are also used and other ingredients ca","img":"Lolly cake (2792116118).jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lolly_Cake","i":"wb-en-2562","im":["6/60/Lolly_cake_%282792116118%29.jpg/960px-Lolly_cake_%282792116118%29.jpg","brent simpson from Auckland, New Zealand/Aotearoa","CC BY-SA 2.0","Lolly cake (2792116118).jpg","r"],"on":"Lolly Cake","og":["250 g (1 packet) malt biscuits","1 pinch of cinnamon (optional)","120 g (1.5 sticks) of butter","200 g (½ can or 7 ounces) condensed milk","180 g (1 packet) Fruit Puffs","Shredded coconut"]},{"n":"Lomo Saltado (peruanisches Rindfleisch aus der Pfanne)","c":"fleisch","k":"Peru","p":6,"t":80,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["900 g Rinderfilet oder ein anderes zartes Steak","¼ Tasse Rotwein (z. B. Burgunder)","2 EL zerdrückter Knoblauch","2 mittelgroße Zwiebeln, in Streifen geschnitten","4 Tomaten, Kerne entfernt, im Mixer püriert","5 Kartoffeln, geschält und in Stifte geschnitten, zum Frittieren","1 gelbe peruanische Chili (Ají Amarillo) (Ají), in dünne Streifen geschnitten","1 EL Essig","2 EL Sojasoße","Pflanzenöl zum Braten","Salz","Pfeffer","Culantro oder Koriander"],"s":["Cut the meat into thin strips and marinate them in the wine for 1 hour.","Use a wok to cook garlic in oil over medium heat and add the meat. Reserve the juice.","Add the tomato purée, salt and pepper. Cook for a few minutes.","Add the soy sauce while stirring the meat in the wok.","Add the onions, aji strips, cilantro and vinegar. Combine the juice from the meat.","Fry the potatoes in a separate pan and add to the other ingredients.","Serve the dish with white rice."],"x":["Instead of puréeing the tomatoes, you can cut them into slices.","You may omit the wine and use a greater quantity of vinegar.","Using a different kind of hot pepper changes the flavor of this dish completely.","You may choose not to marinate the beef."],"desc":"Lomo saltado is a dish of marinated steak, vegetables and fried potatoes, usually served over white rice. It is one of the most popular recipes in Peru and is often found on the menu at many smaller restaurants at a very reasonable price.","img":"Lomo saltado.JPG","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lomo_Saltado_(Peruvian_Steak_Stir-fry)","i":"wb-en-2563","im":["2/26/Lomo_saltado.JPG/960px-Lomo_saltado.JPG","No machine-readable author provided. Manuel González Olaeche","CC BY-SA 3.0","Lomo saltado.JPG","r"],"on":"Lomo Saltado (Peruvian Steak Stir-fry)","og":["3 pounds (900 g) beef tenderloin or other tender steak","¼ cup red wine (e.g. Burgundy)","2 tablespoons crushed garlic","2 medium onions, cut in strips","4 tomatoes, seeds removed, puréed in a blender","5 potatoes peeled and cut into strips for frying","1 yellow Peruvian Chili Pepper (aji), cut into thin strips","1 tablespoon of vinegar","2 tablespoons of soy sauce","Vegetable oil for frying","Salt","Pepper","Culantro or cilantro"]},{"n":"London Broil (gegrilltes Flanksteak)","c":"fleisch","k":"USA","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 TL Salz","1 EL frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","¾ TL Cayennepfeffer","2 ½ TL getrockneter Rosmarin","¼ TL Mesquite-Rauchpulver","1 Flanksteak","Dijonsenf"],"s":["Combine salt, pepper, cayenne, rosemary, and smoke powder. Set aside.","Brush steak liberally with Dijon mustard. Apply seasoning mixture and gently rub into meat. Refrigerate for at least 1 hour.","Heat a charcoal grill with a chimney starter (not that solvent stuff). Reapply the grate and place the steak on top. Cook, flipping once, until internal temperature reaches 145°F for medium rare.","Remove and let rest for 10 minutes. Slice as thinly as humanly possible across the grain. Serve warm."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:London_Broil","i":"wb-en-2564","im":["3/30/London_broil.jpg/960px-London_broil.jpg","Jeremy Keith","CC BY 2.0","London broil.jpg","w"],"on":"London Broil","og":["1 tsp salt","1 tbsp freshly-ground black pepper","¾ tsp cayenne pepper","2 ½ tsp dried rosemary","¼ tsp mesquite smoke powder","1 ea. (1 pound) flank steak","Dijon mustard"]},{"n":"London Fog (Earl Grey mit Milch und Vanille)","c":"welt","k":"Kanada","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Beutel Earl-Grey-Tee","½ Tasse kochendes Wasser","450 g Milch (2 % oder Vollmilch)","1 Schuss Vanillesirup"],"s":["Add the boiling water to a mug along with the tea bag. Let steep for 2–4 minutes to achieve optimum flavor—the result is an Earl Grey tea concentrate.","Heat up milk. Access to a steamer is preferred. Mix in vanilla syrup.","Add hot milk to the tea as desired. Adjust components according to taste."],"x":["Oregon Mist: Replace the Earl Grey tea with green tea and the vanilla syrup with amaretto; popularized by the Glenwood restaurants in Eugene, Oregon.","Manchester Fog: Replace the milk with soy milk.","Dublin Fog: Replace the Earl Grey tea with Irish breakfast tea.","Bangalore Fog: Replace the Earl Grey tea with a chai tea blend; created by Kavya Raman at Roosters Coffeehouse, Carleton University, Ottawa ON; also known as a Bombay Fog (coined in Concordia-Loyola's Second Cup, Montreal, QC).","Atlantic City Fog: Replace the Earl Grey tea with with rose tea; created by Alexis V. Juneau at MCB Quantico, Quantico, Virginia.","Winter Fog: Reduce the vanilla syrup and add clover honey to taste."],"desc":"London fog (also known as Vanilla Tea Misto or an Earl Grey Tea Latte) is the name of a drink which originated in Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada, although the creator remains unknown, among several claims. One such claim is from Buckwheat Cafe on 4th Avenue in Vancouver (now closed) when in Dec","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:London_Fog","i":"wb-en-2565","im":["5/57/Tumbleweed_Coffee_House_-_London_Fog_%2815606105942%29.jpg/960px-Tumbleweed_Coffee_House_-_London_Fog_%2815606105942%29.jpg","Elsie Hui","CC BY 2.0","Tumbleweed Coffee House - London Fog (15606105942).jpg","c"],"on":"London Fog","og":["1 bag Earl Grey tea","½ cup boiling water","16 oz milk (2% or whole)","1 shot vanilla syrup"]},{"n":"Long Island Iced Tea","c":"getraenke","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["¼ Teil Wodka","¼ Teil weißer Rum","¼ Teil Gin","¼ Teil Tequila oder Triple Sec","1 Teil Sweet-and-Sour-Mix oder Zitronen- bzw. Limettensaft, nach Geschmack","1 ein Schuss Cola oder Kaffeelikör","Zitrone, in Scheiben zum Garnieren"],"s":["Shake all the ingredients except the cola with ice in a cocktail shaker.","Strain into a highball glass.","Float the cola on the top and serve with a lemon slice.","Fill a highball glass until it's almost full with ice.","Add vodka, gin, rum, and tequila.","Add sweet and sour mix, leaving some room on top.","Splash in the cola and enjoy."],"x":["Don't forget—it has to look like an iced tea, so don't add too much cola.","To make a Long Beach Tea, use cranberry juice instead of cola."],"desc":"A Long Island iced tea is a mixed cocktail originating in the prohibition era and made popular in New York speakeasies. Despite its name, the drink does not contain any tea whatsoever.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Long_Island_Iced_Tea","i":"wb-en-2566","im":["4/45/Long_Island_Iced_Teas.jpg/500px-Long_Island_Iced_Teas.jpg","Eduardo Quagliato from Curitiba, Paraná, Brasil","CC BY 2.0","Long Island Iced Teas.jpg","w"],"og":["¼ part vodka","¼ part white rum","¼ part gin","¼ part tequila or triple sec","1 part sweet and sour mix OR lemon/lime juice to taste","1 splash cola or coffee liqueur","Lemon, sliced for garnish"]},{"n":"Long-Island-Babyente aus dem Ofen","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":3,"t":150,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 ganze Pekingente (1,5 bis 3 kg)","Salz","Pfeffer","Antihaft-Backspray mit Buttergeschmack"],"s":["Preheat oven to 450 °F.","Rinse and wipe duckling, removing giblets.","Set bird aside in an airy place to allow the skin to dry.","Rub inside cavity with salt and pepper.","Insert vertical oven roaster (used for \"beer can chicken\") into bird, and prop it upright.","Coat bird on all sides with butter-flavored spray and sprinkle salt and pepper lightly over the skin.","Place bird and vertical roaster into a large roasting pan (use a wire rack insert if you have one) and add ½ cup water to the bottom of the pan.","Leave bird in oven for 30 minutes, then reduce heat to 325 °F until done. No need to prick skin or baste bird, as the fat slowly renders off leaving a wonderful crispy skin. Keep the bottom of the roasting pan covered with water to prevent smoking.","Pour off fat and save, reserving drippings and liquid from the roasting pan."],"x":["Serve with brown rice, rice pilaf or baked sweet potatoes. Cherry sauce and wild rice are also traditional.","Use the duck fat to cook sliced potatoes or to make duck confit.","The fat and liver can be cooked together to make a very tasty paté so don't throw any of it out."],"desc":"According to Alton Brown, host of the Food Network's Good Eats, duck farming got its start on Long Island after an American businessman touring China in 1873 bought 25 white pekin ducks and shipped them to Long Island. Only nine survived the trip but those nine reproduced quickly and their descendan","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Long_Island_Roast_Duckling","i":"wb-en-2567","on":"Long Island Roast Duckling","og":["1 whole pekin duckling (3–6 lbs, 1.5–3 kg)","Salt","Pepper","Butter-flavored nonstick spray"]},{"n":"Long-Island-Babyente aus dem Ofen mit Zitrusfrüchten","c":"fleisch","k":"USA","p":3,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 ganze Pekingente (1,8 bis 2,3 kg)","1 Zitrone, geviertelt","1 Orange, geviertelt oder geachtelt","Salz","Pfeffer"],"s":["Defrost the duck in the fridge if it's frozen.","Remove the giblets and any packages from the body cavity.","Preheat the oven to 375 °F and place an oven rack in the center of the oven.","Rinse the duck and pat it dry both inside and out with paper towels.","Pierce the skin every half inch with prongs, pushing the prongs through the skin and into the fat but not into the meat. The fat will escape through these holes as the duck cooks.","Rub plenty of salt and freshly ground pepper on the skin. Then, place 2 pieces of lemon and 2–4 pieces of orange inside the duck's cavity.","Tie the duck's legs together with a piece of butcher's twine. This will keep the citrus inside the cavity.","Place the duck breast side up on a rack that has been placed on a roasting pan. It's important to use a roasting pan that has some depth so the fat drips into the pan and not the oven.","Push a meat thermometer into one of the thighs.","Place the bird on the center rack of the oven. It will cook in 1–1½ hours depending on its size.","Remove the duck every 20 minutes from the oven and drain the excess fat. Rotate the duck each time you return it to the oven to help it crisp evenly. You'll know it's done when the skin is golden brown and crispy.","Also, the meat thermometer should read no lower than 165 °F.","Remove the bird from the oven. Pour out the liquid from the cavity and discard.","Allow the duck to rest for ten minutes before carving."],"x":[],"desc":"This recipe uses a conventional roasting method based on the one featured on The City Cook website.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Long_Island_Roast_Duckling_with_Citrus","i":"wb-en-2568","on":"Long Island Roast Duckling with Citrus","og":["1 ea. (4–5 pounds, 1.8–3.6 kg) whole pekin duckling","1 lemon, cut into quarters","1 orange, cut into quarters or eighths","Salt","Pepper"]},{"n":"Louis-Dressing","c":"saucen","k":"","p":6,"t":35,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["235 ml Mayonnaise","60 ml Tasse milde Salsa mit grünen Chilis","60 ml Ketchup","1 EL Zitronensaft (15 ml)","1 ½ TL Worcestersoße (7 ml)","scharfe Soße (z. B. Tabasco, Crystal), nach Geschmack"],"s":["Combine all ingredients in a blender, and process until smooth. The goal is to have a pink smooth sauce with little green flecks.","Pour the sauce into a bowl, cover, and chill in the refrigerator for at least 30 minutes prior to use."],"x":["For the traditional recipe, replace the salsa and ketchup with ½ cup chile sauce (or store-bought chile sauce), and 3 tablespoons each of finely-minced green onion and green chili peppers. Instead of using a blender, whisk the ingredients in a bowl.","Keep refrigerated."],"desc":"__NOTOC__ | Salad Recipes | Appetizers | California cuisine","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Louis_Dressing","i":"wb-en-2569","im":["6/6c/Crab_Louie_Salad.jpg/500px-Crab_Louie_Salad.jpg","Waspstar","CC BY 3.0","Crab Louie Salad.jpg","w"],"on":"Louis Dressing","og":["1 cup (235 ml) mayonnaise","¼ cup (60 ml) cup mild salsa with green chile peppers","¼ cup (60 ml) ketchup","1 tablespoon (15 ml) lemon juice","1 ½ teaspoon (7 ml) worcestershire sauce","Hot sauce (e.g., Tabasco, Crystal), to taste"]},{"n":"Loukoumades (griechische Krapfen mit Honig) I","c":"dessert","k":"Griechenland","p":6,"t":45,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1,36 kg Weizenmehl","½ TL Salz","2 Tassen unverdünnte Kondensmilch","4 Eier","2 EL Backpulver","1 Tasse Zucker","gemahlener Zimt","1 TL Vanilleextrakt","4 TL Trockenhefe, in ½ Tasse warmem Wasser aufgelöst","Soja- oder Maiskeimöl zum Braten","Honig"],"s":["In a large mixing bowl, mix the flour, salt, milk, eggs, baking powder, sugar, cinnamon, and vanilla.","Mix the yeast and water together.","Add the yeast mixture to the other ingredients and stir. The mixture should look like smooth cake batter.","Cover the bowl and leave it for 4 hours.","Place 5 cm of oil in a pot and heat it up.","With a tablespoon, drop the batter in and roll. Loukoumades should be sphere-shaped once fried and should look golden or brown from all sides.","After they are fried, remove them from the oil and pour honey over them. Use the cinnamon for extra flavour. You can also use sesame seeds for flavour."],"x":[],"desc":"Loukoumas is a Greek fried pastry, similar to a doughnut.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Loukoumas_(Greek_Donuts_with_Honey)_I","i":"wb-en-2570","im":["1/15/Sam%27dan_lokma_tatlisi.jpg/500px-Sam%27dan_lokma_tatlisi.jpg","elif ayse","CC BY 2.0","Sam'dan lokma tatlisi.jpg","w"],"on":"Loukoumas (Greek Donuts with Honey) I","og":["1.36 kg (48 oz / 6 cups) all-purpose flour","½ teaspoon salt","2 cups undiluted evaporated milk","4 eggs","2 tablespoons baking powder","1 cup white granulated sugar","Ground cinnamon","1 teaspoon vanilla extract","4 teaspoons dry yeast dissolved in ½ cup of warm water","Soy or corn oil for frying","Honey"]},{"n":"Loukoumades (griechische Krapfen mit Honig) II","c":"dessert","k":"Griechenland","p":8,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Ausgebackenes","4 TL Trockenhefe","1 ½ Tassen warmes Wasser","2 Tassen Weizenmehl","1 knapp 1 TL Salz","Pflanzenöl zum Braten","#Belag","Honig (am besten Thymianhonig)","Zimt","Walnüsse, zerdrückt","Sesam"],"s":["Combine the yeast and ½ cup warm water.","Mix the flour with the salt and put it in a deep bowl.","Add the yeast and and 1 cup warm water, and mix well until you make a uniform thin paste.","Cover and leave in the shade for 1½–2 hours until it rises and forms bubbles under the surface.","Heat several inches of oil in a deep frying pan. Add the batter by large spoonfuls to make fritters. Turn the balls as they puff-up, frying 3–5 minutes until golden brown all over. Do not crowd the pan.","Remove with a strainer or ladle, and place on paper towels; keep warm.","Drizzle loukoumas with honey.","Sprinkle with cinnamon, walnuts, and/or sesame seeds to taste."],"x":[],"desc":"Callimachus called these \"honey tokens\" some time during the 3rd century B.C. Loukoumades were the 1st prizes awarded to winners of the ancient Olympics. Now they are the perfect Greek cafe dessert celebratory piece of decadent, or mid-morning snack. They’re especially good on cold wintry afternoons","img":"Loukoumades.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Loukoumas_(Greek_Donuts_with_Honey)_II","i":"wb-en-2571","im":["0/08/Loukoumades.jpg/500px-Loukoumades.jpg","Flickr.com user \"avlxyz\"","CC BY-SA 2.0","Loukoumades.jpg","r"],"on":"Loukoumas (Greek Donuts with Honey) II","og":["#Fritters","4 teaspoons active dry yeast","1½ cups warm water","2 cups all-purpose flour","1 scant teaspoon salt","Vegetable oil for frying","#Topping","Honey (preferably thyme honey)","Cinnamon","Walnuts, crushed","Sesame seeds"]},{"n":"Garnelen mit Grits nach Lowcountry-Art","c":"fisch","k":"USA","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["3–4 dicke, kräftig geräucherte Speckstreifen, in 2,5 cm große Stücke geschnitten","½ Zwiebel, fein gehackt","2–3 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","450 g große Garnelen, geschält (Schalen für Brühe verwenden)","Salz","470 ml Schlagsahne, aufgeteilt","2–2 ½ Tassen Garnelenfond","Butter","schwarzer Pfeffer","Cayennepfeffer","Paprikapulver","Chiliflocken","Limettensaft","1 Rezept grobe Hominy-Grits (Maisgrütze), so getimt, dass es fertig ist, wenn die Garnelen serviert werden","3–4 Frühlingszwiebeln, in Scheiben geschnitten"],"s":["Fry bacon in a pan until not too crisp; remove and reserve.","Sauté onion and garlic in bacon fat until just softened (about 2–3 minutes).","Lightly season shrimp with salt and add to the pan; sauté until about half-cooked and just turning pink. Remove and reserve with the bacon.","Deglaze pan with sherry.","Add 1 cup (250 ml) cream, bring to boil, and reduce.","Add 1 cup shrimp stock, bring to a high simmer, and reduce. The liquid should thicken; if necessary, add floured butter at this point (beurre manié).","Season sauce with salt, pepper, chili flakes, cayenne, and paprika","Add bacon and shrimp to the sauce, and cook gently until shrimp are just done.","Add lime juice.","Serve over grits, and garnish with scallions."],"x":["Make the shrimp stock with shrimp peels and parts, dried shrimp flakes, mirepoix, and peppercorns.","The scallions can be replaced with minced chives."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Low_Country_Shrimp_and_Grits","i":"wb-en-2572","im":["0/06/Grits1.jpg/960px-Grits1.jpg","sashafatcat","CC BY 2.0","Grits1.jpg","w"],"on":"Low Country Shrimp and Grits","og":["3–4 strips thick smoky bacon, cut into 1-inch pieces","½ onion, minced","2–3 cloves garlic, minced","1 lb large shrimp, peeled (use peels to make stock)","Salt","1 pint heavy cream, divided","2–2½ cups shrimp stock","Butter","Black pepper","Cayenne pepper","Paprika","Chile flakes","Lime juice","1 recipe coarse grain hominy grits, timed to finish when shrimp are ready to serve","3–4 scallions, sliced"]},{"n":"Luciabullar (skandinavische Safranbrötchen)","c":"brot","k":"Schweden","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Packungen Trockenhefe","¼ Tasse lauwarmes Wasser","½ TL zerstoßene Safranfäden (¼ TL gemahlen)","180 ml Kaffeesahne (Half and Half), lauwarm","120 g geschmolzene Butter","2 Eier, verquirlt","180 g Zucker","1 TL Salz","4–5 Tassen gesiebtes Weizenmehl","Rosinen zum Verzieren"],"s":["Combine the yeast and warm water.","Mix saffron into the warm half and half and let stand.","Combine the yeast and saffron mixtures. Mix in the melted butter, eggs, sugar, and salt.","Mix half of flour into the wet mixture and beat until well-blended.","Mix in additional flour until dough is smooth but not too firm. Knead on floured surface for ten minutes.","Place dough in buttered bowl and let rise about 1½ hours or until doubled in volume.","Divide the dough into multiple pieces. Roll each piece into a 7 inch-long snake, and form into an 'S' shape with the ends curled in. Place a raisin in each curl.","Place buns on buttered sheet pan, cover, and let rise 45 minutes.","Brush with beaten egg and bake at 375–400°F (190–200°C) for 10–15 minutes until golden and cooked through."],"x":[],"desc":"Lussekatter or luciabullar are Scandinavian saffron buns served on St. Lucia Day (13 December).","img":"2005 baking of saffron buns 04.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Luciabullar_(Scandinavian_Saffron_Buns)","i":"wb-en-2573","im":["8/8b/2005_baking_of_saffron_buns_04.jpg/960px-2005_baking_of_saffron_buns_04.jpg","Tomhe","CC BY 2.0","2005 baking of saffron buns 04.jpg","r"],"on":"Luciabullar (Scandinavian Saffron Buns)","og":["2 packages (4½ tsp) active dry yeast","¼ cup lukewarm water","½ tsp crushed (¼ tsp powdered) saffron threads","¾ cup (180 ml) half and half, lukewarm","½ cup (120 g) melted butter","2 eggs, beaten","¾ cup (180 g) white granulated sugar","1 tsp salt","4–5 cups sifted all-purpose flour","Raisins to decorate"]},{"n":"Lumanda (sambischer Okraeintopf)","c":"suppen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 EL Pflanzenöl","1 Zwiebel, fein gehackt","2 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","1 scharfe Chili, gehackt (für weniger Schärfe entkernen)","1 TL Paprikapulver","1 TL gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","½ TL gemahlene Kurkuma","½ TL gemahlener Koriander","2 Tassen frische Okra in Scheiben","1 Tomate, gewürfelt","Salz, nach Geschmack"],"s":["In a large pot, heat the vegetable oil over medium heat.","Add the chopped onion, minced garlic, and chopped hot pepper to the pot. Sauté until the onions are soft and translucent.","Stir in the ground paprika, ground cumin, ground turmeric, and ground coriander. Cook for a minute or two to release the flavors of the spices.","Add the sliced okra and diced tomato to the pot. Stir well to combine the vegetables with the spice mixture.","Season the stew with salt to taste. Adjust the seasoning according to your preference.","Reduce the heat to low, cover the pot, and let simmer for about 15–20 minutes, or until the okra is tender and cooked through.","Stir occasionally during cooking to prevent sticking and to ensure even cooking of the okra and tomatoes.","Once the stew is ready, remove the pot from the heat and let rest for a few minutes before serving."],"x":["For a thicker stew, you can add a spoonful of cornmeal or cassava meal to the pot during cooking.","Lumanda is traditionally served with nshima, a stiff maize porridge, but it can also be enjoyed with rice or bread."],"desc":"Lumanda is a flavorful Zambian okra stew that celebrates the unique taste and texture of okra. This vegetarian stew is made with fresh okra pods, tomatoes, onions, and a blend of aromatic spices. It is a delightful dish often enjoyed with nshima, a popular Zambian staple food.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lumanda_(Zambian_Okra_Stew)","i":"wb-en-2574","im":["2/26/Bamia-Ocras_tomate_%28cropped%29.JPG/960px-Bamia-Ocras_tomate_%28cropped%29.JPG","Tamorlan","CC BY-SA 3.0","Bamia-Ocras tomate (cropped).JPG","w"],"on":"Lumanda (Zambian Okra Stew)","og":["2 tablespoons vegetable oil","1 onion, finely chopped","2 cloves of garlic, minced","1 hot pepper, chopped (remove seeds for less heat)","1 teaspoon ground paprika","1 teaspoon ground cumin","½ teaspoon ground turmeric","½ teaspoon ground coriander","2 cups sliced fresh okra","1 tomato, diced","Salt, to taste"]},{"n":"Holzfäller-Sandwiches","c":"brot","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse feiner Zucker","1 Tasse weißes Pflanzenfett oder Butter","1 Tasse dunkle Melasse","2 Eier","4 Tassen gesiebtes Mehl (ohne Backpulver)","1 TL Natron","2 TL Zimt","1 TL Ingwer"],"s":["Cream together the sugar and shortening.","Add molasses and eggs, and mix well.","Sift together the flour, spices, and bicarbonate of soda. Add this mixture to the egg-butter mixture, and mix well to make a dough.","Put ¼ cup additional white sugar into a small bowl.","Dip fingers into the sugar, then pinch off a ball of dough and roll it into the size and shape of a walnut.","Roll the cookie dough ball into the sugar and place on a greased cookie sheet.","Repeat the shaping and sugar-coating process with the remaining dough, spacing the cookies about 3 inches apart on the sheet.","Bake in a preheated 350°F (175°C) oven for 10–15 minutes.","Let cool completely—the cookies should be soft when cooled."],"x":["Different countries use different strengths of molasses. If you can find the American brand of Grandma's dark molasses then that is perfect.","If you use some muscovado sugar, then add the white and muscovado sugars at the same time."],"desc":"Lumberjacks are a cookie from the Old Sturbridge Village Cookbook, and they reflect baking from 1830s New England.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lumberjacks","i":"wb-en-2575","im":["7/73/Lumberjacks_Bunkhouse-front-3qtr.jpg/960px-Lumberjacks_Bunkhouse-front-3qtr.jpg","Myotus","CC BY-SA 4.0","Lumberjacks Bunkhouse-front-3qtr.jpg","c"],"on":"Lumberjacks","og":["1 cup caster sugar","1 cup white vegetable shortening or butter","1 cup dark molasses","2 eggs","4 cups sifted flour (not self-raising)","1 teaspoon of bicarbonate of soda","2 teaspoons cinnamon","1 teaspoon ginger"]},{"n":"Lumpia (frittierte philippinische Frühlingsrollen)","c":"beilagen","k":"Philippinen","p":6,"t":60,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["680 g Hähnchen- oder Schweinehack","⅓ Tasse gehackte Wasserkastanien","½ Tasse gehackte Zwiebel","4 Eier","¼ Tasse Sojasoße","Salz und frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","2 Packungen kleine bis mittelgroße Frühlingsrollenblätter (Wan-Tan-Blätter)","4 Tassen Speiseöl","süßsaure Soße"],"s":["In a large bowl, combine meat, water chestnuts, onion, eggs, soy sauce, salt, and pepper. Mix well and set aside.","On a clean, dry surface, place one egg roll wrapper with one corner facing you (like a baseball diamond).","Place about 1 tablespoon of the meat mixture in the center of the wrapper.","Dip your fingers in a glass of water and lightly wet the corner pointing away from you (second base).","Fold the corner closest to you (home base) over the mixture, then fold the side corners over that and roll away from your body. The wet corner should seal the roll.","Repeat the filling and shaping process with the remaining ingredients.","Place the rolls in large zip-close plastic bags and freeze overnight.","In a large saucepan, heat the oil to about 350°F (175°C) or until it begins to shimmer and the oil bubbles lightly when a wooden chopstick is inserted.","Using tongs, place each frozen lumpia roll in the hot oil and fry until brown, about 3 to 4 minutes. Use tongs to turn rolls to ensure even cooking.","Remove the rolls to a plate covered with paper towels to absorb excess oil."],"x":["Serve with sweet and sour sauce."],"desc":"Lumpia are a variety of fried Filipino spring rolls, and they make a tasty dish.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lumpia_(Fried_Filipino_Spring_Rolls)","i":"wb-en-2576","im":["4/43/Loenpia_Semarang.JPG/960px-Loenpia_Semarang.JPG","Midori","CC BY-SA 3.0","Loenpia Semarang.JPG","w"],"on":"Lumpia (Fried Filipino Spring Rolls)","og":["1½ pounds (680 g) ground chicken or pork","⅓ cup chopped water chestnuts","½ cup chopped onion","4 eggs","¼ cup soy sauce","salt and freshly ground black pepper, to taste","2 packages (about 40 ea.) small-to-medium size egg roll wrappers (wonton wrappers)","4 cups cooking oil","Sweet and sour sauce"]},{"n":"Lumpiang Shanghai (philippinische Frühlingsrollen mit Schweinefleisch)","c":"fleisch","k":"Philippinen","p":6,"t":60,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["½ kg Schweinehack","1 mittelgroße Knoblauchzehe, fein gehackt","1 Möhre, gerieben","1 Ei, verquirlt","Wasser","1 Packung Lumpia- oder Frühlingsrollenblätter","Pflanzenöl","1 Tasse Bananenketchup"],"s":["Combine the pork, garlic, and carrot in a mixing bowl.","Add the egg, and mix well to combine.","Lay one wrapper flat on your work surface. Place a small amount of the filling mixture on it, shaped like a log.","Fold two opposite sides of the wrapper over the filling to enclose the two ends of the filling. Then, use the rest of the of wrapper to roll everything up length-wise.","Moisten the edge of the wrapper and press it against the roll to seal and prevent it from unwrapping.","Repeat the filling and rolling steps with the remaining filling and wrappers.","Deep fry the rolls in the oil until golden brown all over and cooked through.","Serve with the banana ketchup."],"x":[],"desc":"A version of lumpia that Filipinos love to share at a party.","img":"100Cuisine of Bulacan 06.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lumpiang_Shanghai_(Filipino_Pork_Spring_Rolls)","i":"wb-en-2577","im":["1/1c/100Cuisine_of_Bulacan_06.jpg/960px-100Cuisine_of_Bulacan_06.jpg","Judgefloro","CC0","100Cuisine of Bulacan 06.jpg","r"],"on":"Lumpiang Shanghai (Filipino Pork Spring Rolls)","og":["½ kg ground pork","1 medium-sized clove of garlic, minced","1 carrot, shredded","1 egg, beaten","Water","1 pack lumpia or spring roll wrappers","Vegetable oil","1 cup banana ketchup"]},{"n":"Luwombo (ugandisches gedämpftes Fleisch mit Gemüse)","c":"fleisch","k":"Uganda","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["450 g Rind- oder Hähnchenfleisch, in Stücke geschnitten","1 Tasse gewürfelte rote Zwiebeln","1 EL fein gehackter Knoblauch","1 EL fein gehackter Ingwer","Cayennepfeffer","2 EL Erdnusspaste (oder Erdnussbutter)","1 EL Erdnusspulver (oder Erdnusspulver)","2 EL Palm- oder Erdnussöl","1 Tasse gewürfelte Süßkartoffeln","1 Tasse gewürfelter Maniok","1 Tasse gewürfelte grüne Bananen (Matooke, Kochbananen)","1 Tasse gewürfelte Aubergine","2 EL gemahlene Flusskrebse (optional, für mehr Geschmack)","1 Tasse frische Kokosmilch oder aus der Dose","1 Tasse selbstgemachte Hühner- oder Gemüsebrühe","Salz, nach Geschmack","Bananenblätter, zum Einwickeln"],"s":["In a large bowl, marinate the meat chunks with minced garlic, minced ginger, groundnut paste, groundnut powder, ground crayfish (if using), salt, and cayenne pepper. Allow the meat to marinate for at least 30 minutes to absorb the flavorful blend.","Heat palm oil or groundnut oil in a large pot or skillet over medium-high heat. Add the marinated meat and cook until beautifully browned on all sides, releasing an enticing aroma.","Stir in the diced onions and cook until they soften and become fragrant.","Add the diced sweet potatoes, cassava, green bananas, and eggplant to the pot.","Pour in the fresh coconut milk and homemade chicken or vegetable broth, ensuring all the ingredients are immersed in the rich and creamy goodness. Bring the mixture to a gentle simmer.","Reduce the heat to low, cover the pot with a lid, and let the ingredients steam for about 1–2 hours until the meat is tender.","Meanwhile, prepare the banana leaves by briefly holding them over an open flame to soften and make them pliable for wrapping.","Take a portion of the steamed mixture and place it in the center of a banana leaf, folding the leaf around the mixture to create a packet. Repeat with the remaining mixture and banana leaves.","Once all the packets are prepared, return them to the steamer or large pot with a steaming rack.","Steam the luwombo packets for an additional 30 minutes.","Serve the luwombo packets on individual plates."],"x":["Luwombo is often enjoyed with steamed rice or matooke, a dish made from green bananas, to complete the authentic Ugandan dining experience.","Luwombo offers a well-rounded nutritional profile, boasting proteins from the meat and an array of vitamins and minerals from the diverse vegetables used."],"desc":"Luwombo, a quintessential Ugandan dish, showcases the rich flavors and vibrant culinary traditions of the country. This unique cooking method involves steaming meat, vegetables, and a delightful blend of local spices in banana leaves, infusing the dish with an unmistakably authentic aroma and taste.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Luwombo_(Ugandan_Steamed_Meat_and_Vegetables)","i":"wb-en-2578","im":["4/4c/Chicken_Luwombo.JPG/960px-Chicken_Luwombo.JPG","Namuganyi","CC BY-SA 4.0","Chicken Luwombo.JPG","w"],"on":"Luwombo (Ugandan Steamed Meat and Vegetables)","og":["1 lb (450 g) beef or chicken, cut into chunks","1 cup diced red onions","1 tablespoon minced garlic","1 tablespoon minced ginger","Cayenne pepper","2 tablespoons groundnut paste (or peanut butter)","1 tablespoon groundnut powder (or peanut powder)","2 tablespoons palm oil or groundnut oil","1 cup diced sweet potatoes","1 cup diced cassava","1 cup diced green bananas (matooke)","1 cup diced eggplant","2 tablespoons ground crayfish (optional, for added flavor)","1 cup fresh or canned coconut milk","1 cup homemade chicken or vegetable broth","Salt, to taste","Banana leaves, for wrapping"]},{"n":"Lángos (ungarisches frittiertes Fladenbrot)","c":"brot","k":"Ungarn","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["500 g Weizenmehl","Instant-Trockenhefe","4 Eier","4 EL Joghurt oder saure Sahne","2 TL Salz","Schmalz oder Rapsöl"],"s":["Combine the flour and yeast. Add the eggs, then mix the yoghurt to make a dough.","Add the salt, and knead until the dough is pliant and not too sticky, adding more flour or yogurt as necessary. The correct texture is really a matter of trial-and-error. It's not unlike an egg pasta dough, but it's rather less stiff.","Transfer the dough to an oiled bowl. Cover and let rise overnight in a cool location, like the refrigerator.","Gently deflate the dough.","When you're ready to cook, heat about 2 inches of lard in a pan. The oil should be hot enough that when you put a very small piece of the dough into it, it drops to the bottom, and immediately rises up to the surface frying.","Take a lump of the dough (roughly a bit bigger than a ping-pong ball, but rather smaller than a tennis-ball) and flatten it into a disk shape.","Do this by hand rather than using a rolling pin—just keep pressing it between fingers and thumbs, and turning it round and round. Make the centre of the disk fairly thin, and the edge rather thicker. It should end up about 8 inches across if possible.","Don't worry over-much about getting it too circular and even; the hand-made look is all part of their attraction.","Carefully slide the disk of dough into the hot oil and let it fry for 30 seconds or so. It should start to puff up as it fries; if it doesn't, either the oil isn't hot enough, or the disk is too thick.","Carefully turn the dough over, and fry for another 30 seconds or so. Turn it over and see if the underside is golden brown or not. If not, fry for a while longer until both sides are golden brown, with a 'puffed-up' surface.","Adjust the frying times for subsequent ones accordingly.","Remove from the hot oil and drain away any excess."],"x":["Lángos are traditionally served with a pungent fresh garlic dressing. This is made by mincing up several cloves of garlic and mixing them into a small amount of oil and water, which is left to infuse for a while. You just spread the garlic dressing over the hot bread and eat.","You can also top lángos with crème fraîche, sour cream, or thick yoghurt (as a substitute for something called tejföl that you can't get outside of Hungary), and grated cheese. Fried lardons or diced pancetta are a good topping too.","Three or four of these will leave you feeling pretty full, but if you've really hungry you could also have some good continental sausage (ideally Hungarian kolbász, naturally) to go with them."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Lángos_(Hungarian_Fried_Flatbread)","i":"wb-en-2579","im":["f/f3/Langos_Eger_Hungary.jpg/960px-Langos_Eger_Hungary.jpg","sikeri","CC BY-SA 4.0","Langos Eger Hungary.jpg","w"],"on":"Lángos (Hungarian Fried Flatbread)","og":["500 g all-purpose flour","Instant yeast","4 eggs","4 tbsp yogurt or sour cream","2 tsp salt","Lard or canola oil"]},{"n":"M'batata (Süßkartoffel-Erdnuss-Suppe)","c":"suppen","k":"Afrika","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 EL Pflanzenöl","1 Zwiebel, gehackt","2 Knoblauchzehen, fein gehackt","2 große Süßkartoffeln, geschält und gewürfelt","4 Tassen Gemüse- oder Hühnerbrühe","1 Tasse ungesalzene Erdnüsse","1 TL gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","1 TL gemahlener Koriander","½ TL Chilipulver (optional, für Schärfe)","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","1 Tasse Kokosmilch (optional)","gehackter frischer Koriander oder Petersilie zum Garnieren (optional)"],"s":["Heat the vegetable oil in a large pot over medium heat. Add the chopped onion and minced garlic, and sauté until the onion becomes translucent and fragrant.","Add the cubed sweet potatoes to the pot and stir them together with the onions and garlic for a couple of minutes, allowing the flavors to blend.","Pour in the vegetable or chicken broth, ensuring that the sweet potatoes are fully submerged. Bring the mixture to a boil and then reduce the heat to a simmer.","Let it cook until the sweet potatoes are tender and easily mashed with a fork, usually around 15–20 minutes.","While the sweet potatoes are cooking, toast the peanuts in a dry skillet over medium heat until they become fragrant and slightly browned. This step helps to enhance the flavor of the peanuts.","Transfer the toasted peanuts to a blender or food processor and process them until they form a smooth peanut butter-like consistency. You may need to scrape down the sides of the blender or food processor a few times to ensure everything is well blended.","Once the sweet potatoes are cooked, remove the pot from the heat and allow it to cool slightly. Use a potato masher or the back of a fork to mash the sweet potatoes until they are smooth and creamy in texture.","Return the pot to low heat and add the peanut butter to the mashed sweet potatoes, stirring well to combine. The soup will become thick and creamy.","Add the ground cumin, ground coriander, chili powder (if desired), salt, and pepper to the pot. Stir everything together, allowing the flavors to meld for a few minutes.","If using coconut milk, pour it into the pot and stir it into the soup, adding an extra layer of creaminess and flavor. Simmer the soup for an additional 5 minutes, stirring occasionally.","Taste the soup and adjust the seasonings as needed, adding more salt, pepper, or spices to suit your preference.","Ladle the m'batata into bowls and garnish with chopped fresh cilantro or parsley, if desired."],"x":["M'batata is best served hot, and it pairs well with crusty bread or a side salad. This comforting soup is a wonderful representation of Central African cuisine, combining the earthy sweetness of sweet potatoes with the richness of peanuts to create a truly delicious and satisfying dish."],"desc":"M'batata is a flavorful and creamy soup popular in the Central African Republic. It combines the natural sweetness of sweet potatoes with the richness of peanuts, resulting in a comforting and nourishing dish.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:M'batata_(Sweet_Potato_And_Peanut_Soup)","i":"wb-en-2580","im":["f/ff/Fufu.jpg/960px-Fufu.jpg","Londonsista","CC BY-SA 3.0","Fufu.jpg","w"],"on":"M'batata (Sweet Potato And Peanut Soup)","og":["1 tablespoon vegetable oil","1 onion, chopped","2 garlic cloves, minced","2 large sweet potatoes, peeled and cubed","4 cups vegetable or chicken broth","1 cup unsalted peanuts","1 teaspoon ground cumin","1 teaspoon ground coriander","½ teaspoon chile powder (optional, for heat)","Salt to taste","Pepper to taste","1 cup coconut milk (optional)","Chopped fresh cilantro or parsley for garnish (optional)"]},{"n":"M'semen (algerisches Schicht-Fladenbrot)","c":"brot","k":"Algerien","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse Weizenmehl","1 Tasse Hartweizengrieß","1 TL Zucker","Salz","¼ TL Instant-Trockenhefe","1 ½ Tassen warmes Wasser","Pflanzenöl"],"s":["Combine both flours, sugar, salt, and yeast in a bowl.","Gradually mix in the warm water until you get a soft dough. If it feels too sticky, mix in a little more all-purpose flour. If too dry, mix in some more water.","On a lightly-floured surface, knead the dough for 10 minutes or until it is smooth.","Divide the dough into smaller pieces, and roll each out into very thin rounds.","Brush each dough round with oil.","Fold the rounds into square envelope shapes, making 4 folds into the center.","Cook each flatbread in a hot, lightly-greased skillet until browned."],"x":[],"desc":"Algerians are very fond of m'semen, a flatbread made from basic ingredients like flour, semolina, butter, and water. The dough can be sticky to the touch while folding, so oiling the hands is necessary. Some people also fill the pancakes with minced meat and vegetables before frying in oil until the","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:M'semen_(Layered_Algerian_Flatbread)","i":"wb-en-2581","im":["c/cd/Flatbread.JPG/960px-Flatbread.JPG","Jonathunder","CC BY-SA 3.0","Flatbread.JPG","w"],"on":"M'semen (Layered Algerian Flatbread)","og":["1 cup all-purpose flour","1 cup semolina flour","1 tsp sugar","Salt","¼ tsp instant yeast","1 ½ cups warm water","Vegetable oil"]},{"n":"MPT (Mozzarella-Nudeln mit Tomate und Basilikum)","c":"veggie","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["2 Mozzarellakugeln (Kuh oder Büffel)","etwa 10 bis 15 kleine Tomaten oder 4 bis 5 größere Tomaten (etwa die gleiche Menge wie Mozzarella)","eine gute Handvoll Basilikumblätter (etwa 15 bis 20 Blätter)","Olivenöl","Salz","schwarzer Pfeffer","250 g frische Eiernudeln"],"s":["Roughly chop the mozzarella and the tomatoes and put them in a big salad-type bowl.","Tear up the basil and sprinkle it over the mozzarella and tomatoes.","Drizzle on lots of extra virgin olive oil (at least 3 tablespoons).","Add a good amount of salt and just a little black pepper. The salt will start to leach moisture out from the other ingredients and create a sauce.","Let rest for at least 30 minutes.","Boil the egg pasta until al dente, then drain.","Add the hot pasta to the bowl of other ingredients. Toss well until the pasta is well-coated. Serve."],"x":[],"desc":"This is a delicious and quick recipe for a sunny day, or to bring back a little memory of summer. It's served warm so may not suit a winter evening! The combination of flavours (milky mozzarella, eggy pasta, sweet tomato and spicy basil) is just wonderful. The secret here is to prepare all the ingre","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:MPT_(Mozzarella_Pasta_with_Tomato_and_Basil)","i":"wb-en-2582","im":["4/4d/MPT-4_in_Ukraine_02.jpg/960px-MPT-4_in_Ukraine_02.jpg","Novoklimov","CC0","MPT-4 in Ukraine 02.jpg","c"],"on":"MPT (Mozzarella Pasta with Tomato and Basil)","og":["2 mozzarella balls (cow or buffalo)","About 10–15 small tomatoes or 4–5 larger tomatoes (you need about the same amount as the mozzarella)","A good handful of basil leaves (about 15–20 leaves)","Olive oil","Salt","Black pepper","250 g fresh egg pasta"]},{"n":"Ma'amoul (arabisches gefülltes Gebäck)","c":"brot","k":"Nahost","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Pistazienfüllung","250 g fein gehackte Pistazien","115 g Zucker","1 EL Rosenwasser","#Walnussfüllung","250 g fein gehackte Walnüsse","115 g Zucker","1 EL gemahlener Zimt","#Dattelfüllung","500 g entsteinte Datteln, gehackt","½ Teetasse Wasser","Butter (optional)","#Gebäck","500 g Weizenmehl (Type 405) (bis zu einem Viertel des Mehls kann durch feinen Grieß ersetzt werden)","2 EL weißer Zucker","1 Prise Salz (optional)","Backpulver (optional)","250 g ungesalzene Butter (am besten Butter aus der Normandie)","1–2 EL Rosen- oder Orangenblütenwasser","2 EL Wasser oder Milch","Puderzucker"],"s":["Mix chopped pistachios with sugar and rose water.","Mix chopped walnuts with sugar and cinnamon.","Combine the chopped dates and water in a pot. Bring to a boil, squashing the mixture against the side of the pan with a wooden spoon until approximately uniform in consistency. Mix in the butter if using.","Blend with an electric chopper if desired to make a smoother paste. Allow to cool.","Sift the flour into a mixing bowl. Mix with the white sugar, and a pinch of salt if desired. Some people add a very small quantity of baking powder.","Work in the butter until the consistency is as uniform as possible; one way is to heat the butter in the microwave first until it is nearly melted, and then mix it with the flour into a sort of crumble.","Cover and leave at room temperature for several hours to overnight.","Break up the dough with your fingers, and add the rose water or orange flower water and 2 tbsp water or milk until it is malleable. Knead the whole into a smooth ball.","Take a walnut-sized ball of the dough, stick your thumb into it, and hollow out into a cup shape so that the walls are as thin as possible without breaking.","Insert filling to about three-quarters full, and pinch the aperture closed. Pat gently into a ball, not letting the walls break.","Decorate the ball on top with tweezers or the prongs of a fork. Alternatively, pat it into a wooden mould and flatten the exposed bottom surface, then bang the mould face down on the work surface to extract the moulded pastry.","Repeat the assembly steps until all the dough and the filling is used. If at any stage the remaining dough shows signs of drying out, knead in a little more water or milk.","Place the pastries on an ungreased baking sheet and bake in a preheated oven (180°C / 355°F; 160°C if a fan oven) for 20 minutes: they must not be allowed to become hard or brown.","In fact they should look a little moist and underdone when removed from the oven: they will steam off and harden as they cool.","Leave the pastries to cool, and dust with icing sugar when cold. Keep in a sealed plastic box or biscuit tin."],"x":["Some people use ground almonds, with or without green food colouring, instead of pistachios for the filling."],"desc":"Ma'amoul are pastries filled with dates or nuts, and they are popular throughout the Arab world. They can be made in special ma'amoul moulds, and there are three shapes of mould. The flattish circular shape is used for date ma’amoul; the round domed shape for walnut ma’amoul; the long oval for pista","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Ma'amoul_(Arabian_Filled_Pastries)","i":"wb-en-2583","im":["9/9e/Mamoul_biscotti_libanesi.jpg/960px-Mamoul_biscotti_libanesi.jpg","fugzu","CC BY 2.0","Mamoul biscotti libanesi.jpg","w"],"on":"Ma'amoul (Arabian Filled Pastries)","og":["#Pistachio filling","½ lb (250 g) finely-chopped pistachios","¼ lb sugar","1 tbsp rose water","#Walnut filling","½ lb (250 g) finely-chopped walnuts","¼ lb sugar","1 tbsp ground cinnamon","#Date filling","1 lb (500 g) pitted dates, chopped","½ teacup water","Butter (optional)","#Pastries","1 lb (500 g) plain white flour (up to a quarter of the flour may be replaced with fine semolina)","2 tbsp white sugar","1 pinch of salt (optional)","Baking powder (optional)","½ lb (250 g) unsalted butter (Normandy butter is best)","1–2 tbsp rose water or orange flower water","2 tbsp water or milk","Icing sugar"]},{"n":"Makkaroni-Auflauf","c":"beilagen","k":"Karibik","p":4,"t":45,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Packung getrocknete Makkaroni (225 g)","2 Eier","2 Tassen geriebener Käse","1 ½ Tassen Kondensmilch (ungesüßt)","1 kleine Zwiebel, fein gehackt","1 Möhre, gerieben","1 TL Salz","¼ TL weißer Pfeffer","1 TL gelber Senf (amerikanisch)","1 Stückchen ungesalzene Butter, geschmolzen","Semmelbrösel"],"s":["Boil macaroni in salted water until tender; drain.","Beat eggs until fluffy.","Combine macaroni, eggs, cheese, milk, onion, carrot, salt, white pepper, mustard, and butter.","Pour into a greased baking dish and sprinkle shredded cheese and bread crumbs evenly on top.","Bake at 175°C (350°F) until firm (about 30 minutes). A fork or metal skewer should come out dry when you press it all the way through the pie."],"x":["Macaroni pie can be enhanced further by adding ingredients such as tomato, chopped herbs, minced beef, or roasted onions. Also try using a few varieties of cheese together.","Usually best when the surface has browned to an even colour."],"desc":"Macaroni pie is a side dish that goes well with stewed chicken, callaloo or any stewed peas like pigeon peas or lentils. It can also be enjoyed on its own.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Macaroni_Pie","i":"wb-en-2584","im":["8/8c/Macaroni_pie_1.jpg/960px-Macaroni_pie_1.jpg","Wendy Harman from Washington DC, USA","CC BY 2.0","Macaroni pie 1.jpg","w"],"on":"Macaroni Pie","og":["1 package (225 grams / 8 oz) dried macaroni pasta","2 eggs","2 cups grated cheese","1½ cups evaporated milk","1 small onion, finely chopped","1 carrot, grated","1 tsp salt","¼ tsp white pepper","1 tsp prepared yellow mustard","1 pat of unsalted butter, melted","Breadcrumbs"]},{"n":"Makkaronisalat","c":"salate","k":"","p":8,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["½ Tasse Mayonnaise","1 TL Senfpulver","1 TL Zucker","2 EL Apfelessig","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","450 g Hörnchennudeln, gegart, abgetropft, und gekühlt","⅓ Tasse gehackte rote Zwiebel","⅓ Tasse gehackter Staudensellerie"],"s":["Whisk together mayonnaise, mustard, sugar, and vinegar in small bowl. Add salt and pepper to taste.","Toss the pasta, onion, and celery in a large bowl. Pour the dressing over top, and toss to combine.","Cool before serving."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Macaroni_Salad","i":"wb-en-2585","im":["1/1d/Macaroni_salad.jpg/960px-Macaroni_salad.jpg","Bill McChesney from USA","CC BY 2.0","Macaroni salad.jpg","w"],"on":"Macaroni Salad","og":["½ cup mayonnaise","1 teaspoon dry mustard","1 teaspoon sugar","2 Tablespoons cider vinegar","Salt to taste","Pepper to taste","1 lb elbow macaroni pasta, cooked, drained, and chilled","⅓ cup chopped red onion","⅓ cup chopped celery"]},{"n":"Makkaroni mit Käse (überbacken)","c":"beilagen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["#Boden","227 g Hörnchennudeln","3 EL Butter","3 EL Mehl","1 EL Senfpulver","3 Tassen Milch","1 rote Zwiebel, fein gehackt","2 TL Tabasco","1 Lorbeerblatt","½ TL Paprikapulver","1 Ei (Größe M)","340 g würziger Cheddar, gerieben","1 TL Salz","frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","#Belag","3 EL Butter","1 Tasse Panko-Paniermehl"],"s":["Preheat oven to 350 °F.","In a large pot of boiling, salted water, cook the pasta until it is al dente.","While the pasta is cooking, melt the butter in a separate pot.","Whisk in the flour and mustard and keep it moving for about five minutes. Make sure it is free of lumps.","Stir in the milk, onion, bay leaf, and paprika. Simmer for ten minutes and remove the bay leaf.","Temper in the egg.","Stir in ¾ of the cheese.","Season with salt and pepper.","Fold the macaroni into the mix and pour into a 2-quart casserole dish.","Top with remaining cheese.","Melt the butter in a sauté pan, add breadcrumbs, and toss to coat.","Top the macaroni with the bread crumbs.","Bake for 30 minutes.","Remove from oven and rest for 10 minutes before serving."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Macaroni_and_Cheese_(Baked)","i":"wb-en-2586","im":["4/44/Original_Mac_n_Cheese_.jpg/960px-Original_Mac_n_Cheese_.jpg","Texasfoodgawker","CC BY-SA 4.0","Original Mac n Cheese .jpg","w"],"on":"Macaroni and Cheese (Baked)","og":["#Base","½ lb (227 g) dry elbow macaroni","3 Tbsp butter","3 Tbsp flour","1 Tbsp powdered mustard","3 cups milk","1 red onion, finely chopped","2 tsp Tabasco pepper sauce","1 bay leaf","½ tsp paprika","1 standard egg","12 oz (340 g) sharp cheddar, shredded","1 tsp salt","Fresh black pepper","#Topping","3 Tbsp butter","1 cup panko bread crumbs"]},{"n":"Makkaroni mit Käse (aus der Mikrowelle)","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["ungekochte Makkaroni","Käse, gerieben","½ Tasse Milch","Salz","Pfeffer","Schnittlauch, gehackt","Wasser"],"s":["Add macaroni in a bowl and add water for the macaroni to absorb. Cook in the microwave for 3 minutes.","Remove from the microwave. Add cheese and milk then stir. Insert into the microwave again for 30 seconds.","Add salt and pepper","Add chives for garnish"],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Macaroni_and_Cheese_(Microwaved)","i":"wb-en-2587","im":["4/44/Original_Mac_n_Cheese_.jpg/960px-Original_Mac_n_Cheese_.jpg","Texasfoodgawker","CC BY-SA 4.0","Original Mac n Cheese .jpg","w"],"on":"Macaroni and Cheese (Microwaved)","og":["Uncooked macaroni pasta","Cheese, grated","½ cup milk","Salt","Pepper","Chives, chopped","Water"]},{"n":"Makkaroni mit Käse (vegan)","c":"beilagen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":2,"l":"en","g":["450 g Makkaroni","½ Tasse Margarine","½ Tasse Mehl","1 Tasse Hefeflocken","3 ½ Tassen Wasser oder Reismilch, kochend","1 ½ TL Salz","1 ½ TL Knoblauchpulver","1 Prise Kurkuma","2 EL Sojasoße"],"s":["Bring 4 quarts of water to a boil, add salt to taste, and add the macaroni.","Melt the margarine over low heat. Beat in flour with a wire whisk. Continue to beat over medium heat until mixture is smooth and bubbly.","Whisk in the 3 ½ cups water. Then, add salt, garlic powder, soy sauce, and turmeric to the liquid.","The sauce should cook until it thickens and bubbles. When that happens, beat in nutritional yeast flakes; if the sauce is too thick, add more water.","When the macaroni is cooked, drain and add the sauce. Serve immediately."],"x":["For a variation, add mustard to the sauce."],"desc":"Macaroni and nutritional yeast is a vegan alternative to macaroni and cheese.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Macaroni_and_Cheese_(Vegan)","i":"wb-en-2588","im":["4/44/Original_Mac_n_Cheese_.jpg/960px-Original_Mac_n_Cheese_.jpg","Texasfoodgawker","CC BY-SA 4.0","Original Mac n Cheese .jpg","w"],"on":"Macaroni and Cheese (Vegan)","og":["1 pound dry macaroni pasta","½ cup margarine","½ cup flour","1 cup nutritional yeast flakes","3 ½ cups water or rice milk, boiling","1 ½ tsp salt","1 ½ tsp garlic powder","1 pinch of turmeric","2 Tbsp soy sauce"]},{"n":"Makkaroni mit Käse I","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["125 g Butter","70 g Mehl","1 l Milch, erwärmt","125 g Cheddar","125 g Parmesan oder Monterey Jack","½ TL Cayennepfeffer, oder nach Geschmack","450 g Makkaroni, gekocht und abgetropft"],"s":["Make a roux using the butter and flour.","Add the heated milk, and whisk until smooth to complete the white sauce.","Mix in the cheese and cayenne pepper.","Mix the cheese sauce into the cooked macaroni noodles until well-coated."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Macaroni_and_Cheese_I","i":"wb-en-2589","im":["4/44/Original_Mac_n_Cheese_.jpg/960px-Original_Mac_n_Cheese_.jpg","Texasfoodgawker","CC BY-SA 4.0","Original Mac n Cheese .jpg","w"],"on":"Macaroni and Cheese I","og":["½ cup (8 tbsp / 1 stick / 125 g / 4.4 oz) butter","½ cup (70 g / 2.5 oz) flour","4 cups (1 L / 1.1 quart) milk, heated","1 cup (125 g / 4.4 oz) cheddar cheese","1 cup (125 g / 4.4 oz) Parmesan or Monterey Jack cheese","½ tsp cayenne pepper, or to taste","1 pound (450 g) macaroni noodles, boiled and drained"]},{"n":"Makkaroni mit Käse II","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["230 g Hörnchennudeln","Salz, nach Geschmack","½ Tasse Milch","½ Tasse Käse (nach Wahl des Kochs), gerieben","¼ Tasse Butter","1 Ei","Spritzer getrocknete Petersilie und Oregano"],"s":["Fill a pot with water, and add macaroni and salt. Bring to boil, stirring occasionally.","While waiting for the pasta to cook, heat the milk in a pot. Stir the grated cheese into milk. This should create a basic cheese sauce. If too thin, add more grated cheese; if too thick, add more milk.","When pasta becomes tender (chef's discretion), drain.","Melt the butter in a pot, and stir in the drained macaroni until pasta is completely coated. Crack the raw egg into the mixture, and stir until completely incorporated. Add cheese sauce and herbs.","Stir well, and serve hot."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Macaroni_and_Cheese_II","i":"wb-en-2590","im":["4/44/Original_Mac_n_Cheese_.jpg/960px-Original_Mac_n_Cheese_.jpg","Texasfoodgawker","CC BY-SA 4.0","Original Mac n Cheese .jpg","w"],"on":"Macaroni and Cheese II","og":["8 oz elbow macaroni","Salt to taste","½ cup milk","½ cup cheese (of the chef's preference), grated","¼ cup butter","1 egg","dash of dried parsley and oregano"]},{"n":"Machacado con huevo (Eier mit gezupftem Trockenfleisch)","c":"fruehstueck","k":"Mexiko","p":10,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 EL Butter oder Margarine","6 große Eier, leicht verquirlt","2 Tassen Füllung aus gezupftem Rindfleisch","10 weiche Weizentortillas in Taco-Größe (20 cm), erwärmt","1 Dose Refried Beans (Bohnenmus) (450 g), erwärmt","230 g geriebener Cheddar oder Monterey Jack","Salsa als Beilage"],"s":["Heat butter in large skillet over medium-high heat.","Add eggs; cook, stirring frequently, for 2–3 minutes or until eggs just begin to set.","Stir in shredded beef filling. Cook, stirring occasionally, for 2 to 3 minutes or until eggs are cooked and beef is heated through.","Serve eggs with tortillas, beans, cheese, and salsa."],"x":["Machacado con huevo can be served in a big bowl, and with some soft tortillas at hand can be prepared in your plate, can be served in the table as tacos, or can be eaten without using tortillas at all.","Queso fundido con chorizo (melted cheese with chorizo) is also something that can be found at the table when eating machacado con huevo. It is usually served at the table in a pan, and added to the taco."],"desc":"Machacado con huevo is a dish which consists of shredded dry beef that is scrambled with eggs. Its name means \"shredded with eggs\" in Spanish. The shredded dry beef, carne seca, is said to have originated in the town of Ciénega de Flores, about an hour north of Monterrey, Mexico. The early settlers ","img":"Machacado con huevo.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Machacado_con_Huevo_(Eggs_with_Shredded_Beef)","i":"wb-en-2591","im":["1/1a/Machacado_con_huevo.jpg/960px-Machacado_con_huevo.jpg","C","CC BY-SA 2.5","Machacado con huevo.jpg","r"],"on":"Machacado con Huevo (Eggs with Shredded Beef)","og":["1 tablespoon butter or margarine","6 large eggs, lightly beaten","2 cups shredded beef filling","10 ea. 8-inch soft taco-size flour tortillas, warmed","1 can (16 ounces) refried beans, warmed","2 cups (8 ounces) shredded cheddar or Monterey Jack Cheese","Salsa for accompaniment"]},{"n":"Macho-Nachos","c":"snacks","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["scharfe Chilisoße","1 Dose fertiger Bohnendip (260 g)","Tortillachips","geriebener Cheddar","Guacamole (fertig gekauft)","saure Sahne","Jalapeños in Ringen"],"s":["Stir cayenne pepper into the bean dip to taste. Spread this mixture on chips, and transfer to a baking sheet.","Sprinkle chips with cheese, and bake at 400°F for 2 minutes or until cheese melts.","Top with guacamole dip and sour cream; garnish liberally with sliced jalapeño peppers."],"x":[],"desc":"This recipe is attributed to Jack Cochran.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Macho_Nachos","i":"wb-en-2592","im":["8/87/Nachos-cheese.jpg/960px-Nachos-cheese.jpg","chee.hong from Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia","CC BY 2.0","Nachos-cheese.jpg","w"],"on":"Macho Nachos","og":["Cayenne pepper sauce","1 can (9 oz) prepared bean dip","Tortilla chips","Shredded cheddar cheese","Guacamole (ready-made)","Sour cream","Sliced jalapeño peppers"]},{"n":"Madbucha (nordafrikanische Paprika mit Tomaten)","c":"beilagen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["Öl","2 Zwiebeln, gehackt","2 Zehen Knoblauch, gehackt","15 Tomaten, gewürfelt","10 Paprikaschoten, in kleine Stücke geschnitten","5 Chilischoten, klein gehackt","330 ml Tomatenmark","Salz","Pfeffer","Kreuzkümmel","Petersilie","Oregano"],"s":["Take a pot that is big enough for all of the above ingredients, cover the bottom with oil, and put it on a flame.","When the oil gets hot, add the onion and garlic.","When they start to fry, add the rest of the vegetables and salt.","Mix it up a bit and cover the pot.","Leave it to cook, mixing it every so often, until the level of the liquid is higher than the level of the vegetables.","Drain off most (but not all) the liquid.","Add the tomato paste and the spices.","Mix, and let it cool."],"x":["When chopping the peppers, you want them small but not so small that they disappear when cooked.","The peppers can be any color, but red is traditional."],"desc":"Madbucha or matbucha is a North African dish of stewed tomatoes and peppers. It can be used as a side dish with meats, as well as put on bread or white rice. There's more than one way to make it, and the following recipe is a family recipe.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Madbucha_(North_African_Peppers_and_Tomatoes)","i":"wb-en-2593","on":"Madbucha (North African Peppers and Tomatoes)","og":["Oil","2 onions, chopped","2 cloves garlic, chopped","15 tomatoes, cubed","10 bell peppers, cut into small pieces","5 chile peppers, chopped small","330 ml canned tomato paste","Salt","Pepper","Cumin","Parsley","Oregano"]},{"n":"Madeleines","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":36,"t":30,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 Eier","100 g Zucker","1 Prise Salz","100 g Weizenmehl","1 TL Backpulver","abgeriebene Schale von 1 Zitrone","75 g geschmolzene Butter"],"s":["Beat the eggs, sugar and salt in a mixing bowl until frothy.","Combine the flour, baking powder, and lemon zest, and fold into the egg mixture. Fold in the melted butter.","Divide the dough into greased madeleine molds, keeping in mind that the dough will rise in the oven to fill the molds.","Bake in a preheated oven at 180°C / 350°F for 12–15 minutes until the cakes are springy but not browned.","Cool and unmold the madeleines.","Serve fresh."],"x":[],"desc":"Madeleines small French cakes baked in special baking trays that give them a shell-like shape. The Spanish counterparts, Madalenas, are sometimes served in paper cases and then resemble muffins.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Madeleines","i":"wb-en-2594","im":["2/23/Madeleines_de_Commercy.jpg/960px-Madeleines_de_Commercy.jpg","myself (Bernard Leprêtre)","CC BY-SA 2.5","Madeleines de Commercy.jpg","c"],"og":["4 eggs","100 g white granulated sugar","1 pinch of salt","100 g all-purpose flour","1 teaspoon baking powder","grated zest of 1 lemon","75 g melted butter"]},{"n":"Madras-Filterkaffee","c":"getraenke","k":"Indien","p":1,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["¼ Tasse Wasser","½–2 TL Instantkaffee mit Zichorie","¾ Tasse Milch","Zucker (optional)"],"s":["Bring the water to a boil, and stir in the coffee. Ensure there are no lumps.","Bring the milk to a boil.","Add the coffee mixture to the milk, and sweeten with sugar to taste.","While the coffee is still boiling hot, pour it into a mug or, preferably, a stainless steel tumbler. While pouring the coffee, slowly raise the saucepan so the coffee falls into the mug from a height of about 1–1½ ft.","This will cause the coffee to froth like espresso.","If desired, you can dip a teaspoon in the coffee and lightly spread a few drops of it over the froth in the mug.","Serve piping hot."],"x":["Filter coffee in India is actually made in a closed steel container called a coffee filter."],"desc":"Traditional Madras filter coffee requires the use of specific fresh-roasted coffee beans and chicory roots, which are not always available outside India. This recipe uses Indian instant coffee that has chicory in it, which is available in some Indian stores and supermarkets. Nestle Bru instant coffe","img":"Indian filter coffee in Dabarah.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Madras_Filter_Coffee","i":"wb-en-2595","im":["8/84/Indian_filter_coffee_in_Dabarah.jpg/500px-Indian_filter_coffee_in_Dabarah.jpg","unbekannt","CC BY-SA 3.0","Indian filter coffee in Dabarah.jpg","r"],"on":"Madras Filter Coffee","og":["¼ cup water","½–2 tsp instant coffee with chicory root","¾ cup milk","Sugar (optional)"]},{"n":"Maffé (westafrikanischer Erdnusseintopf) I","c":"suppen","k":"Afrika","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 EL Pflanzenöl","450 g Rind- oder Hähnchenfleisch, gewürfelt","1 große Zwiebel, fein gehackt","3 Knoblauchzehen, fein gehackt","1 Tasse cremige Erdnussbutter","1 TL gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","1 TL Paprikapulver","1 TL Chilipulver (auf die gewünschte Schärfe anpassen)","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","1 Dose gewürfelte Tomaten (400 g)","4 Tassen Rinder- oder Hühnerbrühe","2 Möhren, gewürfelt","2 Kartoffeln, gewürfelt","1 Paprikaschote (Farbe nach Wahl), gewürfelt","1 Tasse Okra in Scheiben","1 Tasse gehacktes Blattgemüse (z. B. Spinat oder Grünkohl)","frischer Koriander oder Petersilie, gehackt (zum Garnieren)"],"s":["Heat the vegetable oil in a large pot or Dutch oven over medium-high heat. Add the beef or chicken cubes and cook until browned on all sides. Remove the meat from the pot and set it aside.","In the same pot, add the chopped onions and minced garlic. Sauté until the onions become translucent and the garlic is fragrant.","Reduce the heat to low and add the peanut butter to the pot. Stir constantly until the peanut butter melts and combines with the onions and garlic.","Add the ground cumin, paprika, chili powder, salt, and pepper to the pot. Stir well to incorporate the spices into the peanut sauce. Then add the diced tomatoes, including their juices, and mix everything together","Gradually pour the beef or chicken broth into the pot, stirring continuously to create a smooth sauce. Return the seared meat to the pot and stir to coat it with the sauce.","Cover the pot with a lid and let the stew simmer over low heat for about 30 minutes, allowing the flavors to meld together and the meat to become tender.","After 30 minutes, add the diced carrots, potatoes, bell pepper, okra, and chopped leafy greens to the pot. Stir well, ensuring that all the vegetables are submerged in the sauce.","Cover the pot again and let the stew simmer for an additional 15–20 minutes, or until the vegetables are cooked to your desired tenderness.","Remove the pot from heat and let it sit for a few minutes. This allows the stew to thicken slightly. Serve hot, garnished with fresh cilantro or parsley."],"x":[],"desc":"Maffé is a traditional West African dish that is popular in countries such as Senegal, Mali, and Gambia. This rich and hearty stew is made with a peanut sauce base and typically includes a combination of vegetables, meat (such as beef or chicken), and aromatic spices. Maffé is known for its creamy t","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maffé_(West_African_Peanut_Stew)_I","i":"wb-en-2596","im":["3/31/Mafe.malien.jpg/960px-Mafe.malien.jpg","Marshiayers","CC0","Mafe.malien.jpg","w"],"on":"Maffé (West African Peanut Stew) I","og":["2 tablespoons vegetable oil","1 pound beef or chicken, cut into cubes","1 large onion, finely chopped","3 garlic cloves, minced","1 cup smooth peanut butter","1 teaspoon ground cumin","1 teaspoon paprika","1 teaspoon chile powder (adjust to your preferred level of spiciness)","Salt to taste","Pepper to taste","1 can (14 ounces) diced tomatoes","4 cups beef or chicken broth","2 carrots, diced","2 potatoes, diced","1 bell pepper (any color of your choice), diced","1 cup sliced okra","1 cup chopped leafy greens (such as spinach or kale)","Fresh cilantro or parsley, chopped (for garnish)"]},{"n":"Maffé (westafrikanischer Erdnusseintopf) II","c":"suppen","k":"Afrika","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 EL Pflanzenöl","2 Zwiebeln, sauber fein gehackt","3 Knoblauchzehen, sauber fein gehackt","1 ½ TL geriebener Ingwer","2 Tassen stückige Tomaten","4 Hühnerbrühwürfel, zerbröselt","1 Tasse Erdnussbutter","4 afrikanische Auberginen, geschält und gehackt","2 Süßkartoffeln, geschält und gehackt","1 mittelgroßer Weißkohl, gewaschen und gehackt","4 mittelgroße Möhren, gewaschen und gewürfelt","3 mittelgroße Speiserüben, gewaschen und gehackt","2 mittelgroße Habanero-Chilis","15 mittelgroße Okraschoten, gewaschen, geputzt, und gehackt","Salz, nach Geschmack","schwarzer Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","gehackte Erdnüsse (optional)"],"s":["In a large pot, heat the oil over medium heat.","Add the onions, garlic, grated ginger. Cook, stirring, for about 5 minutes until the onions become translucent.","Add the tomato paste, bouillon cubes, and 6 cups (about 1.5 litres) hot water. Simmer over low heat for 10 minutes.","Stir in the peanut butter until fully incorporated. Add the eggplant, sweet potatoes, green cabbage, carrots, turnips, and habanero, then stir carefully to avoid fully crushing the habanero.","Cover and cook for about an hour over low heat until thickened.","Stir in the okra, then season with salt and black pepper to your desired taste. Cook for about 30 minutes until the vegetables become soft.","Remove the chilli pepper and sprinkle it with peanut butter if you will like and if not leave it like that.","Serve hot."],"x":[],"desc":"Mafe is a spicy and delicious African peanut stew. It is eaten throughout Africa, especially by the people of Ivory Coast.","img":"African Chicken Peanut Stew (37673757141).jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maffé_(West_African_Peanut_Stew)_II","i":"wb-en-2597","im":["e/e8/African_Chicken_Peanut_Stew_%2837673757141%29.jpg/960px-African_Chicken_Peanut_Stew_%2837673757141%29.jpg","A Healthier Michigan from Detroit, United States","CC BY-SA 2.0","African Chicken Peanut Stew (37673757141).jpg","r"],"on":"Maffé (West African Peanut Stew) II","og":["4 tablespoons vegetable oil","2 onions, neatly minced","3 garlic cloves, neatly minced","1½ teaspoons grated ginger","2 cups crushed tomatoes","4 chicken flavour bouillon cubes, crumbled","1 cup peanut butter","4 African eggplants, peeled and chopped","2 sweet potatoes, peeled and chopped","1 medium size green cabbage, washed and chopped","4 medium size carrots, washed and diced","3 medium size turnips, washed and chopped","2 medium size habanero chile peppers","15 medium size okra, washed, trimmed, and chopped","Salt to taste","Black pepper to taste","Chopped peanuts (optional)"]},{"n":"Maffé (westafrikanischer Erdnusseintopf) III","c":"suppen","k":"Afrika","p":4,"t":15,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["910 g Rindergulasch","½ Tasse Erdnussbutter","1 Tasse Wasser","1 TL schwarzer Pfeffer","1 TL Salz","2 EL Tomatenmark","1 Zwiebel","Knoblauch (optional)"],"s":["Boil meat in a pot with salt and onion.","Fry the meat in a pan of oil.","Blend together the tomato, pepper, and garlic until smooth.","Pour the blended mixture into a pot and add the peanut paste. Stir until thick."],"x":["Maafe is usually eaten with white rice, tuwo, fonio, fufu and sweet potatoes","It is usually made with vegetables in Ivory Coast, and the stew is cooked with boiled egg in Ghana.","When using beef to make maafe, use chuck, short ribs, or oxtail."],"desc":"Maafe is a stew made from groundnuts. It originated from the Madinkwa and Bambara people of Mali.","img":"Maafé.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maffé_(West_African_Peanut_Stew)_III","i":"wb-en-2598","im":["0/0b/Maaf%C3%A9.jpg/960px-Maaf%C3%A9.jpg","Nicolas PHULPIN","CC BY-SA 4.0","Maafé.jpg","r"],"on":"Maffé (West African Peanut Stew) III","og":["2 lbs stew beef","½ cup peanut butter","1 cup water","1 teaspoon black pepper","1 teaspoon salt","2 tablespoons tomato paste","1 onion","Garlic (optional)"]},{"n":"Mafrum bil Lahm (libysches Fleisch mit Kartoffeln aus dem Ofen)","c":"fleisch","k":"Libyen","p":4,"t":60,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 Kartoffeln, geschält und in dicke Scheiben geschnitten","2 EL Olivenöl","1 Zwiebel, fein gehackt","3 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","500 g Rinder- oder Lammhack","1 TL gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","1 TL Paprikapulver","½ TL gemahlener Cayennepfeffer (je nach gewünschter Schärfe anpassen)","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","400 g Tomaten aus der Dose, zerdrückt","frische Petersilie oder Koriander, gehackt, zum Garnieren"],"s":["In a large pot, bring water to a boil and add the potato slices. Boil them for about 5 minutes, or until slightly tender. Drain and set aside.","In a skillet, heat the olive oil over medium heat. Add the chopped onion and minced garlic, and sauté until they become translucent and fragrant.","Add the ground beef or lamb to the skillet and cook until browned. Break up the meat with a wooden spoon or spatula as it cooks.","Stir in the ground cumin, paprika, cayenne pepper, salt, and pepper, and cook for another minute to toast the spices.","Remove the skillet from the heat and set aside.","Preheat the oven to 180°C (350°F).","Take a slice of the boiled potato and flatten it with the palm of your hand. Place a spoonful of the cooked meat mixture in the center of the potato slice, and fold the sides over to enclose the filling. Repeat with the remaining potato slices and meat mixture.","Arrange the stuffed potato slices in a single layer in a baking dish.","In a separate bowl, mix the crushed tomatoes with salt, pepper, and any remaining spices. Pour the tomato sauce over the stuffed potatoes, ensuring they are well-coated.","Cover the baking dish with aluminum foil and bake in the preheated oven for 45 minutes.","Remove the foil and continue baking for an additional 10–15 minutes, or until the potatoes are fully cooked and golden brown on top.","Garnish with fresh parsley or cilantro before serving."],"x":["Mafrum bil lahm can be served as a main course accompanied by a salad or crusty bread.","Leftovers can be refrigerated and reheated for later enjoyment.","Adjust the spiciness of the dish by adding more or less cayenne pepper according to your preference.","For added flavor, you can sprinkle grated cheese on top of the mafrum before baking it in the oven.","Feel free to experiment with different seasonings and spices to personalize the dish to your taste.","Vegetarian variation: Replace the ground meat with a combination of cooked and seasoned vegetables such as zucchini, eggplant, and bell peppers."],"desc":"Mafrum bil Lahm is a traditional Libyan dish that features layers of seasoned meat and potatoes, topped with a flavorful tomato sauce. It is a delicious and satisfying meal that is often enjoyed during festive occasions and gatherings.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mafrum_bil_Lahm_(Libyan_Baked_Meat_and_Potatoes)","i":"wb-en-2599","on":"Mafrum bil Lahm (Libyan Baked Meat and Potatoes)","og":["4 potatoes, peeled and cut into thick slices","2 tablespoons olive oil","1 onion, finely chopped","3 cloves of garlic, minced","500 grams (1 lb) ground beef or lamb","1 teaspoon ground cumin","1 teaspoon ground paprika","½ teaspoon ground cayenne pepper (adjust according to spice preference)","Salt to taste","Pepper, to taste","400 grams (14 oz) canned tomatoes, crushed","Fresh parsley or cilantro, chopped, for garnish"]},{"n":"Magische Brownies","c":"dessert","k":"","p":9,"t":240,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["Cannabis, gemahlen","60 g Butter","300 g Schokotropfen","180 ml Zucker (160 g)","2 Eier (Größe M)","5 ml Vanilleextrakt","1 Prise Salz","abgeriebene Zitronenschale","250 g selbsttreibendes Mehl (Mehl mit Backpulver)"],"s":["Melt the butter in a small saucepan, and stir in the cannabis. Cook slowly over a low temperature for 2–3 hours. Do not allow to boil or exceed 200 °F (93°C).","If desired, strain the butter to remove the cannabis solids.","Melt the chocolate chips in the microwave or over a double boiler. Combine the melted chocolate and infused butter, stirring until smooth.","Stir in the sugar, and allow the mixture to cool if needed.","Stir in the eggs, vanilla, salt, and lemon zest until smooth.","Fold in the flour just until combined.","Transfer the batter to a greased and/or parchment-lined pan.","Bake at 360°F/180°C for about 20–25 minutes or until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out without any batter on it."],"x":["Try using brown cane sugar instead of white sugar.","Melt some chocolate and mix with a little sugar, vanilla, lemon, and a little more weed. Drizzle on the freshly cooked brownies for a little added flavour and high. This creates a nicer tasting brownie with more of a kick.","Try adding a few crushed up biscuits before baking for a more varied taste."],"desc":"A magic brownie is a brownie that has been infused with cannabis. Eating the brownie results in a cannabis high one to a few hours after consumption—as a result, care should be taken not to eat too many of them to avoid adverse effects.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Magic_Brownies","i":"wb-en-2600","on":"Magic Brownies","og":["cannabis, ground","60 g (½ stick/2.1 oz) butter","300 g (3½ cups/11 oz) chocolate chips","180 ml (¾ cup/160 g/5.6 oz) white granulated sugar","2 standard eggs","5 ml (1 teaspoon) vanilla extract","1 pinch of salt","Grated lemon zest","250 g (1¾ cups/8.8 oz) self-raising flour"]},{"n":"Baingan Bharta nach Maharashtra-Art (Aubergine mit Chili)","c":"welt","k":"Indien","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["Öl","1–2 große Auberginen","1 Handvoll plus etwas mehr fein gehackte Frühlingszwiebel, weiße und grüne Teile","2–3 TL fein gehackter junger Knoblauch (optional)","¼ Tasse frische Erbsen","Kreuzkümmelsamen","braune Senfsamen (Rai) (Senfsamen)","Salz, nach Geschmack","1–2 grüne Chilis, in 2 bis 3 Stücke gebrochen","¼ TL Kurkuma (optional)","½ TL rotes Chilipulver (optional)"],"s":["Wash, then wipe dry eggplant. Apply some oil on the surface of each one of them.","Blacken eggplants over direct heat. Alternatively, char-roast in an oven or over a fire to infuse smoke.","Once the skin is blackened and comes away on touch, let them cool a bit and then peel the burnt skin. Reserve the drippings.","Mash the eggplant flesh by hand until smooth. Transfer flesh to a large bowl.","Mix in the green onion, green garlic (if using), peas, and salt to taste.","Heat some oil in a pan. Once heated sufficiently add rai, then cumin seeds, then green chilies. Let the chilies fry for 10–12 seconds.","Pour this spice mix onto the eggplant mixture in the bowl. Mix well and serve with bhakri and thecha/kharda below.","Follow steps 1 through 5 as directed above.","In the step 6 above add turmeric after chilies. Add the eggplant mixture to the pan of tadka. Sauté for about 1–2 minutes. If required add some of the reserved eggplant drippings to moisten the bharta.","Serve hot.","Wash and dry about 10–15 green chilies and half handful of fresh coriander. Peel 5–7 cloves of garlic; break the chilies in to 2–3 pieces each.","Heat about 1–1½ tbsp of oil on the griddle (tava).","Once heated sufficiently add chilies and garlic (make sure you have exhaust turned on and working).","Fry them for 30–40 seconds over low heat. Turn the heat off. Now add salt to taste. Put this mix in a blender along with chopped coriander and blend it roughly.","Thecha is ready to serve. While serving put some raw groundnut oil on each serving. This is very very hot dish depending the chilies used. Eat and handle carefully!"],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maharashtrian_Baingan_Bartha_(South_Indian_Eggplant_with_Chili)","i":"wb-en-2601","im":["4/4d/Baigan_Bharta_from_Nagpur.JPG/960px-Baigan_Bharta_from_Nagpur.JPG","Dheerajk88","CC BY-SA 4.0","Baigan Bharta from Nagpur.JPG","w"],"on":"Maharashtrian Baingan Bartha (South Indian Eggplant with Chili)","og":["Oil","1–2 large eggplants","1 handful plus some more finely chopped green onion, both white and green parts","2–3 tsp finely-chopped green garlic (optional)","¼ cup fresh peas","Cumin seeds","Rai (mustard seed)","Salt to taste","1–2 green chiles broken into 2–3 pieces each","¼ teaspoon turmeric (optional)","½ teaspoon red chile powder (optional)"]},{"n":"Pakoda nach Maharashtra-Art (frittierte Kichererbsen-Curry-Snacks)","c":"snacks","k":"Indien","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["5–6 Zwiebeln, geschält und in dünne Scheiben geschnitten","2–3 grüne Chilis, gewaschen und fein gewürfelt","Salz","½ TL gemahlene Kurkuma","½ TL Chilipulver","1 TL gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","1 TL gemahlener Koriander","Kichererbsenmehl","Öl"],"s":["Combine onions and chiles. Mix in salt, and let sit 10–15 minutes.","Mix in turmeric, chili powder, cumin, and coriander. By this time the onion mix should be moist due to added salt and spices. If a moister mix is required, allow to stand another 5 minutes.","Start adding gram flour to the onion mix a little at a time. The mixture should not be dry. Add the flour just to absorb the moistness. You should end up with a somewhat sticky mixture.","Heat sufficient oil in a wok or frying pan. Once heated sufficiently, carefully take around 2–3 tbsp of hot oil and add to the onion and gram flour mix. Mix well.","Drop a few small to medium chunks of dough at a time in the medium hot oil. Fry until it gets a golden brown colour. If you have used 4–5 large onions and a medium wok you are likely to need 3–4 batches of frying to finish the mixture.","Serve hot with green chutney or tomato ketchup."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maharashtrian_Deep_Fried_Chickpea_Dough_Curry_Snacks_(Pakoda)","i":"wb-en-2602","on":"Maharashtrian Deep Fried Chickpea Dough Curry Snacks (Pakoda)","og":["5–6 onions, peeled and sliced thin","2–3 green chiles, washed and finely diced","Salt","½ tsp turmeric powder","½ tsp chile powder","1 tsp ground cumin","1 tsp ground coriander","Gram flour","Oil"]},{"n":"Mahshi (ägyptisches gefülltes Gemüse)","c":"veggie","k":"Ägypten","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["verschiedenes Gemüse zum Füllen, z. B. Zucchini, Aubergine, Paprika, und Tomate","1 Tasse Mittelkornreis","½ Tasse Tomatenmark","¼ Tasse Olivenöl","¼ Tasse frische Petersilie, fein gehackt","¼ Tasse frische Minzblätter, fein gehackt","2 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","1 TL gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","1 TL gemahlener Koriander","Salz, nach Geschmack","schwarzer Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","Wasser, nach Bedarf"],"s":["Prepare the vegetables for stuffing by carefully cutting off the tops and scooping out the seeds and flesh, creating hollow shells. Set aside the scooped-out vegetable flesh for later use.","In a mixing bowl, combine the medium-grain rice, tomato paste, olive oil, finely chopped parsley, finely chopped mint leaves, minced garlic, ground cumin, ground coriander, salt, and black pepper. Mix well until all the ingredients are thoroughly combined.","Fill each hollowed vegetable with the rice and herb mixture, packing it firmly and leaving some space at the top for the rice to expand while cooking.","Arrange the stuffed vegetables in a baking dish or casserole dish, placing them closely together to support each other.","Use the reserved vegetable flesh to fill any empty spaces between the stuffed vegetables. This helps to prevent them from shifting during cooking.","Pour enough water into the baking dish to partially cover the stuffed vegetables. This will help create a moist cooking environment.","Cover the baking dish with aluminum foil, ensuring it is tightly sealed to retain moisture.","Preheat the oven to 180°C (350°F) and bake the mahshi for about 60–75 minutes, or until the vegetables are tender and the rice filling is cooked through.","Remove the foil and continue baking for an additional 10–15 minutes to allow the tops of the stuffed vegetables to slightly brown.","Once cooked, remove the mahshi from the oven and let it cool slightly before serving."],"x":[],"desc":"Mahshi is a delicious Egyptian dish that involves stuffing various vegetables with a flavorful mixture of rice, herbs, and spices. It is a versatile and satisfying dish that can be customized to individual tastes. Mahshi is typically served as a main course and is enjoyed by families and friends dur","img":"Mahshi.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mahshi_(Egyptian_Stuffed_Vegetables)","i":"wb-en-2603","im":["1/15/Mahshi.jpg/960px-Mahshi.jpg","Aseel zm","CC BY-SA 4.0","Mahshi.jpg","r"],"on":"Mahshi (Egyptian Stuffed Vegetables)","og":["Assorted vegetables for stuffing, such as zucchini, eggplant, bell pepper, and tomato","1 cup medium-grain rice","½ cup tomato paste","¼ cup olive oil","¼ cup fresh parsley, finely chopped","¼ cup fresh mint leaves, finely chopped","2 cloves garlic, minced","1 teaspoon ground cumin","1 teaspoon ground coriander","Salt to taste","Black pepper to taste","Water, as needed"]},{"n":"Maitorieska (finnisches Gerstenfladenbrot)","c":"brot","k":"Finnland","p":1,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["250 ml kalte Milch","⅓ TL Salz","250–330 ml Gerstenmehl"],"s":["Preheat oven to 300°C (570°F), or as high as it will go.","Combine milk and salt, and add flour. Mix the ingredients well to make a dough.","Knead into a flat, round bread (about 0.5 cm / ¼ inch thick).","Bake on an oven tray for about 10 minutes or until the surface gets some darker spots. Alternatively, fry it in a pan on the stove or on open fire.","Eat fresh with butter and cold milk."],"x":[],"desc":"Maitorieska (milk rieska, pronounced \"RE-ehskuh\") is a barley-based flatbread that is a local specialty and a very traditional food in the Ylivieska area of Finland.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maitorieska_(Finnish_Barley_Flatbread)","i":"wb-en-2604","im":["c/cd/Flatbread.JPG/960px-Flatbread.JPG","Jonathunder","CC BY-SA 3.0","Flatbread.JPG","w"],"on":"Maitorieska (Finnish Barley Flatbread)","og":["250 ml (1 cup) cold milk","⅓ teaspoon salt","250–330 ml (1–1½ cups) barley flour"]},{"n":"Maja Blanca (Kokosmilchpudding)","c":"dessert","k":"Philippinen","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Tassen Speisestärke","4 Tassen Kokosmilch","1 Dose gezuckerte Kondensmilch (400 g)","1 Dose Kokoscreme (380 g)","¾ Tasse Zucker","1 Tasse Maiskörner (optional)","¼ Tasse geröstete Kokoschips (optional)"],"s":["In a bowl, dissolve cornstarch in 1 cup of coconut milk. Set aside.","In a pot, combine the remaining coconut milk, condensed milk, coconut cream, and sugar. Bring to a gentle boil over medium heat.","Gradually pour the cornstarch mixture into the pot while continuously stirring. Lower the heat and continue stirring until the mixture thickens, about 10–15 minutes.","If desired, add corn kernels into the mixture and stir for an additional 2–3 minutes.","Pour the mixture into a greased baking dish or other mold. Let it cool and set for at least an hour in the refrigerator.","Once set, slice the pudding into squares and sprinkle toasted coconut flakes on top before serving."],"x":[],"desc":"Maja blanca is a gelatin-like comfort food.","img":"Majablanca.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maja_Blanca_(Coconut_Milk_Pudding)","i":"wb-en-2605","im":["7/7d/Majablanca.jpg/500px-Majablanca.jpg","kawalingpinoy","CC BY-SA 4.0","Majablanca.jpg","r"],"on":"Maja Blanca (Coconut Milk Pudding)","og":["2 cups cornstarch","4 cups coconut milk","1 can (14 oz) sweetened condensed milk","1 can (13.5 oz) coconut cream","¾ cup white granulated sugar","1 cup corn kernels (optional)","¼ cup toasted coconut flakes (optional)"]},{"n":"Makizushi (Maki-Rolle)","c":"welt","k":"Japan","p":4,"t":0,"d":3,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["vorbereiteter Sushireis","Füllungen, nach Belieben (z. B. roher oder geräucherter Lachs, Thunfisch usw. oder Gurke bzw. Avocado)","Noriblätter","Wasabipaste","Wasser","Sesam, für Inside-out-Rollen mit Reis außen (optional)"],"s":["Place the roller on a cutting board. If making inside-out rolls with rice on the outside, wrap the roller in a double layer of plastic wrap to prevent rice from sticking to the roller.","Place a sheet of nori shiny side-down on top of the roller.","Dampen your hands before applying the rice. Grab the rice with one hand and put a fistful on the center of the nori. Spread the rice over the nori approximately 6 mm thick, leaving a 2 cm gap on the side parallel to the bamboo.","As a general rule, if you can't see the nori through the rice, you have too much.","If making an inside out roll, flip over the nori and rice quickly onto the sushi roller. The rice should now be on on the surface of the plastic wrap, with the nori facing you.","Place the primary ingredients in a row in the middle. Slowly use the roller to push the nori against itself (rolling it away from you), using your thumbs and heels of hands for stability.","Be careful when you reach the row of ingredients, making sure that it goes underneath the roll rather than just being pushed along.","When you reach the end of the nori sheet, use the roller to compact the roll a little, making sure the rice sticking it together. When evening out a bumpy roll, don't squeeze too hard on the sides and don't flatten the roll from the top.","To fix the ends of the roll, poke about ½ inch out from one side of mat and while gently holding it in place, press it with the heel of your hand a little.","Remove the maki from the sushi roller, and put it on the cutting board below.","Wet a sharp knife before slicing. Slice the rolls from the center outwards, into sections of 5, 6, or 8 (depending on the roll and your preference). Cutting from the center first ensures that all ingredients will shift towards the outside two pieces.","For the rolls of 6 or 8, cut from the center, then put one roll behind the other, and cut each half in half.","If making an inside-out roll, you may garnish the exterior rice with sesame seeds.","Serve with soy sauce for dipping. You may also want chopsticks, pickled ginger, and wasabi if culture allows. Sashimi, miso soup, other sushi, or just general Japanese food is also often served alongside it.","Green tea is considered the drink of choice to have with sushi."],"x":["Dampening the hands before handling the rice will prevent clumping and the rice sticking to your hands. However, too much moisture may also make the rice less sticky, so don't go overboard.","Common maki rolls include","California roll: avocado, crab meat or imitation crab, cucumber.","Tuna roll: Tuna, wrapped in rice and seaweed. This same combination is used to make plain rolls with any other type of fish.","Spicy tuna roll: Tuna, spicy sauce (mixture of Japanese mayonnaise and sriracha)","Kamikaze roll: Tuna, yellowtail, spicy sauce"],"desc":"Makizushi, also called rolled sushi or maki roll, is a variety of sushi. It is made by layering nori, seasoned sushi rice, and fillings, before rolling up and slicing into individual pieces. The outer layer of the maki roll varies, having either nori or rice on the exterior—the latter is sometimes c","img":"Makizushi2.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Makizushi_(Maki_Roll)","i":"wb-en-2606","im":["0/03/Makizushi2.jpg/960px-Makizushi2.jpg","pasqualeschiavoneph","CC0","Makizushi2.jpg","r"],"on":"Makizushi (Maki Roll)","og":["Prepared sushi rice","Fillings, as desired (this may consist of either raw/smoked salmon, tuna, etc or perhaps cucumber or avocado)","Nori sheets","Wasabi paste","Water","Sesame seeds, if making inside-out rolls with rice on outside (optional)"]},{"n":"Makki di Roti (indisches Maismehlfladenbrot)","c":"brot","k":"Indien","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Handvoll Maismehl","1 Löffel ungesalzene Butter, weich","1 Tasse lauwarmes Wasser"],"s":["Heap the cornmeal in a praat (a wide flat mixing tray) so it forms a hill. Make a well, and pour in a small quantity of the lukewarm water.","Start to mix the cornmeal and water into a dough. The dough should remain moist but not become sticky. Add water in small quantities to retain a moist feel.","The final dough should not be sticky (sprinkle some extra cornmeal if needed to help soak up excess moisture).","Add the soft butter (makhan) at the end and give it a final kneading.","Take a small hand-sized portion of the dough from the mixing tray and roll it into a small ball (ladu) between the two hands. Gradually start to flatten the ball between the palms of the two hands (wet the hands and fingers to help the dough to stretch).","At the same time rotate the flattening dough so that the thinning of the roti is even. It may start to crack at the edges. Repair any cracks by pressing them at the rims.","Wetting the fingers and the palm of the hand will help to spread and give the roti a circular shape. Aim for an evenly thinned roti.","When the roti is about the size of a small plate (or a little larger then a spread-out hand) place it on the preheated tahva. Leave the roti to take in the heat (it takes a while for roti to get cooked).","Some areas of the roti will change in colour as the water evaporates. Soon after, the roti will be able to be moved on the tahva. With a dry cloth, press the areas of the roti that look moist.","It is a matter of judgement when the roti can be turned over and heated on the other side. When the roti have been well cooked they should not have any moist looking areas. Some areas will have burned slightly but this is normal."],"x":["The roti can be heated on open flames of the cooker or on a tava. This process of placing roti on open flames is called radhna. It takes time to get the thick roti to be well cooked.","The cooked roti is smeared with some clarified butter (ghee). This is called chopardna. The roti is then put into a serving dish. Traditionally, the roti is served as it gets prepared and is eaten fresh. On occasions when it has to be stored before serving it is placed in a dry tray called chahba."],"desc":"Roti, in general, refers to an Indian flatbread cooked on an iron griddle (tava). Makki di roti (lit. \"roti made from corn\") refers to a special roti where cornmeal is used instead of the usual wheat flour. It is a famous delicacy from the north-Indian state of Punjab, and is cooked in the winters a","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Makki_di_Roti_(Indian_Cornmeal_Flatbread)","i":"wb-en-2607","im":["4/49/Makki_Di_Roti.JPG/960px-Makki_Di_Roti.JPG","Vsigamany","CC BY-SA 4.0","Makki Di Roti.JPG","w"],"on":"Makki di Roti (Indian Cornmeal Flatbread)","og":["1 handful cornmeal","1 spoonful unsalted butter, softened","1 cupful lukewarm water"]},{"n":"Maqluba (Reis mit Fleisch und Gemüse)","c":"fleisch","k":"Palästina","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["230 g Rinderhack","½ Zwiebel, gehackt","Olivenöl","1 Tasse Reis","1 ½ Tassen Wasser","Salz","schwarzer Pfeffer","Piment","Naturjoghurt"],"s":["In a saucepan, brown ground beef and onion with salt, pepper, and allspice in a little olive oil (use more allspice than pepper). Remove from heat.","Add the rice and water. Bring to a boil over medium heat.","Turn down to medium low, and cover with the lid tilted to let some steam escape.","When most of the water has evaporated and the surface of the rice becomes pitted, put the lid on tight. Cook on low heat for 15 minutes.","Remove from heat and leave covered for 2–3 minutes. Serve with yogurt."],"x":[],"desc":"Maklubi, also known as maqluba or maklouba, is a dish of rice, meat, and vegetables found throughout the Levant.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maklubi_(Rice_with_Meat_and_Vegetables)","i":"wb-en-2608","on":"Maklubi (Rice with Meat and Vegetables)","og":["½ pound ground beef","½ onion, chopped","Olive oil","1 cup rice","1 ½ cups water","Salt","Black pepper","Allspice","Plain yogurt"]},{"n":"Malai-Gemüsecurry","c":"veggie","k":"Indien","p":10,"t":30,"d":2,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["3 grüne Paprika (Paprika)","1 Orange, gelb, und rote Paprika","1 Tasse Paneerwürfel","Cashewkerne","4 große Tomaten","1 Tasse gehackte Möhre","1 Tasse Erbsen","3–4 grüne Chilis (je nach gewünschter Schärfe), fein gehackt","getrocknete Petersilie und Koriander","1 EL Butter oder Öl","Garam Masala","rotes Chilipulver","Salz, nach Geschmack","Kurkuma","950 ml Schlagsahne","1 EL saure Sahne","Koriandergrün zum Garnieren"],"s":["Cut the bell peppers into ½-inch pieces.","Sauté paneer until golden brown; set aside.","Soak a handful of cashew nuts in warm water.","Grind the tomatoes and the soaked cashew into a fine paste. Keep this paste aside.","Sauté the chopped vegetables, green chillies, and dried parsley in the butter/oil until they are cooked. You could also microwave the vegetables for ~10 minutes without water, and then sauté them in butter for a minute.","Add the tomato paste to the vegetables and cook for 5 minutes.","Add the garam masala, red chilli powder, salt, and turmeric according to taste; simmer for 2 minutes.","Add the whipping cream and the sour cream, and let it cook until the cream thickens.","Add the paneer and mix well.","Garnish with cilantro and cashew nuts.","Serve hot with naan or roti."],"x":["You could choose other vegetables like zucchini or broccoli if you like."],"desc":"Malai mixed vegetable, is a creamy side dish for Indian bread.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Malai_Mixed_Vegetable_Curry","i":"wb-en-2609","on":"Malai Mixed Vegetable Curry","og":["3 green capsicums (bell peppers)","1 each orange, yellow, and red capsicum","1 cup paneer cubes","Cashew nuts","4 large tomatoes","1 cup chopped carrot","1 cup peas","3–4 green chillies (depending on spice requirement), finely chopped","Dried parsley and cilantro","1 Tbsp butter or oil","Garam masala","Red chilli powder","Salt to taste","Turmeric","1 quart whipping cream","1 Tbsp sour cream","Cilantro for garnishing"]},{"n":"Malawach (blättriges Fladenbrot)","c":"brot","k":"Nahost","p":12,"t":5,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 kg Weizenmehl (Type 405)","½ Tasse Zucker","2 TL Trockenhefe","1 EL Salz","2–3 Tassen lauwarmes Wasser (oder so viel, wie zum Kneten nötig ist)","Pflanzenöl (so viel, dass die Pfanne ausgekleidet ist)","200 g geschmolzene Butter oder Margarine"],"s":["Mix together the flour, sugar, yeast, salt, and water, starting with only 2 cups of water. Knead the dough well, adding additional water if necessary to make it soft and pliable.","Cover and let dough rest until it doubles in size.","Take up dough and begin to knead it by hand. Divide dough into 12 smaller portions and place upon oiled surface. Let dough rest until each portion rises and doubles in size, occasionally oiling the surface of dough.","Grease a work surface with oil. Roll out each piece of dough with a rolling pin to get very large, almost paper-thin, rounds of dough.","Brush each round liberally with melted butter. Fold the dough in half, from the top towards the bottom. Then, roll it up from the top towards the bottom as one would roll-up a sleeping bag, forming a rope. Coil the rope around itself into a spiral.","Cover and allow the dough to rest until it rises and doubles in size.","Roll each spiral out again into a thin round. Brush again with butter, then repeat the rolling and coiling process.","Allow the dough to rest once more while covered until it rises.","Heat a skillet with a little vegetable oil.","Use your hands to flatten out the dough coils on a greased surface.","Place flattened dough portions in skillet and cover with lid. Fry the dough on a medium to low heat until the bottom turns an amber color. Flip over and fry on reverse side without the lid.","Serve hot."],"x":["Malawach is often served with a hard-boiled egg, along with tomato salsa that has been flavored with freshly-chopped coriander."],"desc":"Malawach is a layered, flaky flatbread that is popularly eaten in Israel, and now made popular in other regions. It is typically brushed with oil or fat and cooked flat in a frying pan.","img":"Malawach.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Malawach_(Flaky_Flatbread)","i":"wb-en-2610","im":["7/78/Malawach.jpg/500px-Malawach.jpg","Ayala Sender","CC BY 2.0","Malawach.jpg","r"],"on":"Malawach (Flaky Flatbread)","og":["1 kg white all-purpose wheat flour","½ cup white granulated sugar","2 tsp dried yeast","1 tbsp salt","2–3 cups lukewarm water (or such as is sufficient for kneading dough)","Vegetable oil (sufficient for lining skillet)","200 g melted butter or margarine"]},{"n":"Malpua (südasiatischer süßer Pfannkuchen)","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":10,"t":45,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 l Milch","¼ Tasse Weizenmehl","¼ Tasse Hartweizengrieß","Ghee","Wasser"],"s":["Boil the milk until it reduces to half of its original volume.","Roast the semolina until light brown.","Mix the all-purpose flour and milk into the toasted semolina to make a batter. It should be smooth and lump-free.","Heat the ghee in a skillet.","Use a circular pouring motion to pour batter in the pan and make a small pancake.","Keep turning over. Take care that it does not become crisp or harsh.","Make a sugar syrup of good consistency. Dip the malpua in the syrup.","Serve."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"Malpua.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Malpua_(South_Asian_Sweet_Pancake)","i":"wb-en-2611","im":["8/81/Malpua.jpg/960px-Malpua.jpg","ampersandyslexia","CC BY-SA 2.0","Malpua.jpg","r"],"on":"Malpua (South Asian Sweet Pancake)","og":["1 litre milk","¼ cup all-purpose flour","¼ cup semolina flour","Ghee","Water"]},{"n":"Maltesische Mandelkekse (Biskuttini tal-Lewż)","c":"brot","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["300 g gemahlene Mandeln","250 g Zucker","1 EL Zitronensaft","2 Eiweiß","1–2 Tropfen Bittermandelaroma","Vanillearoma","ganze Mandeln zum Verzieren","Reispapier"],"s":["Combine ground almonds, sugar, lemon juice, and almond essence in a bowl.","Whip the egg whites until stiff, then add to the almond mixture. Mix well to make a dough.","Lay rice paper on flat baking dish.","Place a tablespoon of the dough in your palm and roll it into a small ball. Place on rice paper, and flatten slightly.","Repeat the shaping process with the remaining dough.","Press an almond into the top of each cookie, and bake at 375°F for 25 minutes or until light golden brown."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maltese_Almond_Cookies_(Biskuttini_tal-Lewz)","i":"wb-en-2612","on":"Maltese Almond Cookies (Biskuttini tal-Lewz)","og":["300 g ground almonds or almond meal","250 g white granulated sugar","1 tbsp lemon juice","2 egg whites","1–2 drops almond essence","Vanilla essence","Whole almonds for decoration","Rice paper"]},{"n":"Maltesischer Kanincheneintopf (Stuffat tal-Fenek)","c":"suppen","k":"Malta","p":4,"t":60,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 großes ganzes Kaninchen (etwa 2 kg)","2 EL Sonnenblumenöl","1 Zehe Knoblauch","300 g weiße Kartoffeln, geschält","1 kleine Möhre, geschält und gehackt","800 g stückige Tomaten oder geschälte Tomaten aus der Dose","200 ml Rotwein","1 EL Zucker","2–3 Lorbeerblätter (mediterran)","Tabasco","frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","Salz, nach Geschmack","100 g Erbsen aus der Dose","½ TL Gewürzmischung (Mixed Spice)"],"s":["Cut up the rabbit at the joints. Cut the rib section into 3–4 pieces, and divide the legs at all the joints. Split the head of the rabbit in half.","The whole animal should be cut into about 10–12 pieces so they are large and chunky, but small enough that they can be easily manipulated with large spoon. Remove and keep internal organs apart.","Mince the garlic. Heat the oil in a large frying pan. Heat some of the garlic in the oil. Add some rabbit pieces and cook through.","Remove cooked meat from the pan and place in a large container. Cook the rest of the meat in the same way in batches, adding some garlic with every batch. The meat should be well cooked but not very brown.","Fry the internal organs whole in the same oil until well-cooked. Take some of the smaller pieces of meat without bone and add them to the organs. Keep these apart from the main meat.","Cut the potatoes into large irregular chunks, slightly smaller than the pieces of meat.","In a stock pot, place the fried rabbit, the potatoes, the chopped carrot, the tomato pulp, wine, sugar and laurel leaves. Add salt, pepper, mixed spice and Tabasco carefully. Cover and simmer on a low flame for 4 hours. Stir occasionally during the first hour.","Once done, add the peas, and cook until tender (about 10 minutes)."],"x":["Start with Maltese galletti, Gbejniet, Zalzett, bigilla, and the internal organs of the rabbit as entrées.","For second plate serve Spaghetti (typically slightly overcooked in Maltese cuisine) with a covering of sauce from the stew.","Serve the rabbit meat and potatoes (with little sauce) as main course, always accompanied by bread, and a strong red wine.","Serve Maltese style Trifle or Traditional Maltese Ice Cream (also called Gelat tan-Nanna) for dessert.","Round off with peanuts in the shell and Anisette.","The best stew is slow cooked on the lowest flame for as long as possible. Using a higher flame you can reduce cooking time to 2 hours, but this is not a dish that should be rushed. If you have the time you can even cook it for 6 hours on a camping-type flame for an even richer taste."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maltese_Rabbit_Stew_(Stuffat_tal-Fenek)","i":"wb-en-2613","im":["a/a8/Malta_Rabbit_fried_with_wine_and_garlic.JPG/330px-Malta_Rabbit_fried_with_wine_and_garlic.JPG","Chattacha","CC BY 3.0","Malta Rabbit fried with wine and garlic.JPG","w"],"on":"Maltese Rabbit Stew (Stuffat tal-Fenek)","og":["1 large (about 2 kg) whole rabbit","2 tbsp sunflower oil","1 clove garlic","300 g white potatoes, peeled","1 small carrot, peeled and chopped","800 g canned crushed tomatoes or canned 'Pelati'","200 ml red wine","1 tbsp sugar","2–3 Mediterranean bay leaves","Tabasco sauce","Freshly-ground black pepper","Salt to taste","100 g canned peas","½ tsp mixed spice"]},{"n":"Malvani-Hähnchencurry","c":"fleisch","k":"Indien","p":4,"t":30,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["8 grüne Chilis, gehackt","2 EL Ingwerpaste","2 EL Knoblauchpaste","800 g mittelgroße Hähnchenstücke","2 EL Öl","1 frische Kokosnuss, Fruchtfleisch gerieben","4 Zwiebeln, gehackt","1 TL Chilipulver","½ TL Kurkuma","2 TL Garam Masala","2 TL Malvani-Masala","Salz, nach Geschmack","fein gehackte Korianderblätter zum Garnieren"],"s":["Grind half of the green chillies to a paste and mix it well with the ginger and garlic pastes.","Make cuts on the chicken pieces, rub this mixture on to them well, and marinate for about an hour at least.","Toast coconut shavings in a pan with a little hot oil until light brown. Cool and grind along with half the onions to a paste.","Heat oil in a heavy-bottomed pan and sauté the onions on medium level for about 2 minute(s) or until they are light brown in color.","Add the remaining chopped green chillies and spice powders and fry for a few seconds. Add the marinated chicken pieces and fry on medium level for about 3 minutes or until they are lightly browned.","Add the paste and salt, then mix well. Add water according to the desired level of consistency and bring to a boil. Cover and cook on low level for about 25 minute(s) or until the chicken pieces are tender and fully cooked.","Garnish with finely-chopped coriander leaves."],"x":["If it is difficult to obtain fresh coconut, it can be replaced by desiccated coconut shavings. For this recipe, there is no need to soak it in warm water. Roast it directly."],"desc":"Kombdi vade is a Malvani dish, which is quite popular in Maharashtra. The dish consists of the traditional Malvani chicken curry (including chicken pieces with bones), vade (also known as puri, which is a fluffy, fried bread of wheat and nachni flour), onion, lemon and solkadhi (a drink made from co","img":"Chickenmalvani.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Malvani_Chicken_Curry","i":"wb-en-2614","im":["https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ee/Chickenmalvani.jpg","Ashay Arekar at English Wikibooks","Public domain","Chickenmalvani.jpg","r"],"on":"Malvani Chicken Curry","og":["8 green chillies, chopped","2 tbsp ginger paste","2 tbsp garlic paste","800 g (1.8 lb / 8 ea.) medium-sized pieces of chicken","2 tbsp oil","1 fresh coconut, flesh grated","4 onions, chopped","1 tsp chilli powder","½ tsp turmeric","2 tsps garam masala","2 tsps Malvani Special Masala","Salt to taste","Finely-chopped coriander leaves for garnishing"]},{"n":"Mandarinenkuchen","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Kuchen","1 Packung Rührkuchen-Backmischung (430 g)","1 Dose Mandarinen (312 g)","3 Eier","#Zuckerguss","1 Packung Instant-Vanillepuddingpulver (144 g)","1 Dose zerkleinerte Ananas (567 g)","1 Becher Schlagcreme (Cool Whip o. Ä.) (340 g)"],"s":["Preheat oven to 350°F (180°C). Grease the sides and bottom of cake pans with shortening, and dust with flour.","Pour yellow cake mix into mixing bowl. Add eggs and the mandarin oranges plus their juice. Blend until moistened, then beat for approximately 2 minutes at medium speed.","Pour batter evenly into prepared baking pans. Bake approximately 30 minutes in the preheated oven or until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean.","Remove from oven and let the cakes cool completely.","Scoop CoolWhip into a clean mixing bowl. Add the instant vanilla pudding mix. Drain all the pineapple juice from the can of crushed pineapples, and fold the pineapple into CoolWhip. Chill icing for about 30 minutes.","After the cakes cool, frost each layer with your icing."],"x":[],"desc":"Mandarin orange cake is a common low-fat cake recipe with unique variations. The cake is simple to make and does not require you to start from scratch. All the ingredients can be found at grocery stores in the United States.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mandarin_Orange_Cake","i":"wb-en-2615","on":"Mandarin Orange Cake","og":["#Cake","1 box (15 oz / 430 g) yellow cake mix","1 can (11 oz / 312 g) mandarin oranges","3 eggs","#Icing","1 box (5.1 oz / 144 g) instant vanilla pudding mix","1 can (20 oz / 567 g) crushed pineapple","1 container (12 oz / 340 g) CoolWhip or other whipped topping"]},{"n":"Mandazi (ostafrikanische Krapfen)","c":"welt","k":"Afrika","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 Milchdosen Weizenmehl, plus etwas zum Bearbeiten des Teigs","1 TL Backpulver","1 Prise Salz","1 TL abgeriebene Zitronenschale","½ Tasse Zucker","½ TL gemahlene Nelken (optional)","2 EL Margarine oder Butter, zimmerwarm","2 Tassen Wasser","1 TL Vanillearoma","Pflanzenöl zum Braten"],"s":["Sift together the flour and baking powder in a bowl.","Mix in the salt, lemon zest, sugar, and cloves.","Rub in the butter until the flour becomes coarse.","Combine the vanilla and water, then mix this into the flour mixture to get a firm dough.","Knead the dough for about 2 minutes until it no longer sticks to your hands. Set aside to rest for 10 minutes.","Flour a work surface, and roll out the dough to about 1-inch thickness.","Cut the dough into 10 equal squares, then roll each square into a ball.","Heat a pan of oil over medium heat. Deep fry the mandazi in batches of 5 for about 10 minutes or until they are puffed, brown all over, and cooked through.","Remove when it is fully done and enjoy your delicious East African Doughnuts."],"x":[],"desc":"Mandazi are East African doughnuts that originated from places like Uganda, Kenya, and Tanzania. They are popular as a street food.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mandazi_(East_African_Doughnuts)","i":"wb-en-2616","im":["6/69/Bowl_of_mandazi.jpg/500px-Bowl_of_mandazi.jpg","The original uploader was ChildofMidnight at English Wikiped","CC BY 2.0","Bowl of mandazi.jpg","w"],"on":"Mandazi (East African Doughnuts)","og":["4 milk cups all-purpose flour, plus extra for working the dough","1 tsp baking powder","1 pinch salt","1 tsp lemon zest","½ cup white granulated sugar","½ tsp ground cloves (optional)","2 tbsp margarine or butter, at room temperature","2 cups water","1 tsp vanilla essence","Vegetable oil for frying"]},{"n":"Mandoca (frittierte Maisringe)","c":"brot","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["3 mittelgroße Bananenpaprika","113 g Mehl","Öl (so viel, wie die Fritteuse braucht)"],"s":["Roll the pepper in the flour until well-coated.","Deep fry for about 2 minutes."],"x":[],"desc":"Mandoca is a Venezuelan snack of deep-fried breaded pepper. It originated at the snack bar in the Ford factory in Pedernales during the 1990s. The simple snack can be made with any types of peppers, although authenic mandocas use banana peppers.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mandoca_(Fried_Breaded_Pepper)","i":"wb-en-2617","im":["4/4f/Mandocas_maracuchas.jpg/960px-Mandocas_maracuchas.jpg","DamianFinol","CC BY-SA 3.0","Mandocas maracuchas.jpg","w"],"on":"Mandoca (Fried Breaded Pepper)","og":["3 medium banana peppers","113 grams (¼ lb) flour","Oil (enough to fill the deep fryer)"]},{"n":"Mango-Atchar (eingelegte Mango)","c":"saucen","k":"Südafrika","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1,5 kg unreife Mangos, gehackt","4 TL Knoblauch-Kräutersalz","3 EL Chilipulver","2 EL gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","1 EL gemahlener Koriander","3 EL Currypulver","360 ml roher Honig oder Fruchtzucker","480 ml Aceto balsamico","120 g Mais- oder Kartoffelstärke","2 EL Senfsamen","1 Handvoll Curryblätter","360 ml natives Olivenöl oder kaltgepresstes Sonnenblumenöl"],"s":["Simmer all the ingredients except the mangoes and the oil until thickened.","Pour mixture over the mangoes, add the oil, and mix well.","Cool and refrigerate for at least 12 hours."],"x":[],"desc":"Atchar is a spicy condiment, often eaten with a curry. It comes from the Indian cuisine in South Africa. In India, it is spelled Achar, and the word means pickle in Hindi. Usually the atchar made in South Africa is made with unripe green mangoes and chillies. The whole mango is used for making atcha","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mango_Atchar","i":"wb-en-2618","im":["3/32/Chilli_pickle_in_a_plate_2.jpg/960px-Chilli_pickle_in_a_plate_2.jpg","Suyash.dwivedi","CC BY-SA 4.0","Chilli pickle in a plate 2.jpg","w"],"on":"Mango Atchar","og":["1.5 kg unripe mangoes, chopped","4 tsp garlic and herb salt","3 Tbsp chilli powder","2 Tbsp cumin powder","1 Tbsp ground coriander","3 Tbsp curry powder","1½ cups (360 ml) raw honey or fructose","2 cups (480 ml) balsamic vinegar","½ cup (120 g) corn or potato starch","2 Tbsp mustard seeds","1 handful curry leaves","1½ cups (360 ml) virgin olive oil or cold-pressed sunflower oil"]},{"n":"Mango-Avocado-Salsa","c":"snacks","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":2,"l":"en","g":["¼ Tasse rote Zwiebel, gewürfelt","1 Jalapeño, entkernt und fein gehackt","1 kleines Bund Koriander, gehackt (etwa 1 Tasse, fest gedrückt)","3 Hass-Avocados, geschält, entkernt, und gewürfelt","1 reife Mango, geschält, entkernt, und gewürfelt (etwa 1 Tasse)","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","Saft von 1 Limette"],"s":["Combine all ingredients in a medium bowl.","Mix well with a spoon and serve with tortilla chips or use it as toppings for another dish."],"x":[],"desc":"​Refreshingly tasty mango avocado salsa is a crowd-pleasing snack or appetizer with tortilla chips.","img":"Mango Avocado Salsa.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mango_Avocado_Salsa","i":"wb-en-2619","im":["8/8e/Mango_Avocado_Salsa.jpg/500px-Mango_Avocado_Salsa.jpg","Sharon Chen","CC BY 3.0","Mango Avocado Salsa.jpg","r"],"on":"Mango Avocado Salsa","og":["¼ cup red onion, diced","1 jalapeño pepper, seeded and minced","1 small bunch of cilantro, chopped (about 1 cup, packed)","3 Hass avocados, peeled, cored, and diced","1 ripe mango, peeled, cored, and diced (about 1 cup)","Salt to taste","Pepper to taste","Juice of 1 lime"]},{"n":"Mango-Chutney (stückig)","c":"saucen","k":"Indien","p":12,"t":60,"d":2,"v":2,"l":"en","g":["6 feste, noch nicht ganz reife Mangos, gewürfelt","75 g Rosinen","250 ml Apfelessig","200 g fest gedrückter heller brauner Zucker","2 EL Knoblauch, fein gehackt","1 fein gehackte mittelgroße Zwiebel","1 ½ EL frischer Ingwer, geschabt und fein gehackt","2 TL Salz","¼ TL Cayennepfeffer","¼ TL frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer"],"s":["Dissolve the sugar and salt in the vinegar and boil for 15 minutes.","Add mangoes, raisins, and onion and bring to the boil again.","Reduce the heat to low, and simmer for 15 minutes, stirring constantly to prevent sticking.","Add the garlic, ginger and seasoning and simmer for 5 minutes.","Remove from heat and allow to cool before serving.","Due to the high sugar and acid content, this chutney may be refrigerated safely for 6 months."],"x":["Serve with hot rice or bread.","This chutney works as an excellent spread on a sandwich.","If it is not too spicy, you can serve it as a dip for tortilla chips.","You could also serve with yoghurt/curd.","This chutney is typically presented in restaurants in a steel dish with a spoon for serving oneself.","Vary amount of salt/spices as needed."],"desc":"Mango chutney is a specialty chutney of the South Indian coastal state of Andhra Pradesh. Mango chutney can be made in many different ways and can be served with poppadoms or with the main course.","img":"Mango Chutney.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mango_Chutney_(Chunky)","i":"wb-en-2620","im":["b/be/Mango_Chutney.jpg/960px-Mango_Chutney.jpg","Simon Law from Montréal, QC, Canada, modified by User:Mike H","CC BY-SA 2.0","Mango Chutney.jpg","r"],"on":"Mango Chutney (Chunky)","og":["6 firm under-ripe mangoes, cubed","75 g raisins","250 ml (1 cup) cider vinegar","200 g (1 cup) packed light brown sugar","2 tbsp garlic, finely chopped","1 ea. (½ cup) finely-chopped medium onion","1½ tbsp fresh ginger, scraped and minced","2 tsp salt","¼ tsp cayenne pepper","¼ tsp freshly ground black pepper"]},{"n":"Mango-Chutney (glatt)","c":"saucen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 große unreife Mango (unreif), geschält und in 2,5-cm-Würfel geschnitten","2 TL Senfsamen","3 EL Pflanzenöl oder natives Olivenöl extra","½ TL Asafoetida (Asant) (Hindi „Heengh“, Tamil „Perungayum“)","3–4 getrocknete rote Chilis","2–3 grüne Chilis (für mehr Schärfe mehr nehmen)","1 TL Limettensaft (falls die Mango nicht sauer genug ist)","1 TL gemahlene Kurkuma","¾ EL Salz (nach Geschmack anpassen)"],"s":["Heat the oil in a frying pan.","Add mustard seeds, asafoetida, green chillies, and red chillies. Wait until the mustard seeds splutter, then remove pan from stove.","Grind the above mixture with mango, lime juice (if needed), turmeric, and salt"],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mango_Chutney_(Smooth)","i":"wb-en-2621","im":["9/9d/Unripe_Mango_Chutney_-_Kolkata_2011-02-23_1714.JPG/960px-Unripe_Mango_Chutney_-_Kolkata_2011-02-23_1714.JPG","Biswarup Ganguly","CC BY 3.0","Unripe Mango Chutney - Kolkata 2011-02-23 1714.JPG","w"],"on":"Mango Chutney (Smooth)","og":["1 large raw (unripe) mango, peeled and cut into 1-inch cubes","2 tsp mustard seeds","3 tbsp vegetable oil or extra-virgin olive oil","½ tsp asafoetida (\"Heengh\" in Hindi, \"Perungayum\" in Tamil)","3–4 dry red chiles","2–3 green chiles (add more if you want it spicier)","1 tsp lime juice (if mango is not sour enough)","1 tsp turmeric powder","¾ tbsp salt (adjust to taste)"]},{"n":"Klebreis mit Mango und Kokos","c":"dessert","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["210 g Kokosmilch","6–7 Pandanblätter","Salz","8 Tassen Kokoswasser","2 Tassen ungekochter Klebreis, gut abgespült","250 g brauner Zucker","Mango","Fruchtfleisch junger Kokosnüsse"],"s":["Bring coconut milk to a boil with pandan leaves. Add a little salt to taste.","Stir in the coconut water. Stir in the sticky rice, and simmer about 15 minutes over low heat.","Stir in the mango, and simmer for 5 minutes.","Add sugar and stir until the sugar has dissolved. Add the coconut meat.","Serve."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mango_Coconut_Sticky_Rice","i":"wb-en-2622","im":["b/bf/Thai_Classic_Mango_%26_Sticky_Rice_with_Coconut_Ice_Cream_-_Namo_2026-07-30.jpg/960px-Thai_Classic_Mango_%26_Sticky_Rice_with_Coconut_Ice_Cream_-_Namo_2026-07-30.jpg","Andy Li","CC0","Thai Classic Mango & Sticky Rice with Coconut Ice Cream - Namo 2026-07-30.jpg","c"],"on":"Mango Coconut Sticky Rice","og":["210 g coconut milk","6–7 pandan leaves","Salt","8 cups coconut water","2 cups uncooked sticky rice, rinsed well","250 g brown sugar","Mango","Young coconut meat"]},{"n":"Mango-Kokos-Chutney (Aam ki Chatni)","c":"saucen","k":"Indien","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 fast reife Mangos","1 EL frische Kokosnuss oder aus der Dose, fein gehackt","1 TL Koriander oder Minze, gehackt","1 EL frischer Ingwer, geschabt und fein gehackt","1 TL Salz","½ TL Cayennepfeffer","2–3 EL frischer Orangensaft, oder eine Mischung aus Orangen- und Limettensaft"],"s":["Place the mango on one side on a work surface and make a slit in the tip across its width with a sharp knife.","Then hold the mango upright on its stem end, on the work surface, and carefully slice the flesh, with the skin attached, off one side of the stone, as close to it as possible. Then turn it the other way and cut off the flesh from the other side of the stone.","Place each mango half, skin-side down, on the work surface, and cut lines through the flesh down to the skin in a lattice pattern so that you end up with a checker-board pattern with ½-inch squares.","Grasp the mango half with both your hands, skin down and your two thumbs on the flesh and your four fingers of each hand underneath on the skin.","Now, turn the skin inside out by pushing the skin inwards with your four fingers of each hand while pushing the two sides downward with your two thumbs.","You will now have the skin of the mango with cubes of flesh attached which can be easily cut off with a sharp knife.","Place the mango cubes in a small bowl.","Add the coconut, cilantro, ginger, cayenne, orange/lime juice, and salt and mix gently with a tablespoon.","Leave to marinate in the refrigerator for 1–2 hours before serving."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mango_and_Coconut_Chutney_(Am_ki_Chatni)","i":"wb-en-2623","im":["a/a5/Coconut_Chutney_-_Home_Made.JPG/960px-Coconut_Chutney_-_Home_Made.JPG","Mailz2kumar","CC BY-SA 4.0","Coconut Chutney - Home Made.JPG","w"],"on":"Mango and Coconut Chutney (Am ki Chatni)","og":["2 almost-ripe mangoes","1 Tbsp fresh or canned coconut, finely chopped","1 tsp cilantro or mint, chopped","1 Tbsp fresh ginger, scraped and finely chopped","1 tsp salt","½ tsp cayenne pepper","2–3 Tbsp fresh orange juice, or a mixture of orange and lime juice"]},{"n":"Curry mit Mango und gelben Schälerbsen","c":"veggie","k":"Indien","p":2,"t":25,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse Toor Dal (gelbe Straucherbsen)","2 Dosen Mango (oder frische Mango, falls erhältlich), in Scheiben geschnitten","1 Zwiebel, gehackt","1 Zehe Galgant oder Ingwer","1 TL Knoblauchpaste","1 TL Ghee","1 TL Asant-Pulver (Hing)","3 TL Kurkuma","1 TL Garam Masala","1 TL Chilipulver","2 TL Senfsamen","1 TL Kreuzkümmel","1 TL Bockshornkleeblätter"],"s":["Soak dal over night.","Boil dal in water. Rinse, drain, and keep in separate container.","Boil mango slices in their juice. Add boiled dal and add additional water if required.","In a separate pan, sauté onion, ginger paste, and garlic paste in oil until golden brown.","In a separate pan heat ghee, hing, turmeric, garam masala, chilli powder, mustard seeds, and cumin.","Add all mixtures together in boiling mango and dal pot.","Add fenugreek leaves, and continue boiling.","Allow to cool and serve with rotis or naan and rice."],"x":[],"desc":"Mango Dal also known as Amchur Dal is a vegetarian dish from Southern India which is also popular in the West. The dish is popular amongst vegetarians and persons who wish to limit the amount of meat in their diet.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mango_and_Yellow_Split_Pea_Curry","i":"wb-en-2624","on":"Mango and Yellow Split Pea Curry","og":["1 cup toor dal","2 cans mango (or fresh mango if available), sliced","1 onion, chopped","1 clove galangal or ginger","1 teaspoon garlic paste","1 teaspoon ghee","1 teaspoon hing powder","3 teaspoons turmeric","1 teaspoon garam masala","1 teaspoon chilli powder","2 teaspoons mustard seeds","1 teaspoon cumin","1 teaspoon fenugreek leaves"]},{"n":"Manhattan Clam Chowder I","c":"suppen","k":"USA","p":6,"t":90,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["425 g Kartoffeln aus der Dose, oder 2 kleine gekochte Kartoffeln","794 g Tomaten im Saft aus der Dose, oder 2 große Tomaten und Tomatensaft","184 g gehackte Venusmuscheln aus der Dose, mindestens","2 Stangen Staudensellerie"],"s":["Core the tomatoes. Remove the pale parts and the seeds; the \"meat\" of the tomato will be what will be used. For canned tomatoes, a strainer will be helpful.","Chop all non-clam ingredients to match the clams in size.","If desired add spices. Suggestions offered include dill seed, basil, thyme, celery seed, tarragon, marjoram, and/or fresh cilantro. Alternatively, oregano can be used in lieu of the marjoram.","Cook the chowder, without boiling, until the celery begins to soften."],"x":["A sturdy type of fish can be used in place of the clams; good choices include catfish, tilapia, and pollock.","Cooked rice can be substituted for the potatoes, the celery can be replaced with spinach or seaweed, and lemon juice can be added."],"desc":"Manhattan clam chowder is a soup traditionally made from clams, herbs, tomatoes, and other vegetables. Despite its name, it originated in Rhode Island, not Manhattan.","img":"ManhattanClamChowder.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Manhattan_Clam_Chowder_I","i":"wb-en-2625","im":["4/47/ManhattanClamChowder.jpg/960px-ManhattanClamChowder.jpg","stu_spivack","CC BY-SA 2.0","ManhattanClamChowder.jpg","r"],"og":["15 ounces (425 g) canned potatoes, or 2 small boiled potatoes","28 ounces (794 g) canned tomatoes in juice, or 2 large tomatoes and tomato juice","6.5 ounces (184 g) canned chopped clams, minimum","2 stalks of celery"]},{"n":"Manhattan Clam Chowder II","c":"suppen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Gläser Venusmuscheln oder 2 Packungen TK-Muscheln (650 g)","1 Tasse Staudensellerie in Scheiben","2 EL gehackte Petersilie","115 g gesalzener Speck, gewürfelt","1 Lorbeerblatt","3 mittelgroße Zwiebeln, gewürfelt","¼ TL Thymian","2 Tassen gehackte Tomaten","2 mittelgroße Kartoffeln, gewürfelt","1,4 l Wasser","1 Tasse gewürfelte rohe Möhren","8–10 Salzcracker","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pfeffer, nach Geschmack"],"s":["Strain the clam juice.","Put the clams through food chopper, using the coarse blade.","Fry pork in a heavy iron pot.","Remove pork, and sauté onions in the fat until tender and lightly browned.","Add tomatoes and cook for 5 minutes.","Add water, carrots, celery, and herbs.","Cover pot and gently simmer for 1½ hours.","Add clams, strained clam juice, and potatoes; cook until potatoes are tender.","Season with salt and pepper to taste.","Bring to a boil, pour over crumbled soda crackers in individual plates, and serve at once."],"x":["You can use a low-fat cut of pork to lower the fat and calories of this dish."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Manhattan_Clam_Chowder_II","i":"wb-en-2626","im":["6/69/Quail_07_bg_041506.jpg/960px-Quail_07_bg_041506.jpg","Jon Sullivan The original uploader was Y6y6y6 at English Wik","Public domain","Quail 07 bg 041506.jpg","w"],"og":["2 jars (23 ounces) clams or 2 packages (24 ounces) frozen clams","1 cup sliced celery","2 tablespoons chopped parsley","¼ pound salt pork, diced","1 bay leaf","3 medium onions, diced","¼ teaspoon thyme","2 cups chopped tomatoes","2 medium potatoes, diced","1½ quarts water","1 cup diced raw carrots","8–10 soda crackers","Salt to taste","Pepper to taste"]},{"n":"Räucherlachs von der Isle of Man","c":"fisch","k":"","p":6,"t":60,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["450 g Bücklinge (Kipper)","450 g Räucherlachs, in Scheiben geschnitten","500–600 ml Sahne","20 g gehackter Schnittlauch","¼–½ Gurke, in dünne Scheiben geschnitten","½ Tomate, in Scheiben geschnitten, entkernt, und gehäutet"],"s":["Boil the kippers in a pot of salty water","Add 4 rings of smoked salmon to a greaseproof tray in foil (slices can go over the edge)","Wait for the kippers to finish boiling then refresh them with cold water for 3–5 minutes. Fillet them, then skin and place them in a blender.","Add cream gradually and blend.","Add chives to the mix.","Add the mixture to the rings and remove any air pockets by shaking.","Fold over the salmon slices and turn over the rings. Cover with clingfilm and refrigerate.","Add about 6 slices of the cucumber to the centre of each plate.","Remove food from refrigerator, remove from oven tray and put them upside down on top of the cucumber slices.","Add more strips of cucumber and tomato to the top of the food. Serve!"],"x":[],"desc":"Fish dishes are popular in Isle of Man, as they are in most islands and coastal regions. Kippers are especially popular in Mann and this recipe is a tasty alternative to many standard meals.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Manx_Smoked_Salmon","i":"wb-en-2627","on":"Manx Smoked Salmon","og":["450 g kippers","450 g smoked salmon, sliced","500–600 ml cream","20 g chopped chives","¼–½ ea. cucumber, thinly sliced","½ tomato, sliced, de-seeded, and skinned"]},{"n":"Baby-Back-Ribs mit Ahorn-Barbecuesoße","c":"fleisch","k":"USA","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Leitern Baby-Back-Ribs","Gewürzmischung für Rippchen","Ahorn-Barbecuesoße","Hickory- und Apfelholzstücke"],"s":["Remove membrane on the bottom of the ribs. Season both sides liberally with rib rub and refrigerate at least 1 hour.","Place enough hickory and applewood chunks in the firebox of a smoker to keep the temperature around 200 °F (95 °C).","Place ribs in smoker and cook, brushing with barbecue sauce every 1½ hours for 4 hours or until very tender, changing chunks as needed.","Brush meat side of ribs liberally with sauce and place meat side down on a very, very hot grill until well browned and slightly charred.","Slice into one-rib portions and serve with additional sauce."],"x":[],"desc":"These ribs have beaten some of the best BBQ joints around, including Famous Dave's and Roscoe's, in local competitions.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maple_Barbecue_Baby_Back_Ribs","i":"wb-en-2628","on":"Maple Barbecue Baby Back Ribs","og":["2 slabs baby-back pork ribs","Rib Rub","Maple Barbecue Sauce","Hickory and applewood chunks"]},{"n":"Ahorn-Barbecuesoße","c":"saucen","k":"USA","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1,9 l Ketchup","1 ½ Tassen Ahornsirup (am besten eine dunkle Sorte)","1 Tasse Apfelessig","¼ Tasse Hickory-Grillgewürz","2 EL gelber Senf (amerikanisch)","½ Tasse Worcestersoße","2 Habanero-Chilis, entstielt"],"s":["Combine all ingredients in a large saucepan or pot.","Bring to a boil over high heat and cook until liquid has reduced by ⅓.","Remove chiles and discard.","Keep refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 3 weeks."],"x":[],"desc":"This maple barbecue sauce is great with chicken, but it contains sugar in this sauce, so put it on things 10–15 minutes before you take them off the heat.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maple_Barbecue_Sauce","i":"wb-en-2629","im":["3/36/Pork_steaks_cooking-1.jpg/960px-Pork_steaks_cooking-1.jpg","Wikipedian Kbh3rd","CC BY-SA 3.0","Pork steaks cooking-1.jpg","w"],"on":"Maple Barbecue Sauce","og":["2 quarts ketchup","1 ½ cups maple syrup (preferably a dark grade)","1 cup apple cider vinegar","¼ cup Hickory BBQ Rub","2 Tbsp yellow mustard","½ cup Worcestershire sauce","2 habanero chiles, stemmed"]},{"n":"Ahorn-Bohnen","c":"beilagen","k":"Kanada","p":4,"t":420,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["625 ml kleine getrocknete weiße Bohnen","2 l Wasser","1 große milde Zwiebel, fein gewürfelt","250 ml Ahornsirup","30 ml dunkler brauner Zucker","30 ml Butter","2 ml Senfpulver","5 ml gemahlener Pfeffer","5 ml Salz","6 Scheiben Bauchspeck oder 60 ml Speckfett"],"s":["Wash beans and place in a saucepan with the water. Cover and bring to a boil, checking regularly.","When water has reached the boiling point, time for 5 minutes and remove from heat. Let sit for 1 hour, covered.","After the hour, return beans and water to heat and bring to a simmer, still covered. Simmer for 45 minutes.","Strain beans and water through a colander, collecting the liquids in a bowl for later use.","Combine the onion, salt, mustard, and maple syrup. Add 625 ml (2 ½ cups) of the aforementioned bean-water to the mix and blend well.","Finely slice the bacon, place in roast pan/casserole dish, and cover with the beans, pouring the liquid mixture over top.","Cover and bake for 3 hours at 165°C (325°F), adding 125 ml (½ cup) of bean-water at the 2 ½ hour mark.","Melt butter and combine with brown sugar. Pour over the baked beans and bake, uncovered, until liquid is no longer visible."],"x":["You can substitute honey or molasses for the maple syrup; maple is used for it's flavouring as much as its sweetness.","Margarine or vegetable oil will do as well as butter for this; butter was used traditionally and is thus listed.","This is often served with ham and sweet cornbread."],"desc":"Maple beans is a modification of the standard Baked Beans made throughout much of Europe and North America. This variant is common through south and central Quebec as well as most of Ontario and can be purchased in cans across Canada.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maple_Beans","i":"wb-en-2630","im":["e/ed/Baked_beans_in_maple_syrup.JPG/960px-Baked_beans_in_maple_syrup.JPG","CoveyHill","CC BY-SA 3.0","Baked beans in maple syrup.JPG","c"],"on":"Maple Beans","og":["625 ml (2 ½ cups) small dried white beans","2 L (8 cups) water","1 large sweet onion, finely diced","250 ml (1 cup) maple syrup","30 ml (2 Tbsp) dark brown sugar","30 ml (2 Tbsp) butter","2 ml (½ tsp) dry mustard","5 ml (½ tsp) ground pepper","5 ml (1 tsp) salt","6 slices side bacon OR 60 ml (¼ cup) bacon runoff"]},{"n":"Ahorn-Butter-Tarte","c":"kuchen","k":"Kanada","p":12,"t":60,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Teig","2 ½ Tassen Weizenmehl","1 TL Salz","1 EL weißer Zucker","1 Tasse kalte ungesalzene Butter, gewürfelt","6–8 EL eiskaltes Wasser","#Füllung","½ Tasse ungesalzene Butter, weich","1 Tasse heller brauner Zucker, fest gedrückt","½ Tasse reiner Ahornsirup","2 Eier (Größe M) (110 bis 125 g mit Schale)","1 TL reiner Vanilleextrakt","1 EL Branntwein- oder Apfelessig","½ Tasse gehackte Pekannüsse, Walnüsse, Haselnüsse, oder Butternüsse","Prisen Salz"],"s":["Preheat oven to 190 °C (375 °F).","Mix the flour, salt, and sugar in the bowl of a food processor.","Cut in the cold butter and mix with a series of short pulses, until the mixture resembles pea-meal. The crust will have a flakier texture if you avoid mixing the butter in too much.","Gradually pulse in ice water, 1 tbsp at a time, until the dough just holds together. You may not need all the water.","Divide into two discs, wrap in plastic, and chill for at least 30 minutes.","Roll the dough to ⅛ inch (3 mm) thick. Cut into 4 inch (10 cm) rounds.","Gently press each round into a cup of a non-stick muffin pan. Chill the pan chill while making the filling.","Cream the butter and brown sugar until smooth.","Whisk in the eggs until light and slightly frothy.","Stir in maple syrup, vanilla, vinegar, and salt. Mix until smooth, but not foamy.","Fill tart shells with the filling to about about two-thirds full.","Sprinkle a spoonful of chopped nuts over the top of each tart.","Bake for 15–18 minutes until the centre is gooey and slightly runny, which is the traditional Canadian style. If you prefer a firmer tart, cook for 20 minutes.","Let cool in the tin for 10 minutes, then carefully lift out and cool on a rack."],"x":["Shorter bake time results in a more gooey centre; longer baking (20–22 minutes) will set the filling more firmly.","Do not overbeat the filling, which would result in a foamy or cakey texture.","These are best served at room temperature or slightly warm."],"desc":"Butter tarts are a traditional Canadian dessert with a flaky pastry shell and a rich, buttery sweetened filling that stays slightly runny in the centre. The tarts are baked in muffin tins, so each is an individual portion. This version uses maple syrup instead of corn syrup for a more complex, espec","img":"Maple Butter Tart.png","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maple_Butter_Tart","i":"wb-en-2631","im":["f/fa/Maple_Butter_Tart.png/960px-Maple_Butter_Tart.png","Cnrowley","CC BY-SA 4.0","Maple Butter Tart.png","r"],"on":"Maple Butter Tart","og":["#Pastry","2½ cups all-purpose flour","1 tsp salt","1 tbsp white sugar","1 cup cold unsalted butter, cubed","6–8 tbsp ice-cold water","#Filling","½ cup unsalted butter, softened","1 cup light brown sugar, packed","½ cup pure maple syrup","2 ea. (110–125 g in-shell) standard eggs","1 tsp pure vanilla extract","1 tbsp white or apple cider vinegar","½ cup chopped pecans, walnuts, hazelnuts, or butternuts","Pinch of salt"]},{"n":"Ahorncreme","c":"saucen","k":"","p":2,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["mindestens 1 Liter reiner Ahornsirup (1 l)","geschmacksneutrales Pflanzenöl"],"s":["Pour the maple syrup into a saucepan. Use a saucepan deep enough to accommodate the syrup without allowing it to boil over and narrow enough to ensure the syrup comes to a depth of at least about 2 inches (5 cm).","If using a traditional (i.e. not instant-read) candy thermometer, place it in the pan now. Make sure the syrup covers the probe section that measures the temperature.","Add just a few drops of vegetable oil to the pan—this will help prevent large bubbles from forming during cooking.","Bring the syrup to a gentle boil without stirring. Cook the syrup, still without stirring, to 230–235 °F (110–113 °C).","Remove the saucepan from the heat, and place it into an ice bath without letting the syrup get wet. Let it cool in the bath without disturbance until the syrup reaches 80–100 °F (27–38 °C). The syrup will thicken considerably.","Transfer the cooled syrup to a bowl. Use a spoon, paddle, or spatula to slowly and continuously stir the syrup for about 15–30 minutes. The mixture should thicken, grow opaque, and lose its gloss.","Once the mixture loses its gloss, stop stirring, and immediately transfer it to a jar or other container. If you wait too long, the mixture will become hard to work with."],"x":["The stirring process encourages the formation of small crystals throughout the maple syrup. Keep it up slowly and continuously.","Don't be tempted to leave all the stirring work to a home mixer. You can use one for perhaps the first half of the process, but it will eventually get too thick and can risk burning out the mixer's motor.","The finished product behaves like a non-Newtonian fluid—if it has solidified too much to easily transfer to a storage container, gently knead and roll it with clean hands until it softens, then press into the container."],"desc":"Maple cream, also called maple butter, is a type of sweet spread or condiment made from cooked maple syrup. It shouldn't be confused with compound butters containing whipped dairy butter and maple syrup. Use maple cream in other confections, baked goods, and breakfast items like pancakes.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maple_Cream","i":"wb-en-2632","im":["6/62/Maple_butter.jpg/500px-Maple_butter.jpg","Gail from Calgary, Canada","CC BY 2.0","Maple butter.jpg","w"],"on":"Maple Cream","og":["At least 1 quart (1 L) pure maple syrup","Neutral-tasting vegetable oil"]},{"n":"Gegrillte Bananen mit Ahorn-Kreuzkümmel-Glasur","c":"dessert","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 Bananen, geschält und längs halbiert","½ Tasse Ahornsirup","2 EL dunkler Rum","½ TL gemahlener Kreuzkümmel"],"s":["Spray bananas and cold grill grate with nonstick cooking spray.","Place a large saucepan over high heat and add rum. Ignite. Once flames have died, remove from heat and whisk in remaining ingredients.","Place bananas cut side down on the preheated grill, and brush with rum mixture. Cook for 2 minutes, then flip and brush grilled side with more rum mixture.","Cook other side until well browned. Flip and cook just until browned. Remove and serve."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maple_Cumin_Glazed_Grilled_Bananas","i":"wb-en-2633","on":"Maple Cumin Glazed Grilled Bananas","og":["4 bananas, peeled and halved lengthwise","½ cup maple syrup","2 tbsp dark rum","½ tsp ground cumin"]},{"n":"Hähnchenbrust mit Ahornglasur","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 Hähnchenbrustfilets ohne Haut","½ Tasse dunkler Ahornsirup (Grade B) (dunkler Ahornsirup, Grade A Dark Amber geht auch)","¼ Tasse Hühnerbrühe","2 EL Worcestersoße","geschmolzene Butter","1 EL Salz","1 EL frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","2 EL Zitronenpfeffer"],"s":["Combine maple syrup, sauce, and broth in a small saucepan over medium-high heat. Bring to a boil and cook until reduced by ⅓. Set aside.","Combine salt, pepper, and lemon pepper. Brush chicken with melted butter and press seasoning mixture into both sides of each chicken breast.","Place chicken in a shallow roasting pan. Insert a probe thermometer into one of the pieces and roast at 375°F (190°C) until internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C).","Brush top of chicken pieces with maple mixture. Remove while your broiler heats up.","Place chicken under your preheated broiler until top is well browned and slightly charred.","Remove to a plate and cover with aluminum foil. Let rest 7 minutes before serving with remaining maple mixture."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maple_Glazed_Chicken_Breasts","i":"wb-en-2634","on":"Maple Glazed Chicken Breasts","og":["4 boneless skinless chicken breasts","½ cup Grade B Amber maple syrup (Grade A Dark Amber would be okay too.)","¼ cup chicken broth","2 tbsp Worcestershire sauce","Melted butter","1 Tbsp salt","1 Tbsp freshly-ground black pepper","2 Tbsp lemon pepper"]},{"n":"Hähnchenbrust vom Ahornholzbrett","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Hähnchenbrustfilets ohne Haut","Olivenöl","Salz","frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","1 TL frisch gemahlener Koriander","2 mittelgroße unbehandelte Ahornholzbretter, mindestens 1 Stunde in Wasser eingeweicht"],"s":["Brush chicken with olive oil. Sprinkle both sides liberally with salt, freshly ground black pepper, and the freshly-ground coriander.","Place chicken on planks and insert a probe thermometer into one of the breasts. Heat one burner or push all the coals to one side and place planks on the cooler side. Cook until internal temperature reaches 165°F.","Remove chicken to a plate and cover with aluminum foil. Let rest 5 minutes before serving."],"x":["Use untreated wood. I don't think any of you would like to be eating pentachloraethylne, creosote, and/or arsenic! If you would not like to eat this stuff, remember to purchase untreated wood that is furniture grade and kiln-dried."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maple_Planked_Chicken_Breasts","i":"wb-en-2635","on":"Maple Planked Chicken Breasts","og":["2 ea. (12–16 ounces) boneless skinless chicken breasts","Olive oil","Salt","Freshly-ground black pepper","1 tsp freshly-ground coriander","2 medium untreated maple planks, soaked in water at least 1 hour"]},{"n":"Lachs vom Ahornholzbrett mit Rumglasur","c":"fisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Seite Rotlachs (Sockeye) (910 g)","Salz","frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","1 EL Olivenöl","½ Tasse dunkler Rum","1 großes unbehandeltes Ahornholzbrett, mindestens 1 Stunde in Wasser eingeweicht"],"s":["Brush salmon with oil. Sprinkle liberally with salt and freshly ground black pepper.","Place salmon on plank. Heat grill to medium on one burner.","Bring rum to a boil in a saucepan over high heat. Remove from heat and ignite. Boil until reduced to ¼ cup.","Place plank on indirect heat and cook for 20 minutes, brushing often with rum.","Let rest 5 minutes. Serve."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maple_Planked_Salmon_with_Rum_Glaze","i":"wb-en-2636","on":"Maple Planked Salmon with Rum Glaze","og":["1 side (1.5–2 lb) of sockeye salmon","Salt","Freshly-ground black pepper","1 tbsp olive oil","½ cup dark rum","1 large untreated maple plank, soaked in water for at least 1 hour"]},{"n":"Lachs vom Ahornholzbrett mit Ahornsirup","c":"fisch","k":"USA","p":4,"t":765,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 Lachssteaks oder einzelne Filets (am besten aus Wildfang)","4 EL frischer Zitronensaft (60 ml), aufgeteilt","2 TL reiner Ahornsirup (10 ml)","2 EL Traubenkernöl (30 ml) (oder ein anderes neutrales Öl)","1 ½ TL Chipotle-Pulver (7 g) (ersatzweise Chipotle-Barbecuesoße)","1 TL zerstoßener getrockneter Rosmarin (5 g)","2 Frühlingszwiebeln, in dünne Scheiben geschnitten zum Garnieren","Salz"],"s":["Completely immerse cedar planks in water for several hours or overnight.","Heat grill to medium-high.","Mix 2 tablespoons (30 ml) lemon juice, the oil, rosemary, maple syrup, and half of the chipotle powder in a small bowl. Coat the salmon with the mixture and let rest at room temperature for 20 minutes.","Mix the remaining lemon juice with the remaining chipotle powder with a fork and set aside as a garnish.","Place plank(s) on grill and close lid. Allow plank to heat for a couple minutes.","Lightly sprinkle salt on plank(s).","Put salmon on plank, keeping fish at least an inch from the edge of the plank (in the case of fillets, place skin-side down). Reduce heat to low and close lid.","Grill for roughly 15 minutes without turning or moving salmon until desired \"doneness\" is reached. Generally, salmon should be cooked until the flesh loses its transparency and the meat can easily be broken with a fork.","Spray with water to douse any flames that light on the sides of the plank.","When cooked, place the salmon on a serving platter and sprinkle with the scallions.","Immerse the cedar plank in water as a safety precaution.","Serve the salmon with the optional lemon juice/chipotle sauce."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maple_Syrup_Planked_Salmon","i":"wb-en-2637","on":"Maple Syrup Planked Salmon","og":["4 salmon steaks or individual fillets (preferably wild-caught)","4 tbsp (60 ml) fresh lemon juice, divided","2 tsp (10 ml) pure maple syrup","2 tbsp (30 ml) grapeseed oil (or other neutral oil)","1½ tsp (7 g) chipotle powder (chipotle barbecue sauce may be substituted for this)","1 tsp (5 g) crushed dried rosemary","2 scallions, thinly sliced for garnish","Salt"]},{"n":"Barbecue-Rippchen mit Ahornglasur","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Leiter Schweinerippchen (Spareribs)","1 EL Salz","3 EL dunkler brauner Zucker","2 EL geräuchertes Paprikapulver","2 EL Cayennepfeffer","1 Tasse Ahornsirup","1 Tasse Weißwein","¼ Tasse Worcestersoße","¼ Tasse Sojasoße","3 EL Apfelessig","Hickoryholzstücke"],"s":["Combine seasonings and rub on pork ribs.","Refrigerate for at least 1 hour.","Place hickory chunks into a 350°F (175˚C) smoker or a charcoal grill set for indirect heat at 350°F.","Combine liquid ingredients and bring to a boil over high heat until reduced by half.","Place ribs in smoker/grill and cook, basting often with maple syrup mixture, for 3–4 hours","Brush ribs with remaining mixture and place on a medium high grill until well browned.","Rest 15 minutes; serve."],"x":[],"desc":"Maple syrup and pork just sort of seem to be made for each other.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maple-Glazed_BBQ_Ribs","i":"wb-en-2638","on":"Maple-Glazed BBQ Ribs","og":["1 slab pork spareribs","1 Tbsp salt","3 Tbsp dark brown sugar","2 Tbsp smoked paprika","2 Tbsp cayenne pepper","1 cup maple syrup","1 cup white wine","¼ cup Worcestershire sauce","¼ cup soy sauce","3 Tbsp cider vinegar","Hickory wood chunks"]},{"n":"Mapo Tofu","c":"fleisch","k":"China","p":2,"t":30,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Zwiebel, in Scheiben geschnitten","1 kleines Stück Ingwer, fein gehackt (etwa 2 TL)","1–2 TL zerstoßene getrocknete Chili","200 g Rinderhack, oder Schwein","4 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","500 g Seidentofu, gewürfelt","2 EL Chili-Bohnenpaste (La Doubanjiang, scharfe Bohnenpaste)","1 EL Szechuanpfeffer, geröstet und gemahlen","1 EL Sojasoße","1 EL Reiswein","3–4 Frühlingszwiebeln, in 2 cm große Stücke geschnitten","2–3 Pilze (am besten Mu-Err-Pilze, optional)"],"s":["If using dried mushrooms, soak them in hot water for 10 minutes while preparing the rest of the ingredients, then slice before adding later.","Sauté onion with ginger and crushed chili.","Add minced meat and garlic, and fry until brown.","Mix in other ingredients (including sliced mushrooms), lower heat, and simmer for 5–10 minutes.","Serve over steamed jasmine rice."],"x":["Some extra chili pepper can be substituted for Szechuan pepper, but the taste and feeling will be different. Szechuan pepper has a numbing sensation, not heat.","A little ground coriander and cumin is very nice in this dish, especially if you cannot find Szechuan pepper easily.","A red bell pepper, a tomato, and fresh coriander leaves are all welcome additions, though not traditional.","The meal is just as good with whole beans instead of tofu.","A vegan/vegetarian version of this meal can be made by substituting the meat with textured vegetable protein (TVP) or ground tofu (e.g. Shiok Food's Vegetarian Ma Po Tofu)"],"desc":"Mápó dòufu (麻婆豆腐), also romanized as mapo tofu, is a classic spicy tofu and meat dish from the Szechuan province of China. It is a very flavourful, easy-to-prepare, and spicy dish.","img":"Mapo tofu.JPG","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mapo_Tofu","i":"wb-en-2639","im":["6/6c/Mapo_tofu.JPG/960px-Mapo_tofu.JPG","unbekannt","CC BY-SA 2.0","Mapo tofu.JPG","r"],"og":["1 onion, sliced","1 small piece of ginger, minced (about 2 tsp)","1–2 tsp crushed dried chile pepper","200 g (7 oz) minced beef, or pork","4 cloves of garlic, minced","500 g (1 lb) silken tofu, cubed","2 tbsp chili bean paste (la doubanjiang)","1 tbsp Szechuan pepper, roasted and ground","1 tbsp soy sauce","1 tbsp rice wine","3–4 green onions, cut into 2 cm (1 inch) pieces","2–3 mushrooms (tree ears preferred; optional)"]},{"n":"Maraq (Fleischsuppe)","c":"welt","k":"Kenia","p":4,"t":0,"d":3,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["500 g Lamm, Ziege, Rind, oder Hähnchen, in Stücke geschnitten","2 EL Pflanzenöl oder Ghee","1 große Zwiebel, gehackt","3 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","2 mittelgroße Tomaten, gewürfelt","2 Möhren, in Scheiben geschnitten","2 Kartoffeln, gewürfelt","1 Zucchini, in Scheiben geschnitten","1 grüne Chilischote (optional)","6 Tassen Wasser oder Brühe","frischer Koriander (Koriandergrün), gehackt","1 TL gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","1 TL gemahlener Koriander","½ TL Kurkuma","½ TL schwarzer Pfeffer","1 TL Xawaash-Gewürzmischung (somalisch) (optional, aber traditionell)","Salz, nach Geschmack"],"s":["Wash and trim the meat if necessary, then cut it into medium-sized pieces. Heat oil or ghee in a large pot over medium heat and add the chopped onions, cooking until soft and golden. Stir in the garlic and cook for another minute until fragrant.","Add the diced tomatoes and cook until softened, then mix in the cumin, coriander, turmeric, black pepper, salt, and xawaash spice blend.","Add the meat to the pot and stir well so it becomes fully coated with the spices. Cook for about 5–7 minutes until lightly browned. Pour in the water or stock and bring the mixture to a boil.","Reduce the heat and allow it to simmer for 45–60 minutes, depending on the type of meat used.","Add the carrots, potatoes, zucchini, and chili pepper, then continue simmering for another 20–25 minutes until the vegetables are tender. Taste the soup and adjust the seasoning if needed. Garnish with fresh coriander before serving hot."],"x":["Maraq is commonly served with","Somali rice (bariis)","Flatbread such as canjeero or laxoox","Fresh lime wedges","Bananas, a common Somali accompaniment to savory dishes"],"desc":"Maraq is a rich and aromatic soup popular across the Horn of Africa, especially in Somalia, Djibouti, Kenya,Ethiopia, and parts of Yemen. The word maraq simply means “broth” or “soup” in Somali. It is traditionally prepared with meat, vegetables, fragrant spices, and herbs, creating a hearty and nou","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Maraq","i":"wb-en-2640","im":["e/ee/Maraq.jpg/960px-Maraq.jpg","Abu Isa","CC BY 4.0","Maraq.jpg","c"],"on":"Maraq","og":["500 g (1 lb) lamb, goat, beef, or chicken, cut into pieces","2 tablespoons vegetable oil or ghee","1 large onion, chopped","3 cloves garlic, minced","2 medium tomatoes, diced","2 carrots, sliced","2 potatoes, cubed","1 zucchini, sliced","1 green chili pepper (optional)","6 cups water or stock","Fresh coriander (cilantro), chopped","1 teaspoon ground cumin","1 teaspoon ground coriander","½ teaspoon turmeric","½ teaspoon black pepper","1 teaspoon Xawaash spice blend (optional but traditional)","Salt to taste"]},{"n":"Margarita-Grillhähnchen","c":"fleisch","k":"Mexiko","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 Hähnchenbrustfilets ohne Haut","½ TL frisch gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","½ Tasse Tequila (empfohlen: José Cuervo Especial Gold)","½ Tasse Margarita-Mix","¼ Tasse Olivenöl","Salz","frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","1 Tasse Mesquite-Räucherchips, 30 Minuten in Wasser eingeweicht","¼ Tasse frisch gepresster Limettensaft","3 EL frischer Koriander","3 Chipotle-Chilis in Adobo, fein gehackt","3 EL Adobo-Soße"],"s":["Combine tequila, oil, mix, lime, cumin, cilantro, adobo, and the chiles in a blender until smooth. Pour into a gallon size zip-top bag and add chicken. Toss to coat and refrigerate overnight.","The next day, preheat grill. Sprinkle both sides of chicken with salt and pepper and place on grill.","Cook, turning often, until internal temperature reaches 165°F (74˚C).","While chicken cooks, run the marinade through a cheesecloth and skim off the oil. Bring to a boil in a large saucepan over high heat and cook until liquid has reduced to 3 ounces.","Once chicken is done, remove to a plate and pour marinade over top. Cover tightly with foil and let rest 15 minutes before serving."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Margarita_Grilled_Chicken","i":"wb-en-2641","on":"Margarita Grilled Chicken","og":["4 boneless skinless chicken breasts","½ tsp freshly-ground cumin","½ cup tequila (recommended: José Cuervo Especial Gold)","½ cup margarita mix","¼ cup olive oil","Salt","Freshly-ground black pepper","1 cup mesquite chips, soaked in water 30 minutes","¼ cup freshly-squeezed lime juice","3 Tbsp fresh cilantro","3 chipotle chiles in adobo, finely chopped","3 Tbsp adobo sauce"]},{"n":"Marinara-Soße","c":"saucen","k":"Italien","p":6,"t":45,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["6 EL natives Olivenöl","225 g Gemüsezwiebel, gewürfelt","4 Zehen Knoblauch, in dünne Scheiben geschnitten","2 TL frische Thymianblättchen (oder ½ TL getrocknet)","4 TL frische Basilikumblätter (oder 1 TL getrocknet)","85 g rote Paprika, gewürfelt","1,3 kg geschälte Eiertomaten (850 g), von Hand zerdrückt","1 EL Zucker","Salz, nach Geschmack"],"s":["Heat the oil in a saucepan over medium heat until it shimmers.","Add the onions and garlic, and sauté them for about 2 minutes until the onions are translucent.","Add the thyme, basil and bell pepper. Cook 5 minutes more.","Add the tomatoes and sugar. Bring to a boil and then lower to a light simmer, stirring occasionally for 30 minutes.","Season with salt to taste.","Serve hot by ladling over pasta, seafood or rice."],"x":[],"desc":"Marinara (mariner's) sauce is a southern Italian tomato sauce usually made with tomatoes, garlic, herbs (such as basil), and onion. However, there are many variations. Some of these include the addition of capers, olives and spices.","img":"Ravioli Marinara.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Marinara_Sauce","i":"wb-en-2642","im":["7/7a/Ravioli_Marinara.jpg/330px-Ravioli_Marinara.jpg","Kim Scarborough","CC BY-SA 2.0","Ravioli Marinara.jpg","r"],"on":"Marinara Sauce","og":["6 tablespoons virgin olive oil","225 grams (8 ounces) Spanish onion, diced","4 cloves garlic, thinly sliced","2 teaspoons fresh thyme leaves (or ½ teaspoon dried)","4 teaspoons fresh basil leaves (or 1 teaspoon dried)","85 grams (3 ounces) red bell pepper, diced","1.3 kilograms (1 pound and 14 ounces) skinless plum tomatoes, crushed by hand","1 tablespoon sugar","Salt to taste"]},{"n":"Marinierte Gurken und Zwiebeln","c":"salate","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["2 Gurken","1 weiße Zwiebel","480 ml Branntweinessig","2 TL Pflanzenöl (10 ml)","1 TL Zucker (5 ml)","1 TL Salz (5 ml)"],"s":["Mix vinegar, oil, salt and sugar for the marinade.","Trim the ends from the cucumbers, peel them, and slice them.","Peel the onion and slice it as thinly as possible.","Pour the marinade over the cucumbers and onions and mix well.","Let it sit in a cool place or refrigerator for at least two hours, stirring occasionally.","Serve in a bowl, marinade and all, using salad tongs or a slotted spoon to dish out servings."],"x":["Any light salad oil may be used. Avoid olive oil, as it congeals when refrigerated.","The cucumber to onion ratio should be from 2:1 to 2.5:1.","There should be just a hint of oil in the marinade and just enough sugar to take the edge off of the vinegar's tartness.","For crisper pickles add a spoonful of oregano."],"desc":"This is a nice, light, cooling salad or side dish to have during the hot summer months.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Marinated_Cucumbers_and_Onions","i":"wb-en-2643","on":"Marinated Cucumbers and Onions","og":["2 cucumbers","1 white onion","2 cups (480 ml) distilled white vinegar","2 teaspoons (10 ml) vegetable oil","1 teaspoon (5 ml) sugar","1 teaspoon (5 ml) salt"]},{"n":"Marinierte grüne Oliven","c":"snacks","k":"Spanien","p":1,"t":10,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["450 g große grüne spanische Oliven mit Stein","7 Zehen Knoblauch, geschält und fein gehackt","2 Lorbeerblätter","½ mittelgroße Zitrone, in Scheiben geschnitten","1 TL getrockneter Oregano","1 TL gemahlene Fenchelsamen","½ TL getrockneter Thymian","½ TL gemahlene Kreuzkümmelsamen","½ TL getrockneter Rosmarin","½ TL spanisches Paprikapulver","½ TL schwarzer Pfeffer"],"s":["Lightly crush the olives with a mallet, or make slight slits on each olive with a knife, to ensure that the marinade permeates them.","Place the olives in a sealable glass jar and add the remaining ingredients.","Fill the jar with water and shake well.","Marinate at room temperature for several days to a week.","Serve the olives with toasted almonds and fresh bread."],"x":[],"desc":"Green olives marinated in herbs and garlic are very common in Spanish restaurants. They are commonly served free when you order a drink, and are often served with toasted, salted nuts.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Marinated_Green_Olives","i":"wb-en-2644","im":["0/01/Marinated_olives.jpg/960px-Marinated_olives.jpg","Juhanson","CC BY-SA 3.0","Marinated olives.jpg","c"],"on":"Marinated Green Olives","og":["2 cups (16 oz/450 g) unpitted large green Spanish olives","7 cloves garlic, peeled and minced","2 bay leaves","½ medium lemon, sliced","1 teaspoon dried oregano","1 teaspoon ground fennel seeds","½ teaspoon dried thyme","½ teaspoon ground cumin seeds","½ teaspoon dried rosemary","½ teaspoon Spanish paprika","½ teaspoon black pepper"]},{"n":"Marinierte Makrele","c":"fisch","k":"Großbritannien","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 oder mehr Makrelen","2 frische Lorbeerblätter, gehackt","6 Zehen","1 Muskatblüte (ein Stück)","1 Zweig frischer Thymian","1 Zwiebel, gehackt","10 Pfefferkörner","Salz","Malzessig"],"s":["Clean and scale fish. Place in a baking dish large enough for the fish and vinegar.","Mix other ingredients, except vinegar, with salt to taste, and pour over fish.","Pour over enough vinegar to cover well.","Place in moderate oven for 40–50 minutes.","Lift fish carefully onto serving dish, and strain liquor over top.","Let cool and serve."],"x":["from Boscastle W.I. in Cornish Recipes, Ancient & Modern, 22nd Edition, The Cornwall Federation of Women's Institutes 1965.","First collected & published by Edith Martin, Tregavethan, Truro, 1929, for The Cornwall F.of W. I."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Marinated_Mackerel","i":"wb-en-2645","im":["7/72/Mackerel_with_pickles_and_mullet_roe_-_Mackerel_sauce_with_white_wine%2C_lemon%2C_capers_and_chilies_in_vinegar%2C_fried_tomato%2C_mullet_roe%2C_mackerel_marinated_in_sugar_and_salt._Mackerel_infusion_%2815250555084%29.jpg/960px-thumbnail.jpg","City Foodsters","CC BY 2.0","Mackerel with pickles and mullet roe - Mackerel sauce with white wine, lemon, capers and chilies in vinegar, fried tomato, mullet roe, mackerel marinated in sugar and salt. Mackerel infusion (15250555084).jpg","c"],"on":"Marinated Mackerel","og":["4 or more mackerels","2 fresh bay leaves, chopped","6 cloves","1 blade of mace","1 sprig of fresh thyme","1 onion, chopped","10 peppercorns","Salt","Malt vinegar"]},{"n":"Marly-Biskuit","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["150 g gemahlene Mandeln","70 g Kuchenmehl (Type 405)","250 g feiner Zucker","250 g Eiweiß","150 g feiner Zucker"],"s":["Mix the almonds, flour, and the first quantity of sugar with a wire whisk.","Whip the egg whites to soft peaks.","Add the second quantity of sugar, little by little, and beat to firm peaks.","Fold the almond mixture into the egg whites.","Line a sheet pan with parchment paper and draw circles of the required diameter on the paper.","Using a pastry bag, pipe spirals of meringue into the circles.","Bake at 350°F (180°C) for 12–15 minutes."],"x":[],"desc":"Marly sponge is a meringue stabilized with flour. It is typically used as a component in other pastries.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Marly_Sponge","i":"wb-en-2646","on":"Marly Sponge","og":["5 oz (150 g) almond meal","2¼ oz (70 g) cake flour","8 oz (250 g) superfine sugar","8 oz (250 g) egg whites","5 oz (150 g) superfine sugar"]},{"n":"Hähnchenschnitzel Marsala","c":"fleisch","k":"Italien","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Hähnchenbrustfilets ohne Haut","4 TL Butter","3 TL Olivenöl","½ Tasse trockener Marsala","½ Tasse Rinder- oder Hühnerbrühe","230 g frischer Spargel","Petersilie","Salz","Pfeffer","Mehl","Oregano","frisches Basilikum"],"s":["Put each chicken breast in a plastic bag and flatten with a meat tenderizer.","Coarsely chop the basil, and then throw it in a deep baking pan along with some flour, oregano. Toss the chicken with it.","Melt 2 tsp of butter in a medium frying pan on low-medium heat. When the butter stops bubbling, add the chicken and brown each section for approximately 3 minutes on each side. Once this is done, cover and set aside on a separate plate.","Drain off most of the liquid from the pan, and raise the heat. Pour a dollop of olive oil in, and sear the asparagus quickly. Remove this and set aside.","Keep at high heat, add the marsala and ¼ of the stock. Boil off for a few minutes. Lower the heat, and return the asparagus to the pan. Add the remaining stock and boil off to reduce. Add a tsp of butter, and cover chicken with sauce.","Sprinkle with parsley and serve."],"x":["At various points during the cooking, you may want to grind some fresh pepper and sprinkle salt over top of the sauce or chicken; do so according to your tastes."],"desc":"Marsala chicken scallopini is a meal in the style of Italian cuisine, with mouthwatering flavors gotten from the fortified Marsala wine.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Marsala_Chicken_Scallopini","i":"wb-en-2647","im":["6/69/Scaloppine_al_limone.jpg/960px-Scaloppine_al_limone.jpg","Xocolatl ( talk ) 15:26, 4 May 2014 (UTC)","CC BY-SA 3.0","Scaloppine al limone.jpg","w"],"on":"Marsala Chicken Scallopini","og":["2 boneless skinless chicken breasts","4 tsp butter","3 tsp olive oil","½ cup dry marsala wine","½ cup beef/chicken stock","½ lb of fresh asparagus","Parsley","Salt","Pepper","Flour","Oregano","Fresh basil"]},{"n":"Marshmallow-Reis-Schnitten I","c":"dessert","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse Mini-Marshmallows","1 Tasse Puffgetreide (z. B. Rice Krispies)"],"s":["Combine marshmallows and cereal in microwaveable bowl.","Microwave for 1–2 minutes, depending on your machine's power.","Stir to coat the cereal with marshmallow. Press into a buttered baking pan or dish.","Cut it into squares and allow it to cool and set."],"x":[],"desc":"This recipe for quick marshmallow rice squares is super-simple and requires little knowledge of cooking!","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Marshmallow_Rice_Squares_I","i":"wb-en-2648","on":"Marshmallow Rice Squares I","og":["1 cup mini marshmallows","1 cup puffed cereal (e.g. Rice Krispies)"]},{"n":"Marshmallow-Reis-Schnitten II","c":"dessert","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse Marshmallows (normal weiß, mit Cream-Soda- oder Kaugummigeschmack)","100–150 ml Milch","¼ Tasse Puderzucker","1 Tasse Puffgetreide (z. B. Rice Krispies)"],"s":["Melt marshmallows in the microwave in 30 second intervals until it melts into a creamy mixture.","Remove marshmallow fluff from microwave, pour in the milk, and mix for 1½ minutes.","Add the powdered sugar and mix for 2 more minutes.","Add the puffed cereal, and mix for 1 more minute.","Put back in microwave and heat for 13 seconds.","Remove from the microwave and mix a final time.","Press into a greased dish or pan. Let set, then cut into pieces."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Marshmallow_Rice_Squares_II","i":"wb-en-2649","on":"Marshmallow Rice Squares II","og":["1 cup marshmallows (either regular white, cream soda flavour, or bubblegum flavour)","100–150 ml milk","¼ cup powdered sugar","1 cup puffed cereal (e.g. Rice Krispies)"]},{"n":"Marshmallows","c":"dessert","k":"","p":4,"t":210,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["etwa 1 Tasse Puderzucker (125 g)","3 ½ Tütchen gemahlene Gelatine (geschmacksneutral) (2 EL plus 2 ½ TL)","125 ml kaltes Wasser","450 g Zucker","160 g heller Maissirup","125 ml heißes Wasser (etwa 46 °C)","¼ TL Salz","2 Eiweiß von großen Eiern","1 TL Vanilleextrakt","125 ml Pflanzenöl"],"s":["Oil the bottom and sides of a rectangular metal baking pan, and dust the bottom and sides with some confectioners' sugar.","In bowl of standing electric mixer or in a large bowl, sprinkle gelatin over cold water and let stand to soften.","In a 3 quart (2.8 L) heavy saucepan, cook granulated sugar, corn syrup, hot water, and salt over low heat, stirring with a wooden spoon, until sugar is dissolved.","Increase heat to moderate and boil mixture, without stirring, until a candy or digital thermometer registers , about 12 minutes. Remove pan from heat and pour sugar mixture over gelatin mixture, stirring until gelatin is dissolved.","Using a standing or a hand-held electric mixer, whip mixture on high speed until white, thick and nearly tripled in volume (about 6–10 minutes).","In a large bowl with cleaned beaters, whip whites (or reconstituted powdered whites) until they just hold stiff peaks. Beat whites and vanilla into sugar mixture until just combined.","Pour mixture into baking pan and sift ¼ cup confectioners' sugar evenly over top. Cool marshmallow, uncovered, until firm (at least 3 hours and up to 1 day).","Run a thin knife around edges of pan and invert pan onto large cutting board. Lifting up 1 corner of inverted pan, with fingers loosen marshmallow and let drop onto cutting board.","With a large knife trim edges of marshmallow and cut marshmallows into roughly 1-inch cubes. Sift remaining confectioners' sugar into a large bowl and add marshmallows in batches, tossing to evenly coat."],"x":["Try coating with toasted coconut or cocoa powder instead of powdered sugar."],"desc":"Marshmallows are a light, spongy confection made primarily with sugar and gelatin, although some recipes contain egg whites.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Marshmallows","i":"wb-en-2650","im":["3/3d/White_Marshmallows.jpg/960px-White_Marshmallows.jpg","John Morgan","CC BY 2.0","White Marshmallows.jpg","w"],"og":["About 1 cup (125 g / 4.4 oz) confectioners' sugar","3 ½ envelopes (2 tbsp plus 2 ½ tsp) unflavored powdered gelatin","½ cup (125 ml / 4.2 oz) cold water","2 cups (450 g / 16 oz) white granulated sugar","½ cup (160 g / 5.6 oz) light corn syrup","½ cup (125 ml / 4.2 oz) hot water (about 115°F / 46.1°C)","¼ tsp salt","2 large egg whites","1 tsp vanilla extract","½ cup (125 ml / 4.2 fl oz) vegetable oil"]},{"n":"Marzipankuchen","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":1,"t":90,"d":3,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Kuchenboden","75 g Butter","125 g Zucker","1 Packung Vanillezucker","4 Eier","100 g Mehl","1 TL Backpulver","100 g gemahlene Mandeln","#Füllung","3 EL Konfitüre","ein paar Tropfen Mandelaroma","1 EL Zucker","3 EL Wasser","2 Packungen Pektin ohne Kochen","600 ml Schlagsahne","75 g Marzipan","#Verzierung","350 g Marzipan","50 g gehackte Mandeln","50 g Puderzucker","200 ml Schlagsahne, geschlagen","Kaffeeweißer auf Stärkebasis","50 g Vollmilchkuvertüre"],"s":["Preheat the oven to 180 °C.","Melt butter in a small saucepan and let cool slightly.","Beat the eggs in a mixing bowl with a mixer at the highest level until frothy. While stirring, sprinkle in sugar mixed with vanilla sugar, then beat the mixture for 2 minutes.","Combine the flour, baking powder and almonds. Stir in briefly at the lowest setting, then stir in the butter briefly.","Spread the batter in a springform pan.","Bake in the oven for 30 minutes.","Let the cake base cool and cut twice horizontally. Place one of the cake bases on a cake platter.","Stir the jam until smooth and spread on the bottom cake base.","Place the middle cake base on top of the jam, and press gently to secure the layers.","Cut the marzipan into small pieces and place in a mixing bowl. Add the bitter almond flavor, sugar, and water, and stir until smooth with the mixer.","Whip the cream with pectin stiffly according to the package instructions. Mix in the marzipan.","Spread about ¾ of the cream on the middle cake layer, and put the final layer on top.","Spread the cake completely with the remaining cream. Place the cake in the fridge for at least 3 hours.","Place a piece baking paper on a large plate.","Crush the couverture and melt it in a bowl over a water bath. Mix the almonds with the chocolate coating.","Spoon 16 small dollops of the almond-chocolate mixture on the baking paper, and keep in the fridge until the chocolate has set.","Sift powdered sugar and knead into the marzipan. Roll out the marzipan mixture into a round flat disc (Ø=36 cm).","Drape the marzipan over the cake. Press the marzipan onto the edge of the cake. Cut off any excess marzipan.","Prepare cream and transfer to a piping bag. Decorate the cake with cream.","Place almond slivers on top and place the cake in the fridge until ready to serve."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"Marzipan cake.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Marzipan_Cake","i":"wb-en-2651","im":["9/99/Marzipan_cake.jpg/960px-Marzipan_cake.jpg","unbekannt","CC BY 2.0","Marzipan cake.jpg","r"],"on":"Marzipan Cake","og":["#Cake base","75 g butter","125 g white granulated sugar","1 packet vanilla sugar","4 eggs","100 g flour","1 teaspoon baking powder","100 g ground almonds","#Filling","3 tablespoons jam","a few drops almond flavor","1 tablespoon white granulated sugar","3 tablespoons water","2 packets of no-cook pectin","600 ml whipping cream","75 g marzipan","#Ornament","350 g marzipan","50 g chopped almonds","50 g powdered sugar","200 ml whipping cream, whipped","starch-based creamer","50 g whole milk chocolate couverture"]},{"n":"Marzipanmuffins","c":"brot","k":"","p":14,"t":40,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["150 g Marzipan","150 g Butter","3 Eier","100 ml Milch","100 g Mehl","100 g Zucker","100 g feine Haferflocken","2 TL Natron","2 Päckchen Vanillezucker"],"s":["Finely dice the marzipan or mash it with a fork. Beat it well with butter, milk, and eggs.","Mix the remaining dry ingredients. Add them to the butter and egg mixture, and mix to make a smooth batter. If it is too dry, add a little more milk.","Place muffin tins on a baking sheet. Spread the batter in the tins and bake at 180°C for 20–25 minutes.","If desired, decorate the muffins with chocolate icing and sprinkles."],"x":[],"desc":"Muffins with oatmeal and marzipan filling.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Marzipan_Muffins","i":"wb-en-2652","on":"Marzipan Muffins","og":["150 g marzipan","150 g butter","3 eggs","100 ml milk","100 g flour","100 g white granulated sugar","100 g fine oatmeal","2 teaspoons baking soda","2 bags of vanilla sugar"]},{"n":"Masa (Hausa-Reispfannkuchen)","c":"kuchen","k":"Nigeria","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Tassen ungekochter Reis","1 TL Hefe","½ Tasse Zucker","Salz","1 TL Backpulver (optional)","Öl, zum Braten"],"s":["Soak the rice in water for at least 8 hours, and up to overnight. Drain the rice.","Take a few tablespoons of the soaked rice, and boil it until tender.","Combine the cooked rice and uncooked rice. Blend until smooth, adding only as much water as you need to get a paste—don’t let it become watery.","Mix yeast and sugar with a small amount of warm water in a small bowl. Leave for a few minutes to foam.","In a large bowl, mix the blended rice with the yeast mixture and baking powder. Cover, and let rest for 6–8 hours.","Season the batter with salt and sugar to taste.","Heat a small amount of oil in a non-stick pan. Pour small dollops of batter into the pan, and fry like pancakes. They should come out fluffy and light.","Serve with hot sauce, and enjoy."],"x":["Sweet masa is made by increasing sugar and serving with honey or syrup. Savory masa uses less sugar and may include onions, pepper, or spices. Coconut milk or regular milk can be added for richer flavor. Spices like ginger or cloves enhance aroma, while egg can be added for a richer, cake-like texture. Mini masa versions are also popular for street snacks."],"desc":"Rice masa, or rice waina, is a type of Nigerian masa from the Hausa people of Nigeria, especially in Northern Nigeria. The recipe varies across households, but it is traditionally made in an oval shape. You can add ginger or onions if desired. Masa may be cooked in a regular skillet or a specialized","img":"Masa (Waina).jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Masa_(Hausa_Rice_Pancake)","i":"wb-en-2653","im":["0/05/Masa_%28Waina%29.jpg/500px-Masa_%28Waina%29.jpg","Aderiqueza","CC BY-SA 4.0","Masa (Waina).jpg","r"],"on":"Masa (Hausa Rice Pancake)","og":["2 cups uncooked rice","1 teaspoon yeast","½ cup sugar","Salt","1 teaspoon baking powder (optional)","Oil, for cooking"]},{"n":"Masala Chai I","c":"veggie","k":"Indien","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["#Masala-Mischung","100 g gemahlener Ingwer","25 g Gewürznelken","100 g schwarze Pfefferkörner","60 g ganzer Zimt, klein gebrochen, oder 40 g gemahlener Zimt","½ Muskatnuss, zerdrückt","35 g grüne Kardamomkapseln","#Chai","½ Tasse Wasser","1 ½ TL Zucker","¾ TL getrocknete Teeblätter (traditionell), am besten ein kräftiger indischer Tee wie Assam","1 Prise Masala-Mischung","½ Tasse Milch"],"s":["Combine all of the spices, and blend well in an electric grinder.","Store the powder in a clean container at room temperature; you only need a small quantity for each cup of chai, and a full recipe will keep you stocked full of chai for months.","Boil water and milk together in a saucepan.","Add sugar, tea leaves, and masala. Boil until the mixture becomes dark (about 5–10 minutes); the longer you boil, the stronger the chai.","Strain into teacups to serve."],"x":["Let the remaining solids cool and sprinkle them on your plants for an excellent fertiliser.","Tea masala or garam masala from a store can be used to get around the masala mixture process; however, pre-ground spices lose their flavor over time.","When making the chai, boil the water and milk separately, and in step two add the tea leaves and masala to the boiling water, boiling until the tea is as strong as you like. Only then add the milk to the mix. This can speed up the process without affecting the flavor. This method is often used by restaurants to serve chai in large quantities quickly as orders are taken.","Optionally turn off the heat in the end, cover, and let sit for about 5 minutes for a richer flavor.","Try adjusting the ratio of milk to water. For a richer milky tea, try two parts milk to one part water.","Leave out the sugar for a more adult flavor. Sugar can be added while drinking if so desired."],"desc":"Masala chai is a spiced version of the typical Indian milk tea. As with much of Indian cuisine, the exact mix of dry spices varies greatly and is often handed down in families from one generation to the next.","img":"Masala Tea and South Indian Filter Coffee.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Masala_Chai_I","i":"wb-en-2654","im":["7/7b/Masala_Tea_and_South_Indian_Filter_Coffee.jpg/500px-Masala_Tea_and_South_Indian_Filter_Coffee.jpg","Alpha from Melbourne, Australia","CC BY-SA 2.0","Masala Tea and South Indian Filter Coffee.jpg","r"],"og":["#Masala mixture","100 grams powdered ginger","25 grams cloves","100 grams whole black peppercorns","60 grams whole cinnamon, broken small, or 40 grams ground cinnamon","½ seed of nutmeg, crushed","35 grams green cardamom pods","#Chai","½ cup water","1 ½ teaspoon sugar","¾ teaspoon dried tea leaves—to be traditional, a strong Indian tea such as an Assam is best.","1 pinch of masala mixture","½ cup milk"]},{"n":"Masala Chai II","c":"welt","k":"Indien","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Tassen kochendes Wasser","2 EL Schlagsahne","1 Beutel schwarzer Tee","2 TL Vanillezucker","½ TL Zimt","1 Prise Kakaopulver","3–4 Kardamomsamen","1 Prise Kümmel","1 Prise Anissamen","1 Prise gemahlener Ingwer (optional)","1 Prise gemahlene Nelken (optional)","1 Prise Safran (optional)","zerstoßene Mandeln (optional)"],"s":["Combine all ingredients in a serving cup. Steep for about 5 minutes.","Stir vigorously to incorporate the cocoa and cinnamon.","Reheat in the microwave if you prefer it very hot."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Masala_Chai_II","i":"wb-en-2655","im":["8/89/Chai_In_Sakora.jpg/500px-Chai_In_Sakora.jpg","Dadhichbittu007","CC BY-SA 4.0","Chai In Sakora.jpg","w"],"og":["2 cups boiling water","2 tbsp heavy cream","1 bag black tea leaves","2 tsp vanilla sugar","½ tsp cinnamon","1 pinch cocoa powder","3–4 cardamom seeds","1 pinch caraway seeds","1 pinch anise seeds","1 pinch ground ginger (optional)","1 pinch ground cloves (optional)","1 pinch saffron (optional)","Crushed almonds (optional)"]},{"n":"Masala Dosa","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Teig","1 Tasse ungekochter Ponni- oder Sona-Masuri-Reis","1 Tasse gekochter Reis","¾ Tasse getrocknetes Urad Dal (ganze geschälte Urdbohnen)","Salz ohne Jod, nach Geschmack","#Füllung","6 mittelgroße Kartoffeln, gekocht und grob zerdrückt","2 mittelgroße Zwiebeln, fein gehackt","3–6 grüne Chilischote, fein gehackt","1 TL fein geriebener Ingwer","1 TL fein geriebener Knoblauch","2 EL Öl","½ TL Senfsamen","1 EL fein gehackter Koriander","1 TL Chana Dal (halbierte Kichererbsen)","1 TL Kurkuma","1 TL grob gehackte Curryblätter","Zwiebel-Chutney","Kokos-Chutney","#Garen","½ Tasse Mischung aus Ghee und Pflanzenfett"],"s":["On the day before cooking the dosa, grind all the batter ingredients in a blender or specialized dosa grinder with water. The final consistency of the batter must be similar to pancake batter.","Leave batter overnight in a warm spot and allow it to ferment. This is a very important process and must not be skipped. During fermentation the batter may rise to almost twice its volume, and therefore the container for the batter must allow for this.","Heat the oil in a wok or other deep pan.","When the oil is hot add mustard seeds, and allow them to splutter.","When the spluttering starts to recede, add chopped green chilies, curry leaves, and channa dal. Stir until the channa dal turns brown. Be careful, as channa dal can go from browned to burnt within seconds.","Add onions and fry until browned. Add turmeric and sauté for 2 minutes. Add ginger and garlic and sauté for a few seconds.","Add boiled and coarsely-mashed potatoes to the preparation, and mix well.","Turn off the heat and add lemon juice and coriander leaves, then mix well.","Dosa can easily be made on a tava, iron frying pan, or non-stick pan. Heat the pan on a medium heat until a drop of water evaporates on contact.","Spread about ½ cup of batter on the pan (like for crêpes) slowing spreading it outwards to form a thin, circular dosa.","Allow it to cook for a minute and, using a flat spatula, flip it over to the other side to cook. As the other side cooks, spread a layer of ghee-shortening mixture on the topside.","Flip it over again. As the bottom crisps add 1 teaspoon of onion chutney on the top, and spread it evenly.","Add some of the filling onto one half of the dosa and fold the other side over. Serve with coconut chutney."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Masala_Dosa","i":"wb-en-2656","im":["b/ba/Masala_Dosa_2023.jpg/960px-Masala_Dosa_2023.jpg","Yakshitha","CC BY-SA 4.0","Masala Dosa 2023.jpg","w"],"og":["#Batter","1 cup uncooked ponni or sona masuri rice","1 cup boiled rice","¾ cup dried urad dal (whole skinless black gram)","Non-iodized salt to taste","#Filling","6 medium sized potatoes, boiled and coarsely mashed","2 medium sized onions, finely chopped","3–6 green chile pepper, finely chopped","1 tsp finely-grated ginger","1 tsp finely-grated garlic","2 Tbsp oil","½ tsp mustard seeds","1 Tbsp finely-chopped cilantro","1 tsp chana dal","1 tsp turmeric","1 tsp coarsely-chopped curry leaves","Onion chutney","Coconut chutney","#Cooking","½ cup mixture of ghee and vegetable shortening"]},{"n":"Mascarpone-Schokoladensoße","c":"saucen","k":"","p":1,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["300 g Mascarpone","½ Tasse Schokoladensirup","2 EL Zucker","1–2 Prisen Salz"],"s":["Whisk together all ingredients in your serving bowl.","Serve as a dipping sauce with beignets or fruit; or, serve over ice cream."],"x":[],"desc":"Mascarpone cheese makes this sauce light and fluffy, while chocolate adds flavor and richness.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mascarpone_Chocolate_Sauce","i":"wb-en-2657","on":"Mascarpone Chocolate Sauce","og":["1 cup (300 g/11 oz) mascarpone cheese","½ cup () chocolate syrup","2 tablespoons white granulated sugar","1–2 pinches of salt"]},{"n":"Erdbeeren mit Mascarpone-Glasur","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["450 g frische Erdbeeren, entkelcht und in Scheiben geschnitten","1 Tasse Mascarpone","3 EL Kaffeelikör","3 EL dunkler Rum","¼ Tasse Schlagsahne","1 Prise Salz","¾ Tasse Zucker","2 EL Butter"],"s":["Melt butter in your largest stainless steel sauté pan over medium heat. Add strawberries and cook until deeply browned. Remove and keep warm.","Deglaze pan with rum and ignite. Stir to dissolve browned bits.","Add remaining ingredients, and boil until reduced by ⅓.","Add strawberries, reduce heat to low, and cook ½ hour.","Remove pan from heat and serve."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mascarpone_Glazed_Strawberries","i":"wb-en-2658","on":"Mascarpone Glazed Strawberries","og":["1 pound fresh strawberries, hulled and sliced","1 cup mascarpone cheese","3 tbsp coffee liqueur","3 tbsp dark rum","¼ cup heavy cream","1 pinch of salt","¾ cup white granulated sugar","2 tbsp butter"]},{"n":"Makkaroni mit Mascarpone-Käsesoße","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["¼ Tasse ungesalzene Butter","¼ Tasse Weizenmehl","1 Tasse Mascarpone","3 EL Zucker","1 Prise Salz","2 Tassen Schlagsahne","450 g gekochte Makkaroni","1 Tasse Schlagsahne, weich geschlagen"],"s":["Melt butter in a large saucepan over medium heat. Whisk in flour and cook until light blond color is achieved.","Add remaining ingredients except for macaroni and whipped cream. Bring to a boil until reduced by half. Remove from heat and gently fold in cream.","Place macaroni in the bottom of a 9x13-inch square baking pan. Pour cheese mixture over and bake in a 350°F oven for 25 minutes, or until bubbly on top and puffed up. Remove and serve."],"x":[],"desc":"Folding in unsweetened whipped cream makes this mac 'n cheese casserole light and airy.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mascarpone_Mac_'n_Cheese","i":"wb-en-2659","on":"Mascarpone Mac 'n Cheese","og":["¼ cup unsalted butter","¼ cup all-purpose flour","1 cup mascarpone cheese","3 tbsp sugar","1 pinch of salt","2 cups heavy cream","1 pound cooked macaroni pasta","1 cup heavy whipping cream, whipped to soft peaks"]},{"n":"Kochbananenstampf mit Schweinekruste (Mofongo)","c":"fleisch","k":"Puerto Rico","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["3 sehr grüne Kochbananen","Pflanzenöl zum Braten","230 g Schweinekrusten (Chicharrones), auch Chicharrones oder Schweinegrieben genannt, gemahlen","3 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","1 Tasse Fond oder Brühe","1 EL Fett (z. B. Olivenöl, Butter oder Schmalz)"],"s":["Peel the plantains and cut into 1-inch diagonal pieces.","Heat the oil in a large skillet. Place the plantains in the oil and fry on both sides (approximately 3 ½ minutes per side).","Remove the plantains from the pan and flatten the plantains by placing a plate over the fried plantains and pressing down.","Return the plantains to the hot oil and fry 1 minute on each side. Then, place on paper towels.","While the plantains are still hot, use a mortar and pestle to mash them with the garlic, fat, and stock or broth. Add the chicharrones, salt, and pepper to taste."],"x":["Packaged pork rinds can be used. Alternatively, any kind of bacon can also be used.","You can also use a food processor for mashing; add the plantains to food processor with bacon, garlic and some salt and pepper. You may have to work in batches. Process to consistency of mashed—not whipped—potatoes. Do not over-process!"],"desc":"Mofongo is a popular Caribbean dish that originated in Puerto Rico. It is made from fried green plantains, seasoned with garlic, fat (olive oil, butter, or lard) and pork cracklings, then mashed. Mofongo is usually served with a fried meat and a chicken broth soup.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mashed_Plantains_and_Pork_Rinds_(Mofongo)","i":"wb-en-2660","im":["4/41/Mofongo.jpg/960px-Mofongo.jpg","Diane","CC BY 2.0","Mofongo.jpg","w"],"on":"Mashed Plantains and Pork Rinds (Mofongo)","og":["3 very green plantains","Vegetable oil for frying","½ pound pork rinds, also known as chicharrones or pork cracklings, ground","3 cloves garlic, minced","1 cup stock or broth","1 tablespoon fat (e.g. olive oil, butter, or lard)"]},{"n":"Kartoffelpüree","c":"beilagen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["etwa 1 kg mehligkochende Kartoffeln (mehligkochend)","60 g bzw. 4 EL Butter","60 ml Milch (¼ Tasse), Kaffeesahne (Half and Half), oder leichte Sahne","Salz","Pfeffer","Muskatnuss (optional)"],"s":["Peel the potatoes and dice them into pieces about 2–3 cm/1 inch thick.","Place the potatoes with about 1 tablespoon of salt into a pot and add about 1.5 liters/1½ quarts of water.","Boil the potatoes for about 15–20 minutes or until tender, then drain.","Either","Put through a potato ricer, then stir in the butter and milk or cream; or","Add the butter and milk or cream, then mash with a potato masher.","Add salt, pepper and (if you like) nutmeg to taste.","Serve hot. Yields 4 servings."],"x":["You can use an electric hand mixer rather than a potato masher or ricer if you prefer, but if you do, be sure to keep it on LOW and do not overbeat the potatoes, or they will become gummy.","Onion mashed potatoes: Prepare some boiled onions, rub them through a sieve, and mix them with potatoes."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mashed_Potatoes","i":"wb-en-2661","im":["5/51/Sous_vide_mashed_potatoes.jpg/960px-Sous_vide_mashed_potatoes.jpg","sousvideguy","CC BY 2.0","Sous vide mashed potatoes.jpg","w"],"on":"Mashed Potatoes","og":["About 1 kg/2¼ lb starchy (floury) potatoes","60 g/4 tablespoons butter","60 ml/¼ cup milk, half-and-half, or light cream","Salt","Pepper","Nutmeg (optional)"]},{"n":"Kürbispüree","c":"beilagen","k":"","p":4,"t":20,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 kleiner Kürbis","1 Prise Salz","1 Prise Pfeffer","etwa 1 EL Butter"],"s":["Clean your pumpkin well, being careful to remove manure, dirt, etc. Chop off the stem.","Bake the cleaned pumpkin in a 375 °F (190 C) oven for about 45 minutes per 250 g. A small pumpkin of less than 500 g works best.","Remove pumpkin and allow to rest for 5–10 minutes.","During this time, take out sea salt, butter, and your pepper mill.","Chop pumpkin in half with cleaver, butcher knife, or kitchen hatchet.","Remove seeds and guts; roast seeds and discard the rest.","Separate the skin from the flesh.","Place hot pumpkin flesh in a food processor, along with salt, pepper, and butter to taste."],"x":["If pumpkin is not soft when removed from oven, place back in for 10–15 minutes each time.","An alternative if you have no food processor is to mash the pumpkin flesh by hand until nearly smooth."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mashed_Pumpkin","i":"wb-en-2662","im":["4/43/Mashedpumpkin.jpg/500px-Mashedpumpkin.jpg","Tim1965","Public domain","Mashedpumpkin.jpg","w"],"on":"Mashed Pumpkin","og":["1 small pumpkin","1 pinch of salt","1 pinch of pepper","About 1 tablespoon butter"]},{"n":"Süßkartoffelpüree","c":"beilagen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["910 g Süßkartoffeln, geschält und in 1 cm große Stücke geschnitten","¾ Tasse brauner Zucker","½ Tasse frisch gepresster Orangensaft","115 g ungesalzene Butter, in Stücke geschnitten","1 TL frisch gemahlener Zimt"],"s":["Cover potatoes in a large pot with cold water by at least an inch.","Cover and bring to a boil over high heat. Reduce heat to a simmer and cook until potatoes are tender (about 15–20 minutes).","Drain potatoes into a colander. Remove water from pot and add potatoes and remaining ingredients. Mash potatoes with either an immersion blender or potato masher.","If you used a potato masher, combine ingredients thoroughly. If you did not, then you can skip this step.","Serve immediately."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mashed_Sweet_Potatoes","i":"wb-en-2663","im":["8/83/Whole_Foods_mashed_sweet_potatoes_-_November_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg/960px-Whole_Foods_mashed_sweet_potatoes_-_November_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch.jpg","Missvain","CC BY 4.0","Whole Foods mashed sweet potatoes - November 2023 - Sarah Stierch.jpg","c"],"on":"Mashed Sweet Potatoes","og":["2 pounds sweet potatoes, peeled and cut into ½-inch pieces","¾ cup brown sugar","½ cup freshly-squeezed orange juice","4 ounces unsalted butter, cut into pieces","1 tsp freshly-ground cinnamon"]},{"n":"Masyaura (nepalesische fermentierte Gemüsebällchen)","c":"veggie","k":"Nepal","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 Tassen Mehl aus schwarzen Linsen","2 Tassen fein gehacktes Gemüse (z. B. Taro, Yams, Taroblätter)"],"s":["Place the lentil flour in a mixing bowl, and add enough water to make a thick paste.","Mix in the vegetables.","Cover the bowl and leave it overnight. This allows the paste to absorb the moisture completely and go through slight fermentation, which gives a nice flavor to the product.","In the morning, make small balls or nuggets by using your hand, and place them on a tray. Wet your hand often with water, which helps prevent the paste from sticking to your hand. The balls should not touch each other.","Place the tray in the direct sun to allow them to dry. It will take around three days to completely sun-dy, and it might take even longer on less sunny or cloudy days. Keep it indoors during the night to speed up the drying process.","Once they are completely dried, keep them in an airtight container store for several months."],"x":["You can also use whole black lentils instead of lentil flour. In this case, soak them in the water for several hours, remove the outer layer, drain water, and then grind them to a thick paste.","In Nepali culture, cooked masyaura is Served with cooked rice."],"desc":"Masyaura are Nepali fermented sun-dried vegetable balls made with a combination of minced vegetables and black lentils. The choice of vegetables is mostly taro, yam, and colocasia leaf. As finding fresh vegetables year-round was hard in the earlier days, masyaura become an alternative nutritious foo","img":"Stir-frying masauras.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Masyaura_(Nepali_Fermented_Vegetable_Balls)","i":"wb-en-2664","im":["3/33/Stir-frying_masauras.jpg/960px-Stir-frying_masauras.jpg","AlexanderVanLoon","CC BY-SA 3.0","Stir-frying masauras.jpg","r"],"on":"Masyaura (Nepali Fermented Vegetable Balls)","og":["4 cups black lentil flour","2 cups minced vegetables (e.g. taro, yam, colocasia leaf)"]},{"n":"Masyaura-Curry","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse Öl, aufgeteilt","1 ½ Tassen Masyaura (getrocknete Linsenklößchen)","1 Prise Kreuzkümmelsamen","½ TL Bockshornkleesamen","1–2 Serrano-Chili oder andere grüne Chilis, fein gehackt","Salz, nach Geschmack","½ TL gemahlene Kurkuma","3 mittelgroße Tomaten, fein gehackt","½ EL Kreuzkümmel-Koriander-Pulver","½ EL rotes Chilipulver","½ EL Ingwer-Knoblauch-Paste","½ EL gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer (optional)","3 Tassen Wasser","2 EL fein gehackter Koriander"],"s":["Heat ½ cup oil in a pan. Add the masyaura, and fry until it becomes red and crispy. Make sure to stir as you fry because it burns fast. Remove masyaura from oil once finished.","In a separate pan heat the remaining ½ cup oil. Add cumin and fenugreek seeds. Once seeds are golden brown, add potato and green chilies. Fry until it becomes golden brown.","Add fried masyaura, salt, and turmeric powder, then stir properly. Cover and cook it on a low to medium heat for 5 minutes.","Add tomato, cumin-coriander powder, ginger-garlic paste, pepper, and red chili powder. Stir, cover, and cook for another 5 minutes.","Add water and stir well. Cook on medium heat and let the mixture boil. Remove from the heat once you get the desired gravy consistency.","Sprinkle with cilantro to garnish."],"x":["Do not cook on high heat. Be patient and cook on medium heat."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Masyaura_Curry","i":"wb-en-2665","on":"Masyaura Curry","og":["1 cup oil, divided","1 ½ cups masyaura","1 pinch cumin seeds","½ tsp fenugreek seeds","1–2 serrano pepper or other green chiles, finely chopped","Salt to taste","½ tsp turmeric powder","3 medium-sized tomatoes, finely chopped","½ tbsp cumin-coriander powder","½ tbsp red chile powder","½ tbsp ginger-garlic paste","½ tbsp ground black pepper (optional)","3 cups water","2 tbsp finely-chopped cilantro"]},{"n":"Matar Paneer","c":"welt","k":"Indien","p":3,"t":40,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["6 EL Öl","200 g Paneer, in 2,5-cm-Würfel geschnitten","1 TL Ingwer-Knoblauch-Paste","1 Tasse gehackte Zwiebeln","1 Tasse pürierte Tomaten","3 grüne Chilis, entkernt und fein gehackt","½ TL Kreuzkümmelsamen","¼ TL gemahlene Kurkuma","½ TL rotes Chilipulver","1 TL gemahlener Koriander","Garam Masala","1 TL Salz","½ Tasse Erbsen","200 ml Wasser","1 EL gehackter Koriander"],"s":["Heat some oil in a deep pan.","Add paneer cubes in it. Fry on all the sides over medium-low heat until golden brown.","Remove paneer from the pan, and drain on paper towels.","Remove excess oil from the same pan, and add ginger-garlic paste.","Add chopped onion to it. Cook, stirring, until onion becomes translucent.","Add chopped tomatoes and mix. Cook well over medium heat.","Turn off the heat when tomatoes have left all the water. Let cool.","Transfer mixture to a blender, and add the chiles.","Blend until smooth.","Heat oil in a pan.","Add cumin seeds, and fry until they start to crackle.","Add turmeric, chilli powder, coriander powder, and garam masala. Mix well over low heat.","Add the blended purée, and mix well over medium heat.","Season with salt, then mix in the peas.","Add some water, cover, and steam until the peas are fully cooked.","Uncover and add the fried paneer. Mix well, adding more water if required.","Heat a small pan/tadka pan.","Add 1 tsp oil and ½ tsp red chilli powder. Mix well.","Turn off the gas and add to the matar paneer while serving."],"x":["Paneer is a pressed uncured cheese usually made fresh. It can be bought in Indian or specialty grocery stores or substituted by tofu if unavailable."],"desc":"","img":"Matar Panir mit Chapati - Mutter Paneer with chapati.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Matar_Paneer","i":"wb-en-2666","im":["6/6b/Matar_Panir_mit_Chapati_-_Mutter_Paneer_with_chapati.jpg/960px-Matar_Panir_mit_Chapati_-_Mutter_Paneer_with_chapati.jpg","Sonja Pauen - Stanhopea","CC BY 2.0 de","Matar Panir mit Chapati - Mutter Paneer with chapati.jpg","r"],"og":["6 tablespoons oil","8 oz (200 g) paneer, cut in 1” cubes","1 teaspoon ginger-garlic paste","1 cup chopped onions","1 cup puréed tomatoes","3 green chilies, seeded and finely chopped","½ teaspoon cumin seeds","¼ teaspoon turmeric powder","½ teaspoon red chilli powder","1 teaspoon coriander powder","Garam masala","1 teaspoon salt","½ cup peas","¾ cup (200 ml) water","1 tablespoon chopped coriander"]},{"n":"Matoke-Rindfleisch-Eintopf","c":"suppen","k":"Uganda","p":4,"t":90,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["8–10 mittelgroße Kochbananen","1 Zitrone (optional), ausgepresst","Pflanzenöl zum Braten","2–3 Tomaten, gehackt","1 Zwiebel, gehackt","1 grüne Paprika, gehackt","1 Chilischote, gehackt","2–3 Knoblauchzehen, zerdrückt","Currygewürze, nach Geschmack","Rindergulasch (optional), in mundgerechte Stücke geschnitten","1 Tasse Rinderfond (optional)","Salz","rotes Chilipulver"],"s":["Peel the plantains and cut into cubes. Toss with lemon juice and set aside.","Heat the oil in a large pan. Add the tomatoes, onions, peppers, and garlic. Fry together.","Stir in the curry spice to taste, then the meat and stock. Cook, stirring, until the meat is nearly done or the mixture is boiling.","Stir in the plantains. Cover and simmer over low heat until until the plantains are tender and the meat is fully cooked.","Season with salt and chili pepper to taste.","Serve and enjoy your delicious meal."],"x":[],"desc":"Matoke refers to a variety of East African plantain or banana, and it is a staple crop. This dish incorporates plantains into a stew. It can be made with or without meat depending on your preference.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Matoke_and_Beef_Stew","i":"wb-en-2667","on":"Matoke and Beef Stew","og":["8–10 medium-size plantains","1 lemon (optional), juiced","Vegetable oil for frying","2–3 tomatoes, chopped","1 onion, chopped","1 green bell pepper, chopped","1 chile pepper, chopped","2–3 garlic cloves, crushed","Curry spices to taste","Beef stew meat (optional), cut in bite-size pieces","1 cup beef stock (optional)","Salt","Red chile powder"]},{"n":"Matze-Lasagne","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":50,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 Matzen","450 g Hüttenkäse","1 ¼ Tassen geriebener Mozzarella","½ Tasse geriebener Parmesan","½ TL schwarzer Pfeffer (optional)","850 g Marinara- oder Tomatensoße"],"s":["Grease a baking pan that will fit the matzah sheets.","Spread about ½ cup sauce in the pan to cover the bottom.","Place 1 matzoh sheet on top.","Spread more tomato sauce over the matzah.","Spread a layer of cottage cheese on top of the matzah.","Sprinkle with mozzarella and Parmesan cheeses.","Repeat these layers until all 4 matzah sheets are used.","Spread tomato sauce and sprinkle mozzarella and Parmesan cheese on top.","Add ½ cup water","Cover with foil, and bake at 350°F (175°C) for 35–40 minutes."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Matzah_Lasagne","i":"wb-en-2668","im":["b/ba/Lasagne_-_stonesoup.jpg/960px-Lasagne_-_stonesoup.jpg","jules / stonesoup","CC BY 2.0","Lasagne - stonesoup.jpg","w"],"on":"Matzah Lasagne","og":["4 sheets of matzah","1 lb (450 g) cottage cheese","1 ¼ cups grated mozzarella cheese","½ cup grated Parmesan cheese","½ teaspoon black pepper (optional)","30–34 ounces marinara sauce or tomato sauce"]},{"n":"Mató de Pedralbes (spanischer Maispudding)","c":"dessert","k":"Spanien","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 l Milch","¼ kg weißer Zucker","100 g Maismehl","10 Eigelb","2 Zimtstangen"],"s":["Stir the maize flour into a glass of the cold milk.","Put the rest of milk in a saucepan, add sugar and yolks, and beat together until blended.","Add cinnamon sticks and heat the mixture. When it begins to boil, add the glass of milk and flour, and mix well. Cook until thickened.","Remove the saucepan from the heat and take out the cinnamon sticks. Pour it into four oval molds and refrigerate until cool.","To serve, unmold the custards and serve with jam or some rosemary honey."],"x":[],"desc":"Mató de pedralbes is a Spanish custard dessert.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mató_de_Pedralbes_(Spanish_Maize_Custard)","i":"wb-en-2669","on":"Mató de Pedralbes (Spanish Maize Custard)","og":["1 litre milk","¼ kilo white sugar","100 grams maize flour","10 yolks","2 cinnamon sticks"]},{"n":"Mayonnaise (vegan)","c":"veggie","k":"","p":10,"t":3,"d":1,"v":2,"l":"en","g":["170 g Tofu (am besten Seiden- oder weicher Tofu)","3 EL Olivenöl"],"s":["Drain the tofu and blend in a food processor/blender until smooth.","Add the oil slowly and gradually to the blended tofu while the blender is still running. This emulsifies the mixture.","Add additional spices (e.g. salt, black pepper, etc.) to taste."],"x":[],"desc":"A recipe for a vegan mayonnaise substitute using tofu and olive oil.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mayonnaise_(Vegan)","i":"wb-en-2670","im":["6/60/Mayonnaise_%281%29.jpg/960px-Mayonnaise_%281%29.jpg","jules","CC BY 2.0","Mayonnaise (1).jpg","w"],"on":"Mayonnaise (Vegan)","og":["6 oz tofu (silky or soft preferred)","3 tablespoons olive oil"]},{"n":"Mazagran (algerischer Eiskaffee)","c":"getraenke","k":"Algerien","p":4,"t":10,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["Eiswürfel","1 Tasse frisch gebrühter schwarzer Kaffee","frisch gepresster Zitronensaft","Zucker oder anderes Süßungsmittel","1 Zitronenscheibe oder -spalte (optional)"],"s":["Fill a tall, narrow glass with the ice cubes.","Pour the coffee over the ice.","Add the lemon juice and sugar to taste.","Add the lemon slice or wedge as a final touch if desired."],"x":["In some recipes, a sugar syrup is poured into the glass first, then a mixture of water and lemon juice is gently and carefully added afterwards so that the two ingredients don't mix. Ice cubes and black coffee are added later with a sprinkle of lemon zest.","Some European variations suggest adding rum."],"desc":"Mazagran (), also called Café Mazagran, is an iced coffee from Algeria. Often deemed the original iced coffee, mazagran originated from a city in Algeria with the same name. It is said that the drink was created by French colonial troops while in captivity in Mazagran Fortress. After they were freed","img":"Café mazagran.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mazagran_(Algerian_Iced_Coffee)","i":"wb-en-2671","im":["c/c1/Caf%C3%A9_mazagran.jpg/500px-Caf%C3%A9_mazagran.jpg","Herbeater","CC BY-SA 4.0","Café mazagran.jpg","r"],"on":"Mazagran (Algerian Iced Coffee)","og":["Ice cubes","1 cup brewed black coffee","Freshly-squeezed lemon juice","Sugar or other sweetener","1 lemon slice or wedge (optional)"]},{"n":"Mazorca desgranada (kolumbianischer Rindfleischsalat)","c":"salate","k":"Kolumbien","p":3,"t":30,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["250 g Rinderlendensteak, in dünne Streifen geschnitten","Remoulade (Tartar Sauce)","gemahlener Piment","gemahlener Pfeffer","Salz","Worcestersoße","½ kleiner knackiger Salatkopf (Batavia-Salat), in dünne Scheiben geschnitten","125 g geriebener Costeño-Käse oder Monterey Jack","1 Dose Maiskörner (425 g)","zerbröselte Kartoffelchips (Kartoffelchips)"],"s":["Fry beef in a medium skillet. Season with allspice, pepper, salt, and Worcestershire sauce.","Heat corn in warm water, then drain well.","Place lettuce into serving dish.","Place corn over the lettuce.","Add shredded cheese on top of the corn.","Top with beef.","Cover everything with crushed potato chips.","Pour tartar sauce all over the dish, and enjoy."],"x":["This recipe is similar to KFC bowls. You can eliminate beef, or replace it with chicken, bacon, pork, sausage, hot dog, and others. You can also mix tartar sauce with ketchup and/or mustard."],"desc":"La mazorca desgranada is typical northern Colombian coast fast food recipe. Is is made of sweet corn, beef, cheese, crushed potato chips, and tartar sauce.","img":"Mazorca_Desgranada.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mazorca_Desgranada_(Colombian_Beef_Salad)","i":"wb-en-2672","im":["b/bd/Mazorca_Desgranada.jpg/960px-Mazorca_Desgranada.jpg","Lgvanegas at English Wikibooks","Public domain","Mazorca Desgranada.jpg","r"],"on":"Mazorca Desgranada (Colombian Beef Salad)","og":["½ pound (250 g) beef loin steak, cut into thin strips","Tartar sauce","Ground allspice","Ground pepper","Salt","Worcestershire sauce","½ small \"Summer Crisp\" (Batavian) lettuce, thinly sliced","¼ pound (125 g) shredded costeño or Monterey Jack cheese","1 can (15oz/425 g) whole kernel corn","Crushed potato chips (crisps)"]},{"n":"Mbahal (gambischer Fisch mit Okra)","c":"fisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["500 g gambischer Räucherfisch (z. B. Wels oder Makrele)","2 EL Palmöl","2 große Zwiebeln, fein gehackt","3 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","2 Tomaten, gewürfelt","2 rote oder grüne Paprika, gewürfelt","2 Scotch-Bonnet-Chilis (oder nach Geschmack), fein gehackt","1 Tasse getrocknete Okra, fein gemahlen","1 EL Tomatenmark","1 TL gemahlener Ingwer","1 TL gemahlener Koriander","1 TL gemahlener Cayennepfeffer (optional, für mehr Schärfe)","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pfeffer, nach Geschmack"],"s":["If the smoked fish still has bones, carefully debone it and flake the flesh into small pieces. Set aside.","In a large pot or saucepan, heat the palm oil over medium heat.","Add the chopped onions and minced garlic. Sauté until they become soft and translucent.","Add the diced tomatoes, diced bell peppers, and finely chopped Scotch bonnet peppers to the pot. Stir well to combine. Cook for a few minutes until the vegetables begin to soften.","Add the dried, ground okra to the pot, stirring continuously to prevent lumps from forming.","Stir in the tomato paste, ground ginger, ground coriander, and ground cayenne pepper (if using). Mix well to combine all the ingredients.","Reduce the heat to low and cover the pot. Allow the mixture to simmer for about 15–20 minutes, or until the okra is cooked and the flavors have melded together.","Add the flaked smoked fish to the pot and gently stir it into the stew. Be careful not to break up the fish too much.","Taste the mbahal and adjust the seasoning with salt and pepper according to your preference.","Serve hot with a side of steamed rice or couscous."],"x":[],"desc":"Mbahal is a traditional Gambian dish that showcases the rich flavors of smoked fish, dried okra, and palm oil. It is a popular delicacy in Gambia, particularly among the Mandinka ethnic group. Mbahal is a hearty and aromatic stew that is enjoyed with rice or couscous, offering a unique and flavorful","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mbahal_(Gambian_Fish_and_Okra)","i":"wb-en-2673","on":"Mbahal (Gambian Fish and Okra)","og":["500 g Gambian smoked fish (such as catfish or mackerel)","2 tablespoons palm oil","2 large onions, finely chopped","3 cloves of garlic, minced","2 tomatoes, diced","2 red or green bell peppers, diced","2 Scotch bonnet chile peppers (or to taste), finely chopped","1 cup dried okra, finely ground","1 tablespoon tomato paste","1 teaspoon ground ginger","1 teaspoon ground coriander","1 teaspoon ground cayenne pepper (optional, for added spiciness)","Salt to taste","Pepper to taste"]},{"n":"Mbahal Kebb (gambische Hähnchenspieße)","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse Erdnusspaste (Erdnuss)","2 mittelgroße Zwiebeln, fein gehackt","3 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","2 Tomaten, gewürfelt","2 EL Tomatenmark","2 EL Pflanzenöl","1 TL gemahlener Cayennepfeffer (je nach gewünschter Schärfe anpassen)","1 TL gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","Salz, nach Geschmack","910 g Hähnchen, in Stücke geschnitten","frische Petersilie oder Koriander, gehackt (zum Garnieren)"],"s":["In a mixing bowl, combine the groundnut paste, finely chopped onions, minced garlic, diced tomatoes, tomato paste, vegetable oil, ground cayenne pepper, ground black pepper, and salt. Mix well to create a marinade.","Add the chicken pieces to the marinade, ensuring they are well coated. Cover the bowl and let the chicken marinate for at least 2 hours, or preferably overnight in the refrigerator, to allow the flavors to develop.","Preheat the grill to medium-high heat.","If using wooden skewers, soak them in water for about 30 minutes to prevent them from burning on the grill.","Thread the marinated chicken pieces onto the skewers, if using, or place them directly on the grill.","Grill the chicken over medium-high heat, turning occasionally, until it is cooked through and has a nice charred appearance. This usually takes about 20–25 minutes, depending on the thickness of the chicken pieces.","Once the chicken is cooked, remove it from the grill and transfer it to a serving dish.","Garnish with freshly chopped parsley or cilantro.","Serve the mbahal kebb hot with rice or couscous."],"x":[],"desc":"Mbahal kebb is a traditional Gambian dish known for its unique combination of flavors and aromatic spices. It is a popular grilled chicken dish that is marinated in a tangy and spicy sauce, giving it a delicious and smoky taste. Mbahal kebb is often enjoyed during special occasions and gatherings, a","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mbahal_Kebb_(Gambian_Chicken_Skewers)","i":"wb-en-2674","im":["6/62/Wooden_skewers.jpg/960px-Wooden_skewers.jpg","Hans Braxmeier","CC0","Wooden skewers.jpg","w"],"on":"Mbahal Kebb (Gambian Chicken Skewers)","og":["1 cup groundnut (peanut) paste","2 medium onions, finely chopped","3 cloves garlic, minced","2 tomatoes, diced","2 tablespoons tomato paste","2 tablespoons vegetable oil","1 teaspoon ground cayenne pepper (adjust according to your spice preference)","1 teaspoon ground black pepper","Salt to taste","2 pounds chicken, cut into pieces","Fresh parsley or cilantro, chopped (for garnish)"]},{"n":"Mbatata a Matenda (malawische Maniokküchlein)","c":"snacks","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Tassen geriebener Maniok","1 Ei, leicht verquirlt","1 Zwiebel, fein gehackt","2 grüne Chilis (optional, für Schärfe), fein gehackt","2 EL Maismehl","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pflanzenöl, zum Braten"],"s":["In a mixing bowl, combine the grated cassava, beaten egg, finely chopped onion, and finely chopped green chilies (if using).","Add the cornmeal to the mixture and mix well until everything is evenly combined.","Season the mixture with salt to taste. Adjust the seasoning according to your preference.","In a frying pan, heat vegetable oil over medium-high heat.","Take spoonfuls of the cassava mixture and carefully drop them into the hot oil. Flatten the fritters slightly with the back of the spoon.","Fry the fritters until they are golden brown and crispy on both sides. Use a slotted spoon to remove them from the oil and place them on paper towels to drain any excess oil.","Repeat the frying process with the remaining cassava mixture.","Allow the fritters to cool slightly before serving."],"x":["You can add grated coconut or grated sweet potato to the cassava mixture for additional flavor and texture.","For a sweeter version, you can add a bit of sugar to the mixture.","These fritters can be served with a dipping sauce or enjoyed on their own.","Mbatata a matenda goes well with a cup of hot tea or as a side snack during gatherings and celebrations."],"desc":"Mbatata a matenda is a popular Malawian snack made from cassava. These cassava fritters are crispy on the outside, soft on the inside, and bursting with flavor. They are a delightful treat that can be enjoyed on their own or with a side of hot tea.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mbatata_a_Matenda_(Malawian_Cassava_Fritters)","i":"wb-en-2675","on":"Mbatata a Matenda (Malawian Cassava Fritters)","og":["2 cups grated cassava","1 egg, lightly beaten","1 onion, finely chopped","2 green chiles (optional, for heat), finely chopped","2 tablespoons cornmeal","Salt, to taste","Vegetable oil, for frying"]},{"n":"Mbong Tchobi (kamerunischer scharfer schwarzer Eintopf)","c":"suppen","k":"Kamerun","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1,8 kg weißer Fisch oder Wels, geputzt und in Steaks geschnitten","10 Njangsa-Samen","1 mittelgroße Zwiebeln, sauber gehackt","2 mittelgroße Frühlingszwiebeln, sauber gehackt","5 große Tomaten, sauber gehackt","5 mittelgroße Knoblauchzehen, sauber gehackt","1 Tasse Basilikum","½ Tasse Petersilie","1 Tasse Pflanzenöl","6 EL Mbongo-Gewürz","2 EL Hühnerbrühpulver","Salz, nach Geschmack"],"s":["Lightly fry the njansan for about 5 minutes. Set aside.","Blend the onions, green onions, tomatoes, njansan, garlic, basil, and parsley together in a blender. You can add some water to the blender to facilitate its blending to a purée.","Place a saucepan on the fire and heat it with a little oil. Add the blended mixture with very little water and bring it to a boil. Let it simmer for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally.","Mix in the mbongo spice, fish, bouillon powder, and salt. Simmer for another 15 minutes or until the fish is fully cooked through. Add a little water if necessary to prevent prevent the stew from getting burnt.","Adjust the seasonings as desired. Enjoy warm with boiled plantains or any complementary dish of your choice."],"x":["If using catfish, place the fish in a sink and pour hot water over it. Soak for 60 seconds, then rinse the fish, clean it, and set aside. This removes the sliminess of catfish."],"desc":"Mbong tchobi is a popular Cameroonian dish. It has a unique colour and taste. It can be served with ripe plantain or any complimentary dish of your choice. If you are seeing this stew for the first time you can be taken aback by its black colour, but if you give it a try it can become one of your fa","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mbong_Tchobi_(Cameroonian_Spicy_Black_Stew)","i":"wb-en-2676","on":"Mbong Tchobi (Cameroonian Spicy Black Stew)","og":["4 pounds white fish or catfish, cleaned and cut into steaks","10 njansan seeds","1 medium-size onions, neatly chopped","2 medium-size green onions, neatly chopped","5 large tomatoes, neatly chopped","5 medium-size garlic cloves, neatly chopped","1 cup basil","½ cup parsley","1 cup vegetable oil","6 tablespoons mbongo spice","2 tablespoons chicken bouillon powder","Salt to taste"]},{"n":"Mbongo Tchobi (kamerunischer schwarzer Eintopf)","c":"saucen","k":"Kamerun","p":6,"t":35,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["großer Fisch nach Wahl, filetiert","½ TL Salz","2 große Tomaten (oder 4 kleine), grob gehackt","1 große Zwiebel, gehackt","7 Knoblauchzehen, geschält","1,2 cm Ingwerwurzel, geschält","½ Lauchstange, gehackt","½ Selleriestange, gehackt","2 Samen der Afrikanischen Muskatnuss, geschält","30 Njangsa-Samen","4 TL gemahlenes Mbongo-Gewürz","½ Tasse Pflanzenöl","¼ TL weißer Pfeffer","1 Habanero-Chilischote","3 kleine Brühwürfel"],"s":["Lightly salt the fish fillets, and set aside.","Combine the tomatoes, half the onions, garlic, ginger, leeks, celery, African nutmeg, njangsa, mbongo spice, and ½ cup water. Blend until smooth.","Pour the mixture over the fish, and marinate for 30 minutes.","Heat the oil in a pot. Add the remaining onions and cook until aromatic. Add the fish, marinade, and peppers, then season with salt and stock cubes. Cover and cook for about 15 minutes.","Uncover and check the seasoning. Thin with water if necessary, then cook for another 5 minutes.","Serve with boiled plantains, rice, or yams."],"x":[],"desc":"__NOTOC__ Mbongo tchobi is type of stew popular among the Bassa people of Cameroon, though it is also eaten in other countries. It can be eaten with rice and yam.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mbongo_Tchobi_(Cameroonian_Black_Stew)","i":"wb-en-2677","im":["5/55/Mbongo_tchobi_et_banae_plantin_malx%C3%A9.jpg/500px-Mbongo_tchobi_et_banae_plantin_malx%C3%A9.jpg","Coco lago","CC BY-SA 4.0","Mbongo tchobi et banae plantin malxé.jpg","w"],"on":"Mbongo Tchobi (Cameroonian Black Stew)","og":["Large fish of choice, filleted","½ teaspoon salt","2 large (or 4 small) tomatoes, roughly chopped","1 large onion, chopped","7 garlic cloves, peeled","½ inch ginger root, peeled","½ leek stem , chopped","½ celery stalk, chopped","2 seeds African nutmeg, peeled","30 njangsa seeds","4 teaspoons ground mbongo spice","½ cup vegetable oil","¼ teaspoon white pepper","1 habanero chile pepper","3 small seasoning cubes"]},{"n":"Mbulawu (malawischer fermentierter Hirsebrei)","c":"fruehstueck","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse Hirsemehl","3 Tassen Wasser","Salz, nach Geschmack","1 EL Pflanzenöl"],"s":["In a saucepan, bring the water to a boil.","Gradually add the millet flour to the boiling water, stirring continuously to prevent lumps from forming.","Reduce the heat to low and let the mixture simmer for about 10 minutes, stirring occasionally.","Add a pinch of salt to taste and continue stirring.","Remove the saucepan from the heat and allow the porridge to cool down to room temperature.","Once the porridge has cooled, cover it with a clean cloth and leave it to ferment overnight or for at least 8 hours. This fermentation process enhances the flavor and nutritional profile of the porridge.","The next morning, heat the vegetable oil in a separate pan.","Pour the fermented millet porridge into the pan and heat it over medium heat, stirring continuously until it reaches the desired consistency. You can add more water if you prefer a thinner consistency.","Serve warm in a bowl."],"x":["You can adjust the amount of millet flour and water to achieve your preferred consistency for the porridge.","For added sweetness, you can serve mbulawu with honey, sugar, or fruit toppings.","Mbulawu can also be made with other grains like sorghum or corn."],"desc":"Mbulawu is a traditional Malawian fermented millet porridge. It is a nutritious and comforting breakfast option that is enjoyed by many in Malawi.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mbulawu_(Malawian_Fermented_Millet_Porridge)","i":"wb-en-2678","im":["6/67/Oatmeal_%281%29.jpg/960px-Oatmeal_%281%29.jpg","Renee Comet (Photographer)","Public domain","Oatmeal (1).jpg","w"],"on":"Mbulawu (Malawian Fermented Millet Porridge)","og":["1 cup millet flour","3 cups water","Salt, to taste","1 tablespoon vegetable oil"]},{"n":"Mchemsho (tansanischer Eintopf)","c":"beilagen","k":"Tansania","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":2,"l":"en","g":["500 g Rindfleisch, gewürfelt","4 grüne Kochbananen, geschält und in Scheiben geschnitten","3 mittelgroße Kartoffeln, geschält und gewürfelt","2 Möhren, in Scheiben geschnitten","1 Tasse grüne Bohnen, geputzt","1 kleiner Kohlkopf, gehackt","1 große Zwiebel, gehackt","3 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","1 EL frischer Ingwer, gerieben","2 Tomaten, gewürfelt","1 grüne Paprika, in Scheiben geschnitten","2 EL Pflanzenöl","5 Tassen Rinderbrühe oder Wasser","1 TL gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","1 TL gemahlener Koriander","½ TL Kurkuma","Salz, nach Geschmack","schwarzer Pfeffer, nach Geschmack","Saft von 1 Limette oder Zitrone","frischer Koriander (Koriandergrün), gehackt, zum Garnieren"],"s":["Place the beef in a large pot and cover with water.","Add half of the onion, half of the ginger, and a pinch of salt.","Simmer until the meat becomes tender, about 1–1½ hours.","Reserve the cooking stock.","Heat the oil in a separate large pot.","Sauté the remaining onion until soft.","Add the garlic and remaining ginger and cook for 1 minute.","Stir in the tomatoes and cook until softened.","Add the cumin, coriander, and turmeric.","Add the potatoes, carrots, green bananas, green beans, cabbage, and bell pepper.","Pour in the reserved stock.","Add the cooked beef.","Bring to a boil, then reduce the heat and simmer for 30–40 minutes.","Cook until all vegetables are tender.","Season with salt, black pepper, and lime juice.","Garnish with chopped coriander.","Serve hot."],"x":["Mchemsho is commonly served with","Chicken mchemsho","Vegetarian mchemsho","Mchemsho with eggplant","Mchemsho with coconut milk","Green cooking bananas give the stew its traditional texture and flavor."],"desc":"Mchemsho is a traditional Tanzanian mixed stew consisting of meat, vegetables, green bananas, and aromatic spices simmered together in a flavorful broth. The name mchemsho comes from the Swahili word chemsha, meaning \"to boil\". The dish is particularly popular in northern Tanzania and is often prepa","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mchemsho_(Tanzanian_cuisine)","i":"wb-en-2679","on":"Mchemsho (Tanzanian cuisine)","og":["500 g beef, cut into cubes","4 green cooking bananas, peeled and sliced","3 medium potatoes, peeled and cubed","2 carrots, sliced","1 cup green beans, trimmed","1 small cabbage, chopped","1 large onion, chopped","3 cloves garlic, minced","1 tbsp fresh ginger, grated","2 tomatoes, diced","1 green bell pepper, sliced","2 tbsp vegetable oil","5 cups beef stock or water","1 tsp ground cumin","1 tsp ground coriander","½ tsp turmeric","Salt, to taste","Black pepper, to taste","Juice of 1 lime or lemon","Fresh coriander (cilantro), chopped, for garnish"]},{"n":"Met","c":"getraenke","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":3,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse zimmerwarmer, sterilisierter Fruchtsaft (optional)","1 Packung Trocken-Weinhefe und Hefenährsalz (Lalvin EC1118, K1V-1116 o. Ä.)","2,85 l Wasser","1,35 kg Honig","450 g Rosinen (optional)"],"s":["Sanitize all of your equipment (see notes).","If desired, create a starter culture by mixing the fruit juice and yeast. Place into a 1-quart container fitted with a rubber stopper and airlock. Keep at room temperature, out of direct sunlight, for 1–2 days until the mixture is bubbling.","This starter culture will cause the fermentation below to begin with vigor and may prevent the mead from failing to ferment.","Heat the water in a pot over medium heat, and slowly stir in the honey until completely dissolved.","There is a common disagreement among mead makers as to whether you should boil the mixture or not; Boiling will alter the flavor but will enhance the clarity of the finished mead.","Remove the pot from the heat, and cool to 170°F (76°C).","Stir in the raisins, and transfer to your fermentation vessel. Cool to room temperature (about 68°F/20°C).","Rehydrate the yeast if you did not make a starter culture. Transfer the yeast mixture to the honey mixture in the vessel, and attach the airlock.","Place the vessel in a cool (68°F/20°C), dark place. After about a day, the airlock should start to allow bubbles to escape, which indicates beginning fermentation. The raisins will rise to the surface of the mixture.","Avoid stirring or agitating the mixture, as it may cause the liquid to rise up and spill out of the airlock.","Let the mead ferment for 4–6 weeks.","If desired, \"rack\" the mead to allow the mead to clear faster: carefully siphon it into a second carboy with a sanitized tube, avoiding the sediment to prevent cloudiness and avoiding splashing to prevent incorporating excess oxygen.","Attach an airlock to the second carboy.","Ferment for another 3 months or until all signs of fermentation have stopped (usually when the airlock doesn't produce any bubbles for a long period of time—typically over 30 seconds between bubbles) and your mead has cleared enough to read a newspaper through it.","Rack the mead once more.","Bottle the mead by sealing in sterilized bottles using airtight caps or quality corks. If the fermentation is not complete, pressure will build up inside the sealed bottles and cause them to explode.","Age the mead in the bottle for at least 6 months (or longer) before drinking."],"x":["Mead should be made in sanitized equipment to ensure food safety. Potassium metabisulphite is a common sanitizing agent. Those who are allergic to sulphites can use other sanitizing methods. Failure to remove all traces of this chemical from the equipment may result in poisonous or otherwise undrinkable mead.","It is imperative that sterile conditions be maintained while the carboys are open to avoid infection.","The mead needs to age, usually for one year, and anywhere up to five or more. Bulk aging can be done done in a tertiary carboy.","Excessive racking will promote oxidation, resulting in an undrinkable mead.","This module uses text from the Wikipedia module Mead under the terms of the GNU Free Documentation License. Please see that module for the authors of the text prior to its adaptations in Wikibooks."],"desc":"Mead or honey wine is a fermented alcoholic beverage made of honey, water, and yeast. It can have a wide range of flavors, depending on the source of the honey, additives including fruit and spices, the yeast used for fermentation, and the aging procedure.","img":"Met Flasche und Glas.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mead","i":"wb-en-2680","im":["2/2c/Met_Flasche_und_Glas.jpg/500px-Met_Flasche_und_Glas.jpg","Stahlkocher","CC BY-SA 3.0","Met Flasche und Glas.jpg","r"],"on":"Mead","og":["1 cup room temperature sterilized fruit juice (optional)","1 packet of dry winemaker's yeast (Lalvin EC1118, K1V1116 or similar) as well as yeast nutrient","3 quarts water","3 pounds (1 quart) honey","1 pound raisins (optional)"]},{"n":"Fleisch-Masala","c":"saucen","k":"Indien","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["50 g ganze getrocknete Chilis","100 g Koriandersamen","2 EL schwarzes Pfefferkorn","1 TL Kreuzkümmelsamen","1 TL Senfsamen","1 TL gemahlene Kurkuma","12 Zehen","¼ TL Kardamomsamen","2 kurze Zimtstangen"],"s":["Toast the chillies, coriander, peppercorn, cumin, and mustard in a frying pan.","Grind all ingredients to a powder.","Store in a glass jar with a tight-fitting lid."],"x":[],"desc":"Meat masala is a spice mix used in Keralan cuisine, typically as a marinade for various types of meat, especially mutton.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meat_Masala","i":"wb-en-2681","im":["e/e8/Fish_and_meat_with_masala_on_sale.jpg/960px-Fish_and_meat_with_masala_on_sale.jpg","Rameshng","CC BY-SA 3.0","Fish and meat with masala on sale.jpg","c"],"on":"Meat Masala","og":["50 g whole dried chillies","100 g coriander seed","2 tbsp black peppercorn","1 tsp cumin seed","1 tsp mustard seed","1 tsp turmeric powder","12 cloves","¼ tsp cardamom seed","2 short pieces of cinnamon"]},{"n":"Fleischfüllung für Ravioli","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["3 EL Butter oder Olivenöl","4 EL fein gehackte Zwiebel","340 g Kalbfleisch, Hähnchen, oder Pute, fein gehackt","340 g TK- oder gegarter Spinat, ausgedrückt und gehackt","½ Tasse frisch geriebener Parmigiano Reggiano","1 Prise gemahlene Muskatnuss","3 Eier","Salz"],"s":["Heat 3 tablespoons of olive oil in a small frying pan and soften the onions in it until translucent, about 7 minutes.","Add the minced meat and cook, stirring constantly, until any trace of pink has gone and all liquid has evaporated.","Remove from the heat and stir in the chopped spinach, Parmesan cheese, and nutmeg.","Season to taste.","Beat the eggs and mix them into the meat mixture.","Refrigerate or cool to room temperature while you roll the dough."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meat_Ravioli_Filling","i":"wb-en-2682","on":"Meat Ravioli Filling","og":["3 tbsp butter or olive oil","4 tbsp finely-chopped onion","¾ lb veal, chicken, or turkey, finely minced","12 oz frozen or cooked spinach, squeezed and chopped","½ cup freshly grated Parmigiano Reggiano","1 pinch ground nutmeg","3 eggs","Salt"]},{"n":"Fleisch und Kartoffeln in Brühe (Nikujaga)","c":"suppen","k":"Japan","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["200 g Rindfleisch in Scheiben","4 kleine Kartoffeln (am besten rotschalige Kartoffeln)","1 weiße Zwiebel, in Scheiben geschnitten","1 ½ Tassen Wasser","2 EL Mirin","3 EL Sojasoße","2 EL Zucker","1 Scheibe Ingwer","100 g Shirataki-Nudeln"],"s":["Cut potatoes into bite-sized pieces. Set aside to soak in cold water.","Combine mirin, soy sauce, sugar, ginger, and beef in a saucepan. Boil lightly for 2–3 minutes.","Remove beef from pan. Add potatoes, sliced onion, and water. Bring to a boil.","Simmer uncovered until the broth reduces to about ⅓ by volume.","Replace beef in pan, add shirataki noodles, and simmer for roughly 5 minutes.","Remove from heat and serve."],"x":["Pork can be substituted for the beef. Vary the amount of potatoes to taste.","The level of liquid does not need to, and in fact should not, completely cover the potatoes at the start of boiling. They will cook via steam, and the comparatively small volume of the liquid helps to concentrate the flavor.","Real mirin is important for preventing the potatoes from crumbling apart, especially when using Russets—it contains certain special sugars that prevent over-softening.","fr:Livre de cuisine/Nikujaga"],"desc":"Niku jaga (肉じゃが nikujaga meaning 'meat and potatoes') is a common Japanese household dish served at dinnertime.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meat_and_Potatoes_in_Broth_(Niku_Jaga)","i":"wb-en-2683","on":"Meat and Potatoes in Broth (Niku Jaga)","og":["200 g (7.1 oz) sliced beef","4 small potatoes (red potatoes recommended)","1 white onion, sliced","1½ cups water","2 tbsp mirin","3 tbsp soy sauce","2 tbsp sugar","1 slice of ginger","100 g (3.53 oz) shirataki noodles"]},{"n":"Paprika mit Fleisch-Reis-Füllung","c":"saucen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["3 Paprikaschoten","500 g Hackfleisch nach Wahl (z. B. Rind, Schwein oder gemischt)","0,5 l Tomatensoße aus der Dose","100 g ungekochter Reis (beliebige Sorte)","Salz","Pfeffer"],"s":["Wash peppers. Use a thin and sharp knife to carefully cut around the stem end and form a 5 cm (2 in) circle to open the pepper. Save this piece. Use a spoon or knife cut inside to remove remaining seeds and white membrane.","Then rinse again inside and out, and put aside.","Boil rice in a medium pot with 1 cup of water for 15 minutes. Set rice aside.","Cook your meat of choice to fill peppers with, and ensure that the fat is drained, if applicable.","Mix rice, meat, and one tablespoon of sauce together in bowl.","Using your fingers, stuff peppers with mixture until full, cover with pepper top which was set aside.","Place in small pot and ensure they will not tip over, then pour in remaining sauce and leftover meat-rice mixture.","Add water until it covers the peppers two-thirds of the way, then cover with a lid.","Cook under medium to high heat (watch so it does not boil over), about 25 minutes for soft peppers, less if you prefer peppers that are firmer. All ingredients are at this point pre-cooked, and safe to eat.","Remove and plate with sauce from pot."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meat_and_Rice-Stuffed_Bell_Peppers","i":"wb-en-2684","im":["2/20/Quinoa_stuffed_peppers.jpg/960px-Quinoa_stuffed_peppers.jpg","Mark Bonica","CC BY 2.0","Quinoa stuffed peppers.jpg","w"],"on":"Meat and Rice-Stuffed Bell Peppers","og":["3 bell peppers","500 g (½ lb) ground meat of your choice (e.g. beef, pork, or a mixture)","0.5 L (16 ounces) canned tomato sauce","100 g (½ cup) uncooked rice (any type)","Salt","Pepper"]},{"n":"Fleisch-Wurst-Ragù mit Nudeln","c":"pasta","k":"","p":6,"t":150,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["454 g getrocknete Nudeln","680 g Rinderschulter, in etwa 4 cm große Stücke geschnitten","450 g italienische Wurst (Salsiccia) (etwa 4 bis 5 Würstchen)","3 EL natives Olivenöl extra","1 mittelgroße Zwiebel, fein gehackt","2 mittelgroße Möhren, fein gehackt","2 Selleriestangen, fein gehackt","3 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","2 Dosen stückige Tomaten (790 g)","170 g Tomatenmark","1 EL getrockneter Oregano","1 EL getrocknetes Basilikum","Salz, nach Geschmack","frisch geriebener Parmigiano Reggiano, zum Servieren"],"s":["Heat the olive oil in a large in a thick-walled pot.","Add the beef chuck. Season the beef lightly with salt.","Cook, turning occasionally, until the beef develops a brown crust, approximately 8–12 minutes. Work in batches if necessary to avoid overcrowding.","Remove the beef from the pot and set aside.","Reduce the heat to medium.","Add the chopped carrots, celery, and onion to the same pot, using the remaining oil and rendered fat from the meat.","Cook for approximately 8–10 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables have softened. Be careful not to burn them.","Make a small opening in the center of the vegetables and add the minced garlic.","Cook until the garlic becomes lightly golden, approximately 30–60 seconds.","Immediately add the crushed tomatoes to prevent the garlic from burning. Stir thoroughly to combine with the vegetables.","Add the tomato paste and mix well until completely incorporated.","Add the oregano and basil, stirring to distribute the herbs evenly throughout the sauce.","Season with salt to taste, keeping in mind that the sausages will contribute additional salt and allow the mixture to simmer for one to two minutes.","Return the browned beef chuck and add the raw Italian sausages to the pot, along with any accumulated juices.","Stir gently, making sure the meat is submerged in the tomato sauce.","Bring the sauce to a gentle simmer, then reduce the heat to low.","Simmer for 2 hours with the pot lid on, leaving it slightly ajar. Stir approximately every 10 minutes to prevent the sauce from sticking to the bottom of the pot. Keep the heat low enough so that the sauce bubbles gently.","Approximately 15 minutes before the sauce finishes simmering, bring a large pot of salted water to a boil.","Add the entire 1-pound box of dried pasta.","Cook until slightly underdone, approximately 1–2 minutes less than the package's recommended cooking time. Do not drain the pasta or discard the cooking water.","Using tongs, transfer the slightly undercooked pasta directly from the boiling water into the pot of ragù.","Stir thoroughly so that every piece of pasta is coated with sauce.","Add one third cup of pasta water and continue simmering over medium-low heat until the pasta is tender but not mushy and the sauce clings evenly to it.","Divide the pasta and ragù among serving plates, distributing the beef and sausage as desired.","Grate fresh Parmigiano Reggiano generously over each serving.","Serve immediately while hot."],"x":[],"desc":"The below recipe is inspired by Neapolitan ragù, a dish that originated in Naples and is widely eaten in the Campania region of Italy. It's also popular among Italian-American families who call it Sunday sauce or Sunday gravy. The recipe presented here deviates from the authentic dish in that it's f","img":"Paccheri rigati al ragù Napoletano.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meat_and_Sausage_Ragu_with_Pasta","i":"wb-en-2685","im":["a/ad/Paccheri_rigati_al_rag%C3%B9_Napoletano.jpg/960px-Paccheri_rigati_al_rag%C3%B9_Napoletano.jpg","CristianoMay","CC BY-SA 4.0","Paccheri rigati al ragù Napoletano.jpg","r"],"on":"Meat and Sausage Ragu with Pasta","og":["1 lb (454 g) dried pasta","1½ lbs beef chuck, cut into approximately 1½-inch chunks","1 lb Italian sausage (approximately 4–5 links)","3 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil","1 medium onion, finely chopped","2 medium carrots, finely chopped","2 celery stalks, finely chopped","3 cloves garlic, minced","2 cans (28 oz each) crushed tomatoes","6 oz tomato paste","1 tablespoon dried oregano","1 tablespoon dried basil","Salt, to taste","Freshly grated Parmigiano Reggiano, for serving"]},{"n":"Teigtaschen mit Fleisch und Garnelen (Potstickers)","c":"fisch","k":"Japan","p":24,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Füllung","230 g Hähnchen- oder Schweinehack (etwa 250 g)","230 g gehackte rohe Garnelen","12 rohe Garnelen, gehackt","½ Tasse Wasserkastanien, geschält und in Scheiben (möglichst frisch)","1 EL helle Sojasoße","1 EL Sesamöl","1 EL Salz","1 Prise weißer Pfeffer (optional)","3 EL Frühlingszwiebel, fein gehackt","3 EL frischer Ingwer, fein gehackt","3 EL Koriandergrün, gehackt","#Zusammensetzen","1 Packung gekaufte Gyoza- oder Wan-Tan-Blätter","Speisestärke","Pflanzenöl"],"s":["Mix together the filling ingredients.","Place a small bowl of water on the work area. If desired, mix in a little cornstarch to make a glue.","Lay out one of the gyoza wrappers in front of you.","Dip your finger in the water and moisten the edges of the wrapper.","Place a heaped teaspoon of filling in the middle of the wrapper.","Fold the gyoza wrapper over the filling and pinch the edges to seal it shut.","Heat 2 tablespoons oil in a large skillet or wok.","When oil is ready, carefully add the dumplings and cook on high heat until golden brown (about 1 minute).","Without turning the dumplings over, add 1 cup of water and cover.","Steam for about 1 minute to cook the raw filling and then turn off the heat (this is to keep the bottom from burning).","Let the dumplings cook for a few more minutes with the heat turned off.","Serve the potstickers with dipping sauce or soy sauce."],"x":[],"desc":"Potstickers (锅贴 鍋貼 guōtiē; literally \"pot stick\") are a Northern Chinese-style dumpling popular as a street food, appetizer, or side order in Japanese and Chinese cuisine. This dish is often served on a dim sum menu, but may be offered independently. The filling for this dish usually contains pork (","img":"Potstickers RTE.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meat_and_Shrimp_Potstickers","i":"wb-en-2686","im":["0/01/Potstickers_RTE.jpg/500px-Potstickers_RTE.jpg","unbekannt","CC BY-SA 3.0","Potstickers RTE.jpg","r"],"on":"Meat and Shrimp Potstickers","og":["#Filling","½ pound (about 250 g) ground chicken or pork","½ pound ground raw prawn or shrimp","12 raw prawns/shrimp, chopped","½ cup water chestnuts (fresh if possible) peeled and sliced","1 tablespoon light soy sauce","1 tablespoon sesame oil","1 tablespoon salt","1 pinch white pepper (optional)","3 tablespoons green/spring onion, minced","3 tablespoons fresh ginger, minced","3 tablespoons cilantro, chopped","#Assembly","1 package store-bought gyoza/wonton wrappers","Cornstarch","Vegetable oil"]},{"n":"Fleischbällchen (vegetarisch)","c":"veggie","k":"","p":30,"t":20,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["1 große Zwiebel, gehackt","1 Packung Hackfleischersatz (Yves Veggie Ground Round) (340 g)","3 EL Hickory-Barbecuesoße oder Barbecuesoße oder Tomatensoße oder Ketchup (empfohlen)","2 Eier","3 EL Semmelbrösel","⅛ TL Paprikapulver","salzarme Sojasoße (optional), nach Geschmack"],"s":["Preheat oven to 350°F.","Sauté onion; pour off oil and set aside.","In a large bowl, beat eggs. Add the ground beef substitute, and break up well with fork.","Add all remaining ingredients and mix well.","Grease a large 12 x 18-inch (31 x 45 cm) baking tray.","Drop mixture onto the tray in tablespoonfuls. You should get 30–40 meatballs. Don't worry if the mixture falls apart a little on tray.","Bake at 350°F for 22 minutes.","Flip meatballs over.","Bake for an additional 9 minutes."],"x":["The barbecue sauce and/or soy sauce add an umami taste to the meatballs, which makes them taste more like real meat.","Any other pre-cooked ground meat substitute should also work."],"desc":"This recipe for Vegetarian Meatballs is delicious and easy to prepare. The meatballs don't come out spherical; they are more of squished hemispheres, flat on one side.","img":"Vegetarian Meatballs.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meatballs_(Vegetarian)","i":"wb-en-2687","im":["c/c0/Vegetarian_Meatballs.jpg/960px-Vegetarian_Meatballs.jpg","Unforgettableid","Public domain","Vegetarian Meatballs.jpg","r"],"on":"Meatballs (Vegetarian)","og":["1 large onion, chopped","1 package (340 g) Yves \"Veggie Ground Round\" ground beef substitute","3 Tbsp hickory smoked barbecue sauce (recommended) OR barbecue sauce OR tomato sauce OR ketchup","2 eggs","3 Tbsp breadcrumbs","⅛ tsp dried paprika","Low-sodium soy sauce to taste (optional)"]},{"n":"Fleischbällchen mit Honig-Limetten-Soße","c":"saucen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["450 g Rinderhack","1 TL Salz","1 TL schwarzer Pfeffer","1 TL Chiliflocken","½ Tasse Semmelbrösel","1 TL getrockneter Rosmarin","1 TL getrockneter Thymian","1 Ei, verquirlt","2 EL Butterschmalz","¼ Tasse Hühnerbrühe","2 EL Honig","3 Limetten, ausgepresst"],"s":["Combine beef, salt, pepper, red pepper flakes, ¼ cup breadcrumbs, rosemary, thyme, and egg.","Refrigerate for at least 1 hour.","Shape into 1-ounce balls and dredge meatballs in remaining breadcrumbs.","Melt butter in your largest sauté pan over low heat.","Raise the heat to medium. Place balls in skillet, working in batches if needed. Cook until well-browned with an internal temperature of 160 °F.","Place meatballs in a 200°F oven to keep warm.","Deglaze pan with broth. Add honey and lime juice, and boil until reduced by ¼.","Return meatballs to pan and toss to coat.","Serve warm."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meatballs_with_Honey_Lime_Sauce","i":"wb-en-2688","on":"Meatballs with Honey Lime Sauce","og":["1 pound ground beef","1 tsp salt","1 tsp black pepper","1 tsp red pepper flakes","½ cup dried breadcrumbs","1 tsp dried rosemary","1 tsp dried thyme","1 egg, beaten","2 tbsp clarified butter","¼ cup chicken broth","2 tbsp honey","3 limes, juiced"]},{"n":"Sloppy Joes ohne Fleisch","c":"snacks","k":"","p":4,"t":30,"d":2,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["2 TL Olivenöl","½ Zwiebel, gehackt","½ grüne Paprika, gehackt","⅓ Tasse geraspelte Möhre","1 Dose Chilibohnen, nicht abgetropft","1 ½ Tassen gekochter Naturreis","¼ Tasse Hickory-Barbecuesoße, oder nach Vorliebe","Hamburgerbrötchen"],"s":["Add olive oil to pan over medium-high heat.","Add onions, bell pepper, and carrots and cook for 3–4 minutes","Add rice, chili beans, and barbecue sauce and cook for approximately 10–15 minutes, stirring frequently to heat thoroughly.","Serve on hamburger buns."],"x":[],"desc":"This recipe is a great choice for a Meatless Monday that still lets you convince the kids that it's a Sloppy Joe! You can serve the finished product on whole-wheat hamburger buns.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meatless_Sloppy_Joes","i":"wb-en-2689","im":["9/90/Sloppy_Joe_%22homemade%22.jpg/960px-Sloppy_Joe_%22homemade%22.jpg","Buck Blues","CC BY 2.0","Sloppy Joe \"homemade\".jpg","w"],"on":"Meatless Sloppy Joes","og":["2 tsp olive oil","½ onion, chopped","½ green bell pepper, chopped","⅓ cup shredded carrot","1 can of chili beans, undrained","1 ½ cups cooked brown rice","¼ cup hickory-smoked barbecue sauce, or to your preference","Hamburger buns"]},{"n":"Hackbraten-Menü","c":"fleisch","k":"USA","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Hackbraten","230 g Hack aus der Rinderhüfte","230 g Rinderhack aus der Schulter","170 g Knoblauch-Croûtons, grob zerstoßen","1 ½ TL Salz","1 ½ TL frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","¼ Tasse Ketchup","¼ Tasse Worcestersoße","1 ⅛ TL Chiliflocken","1 Ei, verquirlt","2 TL Rosmarin, fein gehackt","2 EL Thymian, fein gehackt","6 Zehen Knoblauch, zerdrückt und gehackt","½ große Zwiebel, gewürfelt","3 Möhren, geschält und gewürfelt","½ rote Paprika, gewürfelt","4 dicke Speckstreifen, in 6 Stücke geschnitten und knusprig gebraten","2 EL Speckfett","#Soße","1 Tasse Hühnerbrühe","1 Tasse Schlagsahne","Bratensatz aus der Hackbratenform","2 EL Worcestersoße","#Kartoffelpüree","680 g mehligkochende Kartoffeln, geschält und in 1 cm große Würfel geschnitten","4 EL ungesalzene Butter","¼ Tasse Schlagsahne","1 TL Salz","1 TL frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","1 Eigelb, verquirlt","#Ofengemüse","4 große Möhren, geschält und in 4 cm große Stücke geschnitten","½ Tasse Olivenöl","Salz","frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","6 Zehen Knoblauch, zerdrückt und fein gehackt","1 große Zwiebel, in Spalten geschnitten","½ grüne und rote Paprika, in 6 cm lange Streifen geschnitten"],"s":["Heat a large stainless steel straight-sided sauté pan over medium high heat.","Add the bacon drippings, garlic, and vegetables. Sauté until vegetables are lightly browned around edges. Remove vegetables and set aside until cool.","Mix remaining meatloaf ingredients and sautéed vegetables but leave out the bacon. Shape with a loaf pan and place on an ungreased, unlined baking pan.","Insert a probe thermometer at a 45 degree angle into the center of the loaf. Bake the loaf at 325°F until internal temperature reaches 155°F.","Keep warm on a different pan than the one you used to cook it.","In a separate oven, prepare the vegetables. Toss the vegetables with olive oil and garlic. Sprinkle liberally with kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper.","Lay vegetables in a single layer on a half-sheet pan.","Bake at 450°F, shaking the pan halfway, for about 25 minutes. Keep warm.","Heat meatloaf pan over medium-high heat on two burners.","Whisk in flour and cook, whisking often, until blond.","Deglaze pan with broth and boil until reduced by ⅔.","Add cream and Worcestershire sauce, and reduce heat to below a simmer. Cook until slightly thickened and gravy coats the back of a spoon.","While broth for the gravy is reducing above, prepare the potatoes. Place potatoes in a medium saucepan and cover with cold water.","Set over high heat, cover and bring to a boil. Once boiling, uncover, decrease the heat to maintain a simmer. Cook until tender and easily crushed with tongs, approximately 10–15 minutes.","Place the half-and-half and butter into a microwave-safe container and heat in the microwave until warmed through, about 35 seconds.","Drain the potatoes in a colander and then return to the saucepan.","Mash the potatoes and then add the cream, butter, salt and pepper and continue to mash until smooth. Stir in the yolk until well-combined.","Slice meatloaf nice and thick and place a dollop of mashed potatoes on your plate.","Top with a few slices of meatloaf and some roast vegetables, then smother the whole thing with gravy.","Serve."],"x":[],"desc":"Learn to enjoy it when you hear meatloaf is for dinner. Add mashed potatoes, gravy, and roast vegetables, and you've got a big plate of comfort.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meatloaf_Dinner","i":"wb-en-2690","on":"Meatloaf Dinner","og":["#Meatloaf","½ pound ground sirloin","½ pound ground chuck","6 ounces garlic croûtons, coarsely crushed","1 ½ tsp salt","1 ½ tsp freshly-ground black pepper","¼ cup ketchup","¼ cup Worcestershire sauce","1 ⅛ tsp red pepper flakes","1 egg, beaten","2 tsp rosemary, finely chopped","2 tbsp thyme, finely chopped","6 cloves garlic, smashed and chopped","½ large onion, diced","3 carrots, peeled and diced","½ red bell pepper, diced","4 strips thick cut bacon, cut into 6 pieces and crisp-cooked","2 tbsp bacon fat","#Gravy","1 cup chicken broth","1 cup heavy cream","Fond from meatloaf pan","2 tbsp Worcestershire sauce","#Mashed potatoes","1 ½ pounds Russet potatoes, peeled and cut into ½-inch dice","4 tbsp unsalted butter","¼ cup heavy cream","1 tsp salt","1 tsp freshly-ground black pepper","1 egg yolk, beaten","#Roast vegetables","4 large carrots, peeled and cut into 1½-inch pieces","½ cup olive oil","Salt","Freshly-ground black pepper","6 cloves garlic, smashed and finely chopped","1 large onion, wedged","½ each green bell pepper and red bell pepper, cut into 2½-inch strips"]},{"n":"Hackbraten I","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":4,"t":120,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["900 g Rinderhack","2 Eier","1 Zehe Knoblauch, fein gehackt","1 TL Salz","¼ TL gemahlener Piment","etwas Currypulver zum Bestreuen","1 TL Worcestersoße","1 Zwiebel, gehackt","1–2 Selleriestangen, gehackt","240 g Kräckerbrösel","1–2 Dosen Pilzsuppe"],"s":["Combine the ground beef, eggs, minced garlic, salt, allspice, curry powder, and Worcestershire sauce.","Mix in the chopped onion, celery, and cracker crumbs.","Press the mixture into a standard loaf pan.","Bake at 400°F (200°C) for about 10–20 minutes until browned on top.","Tilt the pan, and drain off any accumulated grease. Add the mushroom soup on top.","Bake another 1.5–2 hours until cooked through."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meatloaf_I","i":"wb-en-2691","im":["4/4d/MeatloafWithSauce.jpg/960px-MeatloafWithSauce.jpg","Renee Comet (photographer)","Public domain","MeatloafWithSauce.jpg","w"],"on":"Meatloaf I","og":["2 lbs (900 g) ground beef","2 eggs","1 clove garlic, minced","1 teaspoon salt","¼ teaspoon ground allspice","Sprinkle of curry powder","1 teaspoon Worcestershire sauce","1 onion, chopped","1–2 celery stalks, chopped","1 cup (240 g) cracker crumbs","1–2 cans of mushroom soup"]},{"n":"Hackbraten II","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":5,"t":15,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Eier","120 ml Wasser","2 EL Sojasoße","1 kleine Zwiebel, gewürfelt","900 g Rinderhack","220 g Packung fertige Füllung (z. B. Stove Top oder Paxo, Füllungsmischung)","Salz, nach Geschmack","Pfeffer, nach Geschmack"],"s":["Preheat oven to 350°F (180°C).","Beat eggs, water, and approximately soy sauce together in a bowl and set aside.","Get a large bowl and mix the ground beef and stuffing together. Make sure to use your hands and combine the mixture well, as this is the most important step.","Slowly work the egg mixture into the meat and stuffing, once again making sure to combine all ingredients well.","Pick up the big ball of meat and pack in hands until you have formed a loaf. Place in ungreased loaf pan.","Bake, uncovered, on the center rack of the oven for 45–55 minutes until center of meatloaf is browned.","Drain excess grease off side of pan and let stand 5–10 minutes before cutting and serving."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meatloaf_II","i":"wb-en-2692","on":"Meatloaf II","og":["2 eggs","½ cup (120 ml) water","2 tablespoons soy sauce","1 small onion, diced","2 lbs (900 g) ground beef","8 oz (220 g) package of pre-made stuffing (e.g. Stove Top or Paxo)","Salt to taste","Pepper to taste"]},{"n":"Hackbraten III","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["675 g Rinderhack","1 Tasse Ritz-Kräcker","2 verquirlte Eier","225 g Tomatensoße","½ Tasse fein gehackte Zwiebel","½ TL Salz","¼ TL Pfeffer"],"s":["Preheat the oven to 350°F (180°C).","Pound the Ritz crackers until fine like bread crumbs.","In a separate bowl, add the meat and the other ingredients and mix with your hands until the mixture is smooth.","Grease a glass baking dish with vegetable shortening.","Put the meat mixture in the pan and shape like a football.","Bake in the oven for 1 hour.","Take out the meat loaf and serve warm."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meatloaf_III","i":"wb-en-2693","on":"Meatloaf III","og":["1 ½ pounds (675 g) ground beef","1 cup Ritz crackers","2 beaten eggs","8 ounces (225 g) tomato sauce","½ cup minced onion","½ teaspoon salt","¼ teaspoon pepper"]},{"n":"Hackbraten IV","c":"fleisch","k":"USA","p":8,"t":120,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Scheiben Vollkornbrot, geröstet und gewürfelt","2 verquirlte Eier","1 große Zwiebel, gehackt","½ Tasse Milch","½ Tasse geriebener Parmesan","3 EL frische Petersilie, fein gehackt","1 EL Dijonsenf","2 TL Worcestersoße","½ TL Salz","¼ TL Pfeffer","680 g Rinderhack","Backtrennspray","½ Tasse Ketchup (oder mehr)"],"s":["Preheat oven to 325°F.","Combine beaten eggs, milk, mustard, onion, Parmesan cheese, parsley, pepper, and salt, then bread cubes.","Crumble beef into mixture.","Fold meat and sauce mixture together.","Heavily spray a 9 x 13-inch glass baking dish or Dutch oven with cooking spray.","Form meat into a loaf shape in pan no more than 3 inches high.","Cover with ketchup, even if it takes more than ½ cup.","Bake 75 minutes or more, if desired."],"x":["If Dutch oven is used, it should not be as hot as for breads.","Great in leftovers for sandwiches."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meatloaf_IV","i":"wb-en-2694","on":"Meatloaf IV","og":["2 slices whole-wheat bread, toasted and cubed","2 beaten eggs","1 large onion, chopped","½ cup milk","½ cup grated Parmesan cheese","3 tablespoon fresh parsley, finely chopped","1 tablespoon Dijon mustard","2 teaspoons Worcestershire sauce","½ teaspoon salt","¼ teaspoon pepper","1½ pounds ground beef","Cooking spray","½ cup (or more) ketchup"]},{"n":"Hackbraten V","c":"fleisch","k":"USA","p":6,"t":1,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Dose Kichererbsen oder andere Bohnen (400–425 g)","400 g gemischtes Hackfleisch (Rind und Schwein)","240 ml Milch","½ TL Salz","¼ TL gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","1 EL Worcestersoße","¼ TL Knoblauchpulver","¼ TL getrockneter Salbei","1 TL Dijon- oder anderer Senf","75 g Haferflocken","Tomatenketchup"],"s":["Preheat the oven to 180°C (350°F).","Drain the chickpeas or white beans, reserving the liquid. Mash the peas or beans to a paste.","Combine the mashed peas/beans, the liquid from the can, the meat, milk, salt, pepper, Worcestershire, garlic powder, sage, mustard, and oats in a large bowl and mix thoroughly.","Pour the mixture into an ungreased loaf pan; spread ketchup on top.","Bake at 180°C (350°F) for 1–1¼ hours. Allow to stand for 15 minutes or so after removing it from the oven before cutting into it."],"x":["Pretty much any variety of cooked beans should work; canned lentils would probably work too.","This meatloaf can be made vegan by making the following one-to-one substitutions","Vegan ground beef substitute (e.g. reconstituted TVP) instead of ground meat","Plant milk (e.g. soy milk) instead of milk","Soy sauce or a vegan version of Worcestershire sauce instead of conventional Worcestershire sauce (which has anchovies in it)"],"desc":"This meatloaf recipe stretches meat using beans or chickpeas. It also uses aquafaba (the liquid from the canned beans or chickpeas) in place of an egg, which reduces both waste and the fat content of the meatloaf.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meatloaf_V","i":"wb-en-2695","im":["4/4d/MeatloafWithSauce.jpg/960px-MeatloafWithSauce.jpg","Renee Comet (photographer)","Public domain","MeatloafWithSauce.jpg","w"],"on":"Meatloaf V","og":["1 can (400–425 g/14–15 oz) chickpeas or other beans","400 g (14 oz) mixed ground beef and pork","240 ml (1 cup) milk","½ tsp salt","¼ tsp ground black pepper","1 Tbsp Worcestershire sauce","¼ tsp garlic powder","¼ tsp dried sage","1 tsp Dijon or other prepared mustard","75 g (¾ cup) rolled oats","Tomato ketchup"]},{"n":"Mediterraner Rindfleischeintopf","c":"suppen","k":"Mittelmeer","p":4,"t":150,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["500 g mageres Rindfleisch zum Schmoren (in Steaks, nicht gewürfelt)","600 g grüne Oliven, Steine entfernt","6 große Tomaten, gewürfelt","1 Zwiebel, fein gehackt","1 große Knoblauchzehe, fein gehackt","Olivenöl"],"s":["In a large saucepan or casserole dish, gently fry the onion and garlic in plenty of good olive oil for a few minutes, taking care not to brown them.","Season the beef well with salt and black pepper and immediately add to the pan. Fry until evenly sealed and lightly browned.","Add the olives and tomatoes to the pan and simmer gently for two hours with the lid on.","Serve."],"x":["If you buy olives in brine, it's a good idea to soak them in fresh water before use so that the resulting dish is not overly salty.","Adding red wine or a dark beer such as a dunkel or stout could result in a richer gravy but may overpower the fresh flavour of the vegetables."],"desc":"This is a hearty and flavoursome beef stew inspired by the Mediterranean. It is based on a dish cooked by Keith Floyd in his Floyd around the Med TV series. The olives make this a filling meal in itself, but it could be served with rice or simply with bread to mop-up the gravy.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mediterranean_Beef_Stew","i":"wb-en-2696","on":"Mediterranean Beef Stew","og":["500 g (1.1 lb) of lean beef stewing/braising steak (in steaks, not diced)","600 g (1.3 lb) of green olives, stones removed","6 large tomatoes, diced","1 onion, finely chopped","1 large clove of garlic, finely chopped","Olive oil"]},{"n":"Mediterranes grünes Hähnchen","c":"saucen","k":"Mittelmeer","p":4,"t":120,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Bund krause Petersilie, gewaschen","2 Schalotten, geschält und grob gehackt","3 Zehen Knoblauch","6 EL Olivenöl","3 EL Dijonsenf","1 EL italienische Kräutermischung","Saft von 1 Zitrone","2 EL schwarzer Pfeffer","¼ TL Salz","1 ganzes Hähnchen, zerteilt (oder 8 beliebige Hähnchenteile aus Keule, Brust, Schenkel und Flügel)"],"s":["In a blender or food processor, combine parsley, shallots, garlic, olive oil, mustard, Italian herb blend, lemon juice, pepper, and salt. Purée.","Transfer mixture to a gallon zip-lock bag.","Add chicken, making sure it's covered on all sides by the marinade.","Seal bag and refrigerate for an hour.","Preheat oven to 300°F (150C).","Transfer chicken pieces to a rimmed baking sheet.","Bake about 40 minutes, turning pieces after 20 minutes, until juices run clear."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mediterranean_Green_Chicken","i":"wb-en-2697","on":"Mediterranean Green Chicken","og":["1 bunch curly parsley, washed","2 shallots, peeled and coarsely chopped","3 cloves garlic","6 tablespoons olive oil","3 tablespoons Dijon mustard","1 tablespoons Italian herb blend","Juice of 1 lemon","2 tablespoons black pepper","¼ teaspoon salt","1 whole chicken, cut up (or any 8 chicken pieces—any combination of leg, breast, thigh, and wing)"]},{"n":"Mediterraner gegrillter Thunfisch","c":"saucen","k":"Mittelmeer","p":4,"t":15,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 frische Thunfischsteaks (600 g)","4 Löffel natives Olivenöl extra","2 Löffel Aceto balsamico","1 Limette, ausgepresst","frische Estragonblätter","Salz","Pfeffer"],"s":["At least one hour before serving, prepare a marinade with the oil, vinegar or lime juice, tarragon leaves, salt and pepper in a flat container. Pour over the tuna steaks and turn them to make sure all pieces are well coated.","Cover with plastic wrap and refrigerate until it is time to grill.","Spray a clean grill or grilling container with non-stick cooking spray.","Drain and reserve the excess marinade from the tuna. Grill tuna for about 4 minutes on each side or until nicely charred on the outside and still a bit pink in the middle.","Place the steaks on individual serving dishes and pour the marinade on the grilled tuna.","Serve with steamed vegetables, steamed rice, or a spinach salad.","it:Libro di cucina/Ricette/Trancio di tonno marinato fr:Livre de cuisine/Thon grillé à la méditerranéenne"],"x":[],"desc":"This is a very simple and quick recipe for delicious fresh tuna steaks.","img":"Tuna steak.JPG","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mediterranean_Grilled_Tuna","i":"wb-en-2698","im":["b/bc/Tuna_steak.JPG/960px-Tuna_steak.JPG","No machine-readable author provided. Chensiyuan assumed (bas","CC BY-SA 3.0","Tuna steak.JPG","r"],"on":"Mediterranean Grilled Tuna","og":["4 ea. (600 g) fresh tuna steaks","4 spoons of extra-virgin olive oil","2 spoons of balsamic vinegar","1 lime , juiced","Fresh tarragon leaves","Salt","Pepper"]},{"n":"Medu Vada (südindische herzhafte Linsenkringel)","c":"veggie","k":"Indien","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":2,"l":"en","g":["240 g geschälte Urdbohnen","Salz, nach Geschmack","¼ TL Asafoetida (Asant)","8–10 Curryblätter","1 TL gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","1 TL zerstoßene schwarze Pfefferkörner","Öl zum Braten"],"s":["Wash and soak urad dal for 6 hours. Grind into a fine paste.","Add salt, asafoetida, curry leaves, cumin powder, and crushed peppercorns to the batter and mix well.","Heat oil in a kadai.","Wet your palms and take batter into the palms.","Shape into balls and make a hole with the thumb in the centre like a doughnut.","Deep-fry this in medium-hot oil until golden brown and crisp.","Serve hot with sambhar and coconut chutney."],"x":[],"desc":"A vada is a savoury South Indian doughnut made from lentils (or sometimes potatoes). This is a recipe for medu vada. It is commonly accompanied by idli.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Medu_Vada_(South_Indian_Savory_Lentil_Donut)","i":"wb-en-2699","im":["1/1b/Medu_Vada.JPG/960px-Medu_Vada.JPG","Lubnakarim06","CC BY-SA 4.0","Medu Vada.JPG","w"],"on":"Medu Vada (South Indian Savory Lentil Donut)","og":["1 cup (240 g) skinless black gram","Salt to taste","¼ tsp asafoetida","8–10 curry leaves","1 tsp cumin powder","1 tsp crushed black peppercorns","Oil to fry"]},{"n":"Barbecue-Rippchen nach Memphis-Art","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Leiter Schweinerippchen (Spareribs)","6 EL Gewürzmischung für Rippchen","1 Tasse Tomatenmark","½ Tasse Melasse","¼ Tasse Apfelessig","2 EL Worcestersoße","2 EL Sojasoße","Hickoryholzstücke"],"s":["Season spareribs with rib rub.","Refrigerate for at least 1 hour.","Place chunks in smoker or charcoal grill set for indirect heat at 250°F (120°C).","Combine liquid ingredients and bring to a boil over high heat.","Reduce liquid by ⅓.","Place spareribs into smoker or grill for 4–5 hours, basting occasionally with sauce.","Brush remaining sauce on top of ribs and place on a medium-high grill until browned. The internal temperature of the ribs before removing from the grill needs to be at least 145°F (63°C).","Let rest for 10 minutes, covered, and carve."],"x":[],"desc":"This is a classic U.S. style of BBQ pork ribs.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Memphis-Style_BBQ_Ribs","i":"wb-en-2700","on":"Memphis-Style BBQ Ribs","og":["1 slab pork spareribs","6 tbsp Rib Rub","1 cup tomato paste","½ cup molasses","¼ cup apple cider vinegar","2 tbsp Worcestershire sauce","2 tbsp soy sauce","Hickory chunks"]},{"n":"Menemen (Eier mit Zwiebel, grüner Paprika und Tomate)","c":"veggie","k":"Türkei","p":2,"t":30,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["4 Eier","2 Zwiebeln","2 grüne Paprika","4 Tomaten","2 EL gehackte Petersilie","2 EL Olivenöl","1–2 TL getrockneter Oregano (optional)","1–2 TL edelsüßes Paprikapulver (optional)","Salz","Pfeffer"],"s":["Prepare a concassée of tomatoes by blanching, peeling, seeding and dicing the tomatoes. Alternately, you may simply grind the tomatoes in a food processor or grate them using a box grater.","Dice the onions and peppers in medium dice and sauté in the olive oil until tender.","Add the oregano and paprika, if using.","Add the tomatoes to the peppers and onion and cook for 5 minutes.","Add the parsley and season with salt and freshly ground black pepper.","Beat the eggs and pour over the mixture in the pan. Stir until cooked.","Serve with Turkish bread."],"x":[],"desc":"Menemen is a Turkish dish of eggs with onion, green pepper and tomato. It can be served as a breakfast or luncheon dish.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Menemen_(Eggs_with_Onion,_Green_Pepper,_and_Tomato)","i":"wb-en-2701","im":["5/55/Menemen%2C_%C4%B0zmir%2C_Turkey.jpg/960px-Menemen%2C_%C4%B0zmir%2C_Turkey.jpg","Ahmet Gürsakal","CC BY-SA 3.0","Menemen, İzmir, Turkey.jpg","w"],"on":"Menemen (Eggs with Onion, Green Pepper, and Tomato)","og":["4 eggs","2 onions","2 green peppers","4 tomatoes","2 tablespoons chopped parsley","2 tablespoons olive oil","1–2 tsp dried oregano (optional)","1–2 tsp sweet paprika (optional)","Salt","Pepper"]},{"n":"Menudo (mexikanische Kuttel-Mais-Suppe)","c":"suppen","k":"Mexiko","p":4,"t":0,"d":3,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Chili","4 getrocknete Ancho-Chilis","#Pozole","2 Schweinerippchen (Country Ribs)","1,35 kg Schweinefüße (Patas, Füße)","2 Dosen weißer Hominy-Mais (450 g), abgetropft","3–4 Chiles de Árbol","#Menudo-Eintopf","1,15 kg Pansen (Netzmagen)","2 EL mexikanischer Oregano","1 Zehe Knoblauch","2 Lorbeerblätter","1 EL Salz","#Menudo-Mischung","2 EL Chiliflocken (mit Kernen)","2 EL getrockneter mexikanischer Oregano","#Servieren","Limette","Maistortillas","gewürfelte weiße Zwiebel oder Frühlingszwiebel","fein gehackter Koriander"],"s":["Wipe the dried Anchos off with a wet paper towel.","If desired, toast dried chilies on each side 15 seconds on a hot griddle (this releases essential oils and enhances the flavor).","Place the dried chilies into the small pot of boiling water and boil for 10 minutes, turning frequently in the boiling water to ensure all sides receive their fair share of punishment.","Remove the chili pot from the stove and drain off the boiling water. Fill with cold water; let it sit a few minutes to cool.","Remove the stems from the chilies, cut chilies longitudinally from stem to tip on one side and open. Flush gently with running cold water to remove the seeds.","Place stemless and seedless reconstituted chilies into a blender and purée.","Remove pure from the blender and place in the refrigerator overnight.","Rinse and drain the white hominy.","Place the patas (feet) and ribs into a pot.","Place the hominy in the pot with the patas (feet).","Put 1 tbsp salt in the pot.","Take 3–4 dried Chilis de Arbol, discard the seeds and stems, and snip the chilis into ringlets and put into the pot.","Cover with water to a height not exceeding 1 cm above the ingredients and bring to a boil.","Cook the posole uncovered until the ribs are finished. Remove from the heat.","Remove the meat from the ribs and dice into small cubes, place back into the pot with the posole, discard the bones.","Place the cooked patas (feet) into the pressure pot you will use to make the menudo.","Place a small pot of water on the stove and set to boil. This will be needed to prepare the chilies.","Cut the fat from off of the tripe. If fat clings to the non-honeycombed side of the tripe, use a stiff brush to remove it.","Cut tripe into small pieces, about ¾–1 inch. Strong scissors work well here!","If the tripe smells overly rank (this is normal), you may want to soak it in clean water for an hour (or possibly boil it in water for five minutes) throwing away the soak (boiling) water.","Place cut tripe into the pressure cooker on top of the patas (feet).","Add the garlic, bay leaves, and Mexican oregano.","Fill pressure cooker with water until about 1 cm. above the height of the stew ingredients.","Cook at pressure 35–40 minutes.","After the stew has cooked in the pressure cooker at full pressure for 35–40 minutes, remove from the heat and let the pot cool off completely until pressure returns to ambient.","Remove the patas from the pot and remove the bones. Put deboned patas into pot with the tripe and discard the bones.","Transfer the stew to a large bowl and add the posole, ensure all savory pieces lie below the waterline, and set in the refrigerator overnight.","In the morning, skim all hardened fat from the surface of the stew which has probably gelatinized overnight.","Reheat a serving portion of the stew in the microwave or on stovetop. When hot, place into a serving bowl.","Add a tablespoon of chili to the stew and blend thoroughly.","The menudo is ready to serve with hot corn tortillas. The spices (oregano and chili flakes) are traditionally combined before serving and placed at the side of the bowl of menudo with a lime wedge for the diner to add just prior to eating.","Along with the spices, diced onion or cilantro are also traditionally added to the stew just prior to enjoying."],"x":["Almost all (but not all) store-bought honeycomb tripe will smell strongly from the bleaching lime as possible. Let your nose be the judge as to whether or not it will require a soaking or boil as described in the steps below.","You may use cow feet instead of pig feet."],"desc":"Menudo is a traditional Mexican dish; a spicy soup made with hominy and tripe. Menudo preparation in the northern state of Chihuahua as well as northern New Mexico requires the preparation of three separate items, all combined at the time of final preparation for the table: Stew, Posole, and Chili. ","img":"Menudo soup Ortegas La Jolla 20050220.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Menudo_(Mexican_Tripe_and_Hominy_Soup)","i":"wb-en-2702","im":["4/40/Menudo_soup_Ortegas_La_Jolla_20050220.jpg/960px-Menudo_soup_Ortegas_La_Jolla_20050220.jpg","Kaihsu Tai","CC BY-SA 3.0","Menudo soup Ortegas La Jolla 20050220.jpg","r"],"on":"Menudo (Mexican Tripe and Hominy Soup)","og":["#Chili","4 dried Ancho chiles","#Posole","2 pork country ribs","3 lb pigs feet (patas)","2 cans (16 oz) white hominy, drained","3–4 chiles de Arbol","#Menudo stew","2½ lb honeycomb tripe","2 tbsp Mexican oregano","1 clove garlic","2 bay leaves","1 tbsp salt","#Menudo mix","2 tbsp red pepper flakes (with the seeds)","2 tbsp dried Mexican oregano","#Serving","Lime","Corn tortillas","Diced white or green onion","Minced cilantro"]},{"n":"Meringata (Baisertorte mit Sahnefüllung)","c":"dessert","k":"Italien","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Baisers","400 g Eiweiß","800 g feiner Zucker","#Füllung","1 Tasse Konditorcreme","2 Eiweiß (75 g)","150 g Zucker","3 EL Wasser (50 ml)","2 Tassen Schlagsahne"],"s":["Whisk the egg whites and sugar in a bowl over simmering water until it reaches 120°F (50°C).","Remove from the heat and continue whipping until the meringue is cool and stiff.","Line a baking sheet with parchment paper and draw two 10-inch circles on the paper.","Using a pastry bag, pipe a spiral beginning in the centre of the circle and working outwards to form a disc about ½ inch thick.","Repeat with the other circle.","With the remaining meringue, pipe 20 small meringues using a star tip.","Bake the meringues for 2–2½ hours at 200–225°F (110°C) until crisp but not brown. For a whiter meringue, bake at 180°F (80°C) overnight.","Use the egg yolks left over from the meringue to make 1 cup of crème pâtissière. Chill well.","Use the egg whites, sugar, and water to make an Italian meringue. Refrigerate to cool thoroughly.","Whip the cream to medium peaks. Fold in the 1 cup of cold pastry cream and Italian meringue. Refrigerate until ready to proceed with the assembly.","Spread one half of the filling on one of the meringue discs.","Place the second disc on top and cover the second disc with the rest of the filling.","Arrange the small meringues in concentric circles on top of the meringata.","Refrigerate for 2 hours before serving."],"x":[],"desc":"Meringata (literally \"meringued\") refers to any type of cake or dessert with a meringue topping or meringue mixed into it such as meringata di limone (lemon meringue pie) or meringata di panna (meringue cream gateaux, pie, or other dessert). The name covers many entirely different confections, one o","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meringata_(Cream-filled_Meringue_Gateaux)","i":"wb-en-2703","on":"Meringata (Cream-filled Meringue Gateaux)","og":["#Meringues","8 oz (1 cup / 400 g) egg whites","16 oz (2 cups / 800 g) superfine sugar","#Filling","1 cup crème pâtissière","2 ea. (75 g) egg whites","5 oz (150 g) sugar","3 Tbsp (50 ml) water","2 cups heavy cream"]},{"n":"Meringata di frutta in coppa (Baiser mit Obst und Sahne)","c":"dessert","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["Vanille-Konditorcreme, selbstgemacht oder gekauft, nach Bedarf","beliebiges Obst oder eine Mischung, nach Bedarf","Crème Chantilly (gesüßte Schlagsahne), nach Bedarf","zerbröselte Baisers, nach Bedarf","frische Minze oder Basilikum","Himbeercoulis oder ein anderer Belag nach Wahl"],"s":["Spoon a few tablespoons of vanilla cream into the bottom of a martini or parfait glass.","Cover the custard with your fruit of choice, leaving enough room for the topping.","Cover the fruit with crème chantilly, and sprinkle crumbled meringue chips on top.","Serve with a sprig of mint or basil and drizzle with raspberry coulis."],"x":[],"desc":"A quick and easy meringata is made as follows","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meringata_di_Frutta_in_Coppa_(Meringue_with_Fruit_and_Cream)","i":"wb-en-2704","on":"Meringata di Frutta in Coppa (Meringue with Fruit and Cream)","og":["Vanilla pastry cream, home-made or store-bought, as needed","Any fruit of choice or a mixture, as needed","Crème chantilly, as needed","Crumbled meringue cookies, as needed","Fresh mint or basil","Raspberry coulis or other topping of choice"]},{"n":"Meringata mit Ingwer und Sahne","c":"dessert","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Becher gekaufte oder selbstgemachte Baisers","1 Tasse eingelegter Ingwer, gehackt","2 Tassen Schlagsahne","4 EL Puderzucker","1 Zitrone, Schale abgerieben und Saft ausgepresst"],"s":["Strain the lemon juice and mix with the zest.","Mix the juice and zest with the heavy cream.","Whip the cream to soft peaks.","Fold in the powdered sugar.","Mix the ginger into the cream.","Crumble the meringues and mix into the cream. Do this just before serving.","Serve immediately, otherwise the meringue will dissolve in the cream over time."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meringata_with_Ginger_and_Cream","i":"wb-en-2705","on":"Meringata with Ginger and Cream","og":["1 container store-bought or homemade meringue cookies","1 cup preserved ginger, chopped","2 cups heavy cream","4 tbsp powdered sugar","1 lemon, zested and juiced"]},{"n":"Baiserkekse I","c":"brot","k":"","p":4,"t":30,"d":2,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["4 Eiweiß","250 ml feiner Zucker, Puderzucker, oder Zucker (am besten halb feiner Zucker, halb Puderzucker)","2 TL Zitronensaft","¼ TL Vanilleextrakt (optional)"],"s":["Whip whites of eggs until stiff and dry.","Add lemon juice.","Gradually add sugar and continue beating until mixture holds shape and is very shiny. Test to make sure the sugar is wholly solved and no grains remain (this can take longer or shorter depending on the sugar used).","Add vanilla.","Drop meringue by spoonfuls on unglazed paper.","Bake in a slow oven 80–90 minutes, depending on size. Use very low heat, as meringues should dry rather than bake and should be dry and only very slightly colored, when finished.","Let cool before serving."],"x":["The tiniest bit of egg yolk or fat prevents the egg white to get stiff.","Meringues are more decorative if shaped with a pastry bag.","Another method of baking is to preheat the oven and bake the meringues 2–3 minutes at moderately hot temperature, then turn down the oven completely and keep it shut for 8 hours.","Meringues do not turn out very well, if the air is very humid (due to climate or due to steam from other cooking).","In the original Swiss recipe, two meringues per serving are filled with sweetened whipped cream, but the cream is often supplemented with strawberries or other fresh fruits and vanilla ice cream."],"desc":"Meringue cookies are crunchy confections made from whipped egg whites and sugar. In Germany and Austria (but not in France) they are called Baiser (from French kiss). Served with whipped cream, they are a traditional dessert in the canton of Bern in Switzerland. See the meringue page for similar use","img":"Meringues 9027.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meringue_Cookies_I","i":"wb-en-2706","im":["1/19/Meringues_9027.jpg/960px-Meringues_9027.jpg","Mike Lehmann, Mike Switzerland 12:44, 27 January 2007 (UTC)","CC BY-SA 3.0","Meringues 9027.jpg","r"],"on":"Meringue Cookies I","og":["4 egg whites","1 cup (250 ml) superfine sugar, powdered sugar, or granulated sugar (ideally a mixture of 50% superfine and 50% powdered sugar)","2 teaspoons lemon juice","¼ teaspoon vanilla extract (optional)"]},{"n":"Baiserkekse mit Schokotropfen","c":"brot","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["⅛ TL Salz","⅛ TL Weinstein","2 Eiweiß","¾ Tasse Zucker","1 TL Vanille","1 Tasse Halbbitter-Schokotropfen"],"s":["Combine egg whites, salt, and cream of tartar. Whip to stiff peaks using a whisk or an electric mixer with the whisk attachment.","Gradually beat in in sugar and vanilla. Do not add the sugar all at once—this will cause your meringue to deflate. The meringue should be stiff, smooth, and glossy.","Fold chocolate chips into the meringue.","Drop meringue by tablespoonfuls onto parchment paper-lined baking sheets.","Bake at 325°F for 25 minutes, or a few minutes longer if needed. Let cool before removing from parchment. The cookies should be crispy all the way through, melt in your mouth, and not be chewy in the middle."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"Meringue cookies.jpg","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meringue_Cookies_with_Chocolate_Chips","i":"wb-en-2707","im":["4/49/Meringue_cookies.jpg/960px-Meringue_cookies.jpg","Benjamin Ikuta","CC BY-SA 4.0","Meringue cookies.jpg","r"],"on":"Meringue Cookies with Chocolate Chips","og":["⅛ tsp salt","⅛ tsp cream of tartar","2 egg whites","¾ cup white granulated sugar","1 tsp vanilla","1 cup semi sweet chocolate chips"]},{"n":"Baisers mit gerösteten Himbeeren und Haselnuss-Vanillesoße","c":"dessert","k":"USA","p":4,"t":240,"d":2,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["5 Eiweiß, zimmerwarm","1 Prise Weinstein","1 Tasse plus 1 EL Zucker, aufgeteilt","⅛ TL Zimt","470 ml frische Himbeeren","1 EL geröstetes Haselnussöl","1 ⅓ Tassen Haselnuss-Vanillesoße, gekühlt"],"s":["Heat the oven to 200°F (90ºC).","In the bowl of a standing mixer or with a hand-held mixer, whip egg whites and cream of tartar on high speed until soft peaks form, about 1 minute.","Reduce mixer speed to low and add 1 cup sugar in a steady stream; continue whipping until stiff and glossy, about 4 minutes.","Whip in cinnamon.","Fill a pastry bag fitted with a medium star tip with the meringue.","Onto a Silpat or oiled piece of parchment paper, pipe the mixture into rounds, starting in the center and moving outward in a spiral to form a 3-inch disk.","Bake for 2 hours, until crisp but not browned.","Cool on the Silpat or parchment, then carefully remove the meringues.","Set aside, uncovered, on a wire rack in a cool, dry place.","Increase oven temperature to 350°F.","Toss raspberries with remaining 1 tablespoon sugar and hazelnut oil.","Mound the berries on a baking sheet lined with Silpat or parchment paper and roast them for about 5 minutes, until glistening and very fragrant, but not mushy.","Remove from the oven.","Pour ⅓ cup of chilled hazelnut creme anglaise into the middle of a soup plate.","Place a cooled meringue in the center, then spoon ¼ of the roasted raspberries on top of each meringue.","Serve immediately."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Meringues_with_Roasted_Raspberries_and_Hazelnut_Creme_Anglaise","i":"wb-en-2708","on":"Meringues with Roasted Raspberries and Hazelnut Creme Anglaise","og":["5 egg whites, at room temperature","1 pinch of cream of tartar","1 cup plus 1 tablespoon granulated sugar, divided","⅛ teaspoon cinnamon","1 pint fresh raspberries","1 tablespoon toasted hazelnut oil","1⅓ cups hazelnut creme anglaise, chilled"]},{"n":"Misir Wat (scharfer äthiopischer Linseneintopf)","c":"suppen","k":"Äthiopien","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Tassen rote Linsen, abgespült","4 Tassen Wasser","1 große Zwiebel, fein gehackt","4 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","2 EL Olivenöl","2 EL Berbere-Gewürzmischung","1 EL Tomatenmark","1 TL gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","½ TL gemahlene Kurkuma","½ TL Salz, oder nach Geschmack","¼ TL schwarzer Pfeffer","frische Petersilie oder Koriander, gehackt, zum Garnieren"],"s":["Place the rinsed red lentils in a large pot and add the water. Bring to a boil over medium-high heat.","Reduce the heat to low and simmer the lentils for about 15–20 minutes or until they are soft and cooked through. Stir occasionally to prevent sticking. Once cooked, remove from heat and set aside.","In a separate large pot, heat the olive oil over medium heat.","Add the chopped onion to the pot and sauté until it becomes translucent and slightly browned.","Add the minced garlic to the pot and sauté for an additional minute until fragrant.","Stir in the berbere spice blend, tomato paste, ground cumin, ground turmeric, salt, and black pepper. Mix well to combine the spices with the onions and garlic.","Add the cooked lentils to the pot, including any remaining cooking liquid. Stir well to incorporate the lentils with the spices.","Bring the mixture to a simmer and cook for an additional 20 minutes, stirring occasionally, to allow the flavors to meld together.","Taste the stew and adjust the seasoning with salt and pepper if needed.","Remove the pot from the heat and let rest for a few minutes before serving.","Garnish with fresh chopped parsley or cilantro. Enjoy hot with injera or bread."],"x":["If you prefer a smoother consistency, you can blend a portion of the cooked lentils before adding them to the pot.","Adjust the spiciness of the stew by adding more or less berbere spice blend according to your taste preferences.","Lentils can vary in cooking time, so make sure to check for doneness and adjust the cooking time accordingly.","For extra richness, you can add a tablespoon of butter or olive oil to the stew towards the end of cooking.","Experiment with different lentil varieties such as brown lentils or green lentils for variations in texture and flavor.","Add vegetables like carrots, potatoes, or spinach to the stew for additional color and nutrients."],"desc":"Mesir wat is a delicious and spicy Ethiopian lentil stew that is packed with flavor. It is a popular vegetarian dish that is enjoyed as a main course or as a side dish in Ethiopian cuisine. Mesir wat is made with red lentils, aromatic spices, and a rich tomato-based sauce. It is traditionally served","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mesir_Wat_(Spicy_Ethiopian_Lentil_Stew)","i":"wb-en-2709","on":"Mesir Wat (Spicy Ethiopian Lentil Stew)","og":["2 cups red lentils, rinsed","4 cups water","1 large onion, finely chopped","4 cloves of garlic, minced","2 tablespoons olive oil","2 tablespoons berbere spice blend","1 tablespoon tomato paste","1 teaspoon ground cumin","½ teaspoon ground turmeric","½ teaspoon salt, or to taste","¼ teaspoon black pepper","Fresh parsley or cilantro, chopped, for garnish"]},{"n":"Mesquite-Barbecue-Burger","c":"fleisch","k":"USA","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["450 g Rinderhack aus der Schulter","½ TL Mesquite-Rauchpulver","2 EL Tomatenmark","½ EL Apfelessig","Salz","frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","2 TL helle Melasse","1 TL Knoblauchpulver","2 TL gelber Senf (amerikanisch)"],"s":["Preheat grill to 500–575°F.","Combine garlic, smoke powder, and 4 heavy pinches each of salt and freshly ground black pepper. Set aside.","Combine remaining ingredients in a mixing bowl. Form into ¾ inch-thick patties and make an indentation in the center of each patty with your thumb.","Sprinkle patties on both sides with seasoning mixture. Place on grill and cook, turning often, until desired \"doneness\" is achieved.","Serve on buns with cook's choice of cheese and desired toppings."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mesquite_BBQ_Burger","i":"wb-en-2710","on":"Mesquite BBQ Burger","og":["1 pound ground chuck","½ tsp mesquite smoke powder","2 tbsp tomato paste","½ tbsp apple cider vinegar","Salt","Freshly-ground black pepper","2 tsp light molasses","1 tsp garlic powder","2 tsp yellow mustard"]},{"n":"Mesquite-Barbecue-Lachs","c":"fisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 Wildlachsfilets mit Haut, Gräten entfernt","¾ Tasse Mesquite-Räucherchips, 30 Minuten in Wasser eingeweicht","¼ Tasse Paprikapulver","2 EL Chilipulver","1 EL grobes Salz","1 EL schwarze Pfefferkörner, geschrotet","1 EL Cayennepfeffer","1 EL Knoblauchpulver","2 EL heller brauner Zucker","Saft von 2 Zitronen","½ Tasse Olivenöl","1 Tasse Barbecuesoße","2 TL Pflanzenöl"],"s":["Combine lemon juice and olive oil in a gallon-size zip-top bag. Add salmon, toss to coat, and marinate in the refrigerator for at least 1 hour.","Wad up a sheet of newspaper and moisten with vegetable oil. Place under chimney full of coals, which you have put in the bottom of the grill, then light. Wait 15 minutes.","While charcoal heats, combine seasonings and sugar. Rub into salmon filets.","Dump coals evenly around grill and toss in wood chips. Re-apply grate, then quickly swab grill with the towel.","Add salmon filets, skin side down, to the hottest part of the grill and cook 2–3 minutes per side for medium rare, rotating 90 degrees halfway through cooking to make grill marks.","Brush meat side with sauce and cook until charred and crispy on the meat side, about 30 seconds. Serve immediately."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mesquite_BBQ_Salmon","i":"wb-en-2711","on":"Mesquite BBQ Salmon","og":["4 ea. (24 ounces) skin-on wild salmon filets, pin bones removed","¾ cup mesquite wood chips, soaked in water for 30 minutes","¼ cup paprika","2 tbsp chili powder","1 tbsp kosher salt","1 tbsp black peppercorns, cracked","1 tbsp cayenne pepper","1 tbsp garlic powder","2 tbsp light brown sugar","Juice of 2 lemons","½ cup olive oil","1 cup barbecue sauce","2 tsp vegetable oil"]},{"n":"Rinderfilet über Mesquite","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Mittelstück vom Rinderfilet","Cognac, nach Bedarf","¾ Tasse eingeweichte Mesquite-Holzchips","3 EL Paprikapulver","1 EL grob gemahlene Koriandersamen","1 ½ TL Salz","1 ½ TL grob gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","1 ½ TL getrockneter Rosmarin","2 TL getrocknete Zitronenschale"],"s":["Place beef in a large zip-top plastic bag. Add cognac to cover and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes.","Place mesquite chips in the hot coal area of a charcoal grill.","Combine paprika, coriander, salt, pepper, rosemary, and lemon peel. Rub this mixture all over beef and bring to room temperature.","Place beef in center of grill, cover, and cook, turning often until internal temperature reaches 135°F for medium rare, 150°F for medium, or 160°F for toast.","Remove, let rest for 10 minutes, and serve."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mesquite_Beef_Tenderloin","i":"wb-en-2712","on":"Mesquite Beef Tenderloin","og":["1 center-cut beef tenderloin roast","Cognac, as needed","¾ cup soaked mesquite wood chips","3 Tbsp paprika","1 Tbsp coarsely-ground coriander seeds","1 ½ tsp salt","1 ½ tsp coarsely-ground black pepper","1 ½ tsp dried rosemary","2 tsp dehydrated lemon peel"]},{"n":"Mesquite-Hähnchen-Sandwich","c":"snacks","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 Hähnchenbrustfilets ohne Haut","1 Tasse Mesquite-Räucherchips, 30 Minuten in Wasser eingeweicht","Mesquite-Gewürz","Olivenöl","4 Ciabatta-Brötchen, halbiert und geröstet","Barbecuesoße","4 Scheiben Monterey Jack"],"s":["Preheat grill and toss chips onto coals.","Brush chicken with oil and season liberally with seasoning. Grill, turning often, until internal temperature reaches","Remove to a plate and cover tightly with aluminum foil. Add a slice of cheese to each one and let rest 5 minutes.","Brush both sides with sauce. Place 1 breast inside each bun and serve immediately."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mesquite_Chicken_Sandwich","i":"wb-en-2713","im":["1/1f/Chicken_salad_sandwich_01.jpg/960px-Chicken_salad_sandwich_01.jpg","Lara604","CC BY-SA 2.0","Chicken salad sandwich 01.jpg","w"],"on":"Mesquite Chicken Sandwich","og":["4 boneless skinless chicken breasts","1 cup mesquite wood chips, soaked in water 30 minutes","Mesquite seasoning","Olive oil","4 ciabatta rolls, split in half and toasted","BBQ sauce","4 slices Monterey Jack cheese"]},{"n":"Mesquite-Hähnchen-Wraps","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Hähnchenbrustfilets ohne Haut","½ Tasse Mesquite-Räucherchips, 30 Minuten in Wasser eingeweicht","Salz","frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","4 Weizen- oder Maistortillas","Olivenöl","2 Tassen geriebener Monterey Jack"],"s":["Brush chicken with olive oil and season very liberally on both sides with salt and pepper. Set aside.","Preheat charcoal grill. Toss wood chips onto coals and reapply grate.","Add chicken and cook, turning often, until internal temperature reaches 165°F. Remove to a plate, and let rest 5–10 minutes.","Shred chicken with two forks. Toss with cheese and sprinkle into each tortilla. Roll lengthwise and wait until cheese is melted before serving."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mesquite_Chicken_Wraps","i":"wb-en-2714","im":["f/f8/Smoked_chicken_and_avocado_wrap.jpg/960px-Smoked_chicken_and_avocado_wrap.jpg","Takeaway","CC BY-SA 3.0","Smoked chicken and avocado wrap.jpg","w"],"on":"Mesquite Chicken Wraps","og":["2 boneless skinless chicken breasts","½ cup mesquite wood chips, soaked in water 30 minutes","Salt","Freshly-ground black pepper","4 flour or corn tortillas","Olive oil","2 cups grated Monterey Jack cheese"]},{"n":"Mexikanischer Schokoladenkuchen mit Mokka-Buttercreme","c":"kuchen","k":"Mexiko","p":10,"t":120,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["Backtrennspray","85 g Ibarra-Schokolade oder Halbbitterschokolade","85 g ungesüßte Schokolade","2 Tassen Kuchenmehl (Type 405)","2 TL Backpulver","½ TL Salz","1 TL Zimt (bei Halbbitterschokolade auf 2 TL erhöhen)","1 Tasse Butter, weich","1 Tasse plus 2 EL Zucker","1 TL Vanille","4 große Eier","1 Tasse Milch","Mokka-Buttercreme","Zimt, ungesüßter Kakao, und Puderzucker, optionale Beläge"],"s":["Preheat oven to 350°F.","Generously spray a deep 9-inch springform pan with nonstick cooking spray.","Melt the chocolates in a double boiler or in a microwave oven at low power.","Set aside to cool.","Sift together the flour, baking powder, salt, and cinnamon into a medium-size bowl.","Place the butter and sugar in a large mixing bowl and cream at high speed with an electric mixer.","Add the vanilla and the eggs, one at a time, beating well after each.","Pour in the cooled chocolate mixture, and beat well until everything is incorporated.","Add ⅓ of the flour mixture, and stir until it is just barely incorporated, then pour in half the milk.","Stir briefly, then repeat with another ⅓ of the flour and the remaining milk.","Add the rest of the flour mixture and stir just enough to blend. Don't over mix, or the cake will toughen.","Spread into the prepared pan and bake for 55 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean.","Cool completely before assembling and frosting.","Cut the cake into 3 equal layers, using a long serrated knife and a gentle sawing motion.","Spread mocha buttercream between the layers, and stack them evenly.","Spread more buttercream on the sides and the top.","Artfully sprinkle the top with extra cinnamon, cocoa, and confectioner's sugar, if desired."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mexican_Chocolate_Cake_with_Mocha_Buttercream","i":"wb-en-2715","im":["5/55/Chocolate_fudge_cake.jpg/500px-Chocolate_fudge_cake.jpg","Tracy Hunter from Kabul,, Afghanistan","CC BY 2.0","Chocolate fudge cake.jpg","w"],"on":"Mexican Chocolate Cake with Mocha Buttercream","og":["Nonstick cooking spray","3 ounce Ibarra or semisweet chocolate","3 ounces unsweetened chocolate","2 cups cake flour","2 teaspoons baking powder","½ teaspoon salt","1 teaspoon cinnamon (increase to 2 teaspoons if using the semisweet chocolate)","1 cup (2 sticks) butter, softened","1 cup plus 2 white granulated tablespoons sugar","1 teaspoon vanilla","4 large eggs","1 cup milk","Mocha Buttercream","Cinnamon, unsweetened cocoa, and confectioner's sugar, optional toppings"]},{"n":"Mexikanische scharfe Habanero-Soße","c":"saucen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["½ Tasse Tomatenmark","10–15 Habanero-Chilis, entstielt","¼ Tasse Malzessig","Salz, nach Geschmack","5 Tropfen rote Lebensmittelfarbe"],"s":["Combine all ingredients in a food processor and pulse until smooth.","Refrigerate in a non-reactive container for up to 2 months."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mexican_Habanero_Hot_Sauce","i":"wb-en-2716","im":["a/a3/Fermented_hot_sauce.jpg/960px-Fermented_hot_sauce.jpg","Veganbaking.net from USA","CC BY-SA 2.0","Fermented hot sauce.jpg","w"],"on":"Mexican Habanero Hot Sauce","og":["½ cup tomato paste","10–15 habaneros chiles, de-stemmed","¼ cup malt vinegar","Salt to taste","5 drops red food coloring"]},{"n":"Mexikanische Rippchen","c":"fleisch","k":"Mexiko & USA","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Leiter Schweinerippchen (St.-Louis-Zuschnitt)","¼ Tasse heller brauner Zucker","1 EL Habanero-Chilipulver","¼ Tasse Ancho-Chilipulver","1 EL getrockneter mexikanischer Oregano","1 EL Salz","1 EL frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","1 EL Chipotle-Pulver","1 Habanero-Chili, entkernt und fein gehackt","1 ½ Tassen Barbecuesoße","¼ Tasse Tequila (empfohlen: José Cuervo Especial)","große Mesquiteholzstücke"],"s":["Combine sugar, chile powders, oregano, salt, and pepper. Remove membrane from ribs and rub both sides with mixture. Refrigerate for at least 1 hour to marinate.","Combine tequila, habanero, and sauce. Bring to a boil in a large saucepan over medium high heat. Set aside.","Place enough mesquite chunks in a smoker to keep the temperature at 200°F. Place ribs in smoker and cook 7 hours, basting every hour with sauce mixture.","Brush meat side liberally with sauce mixture. Place sauce side-down on a high grill and cook until well-browned. Brush other side with sauce and repeat 1 more time.","Slice ribs into 1-rib portions and serve warm with remaining sauce."],"x":[],"desc":"These ribs use a Southwestern style rub, feature a sauce with a lot of prominent Mexican flavors, and are cooked over mesquite instead of hickory, which isn't very easy to find in the South, however mesquite is.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mexican_Ribs","i":"wb-en-2717","on":"Mexican Ribs","og":["1 slab St. Louis pork ribs","¼ cup light brown sugar","1 tbsp habanero chile powder","¼ cup ancho chile powder","1 tbsp dried Mexican oregano","1 tbsp salt","1 tbsp freshly-ground black pepper","1 tbsp chipotle powder","1 habanero chile, seeded and minced","1 ½ cups barbecue sauce","¼ cup tequila (recommended: José Cuervo Especial)","Large mesquite chunks"]},{"n":"Mexikanischer Reis I","c":"beilagen","k":"Mexiko & USA","p":5,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["3 EL Rapsöl","1 Tasse ungekochter weißer Reis (ungewaschen)","½ Zwiebel, gehackt","½ grüne Paprika, gehackt","1 Tasse gehackte Tomaten (aus der Dose abgießen)","1 TL Salz","½ TL Kreuzkümmel","2 Tassen Wasser"],"s":["Over medium-high heat, fry the dry rice in oil until golden brown, stirring often.","Add onions and green peppers and cook until slightly softened.","Add tomatoes, spices, and water. Cover and cook for 20 minutes on low heat."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mexican_Rice_I","i":"wb-en-2718","im":["0/0e/Mexican_rice_144235.jpg/960px-Mexican_rice_144235.jpg","Ralf Peter Reimann","CC BY-SA 2.0","Mexican rice 144235.jpg","w"],"on":"Mexican Rice I","og":["3 tablespoons canola oil","1 cup uncooked white rice (unwashed)","½ onion, chopped","½ green pepper, chopped","1 cup chopped tomatoes (if canned, drain them)","1 teaspoon salt","½ teaspoon cumin","2 cups water"]},{"n":"Mexikanischer Reis II","c":"beilagen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse ungekochter weißer Reis","1 frische rote Chili, entkernt und fein gewürfelt (oder 1 eingeweichte getrocknete Chili)","5 EL Ancho-Enchilada-Soße, durch ein mittelfeines Sieb gestrichen","1 ⅔ Tassen Hühnerbrühe","4 Zehen Knoblauch, geschält und zerdrückt","½ kleine Zwiebel, geschält und fein gewürfelt","1 EL Öl oder Schmalz"],"s":["Sauté garlic, onions, and red chile in oil over medium heat for about 1 minute.","Add in the rice and stir frequently until rice begins to brown.","Mix chicken stock and chile sauce in another saucepan and bring to a boil. When mixed, make sure liquid mixture equals out to 2 cups of liquid.","Add chicken stock and chile sauce mixture to rice and bring to a boil.","Reduce heat and bring rice to slow simmer. Cook for 25–30 minutes with the lid on.","Remove lid and fluff rice with a fork."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mexican_Rice_II","i":"wb-en-2719","im":["0/0e/Mexican_rice_144235.jpg/960px-Mexican_rice_144235.jpg","Ralf Peter Reimann","CC BY-SA 2.0","Mexican rice 144235.jpg","w"],"on":"Mexican Rice II","og":["1 cup uncooked white rice","1 fresh red chile, seeded and finely diced (or 1 dehydrated chile that has been rehydrated)","5 tbsp Ancho Enchilada Sauce, strained through a medium mesh","1 ⅔ cups chicken broth","4 cloves of garlic, peeled and crushed","½ small onion, peeled and finely diced","1 tablespoon oil or lard"]},{"n":"Mexikanischer Reis-Pilaw","c":"beilagen","k":"Mexiko","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Tassen ungekochter weißer Reis","2 EL ungesalzene Butter","¾ Tasse Tequila","¾ Tasse Tomatenmark","2 ½ Tassen Hühnerbrühe","3 Lorbeerblätter","¼ TL Salz","¼ TL frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","2 Habanero-Chilis, entstielt","1 EL getrockneter mexikanischer Oregano"],"s":["Rinse rice with cold water until water runs clear. Pat dry with paper towels.","Melt butter in a large pot over medium heat. Add rice and cook until rice turns golden brown.","Meanwhile, combine tequila, broth, tomato, salt, oregano, and pepper. Pour over rice and bring to a boil. Add bay leaves and habanero chiles.","Cook, stirring occasionally, 30 minutes or until rice reaches the desired tenderness.","Remove bay leaves and chiles. Serve warm."],"x":[],"desc":"There's a lot of Mexican flavors in this dish, like tequila, Mexican oregano, chile powder, habanero chiles, tomato paste, and rice.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mexican_Rice_Pilaf","i":"wb-en-2720","im":["d/dd/Afghan_Palo.jpg/500px-Afghan_Palo.jpg","Jost Wagner","CC BY-SA 1.0","Afghan Palo.jpg","w"],"on":"Mexican Rice Pilaf","og":["2 cups uncooked white rice","2 Tbsp unsalted butter","¾ cup tequila","¾ cup tomato paste","2 ½ cups chicken broth","3 bay leaves","¼ tsp salt","¼ tsp freshly-ground black pepper","2 habanero chiles, stemmed","1 tbsp dried Mexican oregano"]},{"n":"Mexikanische Gewürzmischung","c":"saucen","k":"Mexiko","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["½ Tasse Chilipulver","1 EL Salz","1–2 TL Kreuzkümmel (Samen oder gemahlen)","1 TL oder mehr Knoblauch","1 TL oder mehr der folgenden Zutaten","mexikanischer Oregano","Basilikum","Koriander","Zwiebel (Pulver oder Granulat)","Zimt","Chiliflocken","schwarzer Pfeffer"],"s":["Combine all ingredients.","Store in a cool, dry place."],"x":[],"desc":"Mexican Seasoning is sometimes just chili powder, though many variations on this theme exist. Make your own mixture ahead of time and store in a small shaker for easy use.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mexican_Seasoning","i":"wb-en-2721","on":"Mexican Seasoning","og":["½ cup chili powder","1 tablespoon salt","1–2 teaspoons cumin (seed or powder)","1 teaspoon or more garlic","1 teaspoon or more of the following","Mexican oregano","Basil","Coriander","Onion (powder or granulated)","Cinnamon","Crushed red pepper","Black pepper"]},{"n":"Mexikanische Tequila-Marinade","c":"saucen","k":"Mexiko","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["½ Tasse Tequila","3 EL Mesquite-Honig","¼ TL flüssiger Mesquite-Rauch","¼ Tasse frisch gepresster Limettensaft","1 Habanero-Chili, glatt püriert","1 EL Salz","1 EL frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer"],"s":["Combine all ingredients in an 8-ounce mason jar. Keep refrigerated for up to 2 weeks. Shake well before using."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mexican_Tequila_Marinade","i":"wb-en-2722","on":"Mexican Tequila Marinade","og":["½ cup tequila","3 tbsp mesquite honey","¼ tsp liquid mesquite smoke","¼ cup freshly-squeezed lime juice","1 habanero chile, puréed until smooth","1 tbsp salt","1 tbsp freshly-ground black pepper"]},{"n":"Mexikanische Tomatensuppe","c":"suppen","k":"Mexiko","p":6,"t":10,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["etwa ½ Liter Tomatensoße, passierte Tomaten, oder Ähnliches","2 große Zwiebeln oder entsprechende Menge","2 rote Paprika","2 Tomaten","Zwiebel- oder Lauchgrün","1 Dose Zuckermais","60 ml Pflanzen- oder Olivenöl","Salz","Zucker","weiteres Gemüse nach Geschmack"],"s":["Cut onion fine and fry lightly in a large saucepan with a bit of oil.","Add vegetables, roughly in the order you find logical (ie, tomatoes don't take long, peppers can be there from the start).","Add about ½ teaspoon salt, adjusting to taste. The salt will extract water from the vegetables and make them 'stew' faster.","You can cover the pot if it goes slowly—once again, this slows the evaporation and allows the vegetables to cook in the water they lose themselves.","Add tomato sauce and corn.","Add salt and sugar to taste. Be bold; tomato sauce takes a lot of salt and at least a heaping teaspoon of sugar to taste right. If unsure, separate a small amount and try adding more salt—you will see the tastes changes significantly.","Serve with tortilla chips, or toasted bread if not available."],"x":[],"desc":"Mexican tomato soup is a very simple dish that can be made hot if wanted. It is very nutritious for a soup too.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mexican_Tomato_Soup","i":"wb-en-2723","im":["8/8c/Tomato_soup%2C_plant-based_%2844040252791%29.jpg/960px-Tomato_soup%2C_plant-based_%2844040252791%29.jpg","Ella Olsson from Stockholm, Sweden","CC BY 2.0","Tomato soup, plant-based (44040252791).jpg","w"],"on":"Mexican Tomato Soup","og":["About ½ litre tomato sauce, tomato purée, or similar","2 large onions or equivalent","2 red bell peppers","2 tomatoes","Onion or leek greens","1 can of sweet corn","¼ cup (60 ml) vegetable or olive oil","Salt","Sugar","More vegetables according to your taste"]},{"n":"Mhadjeb (algerisches gefülltes Fladenbrot)","c":"kuchen","k":"Algerien","p":4,"t":60,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse Grieß","½ Tasse Weizenmehl","Salz","Wasser","2 Tomaten","Pflanzenöl","4 Zwiebeln, in dünne Scheiben geschnitten","schwarzer Pfeffer","gemahlene Chili"],"s":["Combine the semolina, flour, and salt together in a bowl. Gradually stir in water with your hands until you get a smooth and soft dough.","Wet a plastic bag in warm water, cover the dough while still dripping, and let it rest. Afterwards, uncover the dough and knead lightly for a few minutes.","Coat your hands in oil, and shape the dough into balls, arranging them beside each other. Cover and allow to rest once more. These extra relaxation periods help to produce superior results.","Peel the tomatoes, then dice them into small pieces.","Heat some oil in a pan over medium-low heat. Add the onions, and stir regularly until they become translucent and soft.","Add the diced tomatoes, seasonings, and salt. Cover the pan and allow the mixture to cook over low heat, stirring occasionally to prevent it from sticking.","Let cool.","On an oiled surface, roll out the first ball of dough and give it a light coating of oil.","Place some filling in the center, and fold the dough over it on four sides to form a square.","Lightly oil the top of the dough and move it to a hot pan over medium-low heat. Cook until the first side is well-browned, then flip it to the other side and brown again. Remove from the pan.","Repeat the shaping and cooking process with the remaining dough and filling.","Serve hot and enjoy!"],"x":[],"desc":"Mhadjeb is a type of thin, flaky Algerian pancake made from semolina and traditionally filled with onion, tomatoes, and even meat with harissa. To ensure the dough turns out well, it must be kneaded for a sufficient amount of time. It has been a favored recipe among Algerian households for many year","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mhadjeb_(Algerian_Stuffed_Flatbread)","i":"wb-en-2724","im":["c/cd/Flatbread.JPG/960px-Flatbread.JPG","Jonathunder","CC BY-SA 3.0","Flatbread.JPG","w"],"on":"Mhadjeb (Algerian Stuffed Flatbread)","og":["1 cup semolina","½ cup all-purpose flour","Salt","Water","2 tomatoes","Vegetable oil","4 onions, sliced thin","Black pepper","Ground chili pepper"]},{"n":"1-2-3-Kuchen aus der Mikrowelle","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":1,"t":8,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Ei","1 EL Honig oder Ahornsirup","2 EL Milch","3 EL Semmelbrösel"],"s":["Beat the egg until smooth.","Add the honey and milk and mix well.","Add the breadcrumbs and mix until uniform.","Let the mixture sit for a few minutes, to allow the breadcrumbs to absorb the moisture.","Pour the mixture into a small silicone mold (e.g. Dollar store loaf pan).","Microwave on high for 4 minutes or a little after it stops rising.","Allow to cool a little; tip out onto a plate if desired.","Top with more maple syrup or honey, if desired."],"x":["Tip: coat the measuring spoon with oil before putting the honey in, so that it slides off easily and doesn't stick to the spoon."],"desc":"Microwave 1-2-3 cake is a quick and easy sweet cake recipe made in the microwave. This recipe is quite forgiving in proportions: careful measurement is not required.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwave_1-2-3_Cake","i":"wb-en-2725","on":"Microwave 1-2-3 Cake","og":["1 egg","1 tablespoon honey or maple syrup","2 tablespoons milk","3 tablespoons bread crumbs"]},{"n":"Apfelmus aus der Mikrowelle","c":"saucen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["5 Äpfel, geschält, entkernt, und gewürfelt","1 ½ Tassen Apfelgelee","¼ Tasse dunkler Ahornsirup (Grade B) (dunkler Ahornsirup, Grade A Dark Amber geht auch)","¼ Tasse frisch gepresster Orangensaft","1 Zimtstange"],"s":["Combine all ingredients in a microwave-safe container.","Cover container, leaving 1 corner open, and microwave on high 7–8 minutes or until apples are easy to mash.","Remove cinnamon stick and discard.","For a chunky sauce, mash the apples with a potato masher. For a slightly smoother sauce, use a hand mixer. For a smooth pureé, use an immersion blender."],"x":[],"desc":"For all of you who would like to make your own applesauce, but without having to do much work, this recipe is for you.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwave_Applesauce","i":"wb-en-2726","on":"Microwave Applesauce","og":["5 apples, peeled, cored, and diced","1½ cups apple jelly","¼ cup Grade B Amber maple syrup (Grade A Dark Amber would be okay too)","¼ cup freshly-squeezed orange juice","1 cinnamon stick"]},{"n":"Schokoladenkuchen aus der Mikrowelle I","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":1,"t":5,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 EL Zucker","4 EL Mehl","4 EL Backkakao","1 Ei","3 EL Milch","3 EL Pflanzenöl (am besten Soja- oder Sonnenblumenöl)","½–1 TL Vanilleextrakt","3 EL Schokotropfen (optional)"],"s":["Mix the dry ingredients well in a small bowl or large mug.","Add the egg and mix thoroughly.","Pour in the milk and oil and mix well.","Add vanilla essence and chocolate chips (if using), mix again.","Pour into two greased 9-inch round baking pans or keep in large mug.","Microwave on high for 3 minutes or until it stops rising.","Allow to cool a little; tip out onto a plate if desired."],"x":["A teaspoon of cinnamon or vanilla adds a nice flavor."],"desc":"A quick and easy chocolate cake recipe made in the microwave.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwave_Chocolate_Cake_I","i":"wb-en-2727","im":["5/55/Chocolate_fudge_cake.jpg/500px-Chocolate_fudge_cake.jpg","Tracy Hunter from Kabul,, Afghanistan","CC BY 2.0","Chocolate fudge cake.jpg","w"],"on":"Microwave Chocolate Cake I","og":["4 Tbsp granulated sugar","4 Tbsp flour","4 Tbsp baking cocoa","1 egg","3 Tbsp milk","3 Tbsp vegetable oil (soybean or sunflower oils work best)","½–1 teaspoon vanilla extract","3 Tbsp chocolate chips (optional)"]},{"n":"Schokoladenkuchen aus der Mikrowelle II","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":1,"t":5,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["4 EL Weizenmehl (60 ml)","4 EL Zucker (60 ml)","2 EL ungesüßtes Kakaopulver (30 ml)","2 EL verquirltes Ei (30 ml)","3 EL Milch (45 ml)","3 EL Pflanzenöl (45 ml)","3 EL Schokotropfen (15 ml), Pinienkerne, oder Haselnüsse","Vanille und/oder Zimt, nach Geschmack"],"s":["Mix all the dry ingredients directly in a microwave-safe mug or bowl.","Add the egg and mix well.","Stir in the milk and oil.","Add the chocolate chips and vanilla. Stir well.","Microwave for 3 minutes at 1000w / 4 minutes at 700w / 3:30 minutes at 750w.","Cool slightly and enjoy."],"x":["If you want a fudgy version, just omit the egg."],"desc":"This recipe is for making an easy chocolate cake, with cheap ingredients that you're sure to have at home. Easy and quickly done in microwave.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwave_Chocolate_Cake_II","i":"wb-en-2728","im":["5/55/Chocolate_fudge_cake.jpg/500px-Chocolate_fudge_cake.jpg","Tracy Hunter from Kabul,, Afghanistan","CC BY 2.0","Chocolate fudge cake.jpg","w"],"on":"Microwave Chocolate Cake II","og":["4 tbsp (60 ml) all-purpose flour","4 tbsp (60 ml) white granulated sugar","2 tbsp (30 ml) unsweetened cocoa powder","2 tbsp (30 ml) whisked egg","3 tbsp (45 ml) milk","3 tbsp (45 ml) vegetable oil","3 tbsp (15 ml) chocolate chips, pine nuts, or hazelnuts","Vanilla and/or cinnamon to taste"]},{"n":"Schokoladenkeks aus der Mikrowelle","c":"brot","k":"","p":1,"t":7,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 EL ungesalzene Butter, bei Zimmertemperatur weich geworden","45 g heller brauner Zucker","½ TL Vanilleextrakt","1 Ei (40 g)","70 g Weizenmehl","1 Prise grobes Salz","40 g Zartbitter-Schokotropfen"],"s":["Line a large microwave-safe plate with parchment.","Beat the butter and sugar in a small bowl until light and fluffy.","Beat in the egg and vanilla.","Sift the flour and salt and fold into the butter mixture. Fold in most of the chocolate chips.","Scoop the dough into center of plate. Decorate with remaining chocolate chips.","Microwave the cookie for 1.5–2 minutes, depending on microwave's power.","Leave the cookie to cool."],"x":[],"desc":"A microwave cookie are a dessert that only takes 2 minutes to cook. This recipe is adapted from the YouTube channel Tasty.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwave_Chocolate_Chip_Cookie","i":"wb-en-2729","im":["b/b4/Choco_chip_cookie.png/500px-Choco_chip_cookie.png","brainloc on sxc.hu (Bob Smith)","CC BY 2.5","Choco chip cookie.png","w"],"on":"Microwave Chocolate Chip Cookie","og":["2 tablespoons unsalted butter, softened at room temperature","¼ cup (45 g / 1.5 oz) light brown sugar","½ teaspoon vanilla extract","1 ea. (around 40 g / 1.5 oz) egg","½ cup (70 g / 2.5 oz) all-purpose flour","1 pinch kosher salt","½ cup (40 g / 1.5 oz) dark chocolate chips"]},{"n":"Schokoladenpudding aus der Mikrowelle","c":"dessert","k":"","p":4,"t":9,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["#Trockene Zutaten","80 g Zucker oder Zuckerersatz","60 g ungesüßtes Kakaopulver","3 EL Speisestärke","⅛ TL Salz","#Feuchte Zutaten","480 ml Milch oder Sojamilch","1 TL Vanilleextrakt oder Vanillearoma"],"s":["In a 1-qt microwave-safe bowl, mix the dry ingredients together.","Add the cold milk and mix well with a small wire whisk or an electric mixer until all the cocoa lumps have dissolved.","Microwave in the bowl, on high (100%) power, for 3 minutes. Stir well.","Microwave, again on high power, for an additional 4–6 minutes, stirring after each minute of cooking.","Remove the bowl from the microwave oven and stir in the vanilla.","Pour the result into 4 small custard cups and chill before serving."],"x":["A microwave-safe lid can be placed, slightly ajar, on the bowl while the pudding is cooking. This will prevent the pudding from splattering all over the microwave.","Keep a close watch on the pudding during the actual cooking, as it can easily boil over."],"desc":"Microwave chocolate pudding is a pudding made with sugar, milk, cocoa powder, and cornstarch. It is prepared in a microwave.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwave_Chocolate_Pudding","i":"wb-en-2730","im":["0/03/2020-03-08_23_43_19_Jell-O_chocolate_pudding_in_the_Dulles_section_of_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/960px-2020-03-08_23_43_19_Jell-O_chocolate_pudding_in_the_Dulles_section_of_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg","Famartin","CC BY-SA 4.0","2020-03-08 23 43 19 Jell-O chocolate pudding in the Dulles section of Sterling, Loudoun County, Virginia.jpg","w"],"on":"Microwave Chocolate Pudding","og":["#Dry ingredients","⅓ cup (80 g) white granulated sugar or sugar substitute","¼ cup (60 g) unsweetened cocoa powder","3 Tbsp cornstarch","⅛ tsp salt","#Wet ingredients","2 cups (480 ml) milk or soy milk","1 tsp vanilla extract or imitation vanilla"]},{"n":"Zitronenpuddings aus der Mikrowelle","c":"dessert","k":"","p":4,"t":15,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["6 EL selbstgemachter oder gekaufter Lemon Curd","4 TL kochendes Wasser","80 g Margarine","⅓ Tasse feiner Zucker","1 Ei","1 Zitrone, Schale abgerieben","½ Zitrone, ausgepresst","½ Tasse selbsttreibendes Mehl (Mehl mit Backpulver)","1 EL Puderzucker","Himbeeren (optional)","Crème fraîche (optional)"],"s":["Grease 4 ea. microwave-safe ramekins.","Mix together the lemon curd and water in a bowl.","Spoon the mixture into the ramekins.","Beat the margarine and sugar together in another bowl.","Beat in the egg and lemon zest.","Fold in the flour, then mix in the lemon juice.","Divide the mixture between ramekins and smooth the tops.","Put the ramekins on a plate and microwave for 4 minutes. Let stand 1 minute.","Dust the puddings with powdered sugar and serve, optionally, with raspberries and crème fraîche."],"x":[],"desc":"These microwave lemon puddings are adapted from a recipe in page 98 of April 2023 edition of Tesco's magazine.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwave_Lemon_Puddings","i":"wb-en-2731","on":"Microwave Lemon Puddings","og":["6 tablespoons homemade or purchased lemon curd","4 teaspoons boiling water","⅓ cup (80 g/2.8 oz) margarine","⅓ cup () superfine sugar","1 egg","1 lemon, zested","½ lemon, juiced","½ cup () self-rising flour","1 tablespoon powdered sugar","Raspberries (optional)","Crème fraîche (optional)"]},{"n":"Haferbrei aus der Mikrowelle","c":"welt","k":"","p":1,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["250 ml Wasser","100 ml Haferflocken","1 Prise Salz"],"s":["Mix water, oat flakes, and salt in a bowl.","Boil on high heat for 2–3 minutes.","Stir and serve immediately.","sv:Gröt i mikrovågsugnen"],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwave_Oat_Porridge","i":"wb-en-2732","on":"Microwave Oat Porridge","og":["250 ml water","100 ml oat flakes","1 pinch salt"]},{"n":"Erdnusskrokant aus der Mikrowelle","c":"dessert","k":"","p":1,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse Zucker","½ Tasse heller Maissirup","1 Tasse geröstete Erdnüsse","1 TL Butter","1 TL Vanille","1 TL Natron"],"s":["Lightly grease a cookie sheet and set aside.","In 1½-quart casserole dish, stir together sugar and syrup. Microwave on high for 4 minutes.","Stir in peanuts. Microwave on high for 3–5 minutes or until light brown.","Add butter and vanilla, mixing well. Microwave at high 1–2 minutes more. The peanuts will be lightly browned and syrup very hot.","Add baking soda and stir gently until light and foamy.","Pour mixture onto greased cookie sheet. Let cool ½–1 hour.","When cool, break into small pieces and store in airtight container."],"x":["Take care not to overcook or under cook. Overcooking results in a burnt taste, and under cooking results in a taffy-like consistency that sticks to the teeth.","Microwave times will depend on the power of your individual microwave. It may take a few experiments before you determine what is the right cooking time.","If you start seeing part of the mixture turning brown, it is probably beginning to burn. Remove immediately."],"desc":"This is an easier version of Peanut Brittle that can be prepared in under 10 minutes using a microwave.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwave_Peanut_Brittle","i":"wb-en-2733","im":["2/21/Golden_peanut_brittle_cracked_on_a_serving_dish.jpg/960px-Golden_peanut_brittle_cracked_on_a_serving_dish.jpg","Janet Hudson","CC BY 2.0","Golden peanut brittle cracked on a serving dish.jpg","w"],"on":"Microwave Peanut Brittle","og":["1 cup white granulated sugar","½ cup white corn syrup","1 cup roasted peanuts","1 teaspoon butter","1 teaspoon vanilla","1 teaspoon baking soda"]},{"n":"Quesadilla aus der Mikrowelle","c":"snacks","k":"Mexiko","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Tortillas","etwa ¼ Tasse geriebener Schmelzkäse (30 ml) (meist Monterey Jack, andere gehen auch)","mindestens eine der folgenden Füllungen","Salsa","Salsa criolla","Chilischoten","gehackte Tomaten und Koriander","gegartes Fleisch oder Meeresfrüchte","Avocado oder Guacamole","frischer Spinat, gewaschen und in kleine Stücke gezupft","schwarze Bohnen aus der Dose, abgespült und gut abgetropft","beliebige der folgenden Beläge","Salsa","Guacamole","saure Sahne"],"s":["Place one tortilla on a microwave-safe plate.","Cover with half the cheese and sprinkle on fillings as desired.","Spread remaining cheese over the toppings, and place second tortilla on top.","Microwave on high power for 30–60 seconds (or until cheese is melted and fillings are warm).","Add desired toppings and enjoy."],"x":["You are not limited to those fillings/toppings listed. However, ensure they can be thoroughly cooked/warmed in the short time necessary to melt the cheese."],"desc":"Microwave Quesadilla is a dish in Tex-Mex or Mexican cuisine, which involves cooking ingredients, most popularly cheese, inside a corn or wheat tortilla","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwave_Quesadilla","i":"wb-en-2734","im":["0/01/Empanada_flor_de_Calabaza.jpg/960px-Empanada_flor_de_Calabaza.jpg","nsaum75 ¡שיחת! ‎","CC BY-SA 3.0","Empanada flor de Calabaza.jpg","w"],"on":"Microwave Quesadilla","og":["2 tortillas","About ¼ cup (30 ml) meltable shredded cheese (typically Monterey Jack cheese, but others are okay)","At least one of the following fillings","Salsa","Sarza criolla","Chili peppers","Chopped tomatoes and cilantro","Cooked meat or seafood","Avocado or guacamole","Fresh spinach, washed and torn into small pieces","Canned lback beans, rinsed and well drained","Any of the following toppings","Salsa","Guacamole","Sour cream"]},{"n":"Risotto aus der Mikrowelle","c":"fleisch","k":"","p":3,"t":40,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["750 ml heiße, simmernde Hühnerbrühe","½ TL Salz","1 Spritzer gemahlener weißer oder schwarzer Pfeffer","2 EL Butter","2 EL Olivenöl","90 g fein gehackte gelbe Zwiebel","125 g ungekochter Mittelkornreis"],"s":["In a saucepan, bring chicken broth, salt and pepper to a low simmer, and keep warm until needed.","In an oven-proof dish (or 10-inch/25 cm quiche dish), heat oil and butter in microwave for 2 minutes.","Add minced onion to the dish, stir to coat with oil, and cook in microwave for 4 minutes.","Add uncooked rice to the dish, stir to coat with oil, and cook in microwave for another 4 minutes.","Pour simmering chicken broth into the dish and stir well. Microwave 9 minutes.","Stir rice and chicken broth well and microwave another 9 minutes.","If a creamier risotto is desired, add ¼ cup () warm water, stir well and microwave for another 2 minutes."],"x":["For a 750-watt microwave, use 100% power settings for each time interval. For 1000 or 1500-watt microwaves, use 70% power settings for each time interval.","As a variation, use 2½ cups () chicken broth and ½ cup () white wine.","Freshly-grated Parmesan cheese may also be added after cooking."],"desc":"Microwave risotto is made using the microwave. It requires very little stirring and turns out quite well.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwave_Risotto","i":"wb-en-2735","im":["a/a5/Risotto_with_speck_and_goat_cheese_%286101067436%29.jpg/960px-Risotto_with_speck_and_goat_cheese_%286101067436%29.jpg","Luca Nebuloni from Milan, Italy","CC BY 2.0","Risotto with speck and goat cheese (6101067436).jpg","w"],"on":"Microwave Risotto","og":["3 cups (750 ml/1.6 pints) simmering hot chicken broth","½ teaspoon salt","1 dash ground white or black pepper","2 tablespoons butter","2 tablespoons olive oil","½ cup (90 g/3.2 oz) minced yellow onion","1 cup (125 g/4.4 oz) uncooked medium grain rice"]},{"n":"Lachs im Pergamentpäckchen aus der Mikrowelle","c":"fisch","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Lachsfilet (230 g)","⅓ Tasse frischer Dill","⅓ Tasse frische Petersilie","⅓ Tasse frischer Oregano","⅓ Tasse frischer Thymian","2 Zweige frischer Rosmarin","Salz","frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","1 TL Paprikapulver","4 Zitronenscheiben","Weißwein","1 EL ungesalzene Butter, gewürfelt"],"s":["Take a 15 x 36-inch piece of parchment paper, and fold it in half like a book. Draw a large half-heart on the paper, with fold of the paper being the center line of the heart. Cut out heart and open.","Place fresh herbs in the bottom of half of the heart. Place 2 lemon slices on top of the herbs and top with the salmon. Sprinkle both sides with salt, paprika, and freshly ground black pepper.","Drizzle salmon with white wine and top evenly with butter cubes. Top with remaining lemon slices.","Fold other side of heart over fish and starting at top of heart shape, fold up both edges of parchment, overlapping folds as you move along. Once you reach the end tip, twist several times to secure tightly.","Place on a microwave-safe plate and microwave on high 4 minutes, or until internal temperature reaches 131°F. Open parchment and serve warm."],"x":["If you don't like the idea of microwaving the salmon, feel free to bake it in the oven for 12 minutes at 425°F."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwave_Salmon_in_a_Parchment_Envelope","i":"wb-en-2736","on":"Microwave Salmon in a Parchment Envelope","og":["1 filet (8 ounces) salmon","⅓ cup fresh dill","⅓ cup fresh parsley","⅓ cup fresh oregano","⅓ cup fresh thyme","2 sprigs fresh rosemary","Salt","Freshly-ground black pepper","1 tsp paprika","4 lemon slices","White wine","1 tbsp unsalted butter, cubed"]},{"n":"Artischocke aus der Mikrowelle","c":"welt","k":"","p":1,"t":10,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 mittelgroße Artischocke","1 Zitrone, ausgepresst","Wasser","Petersilie (optional)","1–2 Knoblauchzehen (optional)","Pfeffer (optional)","30 ml Weißwein (optional)","Dips, z. B. geklärte Butter oder Mayonnaise"],"s":["Cut off top ⅓ of the artichoke, and all but 1 inch of the stem.","Remove base leaves and cut off the tips of the higher leaves.","Sprinkle artichoke with lemon juice to preserve color.","Place artichoke stem up in a microwave-safe dish tall enough to place lid without touching the artichoke.","Fill dish with 1 inch (3 cm) of water and any of the seasonings.","Cover and microwave on high for 6–8 minutes, and allow to rest for 1–2 minutes. The artichoke is cooked when a paring knife can be inserted into the heart without resistance.","Remove artichoke from the dish and place upside down to drain.","Serve whole, with one or more dips. Diners should remove a leaf, dip the base of the leaf in the dip, and eat the fleshy base of the leaf.","When all the leaves are gone, remove the choke, cut the heart of the artichoke into bite sized pieces, and serve with the dip."],"x":[],"desc":"Basic recipe on how to cook artichokes. Similar results can be obtained using the steamed artichoke recipe, but using the microwave oven is much faster.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwaved_Artichoke","i":"wb-en-2737","on":"Microwaved Artichoke","og":["1 medium artichoke","1 lemon, juiced","Water","Parsley (optional)","1–2 garlic cloves (optional)","Pepper (optional)","⅛ cup (30 ml) white wine (optional)","Dips, such as drawn butter or mayonnaise"]},{"n":"Basmatireis aus der Mikrowelle","c":"beilagen","k":"","p":1,"t":40,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["57 g ungekochter Basmatireis","1 Prise Salz","300 ml kochendes Wasser"],"s":["Add rice and salt to the rice cooker.","Mix in boiling water, then fit the double lids on.","Cook as follows, stirring halfway through","700W for 13 minutes, or","750W for 12 minutes, or","800W for 11 minutes, or","850W for 10 minutes.","Let stand for 5 minutes, then drain in a sieve.","Spread the rice onto an oven paper-lined tray and warming it at a very low setting in a conventional oven. Turn the rice gently from time to time."],"x":["If you have a power choice, use a lower one rather than the highest, especially when cooking less than 1 serving."],"desc":"This recipe was tested several times using a cheap plastic microwave 'rice cooker', which is a bowl with a fastening double lid. On each occasion it produced a light, very white, fragrant and delicate result. The amount of water in this recipe allows a slight excess that is important for the rice qu","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwaved_Basmati_Rice","i":"wb-en-2738","on":"Microwaved Basmati Rice","og":["57 g uncooked Basmati rice","1 pinch salt","300 ml boiling water"]},{"n":"Rührei aus der Mikrowelle","c":"welt","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Eier","Butter"],"s":["Crack the eggs and butter in a coffee cup.","Microwave on high power for 30 seconds.","Remove from the microwave, stir, and replace.","Cook for another 30 seconds on high."],"x":["Cooking time may vary slightly depending on the microwave oven's high power default setting."],"desc":"Using a microwave oven is a quick and relatively easy way to cook eggs. Make sure to pop the egg yolk and let it leak with the egg's white. When the yolk is not popped, it may explode.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Microwaved_Scrambled_Egg","i":"wb-en-2739","im":["2/20/Scrambed_eggs.jpg/960px-Scrambed_eggs.jpg","Takeaway","CC BY-SA 3.0","Scrambed eggs.jpg","w"],"on":"Microwaved Scrambled Egg","og":["2 eggs","Butter"]},{"n":"Orientalische Lammspieße","c":"saucen","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["½ TL frisch gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","¼ Tasse Rotweinessig","¼ Tasse Olivenöl","1 EL Cayennepfeffer","1 TL Salz","1 TL frisch gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","1 EL geräuchertes Paprikapulver","4 Zehen Knoblauch, zerdrückt und fein gehackt","450 g Lammkeule (vom Haxenende), in 4-cm-Würfel geschnitten"],"s":["Combine all ingredients except lamb in a gallon size zip-top bag. Add lamb cubes and toss to coat; refrigerate overnight to marinate.","The next day, drain lamb and discard marinade.","Thread 4 lamb cubes onto one skewer. Repeat until all lamb has been skewered.","Fire up a charcoal grill for 15 minutes. Add lamb and cook 8 minutes per side for medium rare.","Serve warm with couscous."],"x":["The vinegar will not turn the lamb into mush as it is not acidic enough to tenderize."],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Middle_Eastern_Lamb_Kabobs","i":"wb-en-2740","on":"Middle Eastern Lamb Kabobs","og":["½ tsp freshly-ground cumin","¼ cup red wine vinegar","¼ cup olive oil","1 tbsp cayenne pepper","1 tsp salt","1 tsp freshly-ground black pepper","1 Tbsp smoked paprika","4 cloves garlic, smashed and minced","1 pound (450 g) leg of lamb (shank end), cut into 1½ inch cubes"]},{"n":"Orientalische Fleischbällchen","c":"saucen","k":"Nahost","p":6,"t":60,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 Tasse fettarmer Naturjoghurt","1–2 TL fein gehackter Knoblauch","1 TL zerriebene getrocknete Minze","Salz, nach Geschmack","340 g mageres Rinderhack (93 %)","½ Tasse gekochter Naturreis","⅓ Tasse fein gehackte Zwiebel","¼ Tasse fest gedrückter Koriander, gehackter Koriander","¼ Tasse fest gedrückte glatte Petersilie, gehackt","½ TL gemahlener Zimt","¼ TL gemahlener Kreuzkümmel","⅛ TL Chiliflocken","⅛ TL gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer","½ TL Salz"],"s":["In a small bowl, whisk together the yogurt, garlic, and mint. Season to taste with salt.","Set the broiler rack 5 inches from the heat.","Preheat the broiler.","In a mixing bowl, combine the meat, rice, onion, cilantro, parsley, cinnamon, cumin, red and black peppers, and ½ teaspoon salt, stirring mixture with a fork until it is well blended","With your hands, form the mixture into 1½-inch meatballs.","As you make them, place the meatballs on a baking sheet that fits under the broiler.","Broil the meatballs until they are well browned on top, 4 to 5 minutes.","Using tongs, turn and cook until the meatballs are browned outside and no longer pink in the center, 3–4 minutes.","Transfer them to a serving plate and serve warm, passing the yogurt sauce in a bowl."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Middle_Eastern_Meatballs","i":"wb-en-2741","im":["c/cb/Soup_with_meatballs-01.jpg/500px-Soup_with_meatballs-01.jpg","ralphhogaboom","CC BY-SA 2.0","Soup with meatballs-01.jpg","w"],"on":"Middle Eastern Meatballs","og":["1 cup low-fat plain yogurt","1–2 teaspoons finely-chopped garlic","1 teaspoon crushed dried mint","Salt to taste","¾ pound 93% lean ground beef","½ cup cooked brown rice","⅓ cup finely-chopped onion","¼ cup packed cilantro, chopped coriander","¼ cup packed flat-leaf parsley, chopped","½ teaspoon ground cinnamon","¼ teaspoon ground cumin","⅛ teaspoon red pepper flakes","⅛ teaspoon ground black pepper","½ teaspoon salt"]},{"n":"Hähnchenflügel nach Art des Mittleren Westens","c":"fleisch","k":"USA","p":6,"t":180,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2 Zehen Knoblauch, fein gehackt","1 EL frischer Ingwer, fein gehackt","1 Tasse Sojasoße","340 g Aprikosenkonfitüre (keine eingemachten Aprikosen, kein Aprikosengelee)","1,8 kg Hähnchenflügel"],"s":["Place all ingredients except chicken into a bowl and mix to make a marinade.","Marinate the chicken in the refrigerator with the marinade for at least 3 hours. A plastic bag sealed tight without much air or free space is believed to provide the best marinating. As with many marinating recipes, the longer the better.","Clean and preheat grill to medium heat.","Place wings on grill. Turn 1–4 times over the next 20 minutes."],"x":["Cut the chicken wings into two pieces at the elbow joint (recommended).","For the health conscious, remove the chicken skin.","Heat marinade on grill along with chicken wings, and add a little to the wings when done (See Warnings below).","1 teaspoon of ginger powder can be substituted for the fresh ginger.","Feel free to apply the marinade recipe to other chicken cuts, such as breasts. A shish-kabob variation of this recipe is also excellent.","Ensure a clean kitchen environment (hands, surfaces, etc), since this recipe requires marinating."],"desc":"Midwestern chicken wings are not to be confused with hot wings; midwestern wings are not spicy.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Midwestern_Chicken_Wings","i":"wb-en-2742","on":"Midwestern Chicken Wings","og":["2 cloves garlic, minced","1 tablespoon fresh ginger, minced","1 cup soy sauce","12 ounces apricot preserves (not preserved apricots, not apricot jelly)","4–5 pounds chicken wings"]},{"n":"Milder salziger Lassi","c":"welt","k":"Indien","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1 TL Kreuzkümmelsamen (4 g)","250 ml Vollmilchjoghurt","250 ml kalte Milch","2 TL Limetten- oder Zitronensaft","½–1 TL Salz (2–4 g)","100 ml Eiswürfel","¼ TL Minze (fein zerbröselt, getrocknet, optional)","1 eine kleine Prise Cayennepfeffer (optional)"],"s":["Dry-roast cumin seeds by cooking them over low heat in a small pan until you can smell the seasoning (about 2–3 minutes). Cool and grind.","In blender, blend cumin seed powder with yoghurt, milk, lemon juice, salt, and ice cubes.","Serve chilled, optionally garnished with crumbled mint and a small pinch of cayenne."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mild_Salty_Lassi","i":"wb-en-2743","im":["f/f1/Salt_lassi.jpg/960px-Salt_lassi.jpg","Raksanand","CC BY-SA 4.0","Salt lassi.jpg","w"],"on":"Mild Salty Lassi","og":["1 teaspoon (4 g) cumin seeds","250 ml (1 cup) full-fat yogurt","250 ml (1 cup) chilled milk","2 teaspoons lime or lemon juice","½–1 teaspoon (2–4 g) salt","100 ml (½ cup) ice cubes","¼ teaspoon mint (finely crumbled, dried; optional)","1 small pinch of cayenne pepper (optional)"]},{"n":"Vollmilchschokoladen-Tarte mit Pfefferwodka","c":"kuchen","k":"USA","p":12,"t":60,"d":2,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["#Boden","½ Tasse Zucker","1 Tasse ungesalzene Butter","1 Ei","½ TL Vanille","340 g Brotmehl (Type 812)","2 geröstete rote Paprika, in Öl eingelegt","#Füllung","280 g Vollmilchschokolade, in Stücke geschnitten","1 Tasse ungesalzene Butter","½ TL Vanille","½ Tasse Pfefferwodka","1 ¼ Tassen Zucker","3 Eier","170 g Brotmehl (Type 812)","#Belag","470 ml Schlagsahne","115 g Puderzucker","¼ Tasse Pfefferwodka","340 g weiße Schokolade, geschmolzen","½ TL Muskatnuss"],"s":["Place sugar, butter, egg and vanilla in a mixing bowl, and mix at low speed until combined.","Add flour and mix until incorporated; do not over mix.","Set the dough on a floured cookie pan and press flat.","Refrigerate until firm enough to roll out, 45 minutes to an hour.","After making filling, line an 11-inch cake pan with the crust.","Line the bottom of the unbaked tart shell with a single thin layer of red bell peppers that have been wiped free of most of the oil.","Melt chocolate and butter over low heat in a saucepan.","Stir in vanilla.","Take off the heat and add pepper vodka and let cool slightly.","While the chocolate mixture is cooling, whip the sugar and eggs until light and fluffy.","Fold into cooled chocolate mixture.","Sift the flour into this mixture, making sure there are no lumps.","Preheat oven to 350°F.","Pour chocolate mixture on top of red bell pepper layer, leaving ¾ inch at the top of pan.","Bake for about 20 minutes. The center should be soft, similar to a pumpkin pie when it is done.","Let cool before taking it out of the pan.","Refrigerate overnight before cutting.","Whip cream and confectioners' sugar until peaks are thick, then slowly whip in vodka.","When vodka is completely mixed in, add melted white chocolate while whisking.","Refrigerate for 4 hours.","Top each piece with plenty of whipped cream, sprinkle lightly with nutmeg and enjoy."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Milk_Chocolate_Pepper_Vodka_Tart","i":"wb-en-2744","on":"Milk Chocolate Pepper Vodka Tart","og":["#Crust","½ cup white granulated sugar","1 cup (2 sticks) unsalted butter","1 egg","½ teaspoon vanilla","2½ cups (12 ounces) bread flour","2 roasted red bell peppers, packed in oil","#Filling","10 ounces milk chocolate, cut into pieces","1 cup (2 sticks) unsalted butter","½ teaspoon vanilla","½ cup pepper vodka","1¼ cups white granulated sugar","3 eggs","1¼ cups (6 ounces) bread flour","#Topping","1 pint heavy whipping cream","1 cup (4 ounces) confectioners' sugar","¼ cup pepper vodka","12 ounces white chocolate, melted","½ teaspoon nutmeg"]},{"n":"Milchtoast I","c":"fruehstueck","k":"","p":1,"t":10,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["570 ml Milch, zum Teil Sahne, wenn das nicht verboten ist","4 Scheiben gutes Brot, frisch geröstet","Süßrahmbutter, wenn erlaubt","Salz","Pfeffer"],"s":["Heat the milk to the simmering point.","Generously butter the toast slices.","Heat a pretty bowl, deeper than it is wide. Break the hot buttered toast into it, pour the steaming but not boiling milk over it, sprinkle a little salt and pepper on the top, and serve at once."],"x":["Although the recipe calls for salt, milk toast may also be made sweet by the omission of salt and pepper and the addition, instead, of sugar. Other optional ingredients for sweet versions include cinnamon, honey or a touch of vanilla, but piquant and exotic ingredients should be avoided, as the primary purpose of milk toast is to provide a food soothing to the palate and to the digestion."],"desc":"Milk toast is a breakfast food consisting of toasted bread dipped in milk. Milk toast was a popular food throughout the late 19th century and early 20th century, especially for young children and for the ailing, for whom the food was thought to be soothing and easy to digest. Although not as popular","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Milk_Toast_I","i":"wb-en-2745","im":["d/d4/Milktoast.jpg/960px-Milktoast.jpg","Icandostuff","CC BY 4.0","Milktoast.jpg","w"],"on":"Milk Toast I","og":["1 pint (570 ml) milk, part cream if the person is not forbidden that","4 slices good bread, freshly toasted","Sweet butter, if allowed","Salt","Pepper"]},{"n":"Milchtoast II","c":"fruehstueck","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":1,"v":1,"l":"en","g":["570 ml abgekochte Milch","½ TL Salz","2 EL Butter","4 EL kaltes Wasser","2 ½ EL Brotmehl (Type 812)","6 Scheiben trockener Toast"],"s":["Gradually add cold water to flour to make a smooth, thin paste.","Add paste to milk, stirring constantly until thickened.","Cover, and cook 20 minutes; then, add salt and butter in small pieces.","Dip slices of toast separately in sauce; when soft, remove to serving dish. Pour remaining sauce over all."],"x":["Although both above recipes call for salt, milk toast may also be made sweet by the omission of salt and pepper and the addition, instead, of sugar. Other optional ingredients for sweet versions include cinnamon, honey or a touch of vanilla, but piquant and exotic ingredients should be avoided, as the primary purpose of milk toast is to provide a food soothing to the palate and to the digestion.","Corn starch may be substituted for flour."],"desc":"Milk toast is a breakfast food consisting of toasted bread dipped in milk. Milk toast was a popular food throughout the late 19th century and early 20th century, especially for young children and for the ailing, for whom the food was thought to be soothing and easy to digest. Although not as popular","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Milk_Toast_II","i":"wb-en-2746","im":["d/d4/Milktoast.jpg/960px-Milktoast.jpg","Icandostuff","CC BY 4.0","Milktoast.jpg","w"],"on":"Milk Toast II","og":["1 pint (570 ml) scalded milk","½ teaspoon salt","2 tablespoons butter","4 tablespoons cold water","2 ½ tablespoons bread flour","6 slices dry toast"]},{"n":"Mince-Pie-Törtchen mit Schweinefleisch","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":36,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["400 g Zucker","300 ml Wein","250 ml Apfelmost","1 Orange, Schale abgerieben und Saft ausgepresst","1 Zitrone, Schale abgerieben und Saft ausgepresst","¼ TL gemahlene Muskatblüte","¼ TL gemahlene Muskatnuss","1 Zimtstange","1 Vanilleschote","1 kg Mincemeat-Mischung (Früchtefüllung)","800 g entkernte Äpfel in Scheiben (von etwa 12 großen Äpfeln)","2 Packungen Mürbeteig","1 kg mageres Schweinehack","100 g Butter"],"s":["Preheat oven to 150 °C (300 °F).","In a pot, bring the sugar, wine, cider, orange, and lemon juice to a simmer. Add mace, nutmeg, and cinnamon. Split the vanilla pod and scrape seeds into pot. Discard vanilla pod.","Stir in sliced apples and fruit mix.","Grease the muffin tins, and line with pastry dough to make tartlet cases. Trim to fit.","Place cases into oven, and bake until lightly golden. Remove from oven and let cool.","Melt butter in a pan. Add minced pork, and sauté until browned.","Remove cinnamon stick from the fruit mixture, and mix in the pork.","Using a tablespoon, fill tartlet cases with the filling—it will probably be mounded.","If desired, trim with excess pastry.","Bake each tray at 120 °C (250 °F) for half an hour."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mince_Pie_Tartlets_with_Pork","i":"wb-en-2747","im":["d/d0/Mince_Pie.jpg/960px-Mince_Pie.jpg","en:User:Jmb","CC BY 2.5","Mince Pie.jpg","w"],"on":"Mince Pie Tartlets with Pork","og":["400 g white granulated sugar","300 ml wine","250 ml cider","1 orange, zested and juiced","1 lemon, zested and juiced","¼ teaspoon ground mace","¼ teaspoon ground nutmeg","1 cinnamon stick","1 vanilla pod","1 kg fruit mince mixture","800 g cored and sliced apples (from about 12 large apples)s","2 packets shortcrust pastry dough","1 kg lean pork mince","100 g butter"]},{"n":"Mince Pie mit Fleisch I","c":"kuchen","k":"","p":15,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["1815 g mageres Rindfleisch, gewürfelt","454 g Butter, Schmalz, oder Pflanzenfett, gewürfelt","907 g Zucker","907 g Obstmischung","1815 g entkernte Äpfel in Scheiben","350 ml Wein","250 ml Apfelmost","1 Zitrusfrüchte (z. B. Orange), Schale abgerieben und Saft ausgepresst","¼ TL gemahlene Muskatblüte","¼ TL gemahlene Muskatnuss","5 Packungen Mürbeteig"],"s":["Sear diced beef in a pan until well-coloured (this can be done in batches). Set aside until cool.","Combined all ingredients except dough in a bowl. Mix well (this step can be done in batches).","Use the pastry dough to line 3 deep, greased pie pans (or 5 greased muffin pans, for tartlets) and create pie shells.","Place shells into oven and set to 150 °C (300 °F). Bake until lightly golden. Remove from oven and let rest until cooled.","Fill pie shells with filling mixture until level or slightly mounded above the rim. Trim with excess pastry.","Bake at 150 °C (300 °F) for 45 minutes per tray (or 35 minutes per muffin tray)."],"x":[],"desc":"","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mince_Pie_with_Meat_I","i":"wb-en-2748","im":["d/d0/Mince_Pie.jpg/960px-Mince_Pie.jpg","en:User:Jmb","CC BY 2.5","Mince Pie.jpg","w"],"on":"Mince Pie with Meat I","og":["1815 g (4 lb) lean beef, diced","454 g (1 lb) butter, lard, or vegetable shortening, diced","907 g (2 lb) white granulated sugar","907 g (2 lb) fruit mix","1815 g (4 lb) cored and sliced apples","350 ml wine","250 ml cider","1 citrus fruit (e.g. orange), zested and juiced","¼ teaspoon ground mace","¼ teaspoon ground nutmeg","5 packets of shortcrust pastry dough"]},{"n":"Mincemeat (Früchtefüllung)","c":"dessert","k":"","p":4,"t":0,"d":2,"v":0,"l":"en","g":["2.7–3.6 kg Baldwin-Äpfel","Rindergulasch (Hals, Brustspitze usw.)","1 ganze Zitrone, Kerne entfernt","160 g kernlose dunkle Rosinen","900 g Zucker","2 ½ TL gemahlener Zimt","½ TL gemahlene Muskatnuss","½ TL gemahlene Nelken","1 EL Instantkaffee (normal oder entkoffeiniert)","1 TL Salz","250 ml Apfelessig","375 ml Fleischbrühe","500 g Sorghumsirup oder normale Melasse","½ TL gemahlener schwarzer Pfeffer"],"s":["Core apples; remove the seeds, but don’t peel.","Cube meat and cover with water. Simmer until tender; this may take up to an hour.","Remove meat and cook the stock down to the amount needed, or thicken slightly with cornstarch.","Run meat through a food mill (medium or coarse blade), or grind to an equivalent fineness in a food processor.","Cut lemon in half and remove seeds. Purée the whole lemon in a blender, rind and all, with some of the liquid ingredients, or process as finely as possible in a food processor.","Grind the apples (or process using a coarse blade—but not too fine).","Combine the apple, meat, and raisins in a large, heavy-bottomed pot.","Add the sugar, spices, liquids, and lemon purée to the meat and apples. Use hot meat stock to rinse the last of the molasses into the mixture. Stir thoroughly.","Cook slowly, uncovered, stirring often to prevent burning until the mixture is pasteurized and enough of the liquids have evaporated to produce the texture and thickness you want in the finished mixture.","Let cool, then stir in the ground pepper.","Refrigerate, allowing the spices to mellow for several weeks."],"x":["If desired, you can substitute ½–¾ cup (125–185 ml/4.2/6.3 oz) of the meat stock with a high quality brandy.","The apples are the most important ingredient, without doubt. Insipid apples make lousy mincemeat. A sharp, crisp, flavor-laden “pie” apple is best—late maturing Baldwins and Cortlands are good. Granny Smiths are crisp and tart but less flavorful. If you can’t find Baldwins or Cortlands, use the best pie apple you can find at their peak of flavor and texture in the autumn.","Mincemeat at its best needs a few weeks to season in the refrigerator, say 6–8 weeks. If you make it in late October or early November, the spices and flavors will continue to mellow and be just right for Thanksgiving and the coming holidays.","The suet can be removed before cooking and the fat skimmed off that renders from the meat as it cooks if desired."],"desc":"Mincemeat is a mixture of spiced chopped fruits. Traditionally mincemeat has contained meat, although many modern recipes omit it. This recipe, however, does contain beef.","img":"","u":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Mincemeat","i":"wb-en-2749","im":["4/46/Making_Mince_pies_-_tarts_in_baking_tray.jpg/960px-Making_Mince_pies_-_tarts_in_baking_tray.jpg","Beck","CC BY 2.0","Making Mince pies - tarts in baking tray.jpg","w"],"on":"Mincemeat","og":["6–8 pounds (2.7–3.6 kg/about 30 ea.) Baldwin apples","stew beef (neck, plate, etc.)","1 whole lemon, seeds removed","2 cups (160 g/5.6 oz) seedless black raisins","4 cups (900 g/2 lb) sugar","2 ½ tsp ground cinnamon","½ tsp ground nutmeg","½ tsp ground cloves","1 Tbsp dried coffee (regular or decaffeinated)","1 tsp salt","1 cup (250 ml/8.5 oz) cider vinegar","1 ½ cups (375 ml/12.7 oz) meat stock","1 ½ cups (500 g/1.1 lb) sorghum molasses or regular molasses","½ tsp ground black pepper"]}]);
